{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:23:36.082Z","ordinal":457321,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a182ae-3012-7261-b9de-064ebfbc93fa","call_id":"call_359499f10ab24f5bb76b46a3721f7bba","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"label\":\"pr300-local\",\"chunk_id\":\"7d6d22\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00003594,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":92,\"output\":\"## v1/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028...origin/v1/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028\\n M docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\\n48c14a09 docs: distinguish PR305 check results\\n270051de docs: correct current release gate states\\ndbeb8c7f docs: refresh release checkpoint after PR304\\n48c14a0937549fc9e243a2da59338a4368338e1d\\n270051dec4170bbaf98ca6d7a0fdc9431db4aa56\\n2026-10-28T13:20:06+00:00\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"label\":\"suite-activity\",\"chunk_id\":\"6428ff\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000041372,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":59,\"output\":\"3209682 2661377 Wed Oct 28 13:23:34 2026 Ss   /usr/bin/zsh -c ps -eo pid,ppid,lstart,stat,cmd | rg '3124759|run_tests.mjs|repl_approval_driver'\\n3209686 3209682 Wed Oct 28 13:23:34 2026 S    rg 3124759|run_tests.mjs|repl_approval_driver\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"label\":\"decision-docs\",\"chunk_id\":\"302807\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000038999,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2637,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2637)\\nTotal output lines: 29\\n\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:1:# Nexus Code v1.0.0: release qualification procedure\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:3:This is the procedure that decides whether a release candidate (RC) may become v1.0.0. It defines:\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:16:| **Independent acceptance** | Did a reviewer other than the implementer agree? |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:22:The release sequence has five distinct stages. Passing an earlier stage is a prerequisite for the next stage, not a substitute for it. Every G0–G4 acceptance ID remains mandatory; the stage determines which exact input and evidence it evaluates, not whether the check applies.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:24:1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:25:2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:26:3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:34:The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. A…137 tokens truncated…T-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:48:| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:84:## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:86:Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:141:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:151:| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:158:## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:211:### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:216:- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:271:| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 20 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:276:| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:284:## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:310:**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \\\"Accept with defects\\\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:332:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI, scripted and manual gates PASS.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:335:- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:339:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker verifies source/tag/artifact/evidence hash bindings; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:346:**Outcome recording.** The release decision record goes in `docs/releases/v1.0.0.md`, with links to every evidence directory.\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1828e-5af5-7fb1-bc6f-34b2f291d340","create_time":1793193816.082714}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
