{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:23:53.889Z","ordinal":457341,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1828e-5af5-7fb1-bc6f-34b2f291d340","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8c631fe5-3998-4a48-a0a3-e26d53eeb733","process_id":"59489","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,240p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md && tail -45 .git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log 2>/dev/null || tail -45 nexus-claims.log"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '1,240p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md && tail -45 .git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log 2>/dev/null || tail -45 nexus-claims.log"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Running multiple agents on this plan without collisions\n\nThese rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\n\n- a concurrent agent overwrote newer evidence;\n- full test suites were contaminated by edits made mid-run;\n- `pkill -f` killed the agent's own shell;\n- HEAD moved during a pause.\n\nThey also follow from audit finding PER-03: the test suite writes into the real `~/.nexus`.\n\n## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n\n- The unit of concurrent work is **one PR slice** from a plan, for example `PLAN-01/PR-1a`. Every slice lists its tasks and its safe change boundary in its plan.\n- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n- An agent must not edit files outside its slice's boundary. The exceptions are the ledger rows and the shared files covered by §4. If the work needs a file outside the boundary, the agent stops and records a **boundary request** (§6). It does not edit the file.\n\n## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n\nClaims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n\n```sh\nCLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\nmkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\nSLICE=\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\"\nif mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\nelse\n  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\nfi\n```\n\n- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n\n## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\n\n| Resource | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\n| Builds | Each worktree builds into its own `core/target`, and `cli/dist` is per worktree. To share the Rust build cache, set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` per worktree, never to one shared directory. |\n| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\n| Processes | Kill only PIDs you started, taken from `$!` or `ps -eo pid,args \\| grep -v grep`. **Never `pkill -f` or `killall`.** Long background jobs are stopped through the agent's own task controls. |\n| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n| Credentials | Agents never read or copy `~/.config/nexus/credentials.json`, `config.env` values, or gateway tokens. The stripped proxy reads the token file itself. |\n\n## 4. Hot files: serialise, do not merge blindly\n\nThese files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n\n| File | Plans that touch it | Rule |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cli/src/agent.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 11 | Claim required. Keep each change local to the line ranges the plan names. Rebase immediately before merge and re-run that slice's tests on the rebased snapshot. |\n| `cli/src/index.ts` | 01, 03, 04, 06, 08, 10, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-06 PR-6b (unified launcher) lands first.** Other plans add commands and flags afterwards. |\n| `cli/src/tools.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 06, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-02 PR-2b (signal plumbing) lands before PLAN-03 PR-3c (`safeFetch`)**. |\n| `cli/src/sidecar.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n| `cli/src/doctor.ts` | 01, 03, 05, 06, 08 | Claim required. Each plan adds **new check functions** in separate blocks. Only PLAN-06 PR-6d changes existing checks. |\n| `cli/src/client.ts` | 03, 05, 08, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-03 PR-3a (env layering) lands before any PLAN-05 slice.** |\n| `cli/src/repl.ts` | 01, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n| `cli/src/config.ts`, `security.ts`, `sandbox.ts`, `mcp.ts`, `plugins.ts` | 01, 03 | Claim required. PLAN-01 PR-1e and PLAN-03 must not run at the same time on `sandbox.ts` or `security.ts`. |\n| `cli/src/core/capabilities.ts` | 01, 02 | **PLAN-01 PR-1a (effect classes) lands first.** PLAN-02 PR-2c adds schema fields afterwards. |\n| `cli/src/tester.ts` | 01, 11 | **PLAN-01 PR-1c lands before PLAN-11 PR-11b/11c.** |\n| `cli/src/core/state.ts` | 04, 08 | **PLAN-08 PR-8a (HOME isolation) lands before everything.** |\n| `core/src/runner.rs`, `core/src/main.rs` | 01, 02, 06 | Claim required. The protocol version number is owned by PLAN-02 PR-2a. PLAN-06 PR-6c only reads it. |\n| `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/{live_state,live_view}.rs` | 01, 02 | Claim required |\n| `package.json`, `cli/package.json`, `core/Cargo.toml`, lockfiles | 01, 06, 07, 08 | **Only one agent at a time.** Version fields are written only by `scripts/sync-version.mjs`. Dependency changes are separate commits that touch only the lockfile and manifest. |\n| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\n| `cli/dist/**` | all, while tracked | Do not commit `cli/dist` from slices. PLAN-07 PR-7d untracks it (DEC-10). Until that merges, only the merging agent rebuilds and commits dist, in a final separate commit, after rebasing. |\n| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\n\n### Ledger updates (`docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md`)\n\nA slice changes only the rows for its own requirement IDs: the status, test-reference and evidence cells, in place. It never reorders, adds or removes rows, and never edits another slice's rows. New requirements discovered during work go to §6, not into the ledger. Because rows are independent lines, git merges these edits cleanly. If a conflict appears anyway, resolve it row by row, keeping both changes.\n\n## 5. Commit and merge discipline\n\n1. Before **every** commit, compare `git rev-parse HEAD` with the commit you last made. Then run `git log <yours>..HEAD` on the branch. If anything foreign appears, stop and reconcile. Never commit generated artifacts (evidence, dist, lockfiles) over a branch that moved (lessons 2026-10-13).\n2. Commits are scoped to the slice. Do not reformat or clean up files outside the boundary.\n3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\n5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n6. Preserve unrelated user work: the untracked `nexus-continuity-validation/`, the stashes, and any dirty files you did not create. Never stash, reset, clean or check out over them.\n\n## 6. Coordination records\n\n| Record | Where | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\n\n## 7. Safe parallel lanes\n\nThe following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\n\n| Phase | Parallel lanes |\n|---|---|\n| M0 | (a) PLAN-08 PR-8a, which must merge first. Then in parallel: (b) PLAN-06 PR-6a, (c) PLAN-09 PR-9a. |\n| M1 | (a) PLAN-01 PR-1a → PR-1b → PR-1c (sequential, owns `capabilities.ts`, `agent.ts` dispatch). (b) PLAN-02 PR-2a (Rust only). (c) PLAN-03 PR-3a → PR-3b (config/egress). (d) PLAN-11 PR-11a (`parser.ts`) and PR-11b (`tester.ts`, after PR-1c). Lanes (b), (c) and (d) do not touch `capabilities.ts`. |\n| M2 (alongside M1) | (a) PLAN-07 PR-7a/7b/7c (workflows, scripts). (b) PLAN-06 PR-6b after PLAN-01 PR-1b (shares `index.ts` flags). |\n| M3 | (a) PLAN-04 (`agent.ts` turn, operation runner). (b) PLAN-05 (`client.ts`, provider modules). (c) PLAN-10 harness (`eval/`, no product files). (d) Held-out task authoring by the agent author, **outside the repository**: no access to Nexus source or the development set (DEC-05). |\n| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\n| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\n\n## 8. Independence constraints\n\n- The held-out task author must not see Nexus source, the development tasks or tuning history. It runs in a separate session with only the task schema and external repositories. Its output is sealed by a sha256 manifest committed before RC1.\n- The independent reviewer in ACCEPTANCE §8 must not be the agent or session that implemented the slices under review.\n- An implementing agent never edits `eval/heldout-manifest.json`, scorer thresholds or ACCEPTANCE §6.4 after the freeze.\n2026-10-28T09:34:00Z\tV1_CHECKPOINT_UNTRACKED_OWNER_PR_20261028 remediation commit=bb057ca69494084e2fcf37ba559b1077157b311a branch=v1/defect-checkpoint-untracked-integration finding=tracked cp.gitRef blob targets omitted from replacement preflight; fixed by unioning manifest paths with non-gitlink blob paths before read-tree/checkout-index; regression asserts ignored canary survives and HEAD/index unchanged; diff_check=PASS tests=NOT_RUN(SUITE held by kimi-main) review=PENDING_FRESH_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW\n2026-10-28T09:34:48Z\tV1_CHECKPOINT_UNTRACKED_OWNER_PR_20261028 second_followup commit=c3aaf60e2822de90df9586db4e2ac74d9c4523b0 finding=git-clean exact-directory preview could bypass descendant scan for tracked target; fixed with descendant inspection rejecting .git, ignored and special entries; ignored/FIFO/nested-repository tests now include post-checkpoint staged delta and assert staged content/index/HEAD plus obstruction preserved; diff_check=PASS tests=NOT_RUN(SUITE held by kimi-main) review=PENDING_FRESH_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW\n2026-10-28T09:36:55Z\tREVIEW-LOOP-TICK-922 origin/main=7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4 (31/31 merged PRs 100% post-merge verified); PR #299 head=51484f05b20309c36ef20473f26223341fdb15bd ACTION_REQUIRED (comment 6465406445: REPL EOF fix in cli/src/repl.ts verified, but new test at cli/test/operator_config_startup.test.ts:136 passes '{}' instead of '{\"version\": 1}' and fails with exit code 2); PR #300 head=f8427883ca7f7e66ce5ad2c829b7a6dcd4a5934d ACCEPT (comment 6463783795, CodeQL 40653234886 SUCCESS, CI 40653235002 SUCCESS — READY FOR MERGE); PR #301 head=fb193bef6e1bba9ab01f77d53d2ad3b121a79b44 ACTION_REQUIRED (comment 6464854056: 3 findings open, CodeQL 40659765355 SUCCESS, CI 40659765270 SUCCESS); PR #302 head=0f04bb58a3f4b7ee81ded48b8219983f6c92fba2 (follow-up remediation in progress per comment 6465406893, CodeQL 40659910420 SUCCESS, CI 40659910410 SUCCESS)\n2026-10-28T09:37:58Z PR299_FIXTURE_REMEDIATION owner=codex-root head=51484f05b20309c36ef20473f26223341fdb15bd finding=EOF test supplied invalid versionless operator config; correction=use {version:1}; diff_check=PASS tests=NOT_RUN(SUITE held by kimi-main) commit_pending\n2026-10-28T09:39:30Z PR302_FOLLOWUP_REVIEW disposition=ACCEPT reviewer=/root/review_pr302 head=c3aaf60e2822de90df9586db4e2ac74d9c4523b0 diff=0f04bb58a3f4b7ee81ded48b8219983f6c92fba2...c3aaf60e2822de90df9586db4e2ac74d9c4523b0 tests=NOT_RUN(SUITE held by kimi-main) hosted_CI=PENDING\n2026-10-28T09:39:30Z PR299_FIXTURE_REMEDIATION review=ACCEPT reviewer=/root/review_pr302 head=8f7fe9888c3e71affdfc4f002faf0f1f98e553ae exact_diff=8f7fe9888c3e71affdfc4f002faf0f1f98e553ae^..8f7fe9888c3e71affdfc4f002faf0f1f98e553ae hosted_CI=PENDING tests=NOT_RUN(SUITE held by kimi-main)\n2026-10-28T09:41:04Z REVIEW-LOOP-TICK-923 origin/main=7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4 REDACTED PR300=checks_pass_entire_pending PR301=terminal_injection_finding_open SUITE=kimi-main_active_since_09:12_local_full_tests_deferred Entire=enabled_637_checkpoints_queued_search_unavailable_keyring_secret_service; acceptance=IN_PROGRESS\n2026-10-28T09:41:45Z REVIEW pr=302 head=c3aaf60e2822de90df9586db4e2ac74d9c4523b0 base=7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4 diff_sha256=a30ea67346d31138df67612ced52d29c0e3777fc9f1048f7bc6801779a43d345 verdict=ACTION_REQUIRED comment=6465653678 notes=\"c3aaf60e fixed untracked file replaced by dir with nested .git/ignored (43/43 tests pass), but adding gitRefBlobPaths(cp.gitRef) to replacementTargets introduced 2 regressions when a tracked file a in cp.gitRef is replaced by a directory a/child.txt: (1) untracked a/child.txt is falsely rejected by assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable because git clean -nd -- a prints Would remove a/child.txt instead of Would remove a/ when a is in the index; (2) committed a/child.txt throws ENOTDIR in removeTrackedDeletions on lstatSync('/.../a/child.txt') after checkout-index -f -a recreates a as a regular file\"\n2026-10-28T09:43:02Z REVIEW pr=299 head=8f7fe9888c3e71affdfc4f002faf0f1f98e553ae base=7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4 diff_sha256=84e405de6cc3e912e179359654db4cb94f6ee616692cfb9c827f9477c3af70cc verdict=ACCEPT comment=6465676347 notes=\"8f7fe988 updated REPL stdin EOF regression test in cli/test/operator_config_startup.test.ts:136 to pass valid config {\\\"version\\\": 1}; verified 8/8 pass in operator_config_startup.test.ts and tsc --noEmit 0 errors in isolated worktree; CodeQL 40665819752 SUCCESS; CI 40665819785 IN_PROGRESS\"\n2026-10-28T09:47:53Z PR302_REVIEW_RETRACTION head=c3aaf60e2822de90df9586db4e2ac74d9c4523b0 previous_accept_withdrawn new_disposition=CHANGES_REQUIRED reviewer_comment=6465653678 findings=clean_preview_false_reject_for_untracked_child;removeTrackedDeletions_ENOTDIR_after_mutation remediation=/root/pr302fix tests=NOT_RUN(SUITE_claim_present) merge=BLOCKED\n2026-10-28T09:48:20Z POSTMERGE_TRACKING pr=301 merge_sha=b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff codeql_run=40666613951(in_progress) ci_run=40666613776(in_progress) open_prs=\"299(8f7fe988:ACCEPT,CI:40665819785),300(f8427883:READY_FOR_MERGE),302(c3aaf60e:ACTION_REQUIRED,comment:6465653678)\" merge_trees=\"299:CLEAN,300:CLEAN,302:CLEAN\"\n2026-10-28T09:49:24Z CLAIM agent=codex-root slice=V1_DEFECT_OPERATION_VIEW_REVIEW_20261028 branch=v1/defect-operation-view-review-20261028 base=b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff worktree=/home/mike/nexus-wt/opview-review-remediation files=cli/src/operation_view.ts,cli/src/operation_cli.ts,cli/test/operation_view.test.ts scope=fix four review findings carried into main by merged PR301 comment=6465715143 suite_claim=not_present_at_claim_time\n2026-10-28T09:49:35Z\tV1_CHECKPOINT_UNTRACKED_OWNER_PR_20261028 third_followup commit=def07ecb findings=clean-preview-child-path falsely rejected ordinary untracked child; committed-child cleanup ENOTDIR; changes=permit safe nonignored untracked descendants only when no tracked descendants, retain tracked-only validation, treat ENOENT/ENOTDIR as absent during deletions; tests_added=untracked-child-success,staged-and-committed-child-success,ignored-and-nested-.git-preflight-rejection-with-index-identity; diff_check=PASS tests=NOT_RUN(SUITE kimi-main active as of 09:41:04Z) review=PENDING_FRESH_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW\n2026-10-28T09:50:00Z\tV1_CHECKPOINT_UNTRACKED_OWNER_PR_20261028 fourth_followup commit=d880a388 finding=committed-child regression previously checkpointed target a as untracked; added regression with a committed before checkpoint then committed a/child; acceptance=restore succeeds, checkpoint blob restored, child absent, HEAD unchanged, index tracks a; diff_check=PASS tests=NOT_RUN(SUITE kimi-main active per 09:41:04Z record) review=PENDING_FRESH_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW\n2026-10-28T09:55:37Z\tCLAIM_RELEASE agent=codex-root-pr302-fix REDACTED,FILE_cli_src_checkpoint.ts,FILE_cli_test_checkpoint_restore.test.ts head=d880a3882512c8f3823200ce4be27dadd03d98d0 independent_review=ACCEPT exact_head=true disposition_reported_by=root suite_validation=handed_to_root_immutable_snapshot push=not_done merge=not_done\n2026-10-28T10:06:40Z REVIEW pr=302 head=d880a3882512c8f3823200ce4be27dadd03d98d0 base=7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4 diff_sha256=a2bb550ddf8f1262754bdda7dd4c325333d83d5a6b181887618c7169eef439b3 verdict=ACTION_REQUIRED comment=6466152315 notes=\"d880a388 fixed removeTrackedDeletions ENOTDIR (catches ENOENT/ENOTDIR), but cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:366 fails (47/48 pass, 1 fail) because git clean -nd -- a outputs empty string when a is still a tracked blob in the index; replacing the preview/tracked split in assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable with !this.directoryContainsOnlyGitCleanRemovableEntries(relativePath) passes all 48/48 tests\"\n2026-10-28T10:13:05Z PREFLIGHT_NOTE branch=v1/defect-operation-view-review-20261028 head=05e3a81714d27aded309bc413c12b311efcf6f22 notes=\"Isolated worktree run of test/operation_view.test.ts on 05e3a817 has 21/23 pass and 2 assertion mismatches in the new tests: (1) line 481 asserts /--events must be/ on watch stderr, which prints '--interval must be a positive number of seconds and --events a non-negative number'; (2) line 501 asserts /hostile forged line end/, whereas safeTerminal replaces ESC/BEL with visible symbols producing 'hostile␛]52;c;payload␇␛[2J forged line end'\"\n2026-10-28T10:22:15Z CI_VERIFIED pr=299 head=8f7fe9888c3e71affdfc4f002faf0f1f98e553ae codeql_run=40665819752(SUCCESS) ci_run=40665819785(SUCCESS:test-matrix-22,test-matrix-24,linux-x86_64) status=READY_FOR_MERGE\n2026-10-28T10:27:30Z POSTMERGE_VERIFIED pr=301 merge_sha=b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff codeql_run=40666613951(SUCCESS) ci_run=40666613776(SUCCESS) consecutive_merges_verified=32/32\n2026-10-28T11:37:30Z REVIEW branch=v1/defect-operation-view-review-20261028 head=dc2e48464a77721ed6c0a1567fd4d1f2dc06295b base=b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff diff_sha256=da4e94cb89ca60f42b5c3c06829056c29a044ab6fad79ae181463fa4713e58ba verdict=ACCEPT notes=\"All 4 PR #301 follow-up items resolved: (1) createCliFixture isolates HOME/XDG_CONFIG_HOME/XDG_DATA_HOME/NEXUS_STATE_DIR and cleans up temporary root via t.after; (2) criticalPath() suppresses memoization when cycleTruncated is true; (3) status --dag and watch reject blank/whitespace --events; (4) watch multiple-operation list sanitizes id/status/objective with safeTerminal and collapses control whitespace. Verified tsc --noEmit (0 errors) and 23/23 pass in test/operation_view.test.ts in isolated worktree.\"\n2026-10-28T11:44:15Z REVIEW pr=303 head=dc2e48464a77721ed6c0a1567fd4d1f2dc06295b base=b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff diff_sha256=da4e94cb89ca60f42b5c3c06829056c29a044ab6fad79ae181463fa4713e58ba verdict=ACCEPT comment=6468065345 notes=\"Opened as PR #303; posted independent review comment 6468065345 (23/23 pass in operation_view.test.ts, tsc --noEmit 0 errors, CodeQL SUCCESS, CI IN_PROGRESS)\"\n2026-10-28T11:44:15Z REVIEW pr=299 head=38837c88e73cb54e4032606941c8aec8262d291c base=b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff diff_sha256=6c53ff744a9956eadcac02c7b17e9bf1ef05022358586a407557aeb1f2ba7fe7 verdict=ACCEPT comment=6468102437 notes=\"Merged origin/main (c0a96157) and updated docs/USER_MANUAL.md:388-391 (38837c88); code unchanged from verified 8f7fe988; CodeQL SUCCESS, CI IN_PROGRESS\"\n2026-10-28T11:44:15Z REVIEW pr=302 head=90d67559620f7191d303c4a3a6ec476bac6e241c base=7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4 diff_sha256=1099e6ff6b68ab9907ac66c908bf45c8ab1af338d3b6a14227d45d60cf35dc29 verdict=ACCEPT comment=6468102940 notes=\"90d67559 removed preview.trim() !== '' gate before directoryContainsOnlyGitCleanRemovableEntries && gitTrackedDescendantPaths.length === 0 in assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable; verified 48/48 pass in checkpoint_restore.test.ts + checkpoint_hook_failure_paths.test.ts and tsc --noEmit 0 errors in isolated worktree; CodeQL SUCCESS, CI IN_PROGRESS\"\n2026-10-28T11:47:15Z REVIEW pr=300 head=d5e255f8ec9fa44ed85bc7f3875ac7261dd7383c base=b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff diff_sha256=450a75b0a0a041ab9dfad58b6578a9a43d87d666ac1c35d102fb5c41e54d00fa verdict=ACCEPT notes=\"Merged origin/main (b293b441) and refreshed docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md with 2026-10-28 11:45 UTC convergence checkpoint; git diff --check PASS; CodeQL SUCCESS; CI IN_PROGRESS\"\n2026-10-28T11:52:15Z REVIEW pr=300 head=6a2f1e4655a0dd132591809dcb01374705623502 base=b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff diff_sha256=9b296944eee04a798745d43a96e963fd078e5affcfc1cef844d3657942a8cb33 verdict=ACCEPT comment=6468274566 notes=\"Updated docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md (11:49 UTC checkpoint) with PR #273 runtime identity dogfooding fix status; git diff -