{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:23:55.290Z","ordinal":457345,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a182ae-7b1a-7241-8f34-4dc30272b77f","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT — no findings.**\n\nReviewed PR #299 head `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` against base `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`. Cumulative diff SHA-256: `55afcdc8ed8044bb0aa0a54932c5ba6513763b564bc8fb76014b3334db33ae38`.\n\nThe malformed-config paths defer errors only so `doctor`/`check` can report repair guidance; normal CLI and sidecar startup remain fail-closed. The EOF regression uses valid version-1 operator config and exercises the REPL path used by non-TTY `nexus </dev/null`. PR304’s operation-policy changes on the base remain covered by the same configuration validation.\n\nNo tests were run. The worktree lacks `.entire/agent-guide.md`, and Entire returned an unrelated ended session, so checkpoint intent was unavailable."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1828e-5af5-7fb1-bc6f-34b2f291d340","create_time":1793193835.2903895,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":21812}}
