ualification. PR #304 adds opt-in v1.1 Git-aware operations to current main; its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. The independent review recorded an unresolved correctness defect: an explicit restart recreates a clean worktree while resuming the old agent conversation. That behavior must be fixed and requalified before an RC built from this main can be accepted.\n \n-**Source PRs:** PR [#303](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/303) is integrated at `4cac22d`; its exact-head required CI and independent review passed. PR [#304](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/304) is integrated at `b2ae2fe`; its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, CodeQL and JS/TS checks passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. Its independent review nevertheless found the restart/conversation defect above. PR [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) addresses that defect at `f7e573ec8de98fb3ec24a96e148a84b4ccab151f`, with independent review ACCEPT at diff SHA-256 `cf1abd6ce5e7083aebe526efaaee85380dee295fced7814a7ddedcd609a11615`. Build and focused test TypeScript check passed; the runtime test was not run locally because `SUITE` is actively claimed by `kimi-main`. Exact-head Node 22/24 and Entire checks are in progress; JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. PR [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) still points remotely at `0f54f5395d9ceb87eb1e6d9fafc1f4d728675e9a` on base `4cac22d`. Its local rebased candidate on `b2ae2fe` is `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f`; diff-check passes, and fresh independent review plus exact-head CI are pending. Issue [#298](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/298) remains open until its fix is integrated and current-main checks pass. PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) still points remotely at stale head `5d2932f0a90516343c52bb36531a93f29aa921cd` on base `b293b44`; its exact-head source checks passed, but Entire Gates **failed** at 12:56:04 UTC and the gate needs disposition before merge. Its local readiness candidate is being refreshed against `b2ae2fe`. PR [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) has since been updated to head `659d6a63a8708ebe98240ec1937b0f2acdcdfac4` on base `b2ae2fe`. Its JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks passed; Node 22/24 and Entire Gates are still running and Linux CI has not yet appeared. The previous head `c45e34ff` had a failed Entire check and a diagnostic of three high-severity findings; disposition on the updated head remains pending.\n+**Source PRs:** PR [#303](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/303) is integrated at `4cac22d`; its exact-head required CI and independent review passed. PR [#304](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/304) is integrated at `b2ae2fe`; its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, CodeQL and JS/TS checks passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. Its independent review nevertheless found the restart/conversation defect above. PR [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) addresses that defect at `f7e573ec8de98fb3ec24a96e148a84b4ccab151f`, with independent review ACCEPT at diff SHA-256 `cf1abd6ce5e7083aebe526efaaee85380dee295fced7814a7ddedcd609a11615`. Build and focused test TypeScript check passed; the runtime test was not run locally because `SUITE` is claimed by `kimi-main`. Exact-head Node 22/24 and Entire checks remain in progress; JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. PR [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) is updated to `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` on base `b2ae2fe`; independent review ACCEPTed the exact head at diff SHA-256 `55afcdc8ed8044bb0aa0a54932c5ba6513763b564bc8fb76014b3334db33ae38`. Its exact-head Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript and Entire checks are running. Issue [#298](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/298) remains open until its fix is integrated and current-main checks pass. PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) is at `48c14a0937549fc9e243a2da59338a4368338e1d` on base `b2ae2fe`, with independent factual review ACCEPT at diff SHA-256 `df5b1a3492b6bf20beafc175d0fbae4aa4927d7378b5cc6390bd6874e97804d3`. Its Node 22/24 checks and Entire Gates remain in progress; JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. The prior head `5d2932f0a90516343c52bb36531a93f29aa921cd` on base `b293b44` had a failed Entire check at 12:56:04 UTC; that result is historical and not the status of this updated head. PR [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) is at `659d6a63a8708ebe98240ec1937b0f2acdcdfac4` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, while Node 24 and Entire Gates remain in progress. The previous head `c45e34ff` had a failed Entire check and a diagnostic of three high-severity findings; disposition on the updated head remains pending.\n \n **Requested codebase-review findings:** The prior checkpoint's implementation and evidence summary remains applicable; the current main includes the capability-category split, scheduler extraction, operation-runner decomposition, bounded diagnostics, `DecisionRejected` guidance, lifecycle tests, and 100 fixed-seed scheduler invariants. The operator config remains intentionally limited to `operationPolicy`; general runtime-default customization is not claimed.\n \n48c14a0937549fc9e243a2da59338a4368338e1d\n48c14a09 docs: distinguish PR305 check results\n270051de docs: correct current release gate states\ndbeb8c7f docs: refresh release checkpoint after PR304\naf8a6922 docs: align readiness checkpoint timestamp\ne5731c5a docs: record failed PR release gates\n275b56c1 docs: refresh v1 release checkpoint\na572f6d4 docs(release): disclose open config defect\n7c172c0f docs(release): record runtime identity fix status\nb0055ffa docs(release): refresh convergence checkpoint\n57bd745c docs(release): bind requirements gate to current main\n4383963e docs(release): refres