{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:30:58.547Z","ordinal":457604,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1828e-5af5-7fb1-bc6f-34b2f291d340","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae1f90e2a38819f948e3ca61affcd02","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"## Entire and release checkpoint\n\n`using-entire` was applied. Entire is enabled and connected, but Brain’s index is unsafe for the dirty shared worktree, so I used live GitHub and Git evidence for current status. The shared checkout at `3130313` remains untouched; authoritative `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe`.\n\n**Work completed:** PR #299’s rebased candidate (`004234de`, based on `b2ae2fe`) received independent **ACCEPT** with zero findings and was pushed using a lease. PR #300’s readiness update (`484cfbf`) was also independently **ACCEPT**ed with zero findings and pushed. Both PRs now have exact-head checks running. I recorded the review and check details in the claims log and PR comments.\n\n**Current checks:** Main CI run `40693030763` passed Node 22 and 24; Linux packaging is still running. Main CodeQL passed. PR #302 has Node 22, JS/TS, and CodeQL passing; Node 24 and Entire Gates remain in progress. PR #305 has JS/TS and CodeQL passing; Node 22/24 and Entire Gates remain in progress. No local tests were run because the `SUITE` claim remains active.\n\nThe `ubuntu-desktop` host is reachable, with xterm, kitty, tmux, GNOME Terminal, and VS Code installed. The manual matrix remains **0/15**: it must be run against a successor RC, since RC10 predates the current source. Held-out custody is still unresolved; the latest metadata-only request on issue #1 has no reply.\n\nThe public release list confirms RC10 is the newest published release. **No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 is published.**\n\n**Disposition: `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE` — acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`.** Next, I’ll continue reconciling exact-head CI, obtain the independent PR #302 review, and proceed to RC and installed-artifact qualification only after source gates pass. The claude-mem observer remains unavailable because Claude’s five-hour allowance is exhausted; I did not restart it.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":778,"lineEnd":789,"note":"release evidence must be refreshed and exact RC qualification remains separate"}],"rolloutIds":["01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0"]}},"started_at_ms":1793194254187,"completed_at_ms":1793194258547}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:31:06.483Z","ordinal":457605,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae1f90e2a38819f948e3ca61affcd02","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"## Entire and release checkpoint\n\n`using-entire` was applied. Entire is enabled and connected, but Brain’s index is unsafe for the dirty shared worktree, so I used live GitHub and Git evidence for current status. The shared checkout at `3130313` remains untouched; authoritative `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe`.\n\n**Work completed:** PR #299’s rebased candidate (`004234de`, based on `b2ae2fe`) received independent **ACCEPT** with zero findings and was pushed using a lease. PR #300’s readiness update (`484cfbf`) was also independently **ACCEPT**ed with zero findings and pushed. Both PRs now have exact-head checks running. I recorded the review and check details in the claims log and PR comments.\n\n**Current checks:** Main CI run `40693030763` passed Node 22 and 24; Linux packaging is still running. Main CodeQL passed. PR #302 has Node 22, JS/TS, and CodeQL passing; Node 24 and Entire Gates remain in progress. PR #305 has JS/TS and CodeQL passing; Node 22/24 and Entire Gates remain in progress. No local tests were run because the `SUITE` claim remains active.\n\nThe `ubuntu-desktop` host is reachable, with xterm, kitty, tmux, GNOME Terminal, and VS Code installed. The manual matrix remains **0/15**: it must be run against a successor RC, since RC10 predates the current source. Held-out custody is still unresolved; the latest metadata-only request on issue #1 has no reply.\n\nThe public release list confirms RC10 is the newest published release. **No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 is published.**\n\n**Disposition: `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE` — acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`.** Next, I’ll continue reconciling exact-head CI, obtain the independent PR #302 review, and proceed to RC and installed-artifact qualification only after source gates pass. The claude-mem observer remains unavailable because Claude’s five-hour allowance is exhausted; I did not restart it.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:778-789|note=[release evidence must be refreshed and exact RC qualification remains separate]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1828e-5af5-7fb1-bc6f-34b2f291d340","create_time":1793194254.1665325,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae1f90e2a38819f948e3ca61affcd02","turn_id":"01a1828e-5af5-7fb1-bc6f-34b2f291d340","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a182b5-0f73-73a0-b450-e2d85b60b0da","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":21821}}
