{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:32:13.550Z","ordinal":457656,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a182b6-156e-74d3-bac2-25d1662b460d","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\nEntire Review:\n\n**Scope:** PR #302 exact head `659d6a63a8708ebe98240ec1937b0f2acdcdfac4` against base `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`. Cumulative diff SHA-256: `1099e6ff6b68ab9907ac66c908bf45c8ab1af338d3b6a14227d45d60cf35dc29`.\n\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED**\n\n- **High — [checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-untracked-integration/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:832): Restore can write into a nested repository when it is an ancestor of a captured untracked path.** The preflight checks symlink and directory ancestors for captured paths, but does not detect nested Git repositories in those ancestors. For a checkpoint containing `a/file`, if `a` is later replaced by a nested repository, the outer `git clean -fd` preserves that repository; the subsequent copy can overwrite its `file` ([copy logic](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-untracked-integration/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:214), restore ordering at lines 847–849). Reject nested-repository ancestors before any restore mutation, and add a regression that checks the canary, index, and HEAD remain unchanged.\n\nThe PR body’s four unresolved high Entire findings are confirmed. GitHub exposes only the summary; the check has no annotations, and its linked details require authentication unavailable here. Source inspection found the issue above, but I cannot map it to any particular opaque Entire finding. The Entire findings and approval remain unresolved external blockers. No tests were run."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a182b5-7df6-71b2-a955-13339511caaf","create_time":1793194333.55066,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":21825}}
