{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:37:16.119Z","ordinal":457869,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a182ba-b357-73a2-b990-9bb1eef0276e","call_id":"call_929280e435bb484889333106467d00c7","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"[\"XERJ tools proxy to a running XERJ engine (ES-compatible). Use xerj_search for retrieval — pass `query` as a plain string for definition-first code search (ranks the defining file first, returns the matching passage instead of whole files, and adds `match_line` for the source line of the match inside that passage), or as an ES query-DSL object for structured queries, xerj_semantic_search for meaning-based recall over a semantic_text field (embedding is server-side, no key), xerj_vector_search for kNN over a dense_vector field, xerj_hybrid_search to fuse lexical + vector results (rrf|linear), and xerj_memory_store / xerj_memory_recall for durable agent memory recalled by meaning. Call xerj_map FIRST on an autoindexed node: it returns each index's field map (names, types, cardinality, covera\"]"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a182b5-7df6-71b2-a955-13339511caaf","create_time":1793194636.1191702}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
