{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:41:47.555Z","ordinal":458090,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a182b5-7df6-71b2-a955-13339511caaf","item":{"type":"McpToolCall","id":"exec-7085968e-e8c4-4459-9dda-4d1fbcec41d0","server":"xerj","tool":"xerj_field_report","arguments":{"agent":"Codex (GPT-6)","used_for":"Locate the explicit-restart warning assertion in Nexus's durable continuity tests before repairing PR #305 CI failures.","verdict":"XERJ search found the relevant exact passage and source line in cli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts (match line 1366); useful for locating the assertion. Entire checkpoint search was separately unavailable due desktop keyring access.","indexed":"nexus-test","notes":"Search result exposed the assertion requiring either the earlier-history-unusable or explicitly-restarted-after-recovery phrase and the remain-unverified warning. No private test payload or secrets were searched."},"status":"completed","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"GitHub is unavailable (error: GitHub is unavailable: the pull request could not be opened (see above)); sent to the endpoint instead.\nsent field report to https://xerj.org/api/field-report (HTTP 200)\n{\"ok\":true,\"stored\":true,\"note\":\"Thanks. The canonical path is a GitHub PR: https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj/tree/main/user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports\"}"}],"isError":false},"duration":{"secs":19,"nanos":252876964}},"started_at_ms":1793194888302,"completed_at_ms":1793194907555}}
