{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:43:31.144Z","ordinal":458178,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a182b5-7df6-71b2-a955-13339511caaf","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae1fc01f7a8819f8e6ce24bb397653f","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The reviewer confirmed a second concrete PR #302 bug: the current guard checks nested Git ancestors for untracked restore paths, but not tracked file destinations. I’m extending the preflight to cover the full restore target set and adding a regression that asserts both repositories’ state is preserved on rejection. Kimi owns the test-suite lane right now, so I will not overlap its test run; exact-head CI can validate this patch once pushed."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793195010016,"completed_at_ms":1793195011144}}
