{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:45:54.012Z","ordinal":458297,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a182c2-9a5c-7f30-ac1e-ffe42e2d12ef","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — cumulative diff SHA-256: `2f1c7fb605077d0b7a06b384c492604fe700e97ad80c565ec9ed2c7c79613367` (base `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`, head `85b68705083f78971e36eaf1ca6088146636c2f0`).\n\nThe shared preflight now scans tracked blob paths and captured untracked paths before `read-tree` ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-untracked-integration/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:856)). The tracked-path regression checks nested and outer HEADs and indexes, plus nested and staged canaries ([checkpoint_restore.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-untracked-integration/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:1041)).\n\nOne ancestor variant remains: the preflight stops when it encounters a symlinked parent at [checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-untracked-integration/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:206). For a tracked destination such as `a/captured.txt`, with `a` symlinked to an in-workspace nested repo, it does not reject or inspect the nested repo; the target check can see a regular-file leaf and allow restore to reach `read-tree`. Reject symlinked parent components for tracked targets and add a test asserting indexes and canaries remain unchanged.\n\nNo tests were run during this review."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a182b5-7df6-71b2-a955-13339511caaf","create_time":1793195154.012216,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":21841}}
