{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:48:34.245Z","ordinal":458439,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a182c5-0c45-7f50-b6eb-a19589618e22","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — cumulative diff SHA-256: `d713fa7c4350dbbfe2dc0ae88272d6a219f1a9e3f206fe5c0236b5ce825b8f2b` (base `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`, head `8ebb8fadd4f09ccbc0c5ab8ea7d53434e1924d71`).\n\nThe shared preflight now rejects symlinked parent components and nested Git repository ancestors. Restore applies it to the union of tracked blob and captured untracked paths before `read-tree` ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-untracked-integration/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:193), [checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-untracked-integration/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:860)). The new regression exercises a tracked destination through a symlink to a nested repository and checks the nested canary, both repositories’ HEADs and indexes, and the staged outer canary ([checkpoint_restore.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-untracked-integration/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:1086)).\n\nNo tests were run during this review."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a182b5-7df6-71b2-a955-13339511caaf","create_time":1793195314.2452457,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":21844}}
