{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:57:33.580Z","ordinal":458888,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a182cd-470c-7b82-b7c0-79abb0188a98","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — cumulative diff SHA-256: `580313edcbbd646fbd419bb37224114f5eb6e48e50f41e774dac3047ff08e25a` (base `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`, head `bb63624755bba487aa51249f7ce3f588c647fbd6`).\n\nThe preflight checks `.git` metadata and the bare-repository layout before restore mutation ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-untracked-integration/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:211)). The bare-repository regression sets up the captured destination, then removes it before initializing the bare repo. Its assertions preserve repository metadata, canary, and outer state, but **do not assert that `nested-bare/captured.txt` remains absent** ([checkpoint_restore.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-untracked-integration/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:1041)). A regression that copied the captured file into the bare repo could pass the test. Add an explicit absence assertion. No tests were run during this review."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a182b5-7df6-71b2-a955-13339511caaf","create_time":1793195853.5804584,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":21861}}
