{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T14:14:04.746Z","ordinal":459476,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a182d5-76db-7c32-855f-8a7a037c7e55","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-45bb921b-8f69-4d72-a3e7-e8a8d800551b","process_id":"69605","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","xerj search \"ConvergenceScheduler\" --prefix nexus-cli --top 5; xerj search \"DEFAULT_OPERATION_POLICY operation policy\" --prefix nexus-cli --top 5; xerj search \"operation lifecycle create schedule execute complete\" --prefix nexus-test --top 5"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"xerj search \"ConvergenceScheduler\" --prefix nexus-cli --top 5; xerj search \"DEFAULT_OPERATION_POLICY operation policy\" --prefix nexus-cli --top 5; xerj search \"operation lifecycle create schedule execute complete\" --prefix nexus-test --top 5"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"xerj search: unexpected argument '--top'\n\nxerj search — retrieve code from a running XERJ node (reference coding, no scripts)\nDefault ranking is lexical: it matches the words you typed, and it is not a neural reading of the code.\n\nUSAGE:\n    xerj search [OPTIONS] \"<what you need, in plain words>\"\n\nOPTIONS:\n    --url <U>       node endpoint (default $XERJ_URL or http://localhost:9200)\n    --prefix <P>    index prefix to search (default \"ax\" — what `xerj autoindex` writes)\n    --api-key <K>   Authorization (or $XERJ_API_KEY; --insecure nodes need none)\n    -k <N>          number of passages to return (default 5). A non-number is a\n                    usage error, not a silent default\n    --full <CHARS>  max characters of each passage to print (default 600)\n    --json          print the raw response instead of formatted passages\n\nEXAMPLE:\n    xerj --insecure -d ./.xerj-data &                 # a node, running\n    xerj autoindex ref/sled                           # index