{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T14:19:37.230Z","ordinal":459666,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a182d5-76db-7c32-855f-8a7a037c7e55","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae204767ee0819faa771fe46e942e37","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Campaign remains active; acceptance is IN_PROGRESS.** `origin/main` is still `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`; the latest published release is RC10.\n\nPR #299 and #300 have all CI checks passing, including Linux packaging, but their Entire gates failed because no reviewer approved trails 14 and 15. PR #302’s Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks now pass; Linux is running, and Entire reports **five unresolved high-severity findings** plus no reviewer approval. PR #305’s Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks pass; Linux and Entire remain active.\n\nThe independent reviewer accepts the exact heads of all four PRs, but cannot access Entire to approve trails or inspect #302’s findings. I’ve asked whether you can arrange an authenticated independent reviewer; that request is pending. **No PRs were merged**, and #302’s findings remain undispositioned.\n\nI also reconciled the codebase improvements you listed: the current `origin/main` already has per-category capability files, extracted scheduler and runner modules, operation policy configuration, `DecisionRejected` documentation, generated scheduler property tests, and convergence lifecycle integration tests. Those changes are **not in RC10**, so the next RC must include them. The Nexus runtime-identity fix is also in `origin/main`, but not RC10.\n\nThe shared dirty checkout remains untouched. Claims and durable work state now record the refreshed reviews and CI. Held-out custody remains unresolved, and the human terminal matrix is still outstanding. No source changes or local tests were made in this iteration."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793197174546,"completed_at_ms":1793197177230}}
