{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T14:22:41.098Z","ordinal":459744,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a182e1-9d40-7cc2-988e-f5c6abfc0cfa","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2052eaab4819f80dbfd6a1511674e","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Campaign remains active; acceptance is IN_PROGRESS.** `origin/main` is still `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`.\n\n- **PRs #299 and #300:** all CI checks pass. Their Entire gates failed because no reviewer approved trails 14 and 15.\n- **PR #302:** Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL pass; Linux is running. Entire reports five unresolved high-severity findings and no reviewer approval. The finding details are not available without an authenticated Entire session.\n- **PR #305:** Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL pass; Linux and Entire are running.\n- **Independent review:** exact-head `ACCEPT` is recorded for all four PRs. No PR was merged while required gates remain unresolved.\n- **Qualification:** held-out custody is still unanswered. The terminal worksheet is blank and requires the installed candidate identity before the 15 human-run cells can begin.\n- **Release:** RC10 remains the latest public prerelease; there is no stable v1.0.0 release.\n\nThe codebase improvements you listed are already present on current `origin/main`, including the module splits, scheduler property tests, lifecycle integration tests, and operation policy configuration. They are absent from RC10, so the next candidate must include them.\n\nThe independent-reviewer access request is still pending. I left the dirty shared checkout untouched and made no source changes."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793197358689,"completed_at_ms":1793197361098}}
