{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T14:34:14.541Z","ordinal":460137,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a182ec-dd91-76f3-bef9-ba00d38b5f54","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a182ec-dd91-76f3-bef9-ba00d38b5f54","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae207e32c48819f9f69a551443da3e9","usage":{"input_tokens":79474,"cached_input_tokens":78336,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":298,"reasoning_output_tokens":231,"total_tokens":79772},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2674015,"cached_input_tokens":2585216,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":8735,"reasoning_output_tokens":4050,"total_tokens":2682750},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8527552238,"cached_input_tokens":8436317312,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24339504,"reasoning_output_tokens":14080915,"total_tokens":8551891742}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T14:34:15.994Z","ordinal":460138,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a182ec-dd91-76f3-bef9-ba00d38b5f54","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2a4e62ba-9783-4ea0-bc15-2989ce14a0f2","process_id":"87691","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","entire recap --help; entire checkpoint list --help; entire session --help"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire recap --help; entire checkpoint list --help; entire session --help"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"Summarize recent checkpoint activity\n\nUsage:\n  entire recap [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --90                   Rolling 90 days\n      --agent string         Agent id to show, or all (default \"all\")\n      --color string         Color output: auto, always, or never (default \"auto\")\n      --day                  Today only (default)\n  -h, --help                 help for recap\n      --insecure-http-auth   Allow plain-HTTP auth (local dev only)\n      --month                This calendar month\n      --static               Print static output instead of opening the interactive recap\n      --view string          Which columns to show: you, team, or both (default \"both\")\n      --week                 Last 7 days\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\nList checkpoints on the current branch.\n\nBy default shows condensed checkpoints from the checkpoints branch for the\ncurrent branch. Use --pending for work that is not a checkpoint yet:\n\n  - A preview of the next checkpoint for each session in this worktree with\n    pending work. Agent turns are recorded in session state, not in git, so\n    this work has no checkpoint ID until you commit it. The preview shows the\n    turns since the last checkpoint, the files touched, subagent task records,\n    and the prompts since the last checkpoint.\n  - Subagent task records of other sessions on HEAD (not yet condensed).\n  - Logs-only resume points recovered from commits whose logs are already\n    condensed.\n\nUse --outgoing to see what your next 'git push' sends: the checkpoints\nqueued for the checkpoint sync remote, read from local state with no network\ncall. Each one shows its ID, age, agent, first prompt (or summary) and the\nfiles it touched. It needs the git-refs checkpoint backend, which pushes one\nref per checkpoint; the git-branch backend pushes entire/checkpoints/v1 as one\nbranch, so --outgoing reports an error there.\n\nOutput modes:\n  --json              Machine-readable JSON instead of the human view.\n  --pending           Select the pending dataset described above.\n  --pending --json    The pending dataset as a JSON array.\n  --outgoing          Select the outgoing dataset described above.\n  --outgoing --json   The outgoing dataset as one JSON object.\n\nEach --pending --json element has id, message, metadata_dir, date (RFC3339),\nis_task_checkpoint, is_logs_only, and when set tool_use_id, condensation_id,\nsession_id and session_prompt. A next-checkpoint preview element has an empty\nid, \"is_next_checkpoint\": true, and a \"next_checkpoint\" object:\n\n  {\"agent\": \"...\", \"turns\": 2,\n   \"files_touched\": [\"...\"],\n   \"task_records\": [{\"tool_use_id\": \"...\", \"subagent_type\": \"...\",\n                     \"description\": \"...\", \"status\": \"running|completed\"}],\n   \"prompts\": [\"...\"]}\n\nThe arrays are always present, possibly empty.\n\nThe --outgoing --json object has checkpoint_push_disabled,\ncheckpoint_sync_remote, checkpoint_sync_remote_source and\ncheckpoint_sync_error (as in 'entire status --json'), stale_queue_entries\nand a checkpoints array of {checkpoint_id, ref, created_at, agent,\nsession_count, prompt, summary, files_touched, error}. The array is always\npresent, possibly empty.\n\nOptionally filter condensed checkpoints by session ID with --session\n(not applicable with --pending or --outgoing).\n\nUsage:\n  entire checkpoint list [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help             help for list\n      --json             Output as JSON instead of the human view\n      --no-pager         Disable pager output\n      --outgoing         List the checkpoints your next git push sends, read locally with no network call (git-refs backend)\n      --pending          List pending work — a preview of the next checkpoint, uncondensed subagent task records, and logs-only resume points\n      --session string   Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\nView and manage agent sessions tracked by Entire.\n\nCommands:\n  list     List all sessions across all worktrees\n  info     Show detailed information for a specific session\n  tokens   Show token usage and optimization recommendations\n  stop     Stop one or more active sessions\n  current  Show the active session for the current worktree\n  attach   Attach an existing agent session\n  adopt    Adopt an active session from another worktree\n  resume   Switch to a branch and resume its session\n\nExamples:\n  entire session list                      List all sessions\n  entire session info <session-id>         Show session details\n  entire session info <session-id> --json  Output as JSON\n  entire session tokens <session-id>       Show token usage\n  entire session stop                      Interactive stop\n  entire session current                   Active session for cwd\n  entire session attach <session-id>       Attach an external session\n  entire session adopt <session-id> --from ../repo  Adopt a moved session\n  entire session resume <branch>           Resume from a branch\n\nUsage:\n  entire session [command]\n\nAliases:\n  session, sessions\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  adopt       Adopt an active session from another worktree\n  attach      Attach an existing agent session\n  current     Show the session running this command, or the most recent one here\n  info        Show detailed session information\n  list        List all sessions\n  resume      Resume a stopped session (interactive picker, or by branch)\n  stop        Stop one or more active sessions\n  tokens      Show token usage and optimization recommendations for a session\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for session\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire session [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":100422683}},"started_at_ms":1793198055893,"completed_at_ms":1793198055994}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T14:34:17.226Z","ordinal":460139,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a182ee-e70a-7b40-bae6-4c1132cb44d5","call_id":"call_c23300a14be14912a0bed3f58864fa5d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Summarize recent checkpoint activity\n\nUsage:\n  entire recap [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --90                   Rolling 90 days\n      --agent string         Agent id to show, or all (default \"all\")\n      --color string         Color output: auto, always, or never (default \"auto\")\n      --day                  Today only (default)\n  -h, --help                 help for recap\n      --insecure-http-auth   Allow plain-HTTP auth (local dev only)\n      --month                This calendar month\n      --static               Print static output instead of opening the interactive recap\n      --view string          Which columns to show: you, team, or both (default \"both\")\n      --week                 Last 7 days\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\nList checkpoints on the current branch.\n\nBy default shows condensed checkpoints from the checkpoints branch for the\ncurrent branch. Use --pending for work that is not a checkpoint yet:\n\n  - A preview of the next checkpoint for each session in this worktree with\n    pending work. Agent turns are recorded in session state, not in git, so\n    this work has no checkpoint ID until you commit it. The preview shows the\n    turns since the last checkpoint, the files touched, subagent task records,\n    and the prompts since the last checkpoint.\n  - Subagent task records of other sessions on HEAD (not yet condensed).\n  - Logs-only resume points recovered from commits whose logs are already\n    condensed.\n\nUse --outgoing to see what your next 'git push' sends: the checkpoints\nqueued for the checkpoint sync remote, read from local state with no network\ncall. Each one shows its ID, age, agent, first prompt (or summary) and the\nfiles it touched. It needs the git-refs checkpoint backend, which pushes one\nref per checkpoint; the git-branch backend pushes entire/checkpoints/v1 as one\nbranch, so --outgoing reports an error there.\n\nOutput modes:\n  --json              Machine-readable JSON instead of the human view.\n  --pending           Select the pending dataset described above.\n  --pending --json    The pending dataset as a JSON array.\n  --outgoing          Select the outgoing dataset described above.\n  --outgoing --json   The outgoing dataset as one JSON object.\n\nEach --pending --json element has id, message, metadata_dir, date (RFC3339),\nis_task_checkpoint, is_logs_only, and when set tool_use_id, condensation_id,\nsession_id and session_prompt. A next-checkpoint preview element has an empty\nid, \"is_next_checkpoint\": true, and a \"next_checkpoint\" object:\n\n  {\"agent\": \"...\", \"turns\": 2,\n   \"files_touched\": [\"...\"],\n   \"task_records\": [{\"tool_use_id\": \"...\", \"subagent_type\": \"...\",\n                     \"description\": \"...\", \"status\": \"running|completed\"}],\n   \"prompts\": [\"...\"]}\n\nThe arrays are always present, possibly empty.\n\nThe --outgoing --json object has checkpoint_push_disabled,\ncheckpoint_sync_remote, checkpoint_sync_remote_source and\ncheckpoint_sync_error (as in 'entire status --json'), stale_queue_entries\nand a checkpoints array of {checkpoint_id, ref, created_at, agent,\nsession_count, prompt, summary, files_touched, error}. The array is always\npresent, possibly empty.\n\nOptionally filter condensed checkpoints by session ID with --session\n(not applicable with --pending or --outgoing).\n\nUsage:\n  entire checkpoint list [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help             help for list\n      --json             Output as JSON instead of the human view\n      --no-pager         Disable pager output\n      --outgoing         List the checkpoints your next git push sends, read locally with no network call (git-refs backend)\n      --pending          List pending work — a preview of the next checkpoint, uncondensed subagent task records, and logs-only resume points\n      --session string   Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\nView and manage agent sessions tracked by Entire.\n\nCommands:\n  list     List all sessions across all worktrees\n  info     Show detailed information for a specific session\n  tokens   Show token usage and optimization recommendations\n  stop     Stop one or more active sessions\n  current  Show the active session for the current worktree\n  attach   Attach an existing agent session\n  adopt    Adopt an active session from another worktree\n  resume   Switch to a branch and resume its session\n\nExamples:\n  entire session list                      List all sessions\n  entire session info <session-id>         Show session details\n  entire session info <session-id> --json  Output as JSON\n  entire session tokens <session-id>       Show token usage\n  entire session stop                      Interactive stop\n  entire session current                   Active session for cwd\n  entire session attach <session-id>       Attach an external session\n  entire session adopt <session-id> --from ../repo  Adopt a moved session\n  entire session resume <branch>           Resume from a branch\n\nUsage:\n  entire session [command]\n\nAliases:\n  session, sessions\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  adopt       Adopt an active session from another worktree\n  attach      Attach an existing agent session\n  current     Show the session running this command, or the most recent one here\n  info        Show detailed session information\n  list        List all sessions\n  resume      Resume a stopped session (interactive picker, or by branch)\n  stop        Stop one or more active sessions\n  tokens      Show token usage and optimization recommendations for a session\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for session\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire session [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a182ec-dd91-76f3-bef9-ba00d38b5f54","create_time":1793198057.2263205}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
