{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T14:34:41.902Z","ordinal":460159,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a182ec-dd91-76f3-bef9-ba00d38b5f54","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae208004f78819fa7d95df6e7f1659a","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I used the Entire workflow. `entire status` works: Entire is enabled on `main`, with five active sessions and 637 checkpoints queued for sync. Searching checkpoints and generating a recap both failed because this session cannot load the Entire login token: the `org.freedesktop.secrets` keyring service is unavailable.\n\nThe local pending-checkpoint list is readable, but it includes the dirty shared workspace; I left it untouched. I couldn’t retrieve authenticated checkpoint history, so I can’t use Entire to verify recorded intent until its keyring access is restored.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":777,"lineEnd":803,"note":"Nexus release context and evidence boundaries"}],"rolloutIds":[]}},"started_at_ms":1793198080361,"completed_at_ms":1793198081902}}
