{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T14:41:23.364Z","ordinal":460430,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a182ef-691b-71a3-bfbc-43ac959f5248","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae209924c30819facd025cae1772251","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The PR #302 local full-suite attempt ended with 49 failures because it ran `make test` without first building the CLI; several failures are explicit missing `cli/dist/index.js`. I’m not counting that as a product failure or a pass. The exact-head GitHub jobs have completed their built test path successfully on Node 22, Node 24, and Linux; Linux is now doing the second reproducibility package build. I’m recording that distinction and continuing to monitor the exact-head checks."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793198482368,"completed_at_ms":1793198483364}}
