{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T14:43:00.411Z","ordinal":460492,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a182ef-691b-71a3-bfbc-43ac959f5248","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-63e829e4-1825-4e04-927c-3cee48e0a30f","process_id":"38840","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","entire trail finding --help; entire trail approvals --help; entire trail show 17 --json"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire trail finding --help; entire trail approvals --help; entire trail show 17 --json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"Manage a trail's agent-native findings.\n\nRunning 'entire trail finding' shows the finding dashboard for the current\nbranch's trail. Pass a project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> to inspect another trail.\n--repo and --branch select the working context; findings apply only to that\nbranch, not the whole trail. Use 'entire trail list' to discover trails.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail finding [<trail>] [flags]\n  entire trail finding [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  add         Create a finding on a trail\n  apply       Apply a finding's unified-diff suggestion\n  dismiss     Dismiss a finding\n  list        List findings for a trail\n  reopen      Reopen a finding\n  resolve     Resolve a finding\n  show        Show a finding\n  update      Update a finding's metadata\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string       Select a repository branch within the trail\n      --cursor string       Continue from the next cursor returned by a previous page\n      --freshness string    Filter code-version freshness: current,stale,any (default \"current\")\n  -h, --help                help for finding\n      --include-dismissed   Include dismissed findings\n      --json                Output as JSON\n  -n, --limit int           Maximum number of findings to show (default 100)\n      --severity string     Filter by comma-separated severity value(s): high,medium,low\n      --status string       Filter by lifecycle status(es): open,resolved,dismissed; use 'any' for all (default \"open\")\n      --trail string        Project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> (defaults to the current branch's parent)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nUse \"entire trail finding [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\nList approval decisions on a trail\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail approvals [<trail>] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string   Select a repository branch within the trail\n  -h, --help            help for approvals\n      --json            Output as JSON\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\nresolve project: refresh login token: load core token: read access token: The name org.freedesktop.secrets was not provided by any .service files\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":133924658}},"started_at_ms":1793198580276,"completed_at_ms":1793198580411}}
