 is the root cause I diagnosed above. A directory target now counts as replaceable only if `directoryContainsOnlyGitCleanRemovableEntries` holds and there are no tracked `<p>/` descendants. That check still refuses `.git` (directory or gitfile), entries ignored by `check-ignore --no-index` (which honours `.gitignor\"}\n{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T12:22:43Z\",\"body\":\"### Independent Verification & Review — `c45e34ff7910931067e645a8499b99af82b4b4f3`\\n\\n- **Base Commit**: `b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff`\\n- **Head Commit**: `c45e34ff7910931067e645a8499b99af82b4b4f3`\\n- **Diff SHA-256**: `1099e6ff6b68ab9907ac66c908bf45c8ab1af338d3b6a14227d45d60cf35dc29`\\n- **Verification**:\\n  - Clean merge of `origin/main` (`b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff`) into `90d67559620f7191d303c4a3a6ec476bac6e241c`; diff against `b293b441` is bit-for-bit identical (`1099e6ff...`) to the previously verified 48/48 pass in `test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts` + `test/checkpoint_hook_failure_paths.test.ts`.\\n  - `git diff --check`: 0 errors.\\n  - CodeQL (`40686797316` / `1228115\"}\n{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T14:00:10Z\",\"body\":\"Review remediation update (exact head `3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7`, base `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`, cumulative diff SHA-256 `d90aeb05a9f5c5d0a35bfa0f597d96cc39a5f6480e22b20094f7523cd4cacdff`):\\n\\n- The bare-repository guard now requires a bare repository layout and `core.bare=true`; an ordinary directory with similarly named files remains restorable.\\n- The bare-repository regression asserts the captured destination file remains absent, as well as preserving the bare repository metadata/canary and the outer index/HEAD/staged canary.\\n- Exact candidate `checkpoint_restore.test.ts` passed 51/51 with isolated HOME and serial execution; `tsc --noEmit` and `git diff --c\"}\n{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T14:26:06Z\",\"body\":\"Exact