{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T14:46:59.037Z","ordinal":460618,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a182ef-691b-71a3-bfbc-43ac959f5248","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae20ade4e7c819fb879eb829a1d04dc","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Campaign status: `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE` · Acceptance: `IN_PROGRESS`.** No RC has been accepted; `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest published release.\n\n- **Current `origin/main`:** `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`; its exact-head CI and CodeQL runs pass. I left the dirty shared checkout untouched.\n- **PRs #299, #300 and #305:** their Node, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks pass. Entire trails 14, 15 and 20 each fail only because no reviewer approved the trail.\n- **PR #302:** exact-head GitHub CI run [40701620444](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40701620444) passed on Node 22, Node 24 and Linux, including packaging, reproducibility and smoke checks. Its Entire trail 17 has **five unresolved high-severity findings** and no reviewer approval. I posted the completed CI evidence on [PR #302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6472066993). I cannot retrieve the finding details: Entire’s authenticated commands fail because the desktop keyring service is unavailable.\n- **Test follow-up:** a local `make test` attempt without first building the CLI ended with 49 failures out of 1,938, including missing `cli/dist/index.js`. I’m not treating that run as product qualification. A corrected `make build` then `make test` run is active under the SUITE claim on a detached PR #302 snapshot **plus an uncommitted two-file patch**; its log was advancing at 14:46 UTC. This is not exact-commit evidence.\n- **Other open gates:** held-out issue #1 remains unassigned with no custodian reply; the final-RC human terminal matrix remains incomplete. No stable release or new RC is ready.\n\nI recorded these updates in the existing release work record. The next concrete actions are to capture the active run’s terminal result, obtain an authenticated independent reviewer to disposition the Entire findings and approvals, and resolve held-out custody before advancing to a new RC.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":777,"lineEnd":803,"note":"Nexus release gates and evidence boundaries"}],"rolloutIds":[]}},"started_at_ms":1793198814327,"completed_at_ms":1793198819037}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T14:46:59.044Z","ordinal":460619,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae20ade4e7c819fb879eb829a1d04dc","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"**Campaign status: `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE` · Acceptance: `IN_PROGRESS`.** No RC has been accepted; `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest published release.\n\n- **Current `origin/main`:** `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`; its exact-head CI and CodeQL runs pass. I left the dirty shared checkout untouched.\n- **PRs #299, #300 and #305:** their Node, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks pass. Entire trails 14, 15 and 20 each fail only because no reviewer approved the trail.\n- **PR #302:** exact-head GitHub CI run [40701620444](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40701620444) passed on Node 22, Node 24 and Linux, including packaging, reproducibility and smoke checks. Its Entire trail 17 has **five unresolved high-severity findings** and no reviewer approval. I posted the completed CI evidence on [PR #302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6472066993). I cannot retrieve the finding details: Entire’s authenticated commands fail because the desktop keyring service is unavailable.\n- **Test follow-up:** a local `make test` attempt without first building the CLI ended with 49 failures out of 1,938, including missing `cli/dist/index.js`. I’m not treating that run as product qualification. A corrected `make build` then `make test` run is active under the SUITE claim on a detached PR #302 snapshot **plus an uncommitted two-file patch**; its log was advancing at 14:46 UTC. This is not exact-commit evidence.\n- **Other open gates:** held-out issue #1 remains unassigned with no custodian reply; the final-RC human terminal matrix remains incomplete. No stable release or new RC is ready.\n\nI recorded these updates in the existing release work record. The next concrete actions are to capture the active run’s terminal result, obtain an authenticated independent reviewer to disposition the Entire findings and approvals, and resolve held-out custody before advancing to a new RC.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:777-803|note=[Nexus release gates and evidence boundaries]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a182ef-691b-71a3-bfbc-43ac959f5248","create_time":1793198814.3083932,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae20ade4e7c819fb879eb829a1d04dc","turn_id":"01a182ef-691b-71a3-bfbc-43ac959f5248","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a182fa-86e4-7142-8993-7ce311b4122a","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":21935}}
