review recorded other unresolved credential/configuration findings; it is not integrated or accepted. T2/T3/T4, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, exact-candidate reproducibility, the manual terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS; no stable v1.0.0 release exists. Publication authority remains granted and gated by acceptance.\n254:The 13:45 checkpoint below remains as historical evidence; this update supersedes its origin/main, post-merge CI, installed-version, terminal-environment, and current blocker observations.\n260:**Candidate and publication state:** Public prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.8) remains the latest release, but its tag resolves to `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, before PR #252 and PR #254. Its Linux archive digest remains `sha256:bbded963a9bcaa9c0764b86d900f752c46ed364bfe30cc67e5bbf23b5fb5f48e`. RC8 reproducibility and isolated-prefix provenance checks apply only to that earlier artifact. It is not an accepted RC for current `main`; a candidate from the current source must be rebuilt and qualified. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The RC8 signing identity remains reported by GitHub as unverified (`bad_email`); stable signing must use a GitHub-verified identity.\n262:**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open. The latest public metadata-only custody request (12:18 UTC) has no custodian response; do not access held-out payloads or begin the held-out run before independent custody acceptance. The last recorded human terminal matrix is 0/15, with real-terminal operator evidence still required. Exact-current-RC installed qualification, standalone/provider acceptance, T2/T3/T4 qualification and independent exact-RC acceptance are not established. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted but gated on all required acceptance and stable-artifact checks.\n264:The 08:05 checkpoint immediately below is retained as historical evidence; this update supersedes its source, CI, candidate and current blocker status.\n274:The 06:24 checkpoint immediately below is retained as a historical snapshot; this update supersedes its CI conclusion, RC publication state, cross-runner status, and current blocker summary.\n278:**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, incorporating PR #249 (`8e562b0f3406e94003806746cb69a5258f72a59f`) and PR #250. PR #249 merged at 05:57 UTC and PR #250 merged at 06:20 UTC. On this exact source, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 requirements explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification), and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` confirms all components are `1.0.0-rc.8`. CodeQL run [40279197561](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40279197561) passed. Exact-main CI [40279197785](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40279197785) is still running; its Node 22 and Node 24 jobs passed Rust tests and release builds and were running the CLI test suite at 06:24 UTC. The current checkpoint does not claim full CI success.\n282:**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1), for held-out T2/T3 corpus custody, remains OPEN (last observed update 02:33:48 UTC); the required custodian sealing and independent private-custody acceptance are not established. Held-out qualification has not started. Provider/standalone coverage, T3/T4 qualification, installed exact-RC qualification, independent RC acceptance, and the human terminal matrix (0/15 at last evidence) remain incomplete. Treat the older entries below as historical snapshots; they do not supersede these current observations.\n289:**PR #246 / `agent.ts`:** PR [#246](https://github.com/mikeh