hen checkpoint creation encounters a Git index lock. Its required checks passed and an independent review accepted the exact diff. This is source remediation on current `main`; RC6 and RC7 artifacts predate it. The next installed RC still needs to be exercised against the reported startup failure before claiming a released fix.\n313:**PR #246 / `agent.ts` handoff:** PR [#246](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/246) remains open at head `a2aa9b1bbeec022c6f289af94373f97913ebc62f`, based on `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`. Exact-head run [40255358554](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255358554) completed successfully across Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64, including Linux package reproducibility. CodeQL run `40255358512` and JavaScript/TypeScript checks also passed. `KimiCode-defect-scan` retains the `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts` claim. A read-only merge-tree preflight against current `main` found no conflicts, but the branch has not yet been updated or merged. The claims log records that Kimi's next step is to update normally onto current `main` and rerun exact-head checks; the old-base run is not integration evidence.\n315:**Checkpoint index-lock defect:** PR [#243](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/243) merged as `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`, an ancestor of current `main`. It adds actionable diagnosis and a final lock recheck when checkpoint creation encounters a Git index lock. Its required checks passed and an independent review accepted the exact diff. This is source remediation on current `main`; RC6 and RC7 artifacts predate it. The next installed RC still needs to be exercised against the reported startup failure before claiming a released fix.\n321:The previous 02:14 and 01:55 checkpoints below are retained as historical snapshots; this 02:19 checkpoint supersedes their current CI and PR #246 status.\n327:**PR #246 / `agent.ts` handoff:** PR [#246](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/246) remains open at `a2aa9b1bbeec022c6f289af94373f97913ebc62f`, based on `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`; `KimiCode-defect-scan` owns the `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts` claim. Its Node 22/24 tests, CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript checks passed. In Linux job 121360325779, the CLI suite passed at 02:12:07 UTC, the first Linux package build passed at 02:13:55 UTC, and the reproducibility package build was still running at 02:14 UTC. A read-only merge-tree preflight against current `main` produced `f9653711777c4ad9be0aff59db816ea57b3dfd83` without conflicts; no branch update or merge has been performed. After all current checks finish, the recorded path remains a normal update onto current `main` followed by exact-head checks.\n329:**Checkpoint index-lock defect:** PR [#243](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/243) merged at 00:16 UTC as `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`, which is an ancestor of current `main`. Its focused change adds actionable diagnosis and a final lock recheck when checkpoint creation encounters a Git index lock; its tests and required PR checks passed, with independent review ACCEPT recorded for the exact diff. This is source-level remediation on current `main`, not behavior in the older RC6 or RC7 artifacts. The installed next RC must still be exercised against the reported startup failure before claiming the issue fixed in a release. The `FILE_cli_src_checkpoint.ts` claim has been released after verifying merge, checks and a clean worktree.\n341:**`agent.ts` handoff / PR #246:** PR [#246](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/246) is open at head `a2aa9b1bbeec022c6f289af94373f97913ebc62f`, still based on `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`. The slice has independent source-review ACCEPT and targeted build/tests passed, while its exact-head Node 22 and Node 24 suites remain in progress; CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript checks passed. At 01:54 UTC the `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts` claim was handed from `codex-root` to `KimiCode-defect-scan` with the branch and worktree recorded. The handoff requires waiting for the current checks to finish, merging current `origin/main` normally, and rerunning exact-head checks before integration.\n377:**Distribution scope:** The release owner confirmed the supported distribution target is the GitHub installer/archive only; npm publication is inapplicable. The current release workflow is the authority for published assets.\n381:**Qualification evidence and blockers:** The RC3 provider record `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json` was independently accepted: ChatGPT sign-in streaming/tool round trip passed; OpenRouter failed authentication and its live task remains outstanding. Public Issue #1 remains open; its latest visible update is coordinator-authored at 10:23 UTC, with no custodian response. The sealed legacy `hidden.command` corpus is not accepted by the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification has started and no private payload was accessed. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, exact-candidate cross-runner reproducibility, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n395:**Held-out and remaining qualification:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest remains incompatible with the current evaluator's `blackbox-v1` contract because it uses legacy `hidden.command`; the independent custodian must convert or replace it, revalidate it, and accept a new immutable manifest. No hidden task or payload was accessed and no held-out run started. Provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4 including long tasks and nine fault classes, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the real-terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n401:**Release source and branch reconciliation:** Release PRs #147, #153, #157, and #159 target `main`; the current release source is `origin/main@1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`. `origin/v1/integration` remains at `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78` from 2026-10-21 and is not the source used by the current RC3 candidate PRs. Do not combine evidence from those different heads. The shared checkout remains dirty and was not modified.\n407:**Held-out and qualification gates:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest uses legacy `hidden.command` tasks, which the current evaluator rejects; the approved path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, and a new immutable manifest identity. No held-out task has been run. Private custody acceptance, current author/custodian ownership and exposure history, independent digest/setup/reference validation, effective access restrictions, and evaluator separation remain unverified. Installed-RC provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, cross-runner reproducibility, and exact-artifact acceptance have not run. The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence; automated PTY tests do not satisfy it.\n417:**Node runtime floor:** The accepted user decision is Node `>=22`. PR #150 integrates that floor in package engines, installer checks, CLI diagnostics and upgrade behavior, CI/release/reproducibility configuration, tests, and current release documentation. Superseded PRs #137 and #146 were closed after their intended policy changes were verified in current main; their older branch evidence is not current qualification evidence.\n419:**Checkpoint failure and remediation:** The operator reports every launch attempt on installed RC1 fails before the turn starts with `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint`. This is confirmed as an RC1 limitation: immutable RC1 source predates the checkpoint-choice flow. PR #153 integrates that flow in current main, offering read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint despite sensitive content, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. This is source-integrated behavior only; the installed candidate must exercise the prompt and selected actions before acceptance. RC1 and RC2 remain unchanged and do not contain this behavior.\n427:## Historical integration checkpoint (observed 2026-10-23 02:13 UTC at `fa16045`; superseded by the current status above)\n431:**Node runtime floor:** The accepted user decision is Node `>=22`. PR #150 integrates that floor in package engines, installer checks, CLI diagnostics and upgrade behavior, CI/release/reproducibility configuration, tests, and current release documentation. Superseded PRs #137 and #146 were closed after their intended policy changes were verified in current main; their older branch evidence is not current qualification evidence.\n435:**Checkpoint failure and remediation:** The operator reports that every attempt to start Nexus RC1 fails with `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint`. This is consistent with RC1's exact source predating PR #147's checkpoint-choice flow. PR #147 is integrated in current main and its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed; the interactive TUI now offers read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint anyway with a sensitivity warning, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. RC1 and RC2 are immutable and do not contain this behavior. The next candidate must include the fix, and the installed candidate must be exercised to verify the choices before any acceptance claim.\n437:**RC identity and publication:** Remote immutable tags are `v1.0.0-rc.1` at `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779` and `v1.0.0-rc.2` at `19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`; both predate the accepted Node 22 floor. GitHub currently publishes RC1 as a prerelease; RC2 has a tag but no published release. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 tag/release is established. The next candidate needs a fresh RC3 identity after its source/version checks; it must be installed and qualified before acceptance.\n441:## Historical integration update (2026-10-22 21:14 UTC; superseded by the current status above)\n443:The authoritative source is `origin/main@269d611ca0a0c8a55244bf70d89fa4a918b9d218`. The Node 22 convergence branch was refreshed without rewriting history and its current candidate head is `v1/node22-floor-converged@658ace9d4ab67901b5b2db1c090f6b01537be27a`; the Node `>=22` source implementation was validated at `fb798a1bd517ac85fd3c99f76d3fda1709540a8d`, and the candidate adds reviewed ruleset and acceptance-stage reconciliations. It is not yet integrated. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes at version `1.0.0-rc.2`. The source requirements check currently fails because REQ-REL-111 remains partial pending exact-candidate checks; REQ-REL-003 remains partial for installed-RC platform qualification and is now explicitly mapped to ACC-PLAT in the exact-RC stage. No threshold or qualification evidence was changed.\n445:The live GitHub `v1-protected-branches` ruleset (ID `25340146`) currently requires `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64`; it does not require Node 20. The checked-in ruleset snapshot now matches that live required-check set. No live protection setting was modified. PR #137 still targets an older base, PR #146 remains a draft, and the refreshed candidate branch has not yet been opened as a replacement PR. Independent review of the refreshed candidate requested these documentation reconciliations; code/runtime review otherwise found no blocker.\n463:**RC and publication:** The published `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag resolves to `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779`, an ancestor of current `main`, and is not an artifact built from current source. Its published asset digest is `8d7dd32f3d00adb98d4f0ea2c6a484ea8e04fc547b4d78b21b060000eda22b9d`. The next candidate needs a new immutable identity, currently expected to be `v1.0.0-rc.2`, with synchronized version metadata and release notes. Exact-RC artifact/install checks, held-out T2, provider and standalone qualification, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, independent RC acceptance, and stable-promotion disposition remain outstanding. Publication authorization is granted but gated on those results. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\n465:**Runtime floor:** The merged DEC-12 and current `main` specify Node `>=20`; the upstream release schedule lists Node 20 end of life as 2026-04-30. Open PR #143 proposes to correct that date in the RC1 release note; its exact checks passed on the prior base, and it still needs a refresh against current `main`. README, quickstart, and the development guide still contain the old date on `main`; edits to those files are part of the separate Node 22 lane. PR #137 is open and ready for review, implementing its stated owner-directed `>=22` target. It remains based on old base `8935918` and needs a current-main refresh. Its Node 22/24, Linux packaging, and CodeQL checks pass on that prior base, but the required `test-matrix (20)` context is absent and it has no independent review. The proposed source change is not integrated and conflicts with accepted DEC-12 and REQ-REL-111, which still specify `>=20` and a Node 20/22/24 matrix. The active ruleset requires `test-matrix (20)`, which this candidate omits; its checks are on the prior base and no independent review is recorded. Do not treat `>=22` as v1 policy until the policy records and required checks are formally reconciled. No runtime-floor change is made by this checkpoint.\n469:This checkpoint supersedes the earlier 2026-10-22 and 2026-10-21 updates below for current source and release status. Historical reports remain bound to their recorded revisions.\n482:**Acceptance status:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n486:- **Exact-head CI:** PR #8 targets `main@db1ca55` from `v1/integration@7d6673f`. On current head, `javascript-typescript` runs [39624982585](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39624982585) and [39624995598](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39624995598) passed, as did CodeQL [119308898279](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/119308898279). The required `test-matrix (20)`, `(22)`, and `(24)` jobs in run [39624995762](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39624995762) were still pending at 15:26 UTC. The successful source workflow [39615105190] ran on parent `8f4504e`, so its results are not represented as exact-`7d6673f` results.\n491:This update supersedes the 14:56 UTC `8f4504e` checkpoint below for current state. Earlier evidence remains bound to its recorded revisions.\n497:**Acceptance status:** `IN_PROGRESS`\n501:This checkpoint reconciles the candidate ledger and acceptance procedure against recorded source and test evidence. It is not a release approval. Historical inspection sections below are preserved as audit evidence and do not represent current branch state where superseded by the 2026-10-21 update.\n509:- **Held-out corpus and custody:** Public T2 manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` remains the 40-task identity `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`; T3 public manifest identity remains `85fb9cafbe18e846bd64fb13eb4bfa0f92df0792bc93d12adaa685e04c9f1383`. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no custodian response since 2026-10-21 12:21 UTC. Current evaluator qualification rejects the sealed T2 corpus's legacy `hidden.command` format; the documented path requires a custodian-owned compatible immutable successor and repeated custody checks. Private digest re-derivation, exposure history, setup/reference validation, effective access separation, and current custody acceptance remain unverified here. No payload, validator, reference solution, or hidden answer was accessed, and no held-out run has started.\n511:- **Version, RC, and publication:** Root and CLI package versions remain `0.1.0-alpha.2`. GitHub currently lists only alpha pre-releases `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`; no `v1.0.0-rc.N` artifact/tag or stable v1.0.0 tag, npm package, or GitHub release exists. Follow the staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md`: pre-RC source gates, RC construction, artifact-bound RC gates, installed-RC qualification and independent G6 acceptance, then stable promotion/publication and post-publication verification.\n517:The 17:16 checkpoint's phrase “nothing has been tagged or published” was too broad. GitHub lists the existing pre-releases `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`, with corresponding tags `7e46bb0da88d06552a66ef703f53a05d1de1f37d` and `c3dcafac93b5f52d913b4dfb6eb292bbcede4566`. Post-merge CI run `39146982849` and CodeQL passed on exact integration `6a16cb60635c9182f13be1635d5f44eddebdcde0`. No v1.0.0 release candidate or stable v1.0.0 publication exists. The superseded 17:16 text below is retained verbatim as historical evidence; this correction is authoritative for current release status.\n529:## Historical current state update (2026-10-18 16:19 UTC, `4bce876`)\n533:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` ran from a detached worktree at exact revision `4bce8760893b222789b76011a477dd61988ecba6` with isolated `HOME`; it failed as required. Ledger result: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 11 below threshold: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, `REQ-QUAL-109`. `REQ-AGT-118` remains tested. `REQ-AGT-010` remains partial; its existing ACC-TRUST-04 source evidence is pinned to `2c70d39`, and the current row still needs exact-revision evidence and a DEC-04-aligned disposition before promotion. The ledger owner was given this exact checker output; no ledger status was changed.\n542:- **Authoritative integration and CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is `519398495b7c3a2e5915ed76eee0bb731feb0bcf`. The earlier reported `2c70d39` and `d2c4bfc` are ancestors of this revision; they are not competing integration heads. PR #9 and PR #23 are integrated as `64ee88b` and `886766b`; PR #24's terminal acceptance kit is integrated at `5193984`. Exact-head integration CI run [39120013759](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39120013759) is in progress, so there is no current-head green claim yet. PR #24's checks passed on its exact head `91eaee9` in run [39117464186](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39117464186); its accepted procedure does not replace the human terminal matrix.\n544:- **PR #26 evaluator boundary:** PR #26 head `c019575` contains the independently reviewed dedicated-tmpfs preflight and adversarial staged-Git/external-store canary; it is rebased on `886766b`, while integration has since advanced to `5193984`. Exact-head CI run [39119705161](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39119705161) is still running its Node 20/22/24 CLI suites at this checkpoint. It must be rebased and requalified on `5193984` before merge. A local synthetic permission probe passed (0711 accepted; 0755 and 0721 rejected); the targeted TypeScript test could not run on this host because no dedicated tmpfs was mounted, and the shared `/dev/shm` correctly failed preflight. That failed local attempt is not counted as a pass.\n545:- **Qualification host:** PR #22 is still based on `a7126aa` (head `7d30494`); its historical exact-head CI passed, but it is not current-base evidence. The owner confirmed the file split with PR #26 and requested owner approval before running `eval/host/provision.sh`. No host account, sudoers, mount unit, or runtime directory has been provisioned. Resource-limit qualification and held-out execution remain blocked until this host boundary is installed and validated.\n687:- The installed-package startup PTY smoke reached the Nexus prompt under isolated HOME. This does not satisfy the §5.2 scripted PTY set or the §5.3 human matrix. An attempted legacy §5.2 driver was invalid: its checkout-layout paths and wait condition do not match the current RC startup/trust prompt; its mock gateway recorded zero requests. No product pass/fail was inferred.\n694:| T2/T3 held-out custody | Blocked. Issue #1 has no custodian reply; the public 40-task manifest does not establish private custody acceptance, and the legacy validator contract is incompatible with the current evaluator. No private payload was accessed or run. | Independent custodian confirms author/handoff, compatible immutable corpus or successor, validation, access separation, digests and custody acceptance; only then prepare and execute the approved runs. |\n695:| Evaluator resource/secret boundary | Synthetic current-source host preflight 10/10; no accepted qualification-host/custody result. | Complete independent host and custody acceptance before any held-out execution. |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":35934}},"started_at_ms":1793201285016,"completed_at_ms":1793201285016}}
