fter #271 and #272. Exact-main CI [40521505143](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40521505143) and CodeQL [40521505001](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40521505001) both passed on `3b7af5d`; CI passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux tests, security gates, packaging, reproducibility, package smoke, and installer smoke. PR #269 merge-commit CI [40519862728](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40519862728) passed on `f059770`. These runs establish CI for their exact commits, not the RC10 release gates.\n\n**Readiness PR #268:** The owner refreshed PR [#268](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/268) onto `main`; GitHub shows it open and mergeable at head `98f87bee6ca112e6d50f6fb2bc480fc47723c648`, based on `3b7af5d3cd46ab1b83e9c8df9862e09cee22b1a7`. Its Node 22, Node 24, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks pass; Linux packaging/reproducibility run [40524245685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40524245685) is still pending. The 14:38 checkpoint update was independently accepted (diff SHA-256 `c8cf46163cd8be8666ea86e8a95a7483588e10aa3e8775fbfa213ce55895d41e`). The current local follow-up records terminal main and #269 CI plus the latest PR state; it has not been pushed, and no PR merge is claimed.\n\n**Merged hook remediations and residual:** PRs #269 (retention shell/hook execution) and #270 (checkpoint Git hooks) are merged at `f059770` and `3b7af5d`; both now have passing exact-merge CI. The merged implementation passes `core.hooksPath=/dev/null` to relevant Git commands. Configured `reference-transaction` hooks may remain callable despite that setting; this was independently reproduced and accepted on a local follow-up to #269 (`d349068`), whose focused tests passed 17/17 on Git 2.54.0 and Git 2.43.0 plus `tsc --noEmit`. That follow-up is not on current main or the merged #269 head and needs a separately refreshed fix and exact-head validation; its source and test fi