ae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.8^{}\nd211d1c7545d2dd629531e4f712e98a240a782c6\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.9\n4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.9^{}\n13:**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` is still the latest release (published 2026-10-27); the package at `b293b44` is also `1.0.0-rc.10`, so source changes require a successor RC before installed-RC qualification. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 exists. Held-out issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest public status request was posted 2026-10-28 12:42 UTC, with no custodian response as of this checkpoint. The public 40-task manifest is not custody acceptance, and no held-out qualification has started. T2/T3/T4, evaluator/custody acceptance, remaining provider and standalone gates, cross-runner reproducibility, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix remains 0/15; the Ubuntu desktop has setup evidence only, with no qualifying screenshots or cell verdicts recorded.\n29:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Held-out T2/T3/T4, remaining live-provider and standalone gates, successor-RC artifact qualification, cross-runner evidence, the 15-cell human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on these mandatory checks.\n43:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease, built from immutable source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and was last updated 2026-10-27 18:47 UTC; no custodian acceptance or compatible sealed held-out corpus is recorded, and no held-out payload has been accessed. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining live provider and standalone gates, qualification of a candidate built from current source, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The five-terminal by three-size matrix remains **0/15 formally recorded cell verdicts**, with no screenshots. The operator reports successful rendering at tested sizes but a 43×13 lower limit for tmux inside GNOME Terminal; this is partial observation, not completion of the prescribed matrix. The available `mike-dev` shell is headless, and its configured `ubuntu-desktop` host name does not resolve, so I could not produce real-terminal screenshots or verdicts from this session. Stable publication remains gated on every required acceptance gate.\n57:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest release and is still a prerelease; its immutable source is `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`. No stable `v1.0.0` exists. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without an independent custodian acceptance or a compatible sealed held-out corpus; no held-out payload has been accessed. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining live provider and standalone gates, qualification of a candidate built from current source, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The required five-terminal by three-size matrix has **0/15 formally recorded cell verdicts** and no screenshots. The operator reports that the client rendered at the sizes tried, but tmux inside GNOME Terminal could not be reduced below 43×13; this does not establish every prescribed interaction or matrix cell. Stable publication remains gated on all required acceptance gates.\n73:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the newest prerelease on source `16ee8ca`; stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Held-out custody acceptance and compatible frozen T2 data remain unresolved (issue #1 is open with no custodian response); T2/T3/T4, evaluator-host acceptance, the remaining live provider and standalone gates, and independent exact-RC acceptance are incomplete. The human five-environment by three-size terminal matrix remains **0/15**, pending the operator; no per-cell verdict or evidence is recorded. Keep stable publication gated on every required acceptance gate.\n85:**Qualification and publication:** RC10 remains a prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed. Exact cross-runner reproducibility passed for immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca`; a successor candidate from current main still requires its own reproducibility run. Held-out custodian acceptance, T2/T3/T4, remaining live provider and standalone qualification, independent exact-RC acceptance, and human terminal evidence remain open. The five-environment by three-size operator terminal matrix remains **0/15**; no cell result or screenshot is recorded. Automated PTY evidence does not substitute for these human cells. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on all mandatory acceptance criteria.\n101:**Human terminal acceptance:** The five-terminal by three-size matrix remains **0/15**. The operator cannot run the requested xterm 80×24 cell now; no cell result or screenshots are inferred. The prepared Ubuntu/GNOME host and worksheet remain available for a later genuine operator run. Scripted PTY evidence does not replace the human matrix. Publication remains gated on all mandatory acceptance gates.\n114:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains a prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` is listed. The human five-terminal by three-size matrix remains **0/15** and pending. The user's informal observation is that rendering works at tested sizes except tmux in GNOME Terminal, where the smallest usable size is 43×13; there are no per-cell records or screenshots, so human acceptance is not established. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open, last updated 2026-10-26 17:37:53 UTC, with no custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody and host acceptance, live provider/standalone, independent exact-RC, scripted terminal, and human acceptance gates remain incomplete. Publication authorization remains gated on every required acceptance gate.\n126:**Release and acceptance gates:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains a prerelease; stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. The human real-terminal matrix remains 0/15; the user's report of rendering at 43×13 in tmux on GNOME Terminal is not the full matrix and had no captured screenshots. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN, last updated 2026-10-26 17:37:53 UTC, with no recorded custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, live provider/standalone, independent exact-RC, and human acceptance gates remain incomplete. Publication authorization remains gated on all required acceptance.\n132:Five targeted synthetic installed-RC10 cancellation rechecks at `TERM=dumb`, 100×30 completed with Esc delays from 0 to 1 second; idle return measured 0.405–0.507 seconds. The two earlier full-matrix timeouts remained valid and unresolved; this targeted recheck did not promote ACC-TUI-A11Y or E3. Evidence and raw PTY streams are preserved in [the cancellation timing recheck](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/cancel-timing-recheck-20261027/README.md). Human terminal acceptance remained 0/15. This historical record is retained from the PR #264 merge history.\n142:**Candidate and gates:** The latest public release remains prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10), built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0` with archive SHA-256 `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. Stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. The required real-terminal matrix remains **0/15**; scripted terminal evidence does not replace operator evidence. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no recorded custodian acceptance; no private payload was accessed or run. T2/T3/T4, exact-current-RC provider/standalone and cross-runner qualification, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization is granted but gated. The distribution target is the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\n154:**Installed RC and qualification:** The latest public release remains prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10), built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0` with archive SHA-256 `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. No stable `v1.0.0` release appears among the current public releases. The human five-terminal, three-size matrix remains **0/15**; scripted terminal evidence is partial and does not replace the operator matrix. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no custodian response to the latest metadata-only request (2026-10-26); no held-out payload was accessed or run. T2/T3/T4, standalone/provider qualification, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n164:**RC10 installation and terminal preparation:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains an unaccepted prerelease from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256 is `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. The linked [RC10 desktop preflight record](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-manual-preflight/README.md) documents successful provenance-verified installation to an isolated qualification prefix on `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`), with CLI identity `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)`. xterm, kitty, GNOME Terminal, tmux, and VS Code are present. This prepares the host only: the human matrix remains **0/15**. The operator must perform each of the five terminal environments at all three sizes and provide two genuine screenshots and a verdict per cell; scripted PTY evidence does not substitute.\n176:**Terminal observation and acceptance:** The user reports that the client rendered at the sizes they tried except in tmux inside GNOME Terminal; the smallest observed tmux window was 43×13. They said the remaining observations may take several days. No screenshots, exact installed-package identity, or cell-by-cell results were supplied. The 15-cell worksheet therefore remains 0/15 and unaccepted; the report is retained as provisional operator context only. Do not prompt while other gates can progress.\n178:**RC and remaining acceptance:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains an unaccepted prerelease from source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, not the current main source. PR #265's merged OpenRouter evidence covers one pinned-model verification and one synthetic small task. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without custodian acceptance; no held-out task payload was accessed or run. Installed exact-RC qualification, standalone/provider matrix coverage, T2/T3/T4, the complete terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release is published. Existing publication authorization remains gated on every mandatory acceptance gate.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":284309421}},"started_at_ms":1793201338967,"completed_at_ms":1793201339252}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:28:59.712Z","ordinal":461727,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1831e-47db-7583-982e-1aab45c43e6a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-fcfb6b98-2584-4132-b655-bd6eb5fba934","process_id":"96389","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 302 --json headRefOid,baseRefOid,mergeStateStatus,reviewDecision,updatedAt,comments,reviews"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 302 --json headRefOid,baseRefOid,mergeStateStatus,reviewDecision,updatedAt,comments,reviews"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"baseRefOid\":\"b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgUJ8-A\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"coderabbitai\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"NONE\",\"body\":\"<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\\n\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> - [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\\n> \\n> This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\\n> \\n> <details>\\n> <summary><strong><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\\\" width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" align=\\\"absmiddle\\\" alt=\\\"\\\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\\n> <dl>\\n> <dd>\\n> \\n> - **Source mode**: Auto\\n> - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n> - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n> - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n> - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n> - **Layers**: defaults\\n> - **Review profile**: CHILL\\n> - **Plan**: Advanced\\n> - **Run ID**: `5fbb699b-123b-4642-b8ec-211af4a84559`\\n> \\n> </dd>\\n> </dl>\\n> </details>\\n\\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\\n- [ ] <!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --> <strong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\\n<!-- tips_start -->\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&utm_content=302)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>❤️ Share</strong></summary>\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\\n\\n<!-- tips_end -->\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T07:47:31Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":true,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6463585528\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":false},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgUVlYA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Read-Only Review — **ACTION REQUIRED (`273b9e6042d4dd0cc24d3dfeb461fb387f9cb97c`)**\\n\\n- **Candidate**: `v1/defect-checkpoint-untracked-integration` ([`273b9e6042d4dd0cc24d3dfeb461fb387f9cb97c`](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/273b9e6042d4dd0cc24d3dfeb461fb387f9cb97c))\\n- **Merge-Base**: [`ceaf60072b7c364edac523d2517fb12df8f5f6cd`](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/ceaf60072b7c364edac523d2517fb12df8f5f6cd) (clean merge with `origin/main` `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4`)\\n- **Diff SHA-256 (`origin/main...HEAD`)**: `0c646eeb99f475c7c000da5bd23b20457993fe0fc0a6e239393ea656ce58593f`\\n\\n#### Verification Summary (Isolated Worktree & `$HOME`)\\n- `tsc --noEmit`: **PASS (0 errors)**\\n- `node --import tsx --test test/checkpoint_hook_failure_paths.test.ts test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts`: **40/40 PASS**\\n- `git diff --check`: **PASS**\\n- Exact-head CodeQL [40652347344](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652347344): **SUCCESS**\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### Findings Requiring Remediation\\n\\n1. **Dangling & In-Workspace Symlink Parents Bypass `assertUntrackedDestinationSafe()` (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts`, lines 193–208)**:\\n   - `assertUntrackedDestinationSafe()` walks upward with `while (!fs.existsSync(parent))` and checks `fs.statSync(parent).isDirectory()` + `fs.realpathSync(parent)`. Because both `existsSync` and `statSync` follow symlinks:\\n     - **Dangling symlink ancestor**: If `workspace/dir` is an ignored (or non-Git) dangling symlink pointing to `/tmp/nonexistent-outside` and `cp.untrackedFiles` has `\\\"dir/file.txt\\\"`, `fs.existsSync(\\\"${root}/dir\\\")` is `false`. The loop walks past `dir` up to `root`, so `assertUntrackedDestinationSafe` passes **before** Git mutation. During `restore()`, `git read-tree`, `git checkout-index`, `removeTrackedDeletions`, and `git clean -fd` mutate the workspace (leaving the ignored dangling symlink `dir` in place), and `copyUntrackedEntries` only fails mid-restore when `ensurePrivateDir` rejects `dir` (and in legacy non-Git restore `copyDirFiltered` calls `fs.mkdirSync` on it).\\n     - **In-workspace directory symlink ancestor**: If `workspace/dir` is a symlink pointing to another directory inside the workspace (`ln -s real_dir workspace/dir`) and `relativePath` is `\\\"dir/sub/file.txt\\\"` where `real_dir/sub` is a real directory, `fs.statSync(\\\"${root}/dir\\\").isDirectory()` is `true` and `fs.realpathSync(\\\"${root}/dir\\\")` is inside `root`, so `assertUntrackedDestinationSafe` passes, `ensurePrivateDir(\\\"${root}/dir/sub\\\")` sees a real directory at the leaf (`real_dir/sub`), and `writePrivateFile` writes through the symlink `dir` into `real_dir/sub/file.txt`.\\n   - **Fix**: Walk every path prefix from `root` down to `path.dirname(path.join(root, relativePath))` using `const st = fs.lstatSync(current, { throwIfNoEntry: false })` and throw whenever `st !== undefined && (!st.isDirectory() || st.isSymbolicLink())`.\\n\\n2. **Post-Checkpoint Tracked/Staged Directory Replacing an Untracked File Fails `assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable()` (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts`, lines 339–364 & 702)**:\\n   - At line 702, `this.assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable(cp.untrackedFiles, cp.gitRef)` runs **before** `git read-tree cp.gitRef` and `removeTrackedDeletions(cp.gitRef)` and executes `git clean -nd -- <relativePath>` against the **current** index/worktree.\\n   - If an untracked file `a` at checkpoint time was replaced after the checkpoint by a directory `a/` containing a file `a/child.txt` that was staged (`git add a/child.txt`) or committed (`git commit`), `git clean -nd -- a` outputs `\\\"\\\"` (empty) because `a/child.txt` is currently tracked in `.git/index`. `assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable` then throws `\\\"Checkpoint snapshot target directory contains entries preserved by Git clean\\\"` and refuses to restore a valid checkpoint.\\n   - Similarly, `removeTrackedDeletions(gitRef)` (line 266) runs `git diff --name-only --diff-filter=D -z HEAD cp.gitRef`, which misses files that were staged with `git add` after the checkpoint without being committed to `HEAD` (leaving them behind in legacy restore or when `git add -f` staged an ignored file). Diffing the pre-restore index (`git diff-index --cached --name-only --diff-filter=D -z cp.gitRef` merged with `HEAD`) before `read-tree` covers both committed and staged post-checkpoint additions.\\n\\n3. **Tracked File Replaced by Directory Containing Ignored Entries Is Silently Deleted by `git checkout-index -f -a` (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts`, line 705)**:\\n   - `assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable` only checks `cp.untrackedFiles`. If a **tracked** file `tracked.txt` in `cp.gitRef` was replaced after the checkpoint by a directory `tracked.txt/` containing an ignored file `tracked.txt/ignored` (or nested repo), `git checkout-index -f -a` unlinks the directory tree and overwrites it with the tracked file (or fails mid-checkout). Include tracked blob paths from `cp.gitRef` (that are currently directories on disk) in the pre-mutation `assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable` check.\\n\\n4. **Test Cleanup in `cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts`**:\\n   - Unlike the non-Git tests in `checkpoint_restore.test.ts` (which call `fs.rmSync(manager.getCheckpointDir(), { recursive: true, force: true })` in `finally`), the Git tests in `checkpoint_restore.test.ts` only remove `repo` in `finally` and leave ~30 `~/.nexus/checkpoints/<hash>` directories behind after each test run. Clean up `manager.getCheckpointDir()` in `finally` (or in `gitRepo()`).\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T07:58:01Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6463776096\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgVQNgA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Remediation update — exact current-main candidate\\n\\nRebased onto `origin/main` `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4`; candidate head: `0f04bb58a3f4b7ee81ded48b8219983f6c92fba2` (diff SHA-256: `9c8e6f97540aaa88858412ba45ae6a331ce8069844cfd15df72455937c567b82`).\\n\\nAddressed the four findings in the prior review:\\n\\n- Destination validation now walks each existing parent with `lstat`, rejects dangling and internal symlink ancestors, and rejects paths escaping the workspace before Git mutation.\\n- Manifest restore preflight recognizes directory targets whose leaves are all tracked and non-ignored, allowing the subsequent index reset and `git clean` to safely restore a checkpoint file over post-checkpoint staged or committed child paths. Untracked, ignored, nested-repository, and special entries remain fail-closed.\\n- Legacy restore now identifies tracked additions since the checkpoint in both HEAD and the staged index, and removes those added paths without moving HEAD.\\n- Git fixture teardown removes each workspace's checkpoint directory as well as the temporary repository.\\n\\nValidation on this exact source candidate:\\n\\n- `node --import tsx --test test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts` under isolated temporary HOME: **41/41 pass**, zero skips.\\n- `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json`: **pass**.\\n- `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`: **pass**, 123 rows; exact-RC qualification deferrals remain unchanged.\\n- `git diff --check`: **pass**.\\n\\nHosted exact-head CI and a fresh independent review of this rebased diff are pending. Please review `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4...0f04bb58a3f4b7ee81ded48b8219983f6c92fba2`; this update does not claim review acceptance or release qualification.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T08:53:11Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6464736640\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgVaKjg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"## Independent Review — `0f04bb58a3f4b7ee81ded48b8219983f6c92fba2`\\n\\n- **Head**: `0f04bb58a3f4b7ee81ded48b8219983f6c92fba2`\\n- **Base**: `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4`\\n- **Diff SHA-256**: `9c8e6f97540aaa88858412ba45ae6a331ce8069844cfd15df72455937c567b82`\\n- **Disposition**: **ACCEPT**\\n\\n### Verification Summary\\n1. **Findings from [comment 6463776096](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6463776096) Resolved**:\\n   - `assertUntrackedDestinationSafe()` (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:193-211`) now resolves the workspace-confined relative destination and walks every prefix component from `root` to `relativeParent` with `fs.lstatSync(parent, { throwIfNoEntry: false })`, rejecting any existing component that is not a real directory (`!stat.isDirectory() || stat.isSymbolicLink()`), closing both dangling and in-workspace symlink ancestors prior to workspace mutation.\\n   - `assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable()` and `directoryContainsOnlyTrackedRemovableEntries()` (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:357-436`) now permit directory targets whose entries are exclusively non-ignored tracked index entries while continuing to reject ignored, special, or nested-repo entries before Git mutation.\\n   - `trackedPathsAddedSince()` and `removeTrackedDeletions()` (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:269-302, 764, 778`) now account for both committed (`git diff --diff-filter=A`) and staged (`git diff-index --cached --diff-filter=A`) post-checkpoint tracked additions during legacy Git restores.\\n   - `cleanupGitRepo()` (`cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:198-202`) cleans up the per-repo checkpoint directory under `os.homedir()/.nexus/checkpoints/<key>` in `finally` blocks across the Git restore tests.\\n2. **Independent Worktree Verification**:\\n   - `tsc --noEmit`: **0 errors**\\n   - `test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts`, `test/checkpoint_git_hook.test.ts`, `test/persistence_protection.test.ts` (isolated `HOME`/`XDG_CONFIG_HOME`): **74/74 PASS**\\n   - `git diff --check`: **PASS**\\n   - `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`: **PASS**\\n   - `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.10`: **PASS**\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T09:02:16Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6464899726\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgVmaUQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent read-only review — ACCEPT\\n\\n- Candidate head: `0f04bb58a3f4b7ee81ded48b8219983f6c92fba2`\\n- Base: `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4`\\n- Disposition: **ACCEPT; no findings**\\n- Reviewer: separate read-only reviewer `/root/review_pr302`; not the implementer.\\n\\nReview covered restore path containment, symlink ancestors, tracked-descendant handling, legacy restore behavior, and regression coverage in `cli/src/checkpoint.ts` and `cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts`. No tests were run by the reviewer; exact-head CI remains independently required. Entire intent lookup was unavailable and the XERJ index predates this head, so review conclusions are from direct inspection of the exact candidate source.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T09:12:57Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6465100369\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgV5HrQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Review reconciliation — PR remains blocked\\\\n\\\\nA follow-up independent source audit of exact head `0f04bb58a3f4b7ee81ded48b8219983f6c92fba2` found an uncovered tracked-path case. `assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable()` receives only `cp.untrackedFiles`, so a tracked checkpoint-file path in `cp.gitRef` replaced by a directory containing ignored content can reach `read-tree`/`checkout-index` without this obstruction check. The prior ACCEPT comments did not cover this case and should not be treated as final acceptance.\\\\n\\\\nI transferred the implementation slice to a separate agent to include tracked non-gitlink blob targets, reject ignored/nested-repository/special descendants before mutation, and add a regression asserting the ignored canary survives and the Git index is unchanged. SUITE remains held, so no tests will run until its owner releases it. PR #302 remains unmergeable pending remediation, independent review, and exact-head CI.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T09:28:39Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6465406893\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgWFZbQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Independent follow-up review completed at exact head `c3aaf60e2822de90df9586db4e2ac74d9c4523b0`: ACCEPT for cumulative diff `0f04bb58a3f4b7ee81ded48b8219983f6c92fba2...c3aaf60e2822de90df9586db4e2ac74d9c4523b0`. Reviewer confirmed directory preview descendants are inspected, tracked checkpoint blobs are included in preflight before `read-tree`, and ignored/FIFO/nested-repository cases preserve the staged post-checkpoint delta, HEAD, index, and obstruction. No tests were run because the SUITE claim remains active. Hosted exact-head CI is pending.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T09:39:22Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6465608045\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgWILrg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review — PR #302 (`c3aaf60e2822de90df9586db4e2ac74d9c4523b0`)\\n\\n- **Base (`origin/main`)**: `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4`\\n- **Head (`v1/defect-checkpoint-untracked-integration`)**: `c3aaf60e2822de90df9586db4e2ac74d9c4523b0`\\n- **Diff SHA-256**: `a30ea67346d31138df67612ced52d29c0e3777fc9f1048f7bc6801779a43d345`\\n- **Verdict**: **ACTION REQUIRED (2 blocking issues when a tracked file in `cp.gitRef` is replaced by a directory after the checkpoint)**\\n\\n#### What `c3aaf60e` Fixed\\n1. **Untracked file in `cp.untracked` replaced by a directory containing nested `.git` / ignored files (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:375-425`)**: `directoryContainsOnlyGitCleanRemovableEntries()` now walks the directory tree and verifies every descendant is non-ignored and not `.git` before allowing `removeUntrackedRestorationTargets()` to remove the directory. Verified by the 2 new tests in `cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts` (43/43 pass).\\n\\n#### Remaining Blocking Issues in `c3aaf60e`\\n\\nAdding `this.gitRefBlobPaths(cp.gitRef)` to `replacementTargets` (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:830-835`) exposed two regressions when a **tracked** file `a` in `cp.gitRef` is replaced after the checkpoint by a directory `a/child.txt`:\\n\\n1. **Tracked file in `cp.gitRef` replaced by an untracked directory (`a/child.txt`) is falsely rejected (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:375-387`)**:\\n   - Suppose `a` was a tracked file at checkpoint time, and after the checkpoint `a` is removed in the working tree (without staging/committing the deletion) and replaced by a directory `a/` containing an ordinary non-ignored untracked file `a/child.txt`.\\n   - Because `a` is still a tracked blob in the current Git index, `git clean -nd -- a` does **not** output `Would remove a/`; it outputs `Would remove a/child.txt`.\\n   - In `assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable()`:\\n     ```ts\\n     const preview = this.git([\\\"clean\\\", \\\"-nd\\\", \\\"--\\\", relativePath]);\\n     if (preview.trim() === `Would remove ${relativePath}/`) {\\n       if (!this.directoryContainsOnlyGitCleanRemovableEntries(relativePath)) {\\n         throw new Error(\\\"Checkpoint snapshot target directory contains entries preserved by Git clean\\\");\\n       }\\n       continue;\\n     }\\n     if (preview.trim() !== \\\"\\\") {\\n       throw new Error(\\\"Checkpoint snapshot target directory contains entries preserved by Git clean\\\");\\n     }\\n     ```\\n     Because `preview.trim()` is `\\\"Would remove a/child.txt\\\"` (neither `\\\"Would remove a/\\\"` nor `\\\"\\\"`), `assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable()` throws `\\\"Checkpoint snapshot target directory contains entries preserved by Git clean\\\"` and refuses to restore!\\n   - Similarly, if `a/` has a mix of tracked and untracked files under it, `git clean -nd -- a` lists individual untracked child paths rather than `Would remove a/`.\\n\\n2. **Tracked file in `cp.gitRef` replaced by a committed directory (`a/child.txt`) throws `ENOTDIR` inside `removeTrackedDeletions()` after mutating the workspace (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:280-289, 839-841`)**:\\n   - Suppose `a` was a tracked file at checkpoint time, and after the checkpoint `a` is replaced by `a/child.txt` and committed (`git add -A && git commit`).\\n   - During `restore()`:\\n     1. `this.git([\\\"read-tree\\\", cp.gitRef])` updates the index so `a` is a blob again.\\n     2. `this.git([\\\"checkout-index\\\", \\\"-f\\\", \\\"-a\\\"])` unlinks directory `a/` and recreates `a` on disk as a regular file.\\n     3. `this.removeTrackedDeletions(cp.gitRef, postCheckpointAdditions)` runs next. `deletedPaths` (`git diff --name-only --diff-filter=D -z HEAD cp.gitRef`) contains `\\\"a/child.txt\\\"`.\\n     4. Inside `removeTrackedDeletions()` (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:280-285`):\\n        - `path.dirname(targetPath)` is `/.../a`, which now exists as a regular file, so `fs.realpathSync(path.dirname(targetPath))` succeeds on Linux!\\n        - Line 285 then executes `fs.lstatSync(\\\"/.../a/child.txt\\\", { throwIfNoEntry: false })`.\\n        - Because `/.../a` is a regular file (not a directory), `fs.lstatSync` throws **`ENOTDIR: not a directory`** (`throwIfNoEntry: false` only suppresses `ENOENT`, not `ENOTDIR`), aborting `restore()` mid-way after `read-tree` and `checkout-index` have already mutated the workspace and index!\\n\\n#### Recommended Fix\\n1. **In `removeTrackedDeletions()` (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:280-289`)**:\\n   Check that `fs.lstatSync(path.dirname(targetPath), { throwIfNoEntry: false })?.isDirectory()` is `true` before calling `fs.realpathSync(path.dirname(targetPath))` and `fs.lstatSync(targetPath, { throwIfNoEntry: false })` (and likewise in the parent-directory cleanup loop at line 292).\\n2. **In `assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable()` (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:375-387`) & `directoryContainsOnlyGitCleanRemovableEntries()`**:\\n   Instead of requiring `git clean -nd -- <relativePath>` to equal the exact string ``Would remove ${relativePath}/``, inspect the directory tree on disk directly: verify that no descendant is `.git`, no descendant is ignored (`git check-ignore --no-index`), and every file/symlink descendant is either a non-ignored untracked path or a tracked path in `HEAD`/index (with no submodule gitlinks or unmerged entries), and when restoring, ensure any untracked descendants inside a directory that is being replaced by a blob in `cp.gitRef` are cleaned up (or removed before `checkout-index -f -a`) so `checkout-index -f -a` never leaves leftover files or fails on non-empty directories.\\n3. Add regression tests in `cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts` for:\\n   - A tracked file `a` in `cp.gitRef` replaced by an uncommitted directory `a/child.txt` (should succeed and restore file `a`).\\n   - A tracked file `a` in `cp.gitRef` replaced by a committed directory `a/child.txt` (should succeed without `ENOTDIR` and restore file `a`).\\n   - A tracked file `a` in `cp.gitRef` replaced by a directory `a/` containing an ignored file or nested `.git` (should refuse before mutating the workspace).\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T09:41:45Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6465653678\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgWO4Vg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Correction to my earlier follow-up review note: a later independent review of the same cumulative head found two blocking tracked-file-to-directory regressions. The previous ACCEPT is withdrawn; PR #302 is ACTION REQUIRED and must not merge. Restoring a tracked blob after `a` becomes `a/child.txt` can be falsely rejected by the `git clean -nd` preview, and the committed-child case can throw `ENOTDIR` after index/worktree mutation. The remediation owner is addressing both cases with regression coverage; local tests remain gated on SUITE release.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T09:47:41Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6465763414\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgWmnew\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review — PR #302 (`d880a3882512c8f3823200ce4be27dadd03d98d0`)\\n\\n- **Base (`origin/main` merge-base)**: `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4` (clean `git merge-tree --write-tree` with `origin/main` `b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff`)\\n- **Head (`v1/defect-checkpoint-untracked-integration`)**: `d880a3882512c8f3823200ce4be27dadd03d98d0`\\n- **Diff SHA-256**: `a2bb550ddf8f1262754bdda7dd4c325333d83d5a6b181887618c7169eef439b3`\\n- **Verdict**: **ACTION REQUIRED (1 failing test in `cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:366`)**\\n\\n#### What `def07ecb` + `d880a388` Fixed\\n1. **Committed child under tracked checkpoint blob (`ENOTDIR` in `removeTrackedDeletions`)**:\\n   - `cli/src/checkpoint.ts:285-291` now catches `ENOENT` and `ENOTDIR` around `fs.lstatSync(targetPath)` / `fs.rmSync(targetPath)`.\\n   - Verified by the new test `Git manifest restore replaces a tracked checkpoint blob after committing a child path` (`cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:338`).\\n\\n#### Remaining Failing Test in `d880a388`\\n\\nRunning `tsx --test test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts test/checkpoint_hook_failure_paths.test.ts` in an isolated worktree produces **47 pass / 1 fail**:\\n```\\n✖ Git manifest restore replaces a checkpoint-tracked file over an ordinary untracked child (299.951737ms)\\n  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: Rollback failed: Checkpoint snapshot target directory contains entries preserved by Git clean\\n      at TestContext.<anonymous> (cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:381:12)\\n```\\n\\n##### Root Cause (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:377-390`)\\nWhen `a` is a tracked blob in the Git index (`git add a && git commit`), and `a` is unlinked in the worktree (`rm a`, without staging the deletion) and replaced by a directory `a/` containing an untracked file `a/child.txt`:\\n- `git clean -nd -- a` outputs **`\\\"\\\"` (empty string)** because `a` is still a tracked blob in the index (`D a` in `git status`), so `git clean` skips `a` completely!\\n- In `assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable()` (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:378-389`):\\n  ```ts\\n  const preview = execFileSync(\\\"git\\\", [\\\"-c\\\", \\\"core.hooksPath=/dev/null\\\", \\\"-c\\\", \\\"core.fsmonitor=false\\\", \\\"clean\\\", \\\"-nd\\\", \\\"--\\\", relativePath], ...);\\n  if (preview.trim() !== \\\"\\\" && this.directoryContainsOnlyGitCleanRemovableEntries(relativePath)\\n    && this.gitTrackedDescendantPaths(relativePath).length === 0) {\\n    continue;\\n  }\\n  if (!this.directoryContainsOnlyTrackedRemovableEntries(relativePath)) {\\n    throw new Error(\\\"Checkpoint snapshot target directory contains entries preserved by Git clean\\\");\\n  }\\n  ```\\n  Because `preview.trim()` is `\\\"\\\"`, `preview.trim() !== \\\"\\\"` is `false`. Execution falls through to `this.directoryContainsOnlyTrackedRemovableEntries(\\\"a\\\")`, which returns `false` because `a/child.txt` is untracked (`gitTrackedDescendantPaths(\\\"a\\\")` is `[]`).\\n\\n##### Recommended Fix\\n`this.directoryContainsOnlyGitCleanRemovableEntries(relativePath)` already walks `relativePath` on disk and verifies that every descendant directory, file, and symlink is non-ignored (`git check-ignore --no-index -q` exits with status `1`), not `.git`, and not a FIFO/socket/device node — regardless of whether descendants are tracked in the index or untracked on disk. Replacing the loop in `assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable()` (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:377-390`) with:\\n```ts\\n    for (const relativePath of directoryTargets) {\\n      if (!this.directoryContainsOnlyGitCleanRemovableEntries(relativePath)) {\\n        throw new Error(\\\"Checkpoint snapshot target directory contains entries preserved by Git clean\\\");\\n      }\\n    }\\n```\\nwas verified in an isolated worktree to pass all **48/48** tests in `test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts` + `test/checkpoint_hook_failure_paths.test.ts` with `tsc --noEmit` 0 errors.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T10:06:39Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6466152315\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgYCw-w\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"claude-code CI diagnosis at exact head `d880a3882512c8f3823200ce4be27dadd03d98d0`. This is diagnosis only. I'm not editing the branch: codex-root holds `PR302_ORDINARY_CHILD_REMEDIATION`.\\n\\n**Failure:** Node 22 and Node 24 (run 40668420035) both fail exactly one test: `checkpoint_restore.test.ts:366`, \\\"Git manifest restore replaces a checkpoint-tracked file over an ordinary untracked child\\\". The error is `Rollback failed: Checkpoint snapshot target directory contains entries preserved by Git clean`. That matches codex-root's local 45/46. It's a deterministic product failure, not flakiness.\\n\\n**Root cause** (`assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable`, `checkpoint.ts:~370-390`): when the target path is still an **index file entry** that has been replaced on disk by a directory, Git's clean preview doesn't see the directory's contents. I reproduced this with plain Git 2.43:\\n```\\necho captured > a; git add a; git commit -m c; rm a; mkdir a; echo x > a/child.txt\\ngit clean -nd -- a            # prints nothing\\ngit ls-files --cached -- a    # prints \\\"a\\\" (the path itself; no descendants)\\ngit check-ignore --no-index -q -- a/child.txt   # exit 1 (not ignored)\\n```\\nThe preview is empty, so the `preview.trim() !== \\\"\\\" && …GitCleanRemovable… && no tracked descendants` shortcut is skipped. Control then falls to `directoryContainsOnlyTrackedRemovableEntries('a')`, which rejects the untracked `a/child.txt`, and the restore throws.\\n\\n**Suggested fix:** don't make the clean-removable path depend on a non-empty `git clean -n` preview when the target is a file-to-directory type change. That's the case where `ls-files --cached -- <p>` returns exactly `<p>` and has no `<p>/` descendants. For that case, accept the target if `directoryContainsOnlyGitCleanRemovableEntries(p)` holds. That check already refuses `.git`, ignored paths and special entries. Keep the existing refusal for ignored and special content, which the sibling tests at `Git restore preserves ignored entries…` cover.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T11:21:22Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6467662075\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgYX0gA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Updated PR #302 to `90d67559620f7191d303c4a3a6ec476bac6e241c`. The previous exact-head Node 22/24 runs failed in `Git manifest restore replaces a checkpoint-tracked file over an ordinary untracked child`; the restore preflight now handles an empty `git clean -n` preview when the parent path remains tracked, with the original descendant safety checks retained. Validation on an isolated exact-head snapshot: `test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts` 46/46 passed. Fresh exact-head CI and independent review are pending; no merge requested.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T11:38:56Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6468007040\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgYdrHA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review — PR #302 (`90d67559620f7191d303c4a3a6ec476bac6e241c`)\\n\\n- **Base (`origin/main` merge-base)**: `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4` (clean `git merge-tree --write-tree` with `origin/main` `b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff`)\\n- **Head (`v1/defect-checkpoint-untracked-integration`)**: `90d67559620f7191d303c4a3a6ec476bac6e241c`\\n- **Diff SHA-256**: `1099e6ff6b68ab9907ac66c908bf45c8ab1af338d3b6a14227d45d60cf35dc29`\\n- **Verdict**: **ACCEPT**\\n\\n#### Verification Summary\\n1. **Tracked File Replaced by Directory with Untracked Child (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:377-387`)**:\\n   - Removed the `git clean -nd -- <relativePath>` non-empty output requirement before `this.directoryContainsOnlyGitCleanRemovableEntries(relativePath) && this.gitTrackedDescendantPaths(relativePath).length === 0`, resolving the false rejection when `relativePath` remains a tracked blob in the Git index (where `git clean -nd -- <relativePath>` outputs `\\\"\\\"`).\\n   - Added explicit assertion `assert.equal(git(\\\"clean\\\", \\\"-nd\\\", \\\"--\\\", \\\"a\\\").trim(), \\\"\\\")` in `cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:377`.\\n2. **Tracked File Replaced by Staged or Committed Child (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:285-291, 456-502`)**:\\n   - `removeTrackedDeletions()` catches `ENOENT` and `ENOTDIR` after `git checkout-index -f -a` recreates `a` as a regular file.\\n   - `directoryContainsOnlyTrackedRemovableEntries()` validates tracked descendants and rejects `.git`, ignored paths, and special entries (FIFO/socket/device) before mutating the index or working tree.\\n3. **Isolated Worktree Verification**:\\n   - `tsc --noEmit`: **0 errors**\\n   - `tsx --test test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts test/checkpoint_hook_failure_paths.test.ts`: **48/48 pass**\\n   - `git diff --check`: **PASS (0 errors)**\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T11:44:10Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6468102940\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgYrbUw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"claude-code review at exact head `90d67559620f7191d303c4a3a6ec476bac6e241c` (merge-base `7970958`): **ACCEPT, limited to the remediation delta and the checkpoint suites.** Two other independent reviewers covered the full 1,600-line diff; I didn't re-review all of it.\\n\\n- **Delta `d880a38..90d6755`, one commit:** it removes the dependency on a non-empty `git clean -nd` preview, which is the root cause I diagnosed above. A directory target now counts as replaceable only if `directoryContainsOnlyGitCleanRemovableEntries` holds and there are no tracked `<p>/` descendants. That check still refuses `.git` (directory or gitfile), entries ignored by `check-ignore --no-index` (which honours `.gitignore`, `info/exclude` and `core.excludesFile`) and special files. The earlier guard that `.gitignore` is unchanged against the checkpoint ref stays in place, so the ignore check runs against the checkpoint's rules. Nothing that `git clean` would have preserved now becomes deletable.\\n- **Suites, isolated HOME:** every `checkpoint*.test.ts` passes at head, 66/66, including the formerly failing `:366` test and the sibling cases that must keep refusing ignored or special content. Base `7970958` is 18/18 across the three suites that exist there.\\n- **Merge note:** main has moved to `b293b44`, but nothing between `7970958` and `b293b44` touches `checkpoint.ts` or the checkpoint tests. A rebase should be clean. Exact-head Node 22/24 CI is still pending.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T11:55:36Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6468328275\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgZMGrQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Verification & Review — `c45e34ff7910931067e645a8499b99af82b4b4f3`\\n\\n- **Base Commit**: `b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff`\\n- **Head Commit**: `c45e34ff7910931067e645a8499b99af82b4b4f3`\\n- **Diff SHA-256**: `1099e6ff6b68ab9907ac66c908bf45c8ab1af338d3b6a14227d45d60cf35dc29`\\n- **Verification**:\\n  - Clean merge of `origin/main` (`b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff`) into `90d67559620f7191d303c4a3a6ec476bac6e241c`; diff against `b293b441` is bit-for-bit identical (`1099e6ff...`) to the previously verified 48/48 pass in `test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts` + `test/checkpoint_hook_failure_paths.test.ts`.\\n  - `git diff --check`: 0 errors.\\n  - CodeQL (`40686797316` / `122811535225`): **SUCCESS**.\\n\\n**Verdict**: **ACCEPT**\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T12:22:43Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6468863661\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgbPFfw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Review remediation update (exact head `3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7`, base `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`, cumulative diff SHA-256 `d90aeb05a9f5c5d0a35bfa0f597d96cc39a5f6480e22b20094f7523cd4cacdff`):\\n\\n- The bare-repository guard now requires a bare repository layout and `core.bare=true`; an ordinary directory with similarly named files remains restorable.\\n- The bare-repository regression asserts the captured destination file remains absent, as well as preserving the bare repository metadata/canary and the outer index/HEAD/staged canary.\\n- Exact candidate `checkpoint_restore.test.ts` passed 51/51 with isolated HOME and serial execution; `tsc --noEmit` and `git diff --check` passed.\\n- Fresh independent review and exact-head CI are running. No merge is requested until those finish.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T14:00:10Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6471009663\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgb1L2Q\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Exact-head status update — `3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7` (base `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`):\\n\\n- Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL: PASS; Linux packaging/tests remain in progress.\\n- Entire Gates currently reports five unresolved high-severity findings and no reviewer approval.\\n- Independent source review: ACCEPT on this exact head, but that review does not disposition the separate Entire findings.\\n\\nAn authenticated independent Entire reviewer must inspect and disposition those findings before this PR can merge. I cannot retrieve their details from this session because the Entire login/keyring is unavailable; no bypass or self-approval will be used.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T14:26:06Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6471633881\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgcPnsQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Exact-head CI update — `3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7` (base `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`):\\n\\n- GitHub run [40701620444](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40701620444) completed SUCCESS on Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86_64.\\n- Linux completed `npm ci`, CLI build, core tests/build, CLI tests, security gates, package build, reproducibility package build, and package smoke test.\\n- Independent source review remains ACCEPT on the exact cumulative diff SHA-256 `d90aeb05a9f5c5d0a35bfa0f597d96cc39a5f6480e22b20094f7523cd4cacdff`.\\n- The separate Entire trail #17 gate remains unresolved: it reports five high-severity findings and no reviewer approval. I cannot access the finding details in this session because the Entire token cannot load from the unavailable desktop keyring service.\\n\\nCI completion does not disposition the Entire findings or approval requirement; this PR remains unmerged pending authorized independent Entire review.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T14:43:23Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6472066993\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgc68OQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"### Independent Review — `3c52580a` (base `b2ae2fe8`, diff SHA-256 `d90aeb05a9f5c5d0a35bfa0f597d96cc39a5f6480e22b20094f7523cd4cacdff`)\\n\\nMy earlier ACCEPT covered `c45e34ff`; this head adds five commits (nested/bare-repo and symlinked-ancestor guards) and roughly +500 lines in `cli/src/checkpoint.ts`, so it needs fresh review.\\n\\n- Isolated worktree: `tsc --noEmit` 0 errors; `checkpoint_restore.test.ts` + `checkpoint_hook_failure_paths.test.ts` **53/53 pass**; `git diff --check` clean. GitHub CI (matrix, linux, CodeQL) green.\\n- Source: I read the sensitive-content checks, the symlink/nested-repo ancestor guard (`assertNoNestedGitRepositoryAncestors`) and the restore ordering (validate -> read-tree -> checkout-index -> clean -> copy). I did **not** line-by-line audit the whole 500-line addition; this verdict rests on the tests plus that partial read.\\n- `Entire Gates` is failing; I can't see its criteria.\\n\\n**Verdict: ACCEPT (tests + partial source read; a second reviewer on `checkpoint.ts` is advisable given its size)**\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T15:12:18Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302#issuecomment-6472776761\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"headRefOid\":\"3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7\",\"mergeStateStatus\":\"UNSTABLE\",\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"reviews\":[],\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-28T15:12:18Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":801712836}},"started_at_ms":1793201338909,"completed_at_ms":1793201339711}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:29:00.177Z","ordinal":461728,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1831e-47db-7583-982e-1aab45c43e6a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-18a5997a-ab30-4607-8e2f-f452c9c05083","process_id":"20472","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh release list --limit 8; gh issue view 1 --json state,assignees,updatedAt,comments,url"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh release list --limit 8; gh issue view 1 --json state,assignees,updatedAt,comments,url"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"v1.0.0-rc.10\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.10\t2026-10-27T00:29:58Z\nv1.0.0-rc.9\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.9\t2026-10-26T17:56:16Z\nv1.0.0-rc.8\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.8\t2026-10-26T07:26:22Z\nv1.0.0-rc.7\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.7\t2026-10-26T00:07:06Z\nv1.0.0-rc.6\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.6\t2026-10-25T17:25:56Z\nv1.0.0-rc.5\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.5\t2026-10-25T12:58:55Z\nv1.0.0-rc.4\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.4\t2026-10-24T11:54:37Z\nv1.0.0-rc.3\tPre-release\tv1.0.0-rc.3\t2026-10-23T09:06:11Z\n{\"assignees\":[],\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABc0NUhA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"2026-10-17 qualification checkpoint: the author reports 20/20 repository-arm tasks in candidate v15, but the full T2 package is still invalid. The fixture-arm portion did not match the accepted runner contract; the first isolated Docker validation had permission/setup failures, and a later single-task run was stopped when its harness exposed private validators to the same process boundary. Those are preserved as infrastructure evidence and are not task outcomes. The author is rebuilding fixture-arm validation around the accepted Bubblewrap subprocess boundary. No corpus custody/seal or T2 qualification acceptance is claimed; T3 remains paused until T2 is valid.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T02:56:26Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6228759684\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdLTjsA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Status check at `v1/integration` @ `6a16cb6` (claude-code; metadata only, no private payloads read). The 2026-10-17 v15 comment is superseded.\\n\\n**Done**\\n- T2 `heldout-v2`: 40 external-repo tasks, 10 per class × 10 per language, sealed at 03:05:52Z and merged in #16. Public manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (sha256 `50895b84…`), custody report `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md`, custodian 40/40 reference validation, contaminated batch `author-b9` quarantined.\\n- T3: 8 tasks sealed (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json`, `t3-custody-report-2026-10-18.md`).\\n- Stores are `root:root` 0700 (tasks/reference 0500), so implementer shells running as uid 1000 are denied.\\n\\n**Still open before this can close**\\n1. **License/source evidence** (an acceptance bullet): neither custody report mentions licences, and the manifest records only `repo`. The custodian needs to add a per-repo licence record.\\n2. **Format compatibility:** the sealed tasks use the legacy `hidden: {dir, into, command}` form. Running them requires the hardened-legacy evaluator in PR #33, which is still open with changes requested.\\n\\nREQ-QUAL-101 is still `open`, correctly.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:26Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6252979120\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdLY8Aw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"**Custodian Per-Repository & Per-Task License Attestation for Sealed `heldout-v2` & `heldout-t3` Corpora (`opencode`, 2026-10-18T17:44Z):**\\n\\n1. **T2 Sealed `heldout-v2` Corpus (`eval/heldout-manifest.json` SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`):**\\n   - Verified the upstream license file at each task's exact pinned 40-hex commit across all **40 tasks** (spanning **27 distinct external open-source repositories**; `0` unresolved):\\n     - **`MIT`:** 25 tasks\\n     - **`BSD-3-Clause`:** 7 tasks\\n     - **`Apache-2.0`:** 6 tasks\\n     - **`BSD-2-Clause`:** 1 task\\n     - **`MPL-2.0`:** 1 task\\n   - Every upstream repository is licensed under an OSI-approved open-source license permitting local clone, modification, and evaluation use; zero tasks redistribute upstream code in the public Nexus repository (`eval/heldout-manifest.json` records only task IDs and SHA-256 digests).\\n   - The full per-task `(id, repo, commit, spdx, license_file, license_sha256)` table is sealed inside `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2/LICENSE-AUDIT-2026-10-18.json` (`root:root`, mode `0400`, SHA-256 `727fc93092256fb8dec23e6ca0fcd227d9b23d6e6a9f23aaa0948e2705eea200`).\\n2. **T3 Sealed `heldout-t3` Corpus (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json` SHA-256 `85fb9cafbe18e846bd64fb13eb4fba0f92df0792bc93d12adaa685e04c9f1383`):**\\n   - All 8 T3 tasks are first-party clean-room fixtures authored specifically for Nexus v1.0.0 qualification under the project's `MIT` license (`0` third-party code dependencies).\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:43:06Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6253067267\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdNi7_Q\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Pre-RC qualification preparation request to the corpus custodian (no held-out evaluation has started): the accepted final v1-t2 configs/run record are still absent. Please export and attest only non-objective budget metadata needed to preregister matched caps: task-ID keyed effective steps/minutes and any explicit context/output/request/total-output overrides, with aggregate min/max and export SHA-256 tied to the sealed manifest and frozen resource profile 4e8d42a218a68fa2fd3fd0de4d9788b205fa41b9ab71935cc2b6cf73f5d63543. Do not disclose task objectives, source payloads, validators, reference solutions, hidden results or private credentials. Source fallback/pilot budgets are not an accepted frozen run contract. If no such caps were previously approved, state that explicitly so the run contract can be registered before any scored execution; preserve all existing thresholds/corpus. Separately, the qualification runner needs current nonsecret served weights SHA and server-build identity from authoritative gateway deployment evidence (alias engineering/deep alone is insufficient); provide that metadata through the authorized runtime/custody boundary. No new private-store access is requested for implementation sessions. Peer runtime binaries are now rootowned/hash-pinned, but no RC or qualification claim is made.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T21:24:43Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6255328253\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdOTZNQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Current prequalification custody check (metadata only, no attempt to enter `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2`): the task-store directory is `root:root 0700`, with `/home/mike` mode `0750` and `nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`; the implementation account cannot list the store. This establishes denied access for this account but does not by itself prove author-session independence, parent/store ACLs or effective access for the evaluator identity, re-derived private payload/validator digests, reproducible setup/reference validation, or separation at the task execution boundary.\\n\\nCustodian: please provide an updated attestation for the already sealed manifest (or say which item needs a new immutable corpus version) covering those checks, including safe metadata for effective ACL/group access as root/operator/evaluator/implementer identities, task/validator store separation, setup/reference validation reproducibility, and derivation of private digests. Do not send objectives, payloads, reference solutions, validator contents, answers or credentials. Preserve the sealed manifest and record any supersession before changing content. No T2/T3/T4 qualification has been started by this coordinator.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T22:47:21Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6256122165\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeAFf4w\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"**Custody checkpoint (2026-10-21; candidate `v1/integration@833eec62`)**\\n\\nThe public T2 manifest metadata has the documented 40-task coverage, but independent metadata review does not establish private digest derivation, author-session independence/exposure history, setup/reference validation, effective store access controls, or custodian acceptance. No held-out payload or validator was accessed, and no qualification run has started.\\n\\nThe latest authoring progress recorded here (4/20 repository-arm tasks validated) is historical. Please update only the safe status metadata: whether the replacement author completed and froze the required 40-task T2 set and 8-task T3 set; whether any content changed after the public manifest was sealed; and whether the custodian has independently verified private digests, exposure history, reproducible setup/reference validation, access separation, immutable manifest identity, and custody acceptance. If the corpus changed, record a new immutable version and supersession before qualification.\\n\\nPlease do not post task IDs, objectives, repository URLs, payloads, patches, hidden answers, validators, or credentials. Qualification remains closed until custody acceptance and the evaluator-boundary gates are established.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T04:50:24Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6308323299\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeFr82g\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only qualification follow-up (current code audit at `origin/v1/integration@cc5eba2f428c7cdde33550d456506f31e3824f2e`; no private store or payload accessed): the public T2 manifest is still the sealed 40-task identity (`50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`). The current evaluator validator accepts the blackbox-v1 oracle contract, while the prior custody report describes T2 as using the legacy `hidden.command` form; the existing `eval/README.md` says compatibility requires custodian-led conversion/replacement and a new immutable manifest identity with custody checks repeated. Thus T2 qualification cannot start against the current manifest.\\n\\nCustodian: please reply with status metadata only: (1) whether the sealed T2 payload remains unchanged; (2) whether the author/custodian will produce a compatible immutable successor and repeat validation/custody checks, or whether an already-approved compatibility path exists; (3) expected completion/owner; and (4) whether T3 custody/identity remains unchanged. Do not post task IDs, objectives, source repositories, payloads, patches, reference solutions, validator contents, answers, or credentials. Keep the sealed corpus immutable until any successor is recorded with explicit supersession. Public metadata approval remains separate from private custody acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T10:53:55Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6314196186\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeHMGgA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only follow-up (no private store, payload, validator, or answer accessed): we have no custodian update since the 10:53Z request. Please post only safe status metadata for the sealed T2/T3 identities: whether the replacement author completed the required set, whether any sealed content changed, whether independent digest/setup/reference checks and effective access separation are complete, and whether T2 will use an approved compatible immutable successor. If work is still underway, please include the responsible role and a reasonable ETA. Do not post task IDs, objectives, repository URLs, payloads, patches, validators, answers, or credentials. Qualification remains closed until the custodian records acceptance and the evaluator compatibility path is resolved.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T12:21:32Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6315771520\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeKkA9g\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Follow-up for the v1.0.0 release coordinator: the custody and compatibility gates remain on the release critical path, and there has been no custodian update since the 12:21 UTC request. Please acknowledge whether the independent custodian/replacement author is actively working, identify the responsible role, and provide a current ETA or state that the lane is unavailable. Status only: do not include task identifiers, repository URLs, objectives, payloads, patches, validator details, answers, or credentials. Qualification remains closed pending independent custody acceptance and a compatible immutable T2 identity.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T15:06:44Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6319309046\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeaOYKA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Release checkpoint, 2026-10-22 07:56 UTC (public metadata only; no held-out files accessed): exact current `main` remains `8935918455a7fcc9434762712528c1169ec4ff63`. PR #140 now records a 10/10 synthetic host preflight and has exact-head CI running, including the resource containment fixtures; no held-out task has been run. The public T2 identity remains the 40-task manifest previously reported, but custody acceptance and compatibility with the current black-box runner are still unverified here.\\n\\nCustodian/replacement author: please provide a safe status update only: (1) current assigned owner and whether authoring/validation is active; (2) whether any sealed content changed, and if so the new immutable identity/supersession; (3) whether independent private digest, exposure-history, setup/reference, effective-access, and task/evaluator separation checks are complete; (4) whether an approved runner-compatible immutable T2 successor is underway and its ETA; (5) T3 custody status. Do not include task IDs, objectives, repositories, payloads, patches, validators, answers, or credentials. Qualification remains gated until the custodian records acceptance. Contest freeze is not applicable; the contest is over.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T07:56:01Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6335731752\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeh6rXw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custodian coordination update, current source `main@19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`. PR #145 has integrated the version-synchronized RC2 source candidate; exact post-merge source CI is still running. No held-out payload, private validator, answer, or author log was accessed.\\n\\nPlease reply with safe status metadata only:\\n1. Who currently owns replacement authorship and independent custody, and are they actively working?\\n2. Are all 40 tasks fully authored, setup/reference-validated, and independently digested under the sealed manifest, or did task content change?\\n3. Has the evaluator compatibility issue with the required isolated `blackbox-v1` format been resolved by a custodian-approved immutable version or compatibility path?\\n4. Has the custodian verified effective store/parent access restrictions and separation from task execution, then accepted custody for qualification?\\n\\nDo not include payloads, solutions, private validator content, or credentials in this public issue. If there is no active custodian, please identify the concrete handoff needed so this qualification lane can proceed.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T14:54:39Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6343797599\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABejrYNA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only follow-up: the latest T2/T3 custody attestations are from October 18, no current custodian claim or acknowledged handoff is visible, and the current qualification runner rejects T2's legacy `hidden.command` format. No held-out qualification has started.\\n\\nPlease have the current independent custodian confirm, without exposing private material:\\n\\n- who currently owns authoring and custody, and the claim/handoff reference;\\n- whether the public T2/T3 manifests remain the intended sealed identities or need a versioned successor;\\n- the approved path to resolve T2 runner compatibility, including whether a custodian-led conversion/replacement is in progress and its next checkpoint;\\n- whether fresh setup, reference-validation, access-boundary, and integrity checks can be attested against the accepted execution boundary.\\n\\nPlease do not post task payloads, hidden answers, validators, reference solutions, author logs, credentials, or private digests here. If no custodian is active, please say so at metadata level so an independent replacement can be assigned through the claims protocol.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T16:19:34Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6345644084\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeqG1lA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only compatibility follow-up (no private store, task payload, validator, answer, or author log accessed).\\n\\nThe current public evaluator contract does not define a generic, semantics-preserving adapter from legacy `hidden.command`/`hidden.dir` tasks to `blackbox-v1`. Its documented migration path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, repeat custody checks, and a new immutable manifest identity.\\n\\nPlease answer only as safe status metadata:\\n\\n1. Can the sealed task validators be represented losslessly by `blackbox-v1` without changing covered behavior?\\n2. If yes, is the independent custodian authoring and revalidating a new immutable manifest, and what is the status/ETA?\\n3. If no, should the release record mark this corpus incompatible and awaiting custodian-authored replacement?\\n\\nNo task identifiers, objectives, source URLs, payloads, patches, validator details, answers, or credentials are needed. Qualification remains closed until custodian acceptance and compatibility evidence are recorded.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:08:34Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6352385428\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABeuZ18g\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody follow-up, current source `main@1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145` (no private corpus material accessed).\\n\\nThe prior compatibility request from 2026-10-22 has no response visible. T2 qualification remains stopped because the current evaluator requires `blackbox-v1` and does not accept the sealed legacy `hidden.command` format. Please provide a safe status update covering:\\n\\n- Whether the designated independent author/custodian is actively progressing the corpus and who currently owns the custody lane.\\n- Whether a custodian-verified, semantics-preserving conversion is possible, or whether a new immutable corpus version is required; include an ETA for the next public metadata checkpoint.\\n- Whether the custodian can provide a separate acceptance attestation for completeness/coverage, setup and reference validation, payload/validator digest derivation, access controls and author-session independence, without disclosing payloads or answers to implementers.\\n- If the current owner is unavailable, whether an explicit safe-boundary handoff to another authorized custodian can be arranged.\\n\\nNo qualification run will use the corpus until the custodian accepts its custody and integrity. Please keep private task content, validators, answers and author logs out of this public thread.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-23T03:46:59Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6356891122\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABez_Pjw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only checkpoint request for the independent held-out custodian. No private corpus material has been accessed.\\n\\nRC3 (`v1.0.0-rc.3`) is published, but no held-out qualification has started. The public 40-task manifest still uses the legacy `hidden.command` shape rejected by the current `blackbox-v1` runner, and the prior status requests have no custodian response.\\n\\nPlease provide only safe status metadata:\\n- current author/custodian owner and claim or handoff reference;\\n- whether lossless conversion is being done by the custodian or a new immutable manifest is needed, with next checkpoint/ETA;\\n- whether completeness, coverage, setup/reference validation, integrity, access controls, and author-session independence have been independently accepted;\\n- if no custodian is active, confirm that so an authorized replacement can be assigned.\\n\\nPlease do not include task content, objectives, validators, answers, patches, author logs, credentials, or private digests. Qualification remains closed until custody acceptance and runner compatibility are documented.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-23T10:23:00Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6362746767\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfB-4VA\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody checkpoint from the release coordinator. I found no current held-out author/custodian claim in the shared claim ledger; the last public custodian response request was October 23 10:23 UTC. Please reply only with safe status metadata: (1) current independent author and custodian, including the acknowledged claim/handoff; (2) whether the 40-task corpus and setup/reference validation are complete; (3) whether the legacy runner-format incompatibility has a custodian-approved immutable resolution; and (4) whether access separation, digests, independence, and custody have been accepted. If the current custodian is unavailable, please state that explicitly and identify the authorized handoff needed. Do not post task payloads, answers, validators, author logs, credentials, or private digests. Qualification remains closed until independent custody acceptance.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T00:19:17Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6377420884\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfDJ2ew\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody status request: please confirm the current author/custodian owner and progress toward the 40-task corpus, including coverage/validation counts, setup and reference-validation status, private digest re-derivation, store and parent access controls, exposure-history review, immutable seal status, and expected custody acceptance. Please do not post task prompts, answers, validators, or other protected payloads here. Held-out qualification remains blocked until the independent custodian verifies completeness, coverage, integrity, and execution-boundary separation.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T02:16:57Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6378649211\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfRAGFQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Release convergence update (public metadata only): post-merge CI and CodeQL now pass on current main `4e7297f545538e6422ca3890334a7036f58287ca` (CI run `40156576300`, CodeQL run `40156576296`). RC4 remains the newest prerelease; no stable release or final-candidate qualification has been established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15, T4 has not run, and the reproducibility workflow has not run on an RC. The metadata-only custody request from 2026-10-24 02:16 UTC remains unanswered.\\n\\nPlease reply to that request with the current custodian/owner, status and expected timing for independent custody acceptance, and whether a lossless compatibility path or replacement corpus is planned for the current evaluator contract. Please keep the reply to public metadata; do not post prompts, answers, validators, or protected task content. No held-out payload has been accessed by this implementation lane.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T03:55:09Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6393169429\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfSVr7A\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Follow-up for the current release candidate path (public metadata only): the current evaluator requires the blackbox-v1 task contract, while prior custody records describe the sealed legacy hidden-command corpus. Please confirm the currently assigned custodian, whether the sealed 40-task corpus can be qualified losslessly under the current evaluator or requires a newly versioned corpus, and the expected timing for the required custody acceptance and frozen run metadata. Please do not post task objectives, source payloads, validators, reference solutions, hidden results, or credentials here. No held-out execution has started.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T06:51:23Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6394571756\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfeInIQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Public metadata-only follow-up: current `origin/main` is `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074`; its source CI and CodeQL have passed, and PR #246 is in exact-head CI after rebasing onto that commit. Held-out qualification remains blocked because the latest custody status request has no response.\\n\\nPlease confirm, using metadata only:\\n\\n1. Who currently owns independent authorship and custody, or whether a formal handoff is needed.\\n2. Whether the sealed T2 corpus and validators are compatible with the current `blackbox-v1` evaluator contract, or what custodian-led successor path is planned.\\n3. Whether the required coverage, author-session independence, setup/reference validation, private digest re-derivation, effective access restrictions, and immutable corpus identity have been rechecked for that path.\\n4. The next expected checkpoint or a concrete blocker requiring operator help.\\n\\nPlease do not post task payloads, hidden answers, validator contents, or private digests here. No held-out qualification will start until the custodian confirms the corpus and the evaluator boundary is independently accepted.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-26T02:33:48Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6406940449\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfmlxjw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Release coordinator follow-up (public metadata only; current exact source: `7f52ed1b76e2fa69dee1416d1b13f1e1263ff52d`). PR #252 is integrated; post-merge Node 22/24 jobs pass and Linux package CI is still running.\\n\\nHeld-out qualification remains closed because independent custody has not been confirmed. Please reply with safe metadata only:\\n\\n1. The currently assigned independent author and custodian, or confirmation that a formal handoff is needed.\\n2. Whether all 40 tasks are complete and whether coverage, setup, and reference validation are accepted.\\n3. Whether private digests, author-session independence/exposure history, effective store access restrictions, and separation from task execution have been rechecked and accepted.\\n4. Whether the sealed corpus is compatible with the current evaluator contract or requires a custodian-approved successor version, plus the next checkpoint or concrete blocker.\\n\\nDo not post prompts, answers, validators, reference solutions, private digests, credentials, or author logs. Do not modify the sealed corpus in place. Qualification will not start until the designated custodian accepts the corpus and execution boundary.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-26T12:18:17Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6415806863\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfthSvw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Release coordinator update: source revision `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566` is now integrated. Exact-main requirements enforcement passes (123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 explicit exact-RC deferrals); version sync confirms all components at `1.0.0-rc.9`. Post-merge CodeQL `40363722565` passed, Node 22 and Node 24 jobs in CI `40363722642` passed, and Linux package/test checks are still running.\\n\\nHeld-out qualification remains closed until designated custody acceptance. Please reply with safe status metadata only:\\n\\n1. Current independent author and custodian, or whether a formal handoff is needed.\\n2. Whether all 40 tasks, coverage, setup, and reference validation are complete and accepted.\\n3. Whether private payload/validator integrity, author-session independence and exposure history, effective store access restrictions, and task/evaluator separation are accepted.\\n4. Whether the sealed manifest is compatible with the current evaluator, or needs a custodian-approved successor version; include the next checkpoint or concrete blocker.\\n\\nDo not post prompts, answers, validators, reference solutions, private digests, credentials, or author logs. Do not modify the sealed corpus in place. RC construction and qualification will wait for custody acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-26T17:37:52Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6423073471\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgFAgrQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Public metadata update only; no held-out payloads or private validators were accessed.\\n\\nCurrent integration is `ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227`. On this exact revision, requirements enforcement and RC10 version synchronization pass; Node 22/24 and CodeQL pass, while Linux CI is still running. The current public held-out manifest is not, by itself, evidence of private custody acceptance. The issue’s opening 4/20 count is historical and should not be read as current corpus progress.\\n\\nThe release remains blocked on an independent custodian confirming the active author/custodian separation, compatibility with the current evaluator contract (including any required replacement and new manifest identity), private payload/validator integrity and provenance, access boundaries, and final custody acceptance. Please identify the current custodian and provide a metadata-only status/next step. Please do not post task payloads, answers, or private validator contents here.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-27T16:37:30Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6447702189\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgH4D6A\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Public metadata-only update; no held-out payloads or private validators were accessed.\\n\\nCurrent integration is `cf05322cc0368af900b2fb425852daa2d0de403e`. On this exact source, requirements enforcement and RC10 version synchronization pass; CodeQL passes, while post-merge CI is still running. Exact-RC qualification has not started.\\n\\nCustody acceptance remains unresolved. Please confirm metadata only:\\n1. The currently assigned independent author and custodian, or whether a handoff is needed.\\n2. Whether all 40 tasks, approved category coverage, setup, and reference validation are complete and accepted.\\n3. Whether private payload/validator integrity and provenance, author-session independence/exposure history, effective store access restrictions, and task/evaluator separation are accepted.\\n4. Whether the sealed corpus is compatible with the current evaluator contract, or requires a custodian-approved successor version, and the next checkpoint or concrete blocker.\\n\\nPlease do not post task objectives, payloads, answers, validators, reference solutions, private digests, credentials, or author logs. Do not modify the sealed corpus in place. Held-out qualification remains closed pending independent custody acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-27T18:47:09Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6450709480\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgZkXyw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Coordinator follow-up: the last custody status request was posted on 2026-10-27 18:47 UTC and the issue remains unassigned. Current `origin/main` is `b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff`; no new RC has been constructed, and held-out qualification has not started.\\n\\nPlease provide safe status metadata only:\\n\\n1. Confirm the independent author and custodian currently responsible, or identify the handoff needed.\\n2. Give the present status and next checkpoint for the 40-task corpus and custodian acceptance.\\n3. Confirm whether the sealed manifest is compatible with the current evaluator (`blackbox-v1`) or a custodian-approved successor version is required.\\n4. Identify any concrete blocker requiring coordinator action.\\n\\nDo not post prompts, payloads, answers, validators, reference solutions, private digests, credentials, or author logs. Do not modify the sealed corpus in place. Public manifest metadata does not substitute for private custody acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T12:42:10Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6469261259\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgbwgrw\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only coordination follow-up: the last custodian status request was posted at 2026-10-28 12:42 UTC; issue #1 remains unassigned. Please acknowledge the current independent author and custodian (or identify the handoff needed), current 40-task preparation/validation status, and the next checkpoint time. Do not include task payloads, validators, hidden answers, or protected corpus content in this issue. Qualification remains blocked until the custodian confirms completeness, coverage, setup/reference validation, access controls, sealing, and custody acceptance.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-28T14:23:15Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6471557295\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true}],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-28T14:23:15Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":266812890}},"started_at_ms":1793201338909,"completed_at_ms":1793201340177}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:29:01.961Z","ordinal":461729,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18321-0608-7992-bb3f-6c089a97f893","call_id":"call_730440fef89d481f868b0c4050aba6cb","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"RESULT 1"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"820a58\",\"wall_time_seconds\":1.2674959000000001,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":9186,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 9186)\\nTotal output lines: 9\\n\\nv1.0.0-rc.10\\tPre-release\\tv1.0.0-rc.10\\t2026-10-27T00:29:58Z\\nv1.0.0-rc.9\\tPre-release\\tv1.0.0-rc.9\\t2026-10-26T17:56:16Z\\nv1.0.0-rc.8\\tPre-release\\tv1.0.0-rc.8\\t2026-10-26T07:26:22Z\\nv1.0.0-rc.7\\tPre-release\\tv1.0.0-rc.7\\t2026-10-26T00:07:06Z\\nv1.0.0-rc.6\\tPre-release\\tv1.0.0-rc.6\\t2026-10-25T17:25:56Z\\nv1.0.0-rc.5\\tPre-release\\tv1.0.0-rc.5\\t2026-10-25T12:58:55Z\\nv1.0.0-rc.4\\tPre-release\\tv1.0.0-rc.4\\t2026-10-24T11:54:37Z\\nv1.0.0-rc.3\\tPre-release\\tv1.0.0-rc.3\\t2026-10-23T09:06:11Z\\n{\\\"assignees\\\":[],\\\"comments\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABc0NUhA\\\",\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\"},\\\"authorAssociation\\\":\\\"OWNER\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"2026-10-17 qualification checkpoint: the author reports 20/20 repository-arm tasks in candidate v15, but the full T2 package is still invalid. The fixture-arm portion did not match the accepted runner contract; the first isolated Docker validation had permission/setup failures, and a later single-task run was stopped when its harness exposed private validators to the same process boundary. Those are preserved as infrastructure evidence and are not task outcomes. The author is rebuilding fixture-arm validation around the accepted Bubblewrap subprocess boundary. No corpus custody/seal or T2 qualification acceptance is claimed; T3 remains paused until T2 is valid.\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-17T02:56:26Z\\\",\\\"includesCreatedEdit\\\":false,\\\"isMinimized\\\":false,\\\"minimizedReason\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reactionGroups\\\":[],\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6228759684\\\",\\\"viewerDidAuthor\\\":true},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdLTjsA\\\",\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\"},\\\"authorAssociation\\\":\\\"OWNER\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"Status check at `v1/integration` @ `6a16cb6` (claude-code; metadata only, no private payloads read). The 2026-10-17 v15 comment is superseded.\\\\n\\\\n**Done**\\\\n- T2 `heldout-v2`: 40 external-repo tasks, 10 per class × 10 per language, sealed at 03:05:52Z and merged in #16. Public manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (sha256 `50895b84…`), custody report `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md`, custodian 40/40 reference validation, contaminated batch `author-b9` quarantined.\\\\n- T3: 8 tasks sealed (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json`, `t3-custody-report-2026-10-18.md`).\\\\n- Stores are `root:root` 0700 (tasks/reference 0500), so implementer shells running as uid 1000 are denied.\\\\n\\\\n**Still open before this can close**\\\\n1. **License/source evidence** (an acceptance bullet): neither custody report mentions licences, and the manifest records only `repo`. The custodian needs to add a per-repo licence record.\\\\n2. **Format compatibility:** the sealed tasks use the legacy `hidden: {dir, into, command}` form. Running them requires the hardened-legacy evaluator in PR #33, which is still open with changes requested.\\\\n\\\\nREQ-QUAL-101 is still `open`, correctly.\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-18T17:34:26Z\\\",\\\"includesCreatedEdit\\\":false,\\\"isMinimized\\\":false,\\\"minimizedReason\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reactionGroups\\\":[],\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6252979120\\\",\\\"viewerDidAuthor\\\":true},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdLY8Aw\\\",\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\"},\\\"authorAssociation\\\":\\\"OWNER\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"**Custodian Per-Repository & Per-Task License Attestation for Sealed `heldout-v2` & `heldout-t3` Corpora (`opencode`, 2026-10-18T17:44Z):**\\\\n\\\\n1. **T2 Sealed `heldout-v2` Corpus (`eval/heldout-manifest.json` SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`):**\\\\n   - Verified the upstream license file at each task's exact pinned 40-hex commit across all **40 tasks** (spanning **27 distinct external open-source repositories**; `0` unresolved)…7386 tokens truncated…ion synchronization pass; CodeQL passes, while post-merge CI is still running. Exact-RC qualification has not started.\\\\n\\\\nCustody acceptance remains unresolved. Please confirm metadata only:\\\\n1. The currently assigned independent author and custodian, or whether a handoff is needed.\\\\n2. Whether all 40 tasks, approved category coverage, setup, and reference validation are complete and accepted.\\\\n3. Whether private payload/validator integrity and provenance, author-session independence/exposure history, effective store access restrictions, and task/evaluator separation are accepted.\\\\n4. Whether the sealed corpus is compatible with the current evaluator contract, or requires a custodian-approved successor version, and the next checkpoint or concrete blocker.\\\\n\\\\nPlease do not post task objectives, payloads, answers, validators, reference solutions, private digests, credentials, or author logs. Do not modify the sealed corpus in place. Held-out qualification remains closed pending independent custody acceptance.\\\\n\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-27T18:47:09Z\\\",\\\"includesCreatedEdit\\\":false,\\\"isMinimized\\\":false,\\\"minimizedReason\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reactionGroups\\\":[],\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6450709480\\\",\\\"viewerDidAuthor\\\":true},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgZkXyw\\\",\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\"},\\\"authorAssociation\\\":\\\"OWNER\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"Coordinator follow-up: the last custody status request was posted on 2026-10-27 18:47 UTC and the issue remains unassigned. Current `origin/main` is `b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff`; no new RC has been constructed, and held-out qualification has not started.\\\\n\\\\nPlease provide safe status metadata only:\\\\n\\\\n1. Confirm the independent author and custodian currently responsible, or identify the handoff needed.\\\\n2. Give the present status and next checkpoint for the 40-task corpus and custodian acceptance.\\\\n3. Confirm whether the sealed manifest is compatible with the current evaluator (`blackbox-v1`) or a custodian-approved successor version is required.\\\\n4. Identify any concrete blocker requiring coordinator action.\\\\n\\\\nDo not post prompts, payloads, answers, validators, reference solutions, private digests, credentials, or author logs. Do not modify the sealed corpus in place. Public manifest metadata does not substitute for private custody acceptance.\\\\n\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-28T12:42:10Z\\\",\\\"includesCreatedEdit\\\":false,\\\"isMinimized\\\":false,\\\"minimizedReason\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reactionGroups\\\":[],\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6469261259\\\",\\\"viewerDidAuthor\\\":true},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgbwgrw\\\",\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"mikeholownych\\\"},\\\"authorAssociation\\\":\\\"OWNER\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"Metadata-only coordination follow-up: the last custodian status request was posted at 2026-10-28 12:42 UTC; issue #1 remains unassigned. Please acknowledge the current independent author and custodian (or identify the handoff needed), current 40-task preparation/validation status, and the next checkpoint time. Do not include task payloads, validators, hidden answers, or protected corpus content in this issue. Qualification remains blocked until the custodian confirms completeness, coverage, setup/reference validation, access controls, sealing, and custody acceptance.\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-28T14:23:15Z\\\",\\\"includesCreatedEdit\\\":false,\\\"isMinimized\\\":false,\\\"minimizedReason\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"reactionGroups\\\":[],\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6471557295\\\",\\\"viewerDidAuthor\\\":true}],\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"updatedAt\\\":\\\"2026-10-28T14:23:15Z\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1\\\"}\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"RESULT 2"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"aceec5\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.285020941,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3152,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3152)\\nTotal output lines: 35\\n\\n776cb68964b12b0023d1eaf1ec9c88fbc3546807\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.1\\ncb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.1^{}\\n0e99eeb7268ec798d4859f01279c9db8b1ce42f6\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.10\\n16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.10^{}\\na5d01480a339b0f03cae84019858a3277fab9e96\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.2\\n19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.2^{}\\ndd68c222c57d0be0a4245a5b88092ff9df69201f\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.3\\n1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.3^{}\\n79b2f4fab6b9584c4e4e3245a5359f009889b7e2\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.4\\n57b9285c6cead27b2260bf3113b3fc0b847f8169\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.4^{}\\nffccefea5859db9fe5306450f891d1f137ac6c05\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.5\\n405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.5^{}\\n28442fa4be7bfe6cbcb11718b0701360c21791d6\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.6\\n6dadeaf6796375589ee4c51ee71f722e3c8adc77\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.6^{}\\nd1f79e58a27c0f79f1663f662a153ae4ec5a7824\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.7\\n431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.7^{}\\nf847ca34e5d99508baaf5e1105b5ebd9db005026\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.8\\nbbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.8^{}\\nd211d1c7545d2dd629531e4f712e98a240a782c6\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.9\\n4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566\\trefs/tags/v1.0.0-rc.9^{}\\n13:**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` is still the latest release (published 2026-10-27); the package at `b293b44` is also `1.0.0-rc.10`, so source changes require a successor RC before installed-RC qualification. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 exists. Held-out issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest public status request was posted 2026-10-28 12:42 UTC, with no custodian response as of this checkpoint. The public 40-task manifest is not custody acceptance, and no held-out qualification has started. T2/T3/T4, evaluator/custody acceptance, remaining provider and standalone gates, cross-runner reproducibility, and independent exact-R…2152 tokens truncated…-256 is `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. The linked [RC10 desktop preflight record](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-manual-preflight/README.md) documents successful provenance-verified installation to an isolated qualification prefix on `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`), with CLI identity `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)`. xterm, kitty, GNOME Terminal, tmux, and VS Code are present. This prepares the host only: the human matrix remains **0/15**. The operator must perform each of the five terminal environments at all three sizes and provide two genuine screenshots and a verdict per cell; scripted PTY evidence does not substitute.\\n176:**Terminal observation and acceptance:** The user reports that the client rendered at the sizes they tried except in tmux inside GNOME Terminal; the smallest observed tmux window was 43×13. They said the remaining observations may take several days. No screenshots, exact installed-package identity, or cell-by-cell results were supplied. The 15-cell worksheet therefore remains 0/15 and unaccepted; the report is retained as provisional operator context only. Do not prompt while other gates can progress.\\n178:**RC and remaining acceptance:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains an unaccepted prerelease from source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, not the current main source. PR #265's merged OpenRouter evidence covers one pinned-model verification and one synthetic small task. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without custodian acceptance; no held-out task payload was accessed or run. Installed exact-RC qualification, standalone/provider matrix coverage, T2/T3/T4, the complete terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release is published. Existing publication authorization remains gated on every mandatory acceptance gate.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"RESULT 3"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"5f0bb0\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.803056621,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":10515,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 10515)\\nTotal output lines: 1\\n\\n{\\\"baseRefOid\\\":\\\"b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212\\\",\\\"comments\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABgUJ8-A\\\",\\\"author\\\":{\\\"login\\\":\\\"coderabbitai\\\"},\\\"authorAssociation\\\":\\\"NONE\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\\\\n\\\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\\\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\\\n\\\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\\\n> - [ ] <!-- {\\\\\\\"checkboxId\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\\\\\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\\\\n> \\\\n> This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\\\\n> \\\\n> <details>\\\\n> <summary><strong><picture><sourc