{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:32:13.109Z","ordinal":461875,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1831e-47db-7583-982e-1aab45c43e6a","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a1831e-47db-7583-982e-1aab45c43e6a","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae21574b728819fa1ff04ef0b3527ce","usage":{"input_tokens":167205,"cached_input_tokens":167040,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":945,"reasoning_output_tokens":839,"total_tokens":168150},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5143896,"cached_input_tokens":5069440,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":21555,"reasoning_output_tokens":14253,"total_tokens":5165451},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8570219602,"cached_input_tokens":8478644224,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24434140,"reasoning_output_tokens":14139661,"total_tokens":8594653742}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:32:14.439Z","ordinal":461876,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1831e-47db-7583-982e-1aab45c43e6a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-423a6a57-00c2-4471-940f-62e93ed8b89e","process_id":"53175","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -C 2 'handoff|release|stale|SUITE|active' /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md | head -90"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -C 2 'handoff|release|stale|SUITE|active' /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md","query":"handoff|release|stale|SUITE|active","path":"CONCURRENCY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"48-| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\n49-| Processes | Kill only PIDs you started, taken from `$!` or `ps -eo pid,args \\| grep -v grep`. **Never `pkill -f` or `killall`.** Long background jobs are stopped through the agent's own task controls. |\n50:| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\n51-| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n52-| Credentials | Agents never read or copy `~/.config/nexus/credentials.json`, `config.env` values, or gateway tokens. The stripped proxy reads the token file itself. |\n--\n54-## 4. Hot files: serialise, do not merge blindly\n55-\n56:These files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n57-\n58-| File | Plans that touch it | Rule |\n--\n86-3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n87-4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\n88:5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n89-6. Preserve unrelated user work: the untracked `nexus-continuity-validation/`, the stashes, and any dirty files you did not create. Never stash, reset, clean or check out over them.\n90-\n--\n94-|---|---|---|\n95-| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n96:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n97-| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n98-| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":30849}},"started_at_ms":1793201534438,"completed_at_ms":1793201534439}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:32:15.701Z","ordinal":461877,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18323-fad4-7e41-a21c-36db2df300bd","call_id":"call_0875d4213c994a66a4c3e5242d6a170e","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"107a53\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000030849,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":737,\"output\":\"48-| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\\n49-| Processes | Kill only PIDs you started, taken from `$!` or `ps -eo pid,args \\\\| grep -v grep`. **Never `pkill -f` or `killall`.** Long background jobs are stopped through the agent's own task controls. |\\n50:| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\\n51-| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\\n52-| Credentials | Agents never read or copy `~/.config/nexus/credentials.json`, `config.env` values, or gateway tokens. The stripped proxy reads the token file itself. |\\n--\\n54-## 4. Hot files: serialise, do not merge blindly\\n55-\\n56:These files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\\n57-\\n58-| File | Plans that touch it | Rule |\\n--\\n86-3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\\n87-4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\\n88:5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\\n89-6. Preserve unrelated user work: the untracked `nexus-continuity-validation/`, the stashes, and any dirty files you did not create. Never stash, reset, clean or check out over them.\\n90-\\n--\\n94-|---|---|---|\\n95-| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\\n96:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\\n97-| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\\n98-| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1831e-47db-7583-982e-1aab45c43e6a","create_time":1793201535.7009916}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
