{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:32:35.218Z","ordinal":461896,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18324-4711-7293-9b12-5003d9b80c9f","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED.** The provided SHA-256 `a1afc80c7e3da4c28980c86d7e936ba9119111a2988740a381f060643fa3b2a7` matches the uncommitted `HEAD`-to-worktree delta. The full cumulative diff from base `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212` to the current worktree hashes to `bc3057de6f18382179eaf0773f50e54decf735a5ee358b0596aeb1c59bbb3505`.\n\nThe current PR heads and CI outcomes match the checkpoint: all four candidates’ Node 22/24, Linux, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks passed; Entire Gates failed, with PR #302’s check reporting five high-severity findings and no reviewer approval. The local-suite paragraph now accurately identifies the missing workspace environment variable as the first failure; the CI fixture setup and current host fixture state also match.\n\nOne factual correction remains at [READINESS.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:7): it says the independent source reviewer recommended a second review of `checkpoint.ts`. My ACCEPT review of exact head `3c52580` made no such recommendation, and I did not run tests. Remove the claim or attribute it to the reviewer who made that recommendation. No tests were run for this review."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1831e-47db-7583-982e-1aab45c43e6a","create_time":1793201555.2179143,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":22011}}
