{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:32:43.274Z","ordinal":461901,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1831e-47db-7583-982e-1aab45c43e6a","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2159aa828819fbaceecd80ba7844f","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The independent reviewer found one attribution issue in the readiness update: the “second review” recommendation came from an owner-authored PR summary, not from that reviewer, and the reviewer did not run tests. I’m correcting the record to separate reviewer disposition from owner-reported test evidence, then I’ll revalidate the exact diff."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793201562686,"completed_at_ms":1793201563274}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:32:43.279Z","ordinal":461902,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2159aa828819fbaceecd80ba7844f","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The independent reviewer found one attribution issue in the readiness update: the “second review” recommendation came from an owner-authored PR summary, not from that reviewer, and the reviewer did not run tests. I’m correcting the record to separate reviewer disposition from owner-reported test evidence, then I’ll revalidate the exact diff.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1831e-47db-7583-982e-1aab45c43e6a","create_time":1793201562.6582599,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae2159aa828819fbaceecd80ba7844f","turn_id":"01a1831e-47db-7583-982e-1aab45c43e6a","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a18324-668e-7652-9a50-9aeebf964659","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":22012}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:32:48.640Z","ordinal":461903,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0db389702a7164cc016ae2159b402c819f8b24336f3a74b99a","status":"completed","call_id":"call_2552bab0cefc4443a0429cf07db9a584","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc-readiness-refresh-20261028/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\\n@@\\n-**Release PRs and exact-head checks:** PRs [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) (`004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f`), [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) (`11dc196fcdd733f8de71dfc95ff70e109d8f4492`), [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) (`3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7`), and [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) (`97f1c6ead710bc059126ba65b37ad1e5fde17666`) are all based on `b2ae2fe`. Exact-head Node 22/24, Linux x86_64, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks passed for these candidates. Their Entire Gates checks are failures, so none is mergeable through the required workflow. PR #302's trail reports five high-severity findings and missing reviewer approval; the independent source reviewer accepted the cumulative diff after tests and a partial source read, and recommended a second review of `checkpoint.ts`. PR #299, #300, and #305 also lack successful Entire approval. No findings were bypassed and no self-approval was recorded.\\n+**Release PRs and exact-head checks:** PRs [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) (`004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f`), [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) (`11dc196fcdd733f8de71dfc95ff70e109d8f4492`), [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) (`3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7`), and [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) (`97f1c6ead710bc059126ba65b37ad1e5fde17666`) are all based on `b2ae2fe`. Exact-head Node 22/24, Linux x86_64, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks passed for these candidates. Their Entire Gates checks are failures, so none is mergeable through the required workflow. PR #302's trail reports five high-severity findings and missing reviewer approval. The independent source reviewer ACCEPTed the cumulative diff after a partial source read and did not run tests as part of that review. A separate owner-authored PR update records `tsc --noEmit` and 53/53 targeted restore tests, and advises a second review of `checkpoint.ts` because of its size. PR #299, #300, and #305 also lack successful Entire approval. No findings were bypassed and no self-approval was recorded.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1831e-47db-7583-982e-1aab45c43e6a","create_time":1793201563.2520244}}}
