{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:40:32.801Z","ordinal":462271,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1832b-90a1-7012-9b99-9be07c52265f","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed current remote head `72939ec8da37bc22509c8c87ebaacc5de7724f02` against base `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`. Cumulative diff SHA-256: `53d55bf0f2da5d7e14ce1d2b761115bca82403f05c032a6ea8a52f07409ce524`.\n\n1. **HIGH — tracked deletions can remove files inside nested repositories.** Preflight builds targets from checkpoint untracked files and checkpoint blobs ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-untracked-integration/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:909)); it omits paths that `removeTrackedDeletions` will delete ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-untracked-integration/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:340)). That deletion runs after `read-tree` and `checkout-index` ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-untracked-integration/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:915)). If a checkpoint predates tracked `a/file`, and `a` is later replaced by a nested repository containing its own tracked `file`, restore can remove that nested repository’s file. Preflight all deletion/removal paths before Git mutation; add a regression checking nested canary, indexes, and HEADs.\n\n2. **HIGH — a bare repository at the exact destination can bypass preflight.** The bare-repository scan checks only destination parents ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-untracked-integration/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:201)). The directory-target validator checks for `.git`, but not a bare-repository layout ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-untracked-integration/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:433)). An untracked checkpoint file whose destination is replaced by a bare repository can pass preflight; `read-tree` runs before cleanup and copy. Cleanup may remove the bare repository, or preserve it and cause copy to fail after the outer index changed. Check the target directory itself and add a no-mutation regression.\n\nThe inspected symlink-leaf path is not a finding: `writePrivateFile` uses temporary-file rename, so replacing a leaf symlink does not follow its target; parent symlinks are rejected. The source review identifies two plausible matches for Entire’s high-severity findings, but I can’t map them to specific finding IDs or text; other findings remain unknown. **No tests were run.**"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1831e-47db-7583-982e-1aab45c43e6a","create_time":1793202032.8016782,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":22025}}
