{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:43:32.252Z","ordinal":462401,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1832d-e18e-7161-a886-2d19338160bd","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-0997916b-7c04-40d2-a12c-be8d1949e91a","process_id":"90901","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '170,225p' cli/src/checkpoint.ts && sed -n '320,365p' cli/src/checkpoint.ts && sed -n '410,475p' cli/src/checkpoint.ts && sed -n '875,940p' cli/src/checkpoint.ts && rg -n \"nested bare|bare repo|tracked deletion|removeTrackedDeletions|restore.*nested\" cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '170,225p' cli/src/checkpoint.ts","name":"checkpoint.ts","path":"cli/src/checkpoint.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '320,365p' cli/src/checkpoint.ts","name":"checkpoint.ts","path":"cli/src/checkpoint.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '410,475p' cli/src/checkpoint.ts","name":"checkpoint.ts","path":"cli/src/checkpoint.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '875,940p' cli/src/checkpoint.ts","name":"checkpoint.ts","path":"cli/src/checkpoint.ts"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'nested bare|bare repo|tracked deletion|removeTrackedDeletions|restore.*nested' cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts","query":"nested bare|bare repo|tracked deletion|removeTrackedDeletions|restore.*nested","path":"checkpoint_restore.test.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"      maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024,\n    }).toString(\"utf8\").split(\"\\0\").filter(Boolean);\n  }\n\n  private assertSnapshotTextSafe(value: string): void {\n    for (const component of value.split(/[\\\\/]/)) assertNoSensitivePersistenceContent(component, \"checkpoint\");\n  }\n\n  private assertUntrackedEntriesSafe(relativePaths: string[], sourceRoot: string, allowSensitive: boolean): void {\n    for (const relativePath of relativePaths) {\n      const sourcePath = path.join(sourceRoot, relativePath);\n      const stat = fs.lstatSync(sourcePath);\n      if (!allowSensitive) this.assertSnapshotTextSafe(relativePath);\n      if (stat.isSymbolicLink()) {\n        if (!allowSensitive) this.assertSnapshotTextSafe(fs.readlinkSync(sourcePath));\n      } else if (stat.isFile()) {\n        if (!allowSensitive) assertNoSensitivePersistenceContent(fs.readFileSync(sourcePath, \"utf8\"), \"checkpoint\");\n      } else {\n        throw new Error(\"Checkpoint untracked entries must be regular files or symbolic links\");\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  private assertNoNestedGitRepositoryAncestors(relativePaths: string[], targetRoot: string): void {\n    const root = fs.realpathSync(targetRoot);\n    for (const relativePath of relativePaths) {\n      const destination = path.resolve(root, relativePath);\n      const relativeDestination = path.relative(root, destination);\n      if (!relativeDestination || relativeDestination === \"..\" || relativeDestination.startsWith(`..${path.sep}`) || path.isAbsolute(relativeDestination)) {\n        throw new Error(\"Checkpoint destination path escapes the workspace\");\n      }\n      const relativeParent = path.dirname(relativeDestination);\n      let parent = root;\n      for (const component of relativeParent === \".\" ? [] : relativeParent.split(path.sep)) {\n        parent = path.join(parent, component);\n        const stat = fs.lstatSync(parent, { throwIfNoEntry: false });\n        if (!stat) break;\n        if (stat.isSymbolicLink()) {\n          throw new Error(\"Checkpoint destination parent is a symbolic link\");\n        }\n        if (!stat.isDirectory()) break;\n        const dotGit = fs.lstatSync(path.join(parent, \".git\"), { throwIfNoEntry: false });\n        const bareHead = fs.lstatSync(path.join(parent, \"HEAD\"), { throwIfNoEntry: false });\n        const bareConfigPath = path.join(parent, \"config\");\n        const bareConfig = fs.lstatSync(bareConfigPath, { throwIfNoEntry: false });\n        const bareObjects = fs.lstatSync(path.join(parent, \"objects\"), { throwIfNoEntry: false });\n        const bareRefs = fs.lstatSync(path.join(parent, \"refs\"), { throwIfNoEntry: false });\n        const bareRepositoryMarkerCount = [bareHead, bareObjects, bareRefs].filter(Boolean).length;\n        const hasBareRepositoryMarkers = bareRepositoryMarkerCount > 0;\n        const hasBareRepositoryShape = bareRepositoryMarkerCount >= 2;\n        if (hasBareRepositoryMarkers && bareConfig && (\n          (bareHead && (!bareHead.isFile() || bareHead.isSymbolicLink()))\n          || (bareObjects && (!bareObjects.isDirectory() || bareObjects.isSymbolicLink()))\n          || (bareRefs && (!bareRefs.isDirectory() || bareRefs.isSymbolicLink()))\n          || !bareConfig.isFile() || bareConfig.isSymbolicLink()\n        )) {\n      cwd: this.workspace,\n      encoding: \"buffer\",\n      maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024,\n    }).toString(\"utf8\").split(\"\\0\").filter(Boolean);\n    const deletedPaths = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"-c\", \"core.fsmonitor=false\", \"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"--diff-filter=D\", \"-z\", \"HEAD\", gitRef], {\n      cwd: this.workspace,\n      encoding: \"buffer\",\n      maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024,\n    }).toString(\"utf8\").split(\"\\0\").filter(Boolean);\n    const mutationPaths = new Set([...checkoutPaths, ...deletedPaths]);\n    if (this.gitUntrackedPaths(true).some((relativePath) => {\n      for (let candidate = relativePath; candidate && candidate !== \".\"; candidate = path.posix.dirname(candidate)) {\n        if (mutationPaths.has(candidate)) return true;\n      }\n      return false;\n    })) {\n      throw new Error(\"Checkpoint legacy restore would overwrite or delete an uncaptured untracked file\");\n    }\n  }\n\n  private removeTrackedDeletions(gitRef: string, addedPaths: string[] = []): void {\n    const deletedPaths = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"-c\", \"core.fsmonitor=false\", \"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"--diff-filter=D\", \"-z\", \"HEAD\", gitRef], {\n      cwd: this.workspace,\n      encoding: \"buffer\",\n      maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024,\n    }).toString(\"utf8\").split(\"\\0\").filter(Boolean);\n    const workspaceRoot = fs.realpathSync(this.workspace);\n    for (const relativePath of new Set([...deletedPaths, ...addedPaths])) {\n      const targetPath = path.join(workspaceRoot, relativePath);\n      let parent: string;\n      try {\n        parent = fs.realpathSync(path.dirname(targetPath));\n      } catch {\n        continue;\n      }\n      if (parent !== workspaceRoot && !parent.startsWith(workspaceRoot + path.sep)) continue;\n      try {\n        if (fs.lstatSync(targetPath, { throwIfNoEntry: false })?.isDirectory()) continue;\n        fs.rmSync(targetPath, { force: true });\n      } catch (error) {\n        const code = (error as NodeJS.ErrnoException).code;\n        if (code !== \"ENOENT\" && code !== \"ENOTDIR\") throw error;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  private directoryHasCleanupPreservedEntries(directory: string): boolean {\n    const ignored = new Set([\"node_modules\", \".git\", \"target\", \"dist\", \".nexus\", \".next\", \".cache\"]);\n    for (const entry of fs.readdirSync(directory, { withFileTypes: true })) {\n      if (ignored.has(entry.name)) return true;\n      if (entry.isDirectory()) {\n        if (this.directoryHasCleanupPreservedEntries(path.join(directory, entry.name))) return true;\n      } else if (!entry.isFile() && !entry.isSymbolicLink()) {\n        return true;\n      }\n    }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  private assertSnapshotTargetsReplaceable(relativePaths: string[]): void {\n    for (const relativePath of relativePaths) {\n      const targetPath = path.join(this.workspace, relativePath);\n      const stat = fs.lstatSync(targetPath, { throwIfNoEntry: false });\n      if (stat?.isDirectory() && this.directoryHasCleanupPreservedEntries(targetPath)) {\n        throw new Error(\"Checkpoint snapshot target directory contains entries preserved by cleanup\");\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  private assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable(relativePaths: string[], gitRef: string): void {\n    const directoryTargets = relativePaths.filter((relativePath) =>\n      fs.lstatSync(path.join(this.workspace, relativePath), { throwIfNoEntry: false })?.isDirectory(),\n    );\n    if (directoryTargets.length === 0) return;\n\n    const changedPaths = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"-c\", \"core.fsmonitor=false\", \"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"-z\", gitRef, \"--\"], {\n      cwd: this.workspace,\n      encoding: \"buffer\",\n      maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024,\n    }).toString(\"utf8\").split(\"\\0\").filter(Boolean);\n    if (changedPaths.some((relativePath) => path.basename(relativePath) === \".gitignore\")) {\n      throw new Error(\"Checkpoint Git ignore rules differ from the current worktree\");\n    }\n\n    for (const relativePath of directoryTargets) {\n      // A clean preview can be empty when the directory path is also tracked in the index,\n      // even though ordinary untracked children beneath it are removable.\n      if (this.directoryContainsOnlyGitCleanRemovableEntries(relativePath)\n        && this.gitTrackedDescendantPaths(relativePath).length === 0) {\n        continue;\n      }\n      if (!this.directoryContainsOnlyTrackedRemovableEntries(relativePath)) {\n        throw new Error(\"Checkpoint snapshot target directory contains entries preserved by Git clean\");\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  /** Tracked file entries that checkout-index may recreate from this checkpoint tree. Gitlinks are not blobs. */\n  private gitRefBlobPaths(gitRef: string): string[] {\n    const entries = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"-c\", \"core.fsmonitor=false\", \"ls-tree\", \"-r\", \"-z\", \"--full-tree\", gitRef], {\n      cwd: this.workspace,\n      encoding: \"buffer\",\n      maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024,\n    }).toString(\"utf8\").split(\"\\0\").filter(Boolean);\n\n    const paths: string[] = [];\n    for (const entry of entries) {\n      const separator = entry.indexOf(\"\\t\");\n      if (separator < 0) throw new Error(\"Could not parse checkpoint Git tree entry\");\n      const objectType = entry.slice(0, separator).split(\" \")[1];\n      if (objectType === \"blob\") paths.push(entry.slice(separator + 1));\n    }\n    return {\n      prunedCount: count,\n      message: failures.length === 0 ? message : `${message} ${failures.length} checkpoint(s) could not be pruned: ${failures.join(\"; \")}`,\n    };\n  }\n\n  public rollbackLast(): { success: boolean; message: string } {\n    const checkpoints = this.listCheckpoints();\n    if (checkpoints.length === 0) {\n      return { success: false, message: \"No checkpoints available to roll back to.\" };\n    }\n    const target = checkpoints[0];\n    return this.restore(target.id);\n  }\n\n  public restore(id: string): { success: boolean; message: string } {\n    const cp = this.getCheckpoint(id);\n    if (!cp) {\n      return { success: false, message: `Checkpoint '${id}' not found.` };\n    }\n\n    try {\n      if (this.isGit && cp.gitRef) {\n        const hookGuardEnv = envWithoutConfiguredHooks(this.workspace, [\"reference-transaction\", \"post-index-change\"]);\n        const postCheckpointAdditions = cp.untrackedFiles === undefined ? this.trackedPathsAddedSince(cp.gitRef) : [];\n        if (cp.untrackedFiles !== undefined && cp.untrackedFiles.length > 0) {\n          if (!cp.snapshotDir) return { success: false, message: `Rollback failed: checkpoint '${cp.id}' is missing its untracked snapshot; workspace was not changed` };\n          try {\n            this.assertUntrackedSnapshotSafe(cp.untrackedFiles, cp.snapshotDir, cp.allowSensitive === true);\n            this.assertUntrackedDestinationSafe(cp.untrackedFiles, this.workspace);\n          } catch {\n            return { success: false, message: `Rollback failed: checkpoint '${cp.id}' has an unsafe untracked snapshot or destination; workspace was not changed` };\n          }\n        }\n        if (cp.untrackedFiles !== undefined) {\n          const replacementTargets = [...new Set([...cp.untrackedFiles, ...this.gitRefBlobPaths(cp.gitRef)])];\n          this.assertNoNestedGitRepositoryAncestors(replacementTargets, this.workspace);\n          this.assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable(replacementTargets, cp.gitRef);\n        }\n        if (cp.untrackedFiles === undefined) this.assertLegacyUntrackedRestoreSafe(cp.gitRef);\n        execFileSync(\"git\", [\"-c\", \"core.hooksPath=/dev/null\", \"-c\", \"core.fsmonitor=false\", \"read-tree\", cp.gitRef], { cwd: this.workspace, stdio: \"ignore\", env: hookGuardEnv });\n        execFileSync(\"git\", [\"-c\", \"core.hooksPath=/dev/null\", \"-c\", \"core.fsmonitor=false\", \"checkout-index\", \"-f\", \"-a\"], { cwd: this.workspace, stdio: \"ignore\", env: hookGuardEnv });\n        this.removeTrackedDeletions(cp.gitRef, postCheckpointAdditions);\n        if (cp.untrackedFiles !== undefined) {\n          execFileSync(\"git\", [\"-c\", \"core.hooksPath=/dev/null\", \"-c\", \"core.fsmonitor=false\", \"clean\", \"-fd\"], { cwd: this.workspace, stdio: \"ignore\", env: hookGuardEnv });\n          if (cp.untrackedFiles.length > 0) {\n            this.copyUntrackedEntries(cp.untrackedFiles, cp.snapshotDir!, this.workspace, cp.allowSensitive === true);\n          }\n          return { success: true, message: `Restored workspace to checkpoint '${cp.name}' (${cp.id})` };\n        }\n        return { success: true, message: `Restored tracked workspace to checkpoint '${cp.name}' (${cp.id}); legacy untracked files were not captured and were left unchanged` };\n      }\n\n      if (cp.snapshotDir && cp.untrackedFiles !== undefined) {\n        try {\n          this.assertUntrackedSnapshotSafe(cp.untrackedFiles, cp.snapshotDir, cp.allowSensitive === true);\n          this.assertUntrackedDestinationSafe([...cp.untrackedFiles, ...this.workspaceSnapshotPaths(this.workspace)], this.workspace);\n          this.assertSnapshotTargetsReplaceable(cp.untrackedFiles);\n        } catch {\n          return { success: false, message: `Rollback failed: checkpoint '${cp.id}' has an incomplete or unsafe snapshot or destination; workspace was not changed` };\n        }\n        this.removeNonSnapshotEntries(cp.untrackedFiles);\n        this.copyUntrackedEntries(cp.untrackedFiles, cp.snapshotDir, this.workspace, cp.allowSensitive === true);\n        return { success: true, message: `Restored workspace files from snapshot '${cp.name}' (${cp.id})` };\n      }\n\n194:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\"legacy tracked deletion\");\n235:test(\"tracked deletion cleanup never follows a parent symlink outside the workspace\", () => {\n969:test(\"Git manifest restore refuses a nested-repository file-target obstruction before Git mutation\", () => {\n994:test(\"Git manifest restore refuses to copy an untracked file into a nested-repository ancestor\", () => {\n1041:test(\"Git manifest restore refuses to copy an untracked file into a nested bare repository\", () => {\n1048:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\"nested bare repository descendant\");\n1057:    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(bareRepo, \"repository-canary.txt\"), \"bare repository canary\\n\");\n1069:    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(bareRepo, \"captured.txt\")), false, \"rejection must not copy the captured file into the bare repository\");\n1070:    assert.equal(fs.readFileSync(path.join(bareRepo, \"repository-canary.txt\"), \"utf8\"), \"bare repository canary\\n\");\n1081:test(\"Git manifest restore refuses a nested bare repository with a symlinked config\", () => {\n1089:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\"nested bare repository with symlinked config\");\n1105:    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(bareRepo, \"captured.txt\")), false, \"rejection must not copy the captured file into the bare repository\");\n1112:test(\"Git manifest restore refuses a nested bare repository with symlinked object storage\", () => {\n1120:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\"nested bare repository with symlinked object storage\");\n1135:    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(bareRepo, \"captured.txt\")), false, \"rejection must not copy the captured file into the bare repository\");\n1142:test(\"Git manifest restore refuses a nested bare repository with continued core config\", () => {\n1149:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\"nested bare repository with continued config\");\n1163:    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(bareRepo, \"captured.txt\")), false, \"rejection must not copy the captured file into the bare repository\");\n1170:test(\"Git manifest restore refuses a partial bare repository whose config declares bare mode\", () => {\n1177:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\"partial nested bare repository\");\n1195:    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(bareRepo, \"captured.txt\")), false, \"rejection must not copy the captured file into the partial bare repository\");\n1212:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\"ordinary directory resembles a bare repository\");\n1226:test(\"Git manifest restore refuses a tracked destination inside a nested repository before changing either index\", () => {\n1271:test(\"Git manifest restore refuses a tracked destination through a symlinked nested repository before mutation\", () => {\n1355:test(\"Git manifest restore refuses special and nested-repository descendants of a tracked checkpoint file\", () => {\n1397:test(\"Git manifest restore rejects a nested-repository descendant of a tracked checkpoint file before mutation\", () => {\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":168755711}},"started_at_ms":1793202211082,"completed_at_ms":1793202212251}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:43:33.856Z","ordinal":462402,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1832e-53e0-7102-b4ab-3e4de3e3d3ca","call_id":"call_3a827e1f2144451dbcf5838b259cad1a","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"a64c39\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.725709227,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":640,\"output\":\"xerj search: these hits are lexical; this command does not consult the embedding.\\n\\n─── checkpoint.ts:126  (score 37.51)\\n    private assertGitChangesSafe(allowSensitive: boolean): void {\\n        const changedPaths = execFileSync(\\\"git\\\", [\\\"-c\\\", \\\"core.fsmonitor=false\\\", \\\"diff\\\", \\\"--name-only\\\", \\\"-z\\\", \\\"HEAD\\\"], {\\n          cwd: this.workspace,\\n          encoding: \\\"buffer\\\",\\n        }).toString(\\\"utf8\\\").split(\\\"\\\\0\\\").filter(Boolean);\\n    \\n        for (const relativePath of changedPaths) {\\n          if (!allowSensitive) assertNoSensitivePersistenceContent(relativePath, \\\"checkpoint\\\");\\n          try {\\n            const indexed = execFileSync(\\\"git\\\", [\\\"-c\\\", \\\"core.fsmonitor=false\\\", \\\"show\\\", `:${relativePath}`], {\\n              cwd: this.workspace,\\n              encoding: \\\"buffer\\n    … (--full 1200 to see more)\\n\\n─── security.ts:301  (score 35.54)\\n    public isCommandBlocked(command: string): { blocked: boolean; reason?: string } {\\n        if (!command || typeof command !== \\\"string\\\") {\\n          return { blocked: false };\\n        }\\n        const trimmed = command.trim();\\n        if (trimmed.length === 0) {\\n          return { blocked: false };\\n        }\\n    \\n        // 1. Custom blocked commands from policy (outside the default tripwire set)\\n        const customPatterns = (this.policy.blockedCommands || []).filter(\\n          (p) => !DEFAULT_BLOCKED_COMMANDS.includes(p)\\n        );\\n        for (const pattern of customPatterns) {\\n          if (pattern && trimmed.includes(pattern)) {\\n            return {\\n    … (--full 1200 to see more)\\n\\n─── agent.ts:4663  (score 20.37)\\n              durationMs: 0,\\n              candidateMutated: false,\\n              status: \\\"DENIED\\\",\\n              timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\\n              simulated: Boolean(this.config.dryRun),\\n            },\\n            shouldExit: false,\\n          };\\n        }\\n    \\n        try {\\n          const isPublicEgress = [\\\"search_web\\\", \\\"fetch_web\\\", \\\"browser_navigate\\\", \\\"browser_type\\\"].includes(toolName);\\n          if (!isPublicEgress) {\\n            const serialized = JSON.stringify(args);\\n            const restored = this.securityManager.getVault().restore(serialized, { isAuthorizedSink: true });\\n            if (restored !== serialized) {\\n              args \\n    … (--full 1200 to see more)\\n\\n─── knowledge.ts:158  [method]  (score 15.34)\\n    public delete(keyOrId: string): boolean\\n\\n─── knowledge.ts  (score 16.46)\\n    knowledge.ts\\n\\n5 passage(s) from 'nexus-cli-*'. Cite ax_path:line (ax_path#locator for a data row) for anything you rely on.\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"6b3b3a\",\"wall_time_seconds\":1.168935911,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3878,\"output\":\"      maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024,\\n    }).toString(\\\"utf8\\\").split(\\\"\\\\0\\\").filter(Boolean);\\n  }\\n\\n  private assertSnapshotTextSafe(value: string): void {\\n    for (const component of value.split(/[\\\\\\\\/]/)) assertNoSensitivePersistenceContent(component, \\\"checkpoint\\\");\\n  }\\n\\n  private assertUntrackedEntriesSafe(relativePaths: string[], sourceRoot: string, allowSensitive: boolean): void {\\n    for (const relativePath of relativePaths) {\\n      const sourcePath = path.join(sourceRoot, relativePath);\\n      const stat = fs.lstatSync(sourcePath);\\n      if (!allowSensitive) this.assertSnapshotTextSafe(relativePath);\\n      if (stat.isSymbolicLink()) {\\n        if (!allowSensitive) this.assertSnapshotTextSafe(fs.readlinkSync(sourcePath));\\n      } else if (stat.isFile()) {\\n        if (!allowSensitive) assertNoSensitivePersistenceContent(fs.readFileSync(sourcePath, \\\"utf8\\\"), \\\"checkpoint\\\");\\n      } else {\\n        throw new Error(\\\"Checkpoint untracked entries must be regular files or symbolic links\\\");\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  private assertNoNestedGitRepositoryAncestors(relativePaths: string[], targetRoot: string): void {\\n    const root = fs.realpathSync(targetRoot);\\n    for (const relativePath of relativePaths) {\\n      const destination = path.resolve(root, relativePath);\\n      const relativeDestination = path.relative(root, destination);\\n      if (!relativeDestination || relativeDestination === \\\"..\\\" || relativeDestination.startsWith(`..${path.sep}`) || path.isAbsolute(relativeDestination)) {\\n        throw new Error(\\\"Checkpoint destination path escapes the workspace\\\");\\n      }\\n      const relativeParent = path.dirname(relativeDestination);\\n      let parent = root;\\n      for (const component of relativeParent === \\\".\\\" ? [] : relativeParent.split(path.sep)) {\\n        parent = path.join(parent, component);\\n        const stat = fs.lstatSync(parent, { throwIfNoEntry: false });\\n        if (!stat) break;\\n        if (stat.isSymbolicLink()) {\\n          throw new Error(\\\"Checkpoint destination parent is a symbolic link\\\");\\n        }\\n        if (!stat.isDirectory()) break;\\n        const dotGit = fs.lstatSync(path.join(parent, \\\".git\\\"), { throwIfNoEntry: false });\\n        const bareHead = fs.lstatSync(path.join(parent, \\\"HEAD\\\"), { throwIfNoEntry: false });\\n        const bareConfigPath = path.join(parent, \\\"config\\\");\\n        const bareConfig = fs.lstatSync(bareConfigPath, { throwIfNoEntry: false });\\n        const bareObjects = fs.lstatSync(path.join(parent, \\\"objects\\\"), { throwIfNoEntry: false });\\n        const bareRefs = fs.lstatSync(path.join(parent, \\\"refs\\\"), { throwIfNoEntry: false });\\n        const bareRepositoryMarkerCount = [bareHead, bareObjects, bareRefs].filter(Boolean).length;\\n        const hasBareRepositoryMarkers = bareRepositoryMarkerCount > 0;\\n        const hasBareRepositoryShape = bareRepositoryMarkerCount >= 2;\\n        if (hasBareRepositoryMarkers && bareConfig && (\\n          (bareHead && (!bareHead.isFile() || bareHead.isSymbolicLink()))\\n          || (bareObjects && (!bareObjects.isDirectory() || bareObjects.isSymbolicLink()))\\n          || (bareRefs && (!bareRefs.isDirectory() || bareRefs.isSymbolicLink()))\\n          || !bareConfig.isFile() || bareConfig.isSymbolicLink()\\n        )) {\\n      cwd: this.workspace,\\n      encoding: \\\"buffer\\\",\\n      maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024,\\n    }).toString(\\\"utf8\\\").split(\\\"\\\\0\\\").filter(Boolean);\\n    const deletedPaths = execFileSync(\\\"git\\\", [\\\"-c\\\", \\\"core.fsmonitor=false\\\", \\\"diff\\\", \\\"--name-only\\\", \\\"--diff-filter=D\\\", \\\"-z\\\", \\\"HEAD\\\", gitRef], {\\n      cwd: this.workspace,\\n      encoding: \\\"buffer\\\",\\n      maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024,\\n    }).toString(\\\"utf8\\\").split(\\\"\\\\0\\\").filter(Boolean);\\n    const mutationPaths = new Set([...checkoutPaths, ...deletedPaths]);\\n    if (this.gitUntrackedPaths(true).some((relativePath) => {\\n      for (let candidate = relativePath; candidate && candidate !== \\\".\\\"; candidate = path.posix.dirname(candidate)) {\\n        if (mutationPaths.has(candidate)) return true;\\n      }\\n      return false;\\n    })) {\\n      throw new Error(\\\"Checkpoint legacy restore would overwrite or delete an uncaptured untracked file\\\");\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  private removeTrackedDeletions(gitRef: string, addedPaths: string[] = []): void {\\n    const deletedPaths = execFileSync(\\\"git\\\", [\\\"-c\\\", \\\"core.fsmonitor=false\\\", \\\"diff\\\", \\\"--name-only\\\", \\\"--diff-filter=D\\\", \\\"-z\\\", \\\"HEAD\\\", gitRef], {\\n      cwd: this.workspace,\\n      encoding: \\\"buffer\\\",\\n      maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024,\\n    }).toString(\\\"utf8\\\").split(\\\"\\\\0\\\").filter(Boolean);\\n    const workspaceRoot = fs.realpathSync(this.workspace);\\n    for (const relativePath of new Set([...deletedPaths, ...addedPaths])) {\\n      const targetPath = path.join(workspaceRoot, relativePath);\\n      let parent: string;\\n      try {\\n        parent = fs.realpathSync(path.dirname(targetPath));\\n      } catch {\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      if (parent !== workspaceRoot && !parent.startsWith(workspaceRoot + path.sep)) continue;\\n      try {\\n        if (fs.lstatSync(targetPath, { throwIfNoEntry: false })?.isDirectory()) continue;\\n        fs.rmSync(targetPath, { force: true });\\n      } catch (error) {\\n        const code = (error as NodeJS.ErrnoException).code;\\n        if (code !== \\\"ENOENT\\\" && code !== \\\"ENOTDIR\\\") throw error;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  private directoryHasCleanupPreservedEntries(directory: string): boolean {\\n    const ignored = new Set([\\\"node_modules\\\", \\\".git\\\", \\\"target\\\", \\\"dist\\\", \\\".nexus\\\", \\\".next\\\", \\\".cache\\\"]);\\n    for (const entry of fs.readdirSync(directory, { withFileTypes: true })) {\\n      if (ignored.has(entry.name)) return true;\\n      if (entry.isDirectory()) {\\n        if (this.directoryHasCleanupPreservedEntries(path.join(directory, entry.name))) return true;\\n      } else if (!entry.isFile() && !entry.isSymbolicLink()) {\\n        return true;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  private assertSnapshotTargetsReplaceable(relativePaths: string[]): void {\\n    for (const relativePath of relativePaths) {\\n      const targetPath = path.join(this.workspace, relativePath);\\n      const stat = fs.lstatSync(targetPath, { throwIfNoEntry: false });\\n      if (stat?.isDirectory() && this.directoryHasCleanupPreservedEntries(targetPath)) {\\n        throw new Error(\\\"Checkpoint snapshot target directory contains entries preserved by cleanup\\\");\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  private assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable(relativePaths: string[], gitRef: string): void {\\n    const directoryTargets = relativePaths.filter((relativePath) =>\\n      fs.lstatSync(path.join(this.workspace, relativePath), { throwIfNoEntry: false })?.isDirectory(),\\n    );\\n    if (directoryTargets.length === 0) return;\\n\\n    const changedPaths = execFileSync(\\\"git\\\", [\\\"-c\\\", \\\"core.fsmonitor=false\\\", \\\"diff\\\", \\\"--name-only\\\", \\\"-z\\\", gitRef, \\\"--\\\"], {\\n      cwd: this.workspace,\\n      encoding: \\\"buffer\\\",\\n      maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024,\\n    }).toString(\\\"utf8\\\").split(\\\"\\\\0\\\").filter(Boolean);\\n    if (changedPaths.some((relativePath) => path.basename(relativePath) === \\\".gitignore\\\")) {\\n      throw new Error(\\\"Checkpoint Git ignore rules differ from the current worktree\\\");\\n    }\\n\\n    for (const relativePath of directoryTargets) {\\n      // A clean preview can be empty when the directory path is also tracked in the index,\\n      // even though ordinary untracked children beneath it are removable.\\n      if (this.directoryContainsOnlyGitCleanRemovableEntries(relativePath)\\n        && this.gitTrackedDescendantPaths(relativePath).length === 0) {\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      if (!this.directoryContainsOnlyTrackedRemovableEntries(relativePath)) {\\n        throw new Error(\\\"Checkpoint snapshot target directory contains entries preserved by Git clean\\\");\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Tracked file entries that checkout-index may recreate from this checkpoint tree. Gitlinks are not blobs. */\\n  private gitRefBlobPaths(gitRef: string): string[] {\\n    const entries = execFileSync(\\\"git\\\", [\\\"-c\\\", \\\"core.fsmonitor=false\\\", \\\"ls-tree\\\", \\\"-r\\\", \\\"-z\\\", \\\"--full-tree\\\", gitRef], {\\n      cwd: this.workspace,\\n      encoding: \\\"buffer\\\",\\n      maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024,\\n    }).toString(\\\"utf8\\\").split(\\\"\\\\0\\\").filter(Boolean);\\n\\n    const paths: string[] = [];\\n    for (const entry of entries) {\\n      const separator = entry.indexOf(\\\"\\\\t\\\");\\n      if (separator < 0) throw new Error(\\\"Could not parse checkpoint Git tree entry\\\");\\n      const objectType = entry.slice(0, separator).split(\\\" \\\")[1];\\n      if (objectType === \\\"blob\\\") paths.push(entry.slice(separator + 1));\\n    }\\n    return {\\n      prunedCount: count,\\n      message: failures.length === 0 ? message : `${message} ${failures.length} checkpoint(s) could not be pruned: ${failures.join(\\\"; \\\")}`,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  public rollbackLast(): { success: boolean; message: string } {\\n    const checkpoints = this.listCheckpoints();\\n    if (checkpoints.length === 0) {\\n      return { success: false, message: \\\"No checkpoints available to roll back to.\\\" };\\n    }\\n    const target = checkpoints[0];\\n    return this.restore(target.id);\\n  }\\n\\n  public restore(id: string): { success: boolean; message: string } {\\n    const cp = this.getCheckpoint(id);\\n    if (!cp) {\\n      return { success: false, message: `Checkpoint '${id}' not found.` };\\n    }\\n\\n    try {\\n      if (this.isGit && cp.gitRef) {\\n        const hookGuardEnv = envWithoutConfiguredHooks(this.workspace, [\\\"reference-transaction\\\", \\\"post-index-change\\\"]);\\n        const postCheckpointAdditions = cp.untrackedFiles === undefined ? this.trackedPathsAddedSince(cp.gitRef) : [];\\n        if (cp.untrackedFiles !== undefined && cp.untrackedFiles.length > 0) {\\n          if (!cp.snapshotDir) return { success: false, message: `Rollback failed: checkpoint '${cp.id}' is missing its untracked snapshot; workspace was not changed` };\\n          try {\\n            this.assertUntrackedSnapshotSafe(cp.untrackedFiles, cp.snapshotDir, cp.allowSensitive === true);\\n            this.assertUntrackedDestinationSafe(cp.untrackedFiles, this.workspace);\\n          } catch {\\n            return { success: false, message: `Rollback failed: checkpoint '${cp.id}' has an unsafe untracked snapshot or destination; workspace was not changed` };\\n          }\\n        }\\n        if (cp.untrackedFiles !== undefined) {\\n          const replacementTargets = [...new Set([...cp.untrackedFiles, ...this.gitRefBlobPaths(cp.gitRef)])];\\n          this.assertNoNestedGitRepositoryAncestors(replacementTargets, this.workspace);\\n          this.assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable(replacementTargets, cp.gitRef);\\n        }\\n        if (cp.untrackedFiles === undefined) this.assertLegacyUntrackedRestoreSafe(cp.gitRef);\\n        execFileSync(\\\"git\\\", [\\\"-c\\\", \\\"core.hooksPath=/dev/null\\\", \\\"-c\\\", \\\"core.fsmonitor=false\\\", \\\"read-tree\\\", cp.gitRef], { cwd: this.workspace, stdio: \\\"ignore\\\", env: hookGuardEnv });\\n        execFileSync(\\\"git\\\", [\\\"-c\\\", \\\"core.hooksPath=/dev/null\\\", \\\"-c\\\", \\\"core.fsmonitor=false\\\", \\\"checkout-index\\\", \\\"-f\\\", \\\"-a\\\"], { cwd: this.workspace, stdio: \\\"ignore\\\", env: hookGuardEnv });\\n        this.removeTrackedDeletions(cp.gitRef, postCheckpointAdditions);\\n        if (cp.untrackedFiles !== undefined) {\\n          execFileSync(\\\"git\\\", [\\\"-c\\\", \\\"core.hooksPath=/dev/null\\\", \\\"-c\\\", \\\"core.fsmonitor=false\\\", \\\"clean\\\", \\\"-fd\\\"], { cwd: this.workspace, stdio: \\\"ignore\\\", env: hookGuardEnv });\\n          if (cp.untrackedFiles.length > 0) {\\n            this.copyUntrackedEntries(cp.untrackedFiles, cp.snapshotDir!, this.workspace, cp.allowSensitive === true);\\n          }\\n          return { success: true, message: `Restored workspace to checkpoint '${cp.name}' (${cp.id})` };\\n        }\\n        return { success: true, message: `Restored tracked workspace to checkpoint '${cp.name}' (${cp.id}); legacy untracked files were not captured and were left unchanged` };\\n      }\\n\\n      if (cp.snapshotDir && cp.untrackedFiles !== undefined) {\\n        try {\\n          this.assertUntrackedSnapshotSafe(cp.untrackedFiles, cp.snapshotDir, cp.allowSensitive === true);\\n          this.assertUntrackedDestinationSafe([...cp.untrackedFiles, ...this.workspaceSnapshotPaths(this.workspace)], this.workspace);\\n          this.assertSnapshotTargetsReplaceable(cp.untrackedFiles);\\n        } catch {\\n          return { success: false, message: `Rollback failed: checkpoint '${cp.id}' has an incomplete or unsafe snapshot or destination; workspace was not changed` };\\n        }\\n        this.removeNonSnapshotEntries(cp.untrackedFiles);\\n        this.copyUntrackedEntries(cp.untrackedFiles, cp.snapshotDir, this.workspace, cp.allowSensitive === true);\\n        return { success: true, message: `Restored workspace files from snapshot '${cp.name}' (${cp.id})` };\\n      }\\n\\n194:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\\\"legacy tracked deletion\\\");\\n235:test(\\\"tracked deletion cleanup never follows a parent symlink outside the workspace\\\", () => {\\n969:test(\\\"Git manifest restore refuses a nested-repository file-target obstruction before Git mutation\\\", () => {\\n994:test(\\\"Git manifest restore refuses to copy an untracked file into a nested-repository ancestor\\\", () => {\\n1041:test(\\\"Git manifest restore refuses to copy an untracked file into a nested bare repository\\\", () => {\\n1048:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\\\"nested bare repository descendant\\\");\\n1057:    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(bareRepo, \\\"repository-canary.txt\\\"), \\\"bare repository canary\\\\n\\\");\\n1069:    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(bareRepo, \\\"captured.txt\\\")), false, \\\"rejection must not copy the captured file into the bare repository\\\");\\n1070:    assert.equal(fs.readFileSync(path.join(bareRepo, \\\"repository-canary.txt\\\"), \\\"utf8\\\"), \\\"bare repository canary\\\\n\\\");\\n1081:test(\\\"Git manifest restore refuses a nested bare repository with a symlinked config\\\", () => {\\n1089:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\\\"nested bare repository with symlinked config\\\");\\n1105:    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(bareRepo, \\\"captured.txt\\\")), false, \\\"rejection must not copy the captured file into the bare repository\\\");\\n1112:test(\\\"Git manifest restore refuses a nested bare repository with symlinked object storage\\\", () => {\\n1120:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\\\"nested bare repository with symlinked object storage\\\");\\n1135:    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(bareRepo, \\\"captured.txt\\\")), false, \\\"rejection must not copy the captured file into the bare repository\\\");\\n1142:test(\\\"Git manifest restore refuses a nested bare repository with continued core config\\\", () => {\\n1149:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\\\"nested bare repository with continued config\\\");\\n1163:    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(bareRepo, \\\"captured.txt\\\")), false, \\\"rejection must not copy the captured file into the bare repository\\\");\\n1170:test(\\\"Git manifest restore refuses a partial bare repository whose config declares bare mode\\\", () => {\\n1177:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\\\"partial nested bare repository\\\");\\n1195:    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(bareRepo, \\\"captured.txt\\\")), false, \\\"rejection must not copy the captured file into the partial bare repository\\\");\\n1212:    const checkpoint = manager.createCheckpoint(\\\"ordinary directory resembles a bare repository\\\");\\n1226:test(\\\"Git manifest restore refuses a tracked destination inside a nested repository before changing either index\\\", () => {\\n1271:test(\\\"Git manifest restore refuses a tracked destination through a symlinked nested repository before mutation\\\", () => {\\n1355:test(\\\"Git manifest restore refuses special and nested-repository descendants of a tracked checkpoint file\\\", () => {\\n1397:test(\\\"Git manifest restore rejects a nested-repository descendant of a tracked checkpoint file before mutation\\\", () => {\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"bf829c\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000035509,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2846,\"output\":\"# Running multiple agents on this plan without collisions\\n\\nThese rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\\n\\n- a concurrent agent overwrote newer evidence;\\n- full test suites were contaminated by edits made mid-run;\\n- `pkill -f` killed the agent's own shell;\\n- HEAD moved during a pause.\\n\\nThey also follow from audit finding PER-03: the test suite writes into the real `~/.nexus`.\\n\\n## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\\n\\n- The unit of concurrent work is **one PR slice** from a plan, for example `PLAN-01/PR-1a`. Every slice lists its tasks and its safe change boundary in its plan.\\n- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\\n- An agent must not edit files outside its slice's boundary. The exceptions are the ledger rows and the shared files covered by §4. If the work needs a file outside the boundary, the agent stops and records a **boundary request** (§6). It does not edit the file.\\n\\n## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\\n\\nClaims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\\n\\n```sh\\nCLAIMS=\\\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\\\"\\nmkdir -p \\\"$CLAIMS\\\"\\nSLICE=\\\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\\\"\\nif mkdir \\\"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\\\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\\n  printf '{\\\"agent\\\":\\\"%s\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"%s\\\",\\\"since\\\":\\\"%s\\\",\\\"pid\\\":%s}\\\\n' \\\\\\n    \\\"$AGENT_NAME\\\" \\\"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\\\" \\\"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\\\" \\\"$$\\\" > \\\"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\\\"\\nelse\\n  echo \\\"claimed by: $(cat \\\"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\\\")\\\"; exit 1\\nfi\\n```\\n\\n- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \\\"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\\\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\\n- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\\n- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\\n- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\\n\\n## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\\n\\n| Resource | Rule |\\n|---|---|\\n| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\\n| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\\n| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\\\"$HOME/.config\\\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\\n| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\\n| Builds | Each worktree builds into its own `core/target`, and `cli/dist` is per worktree. To share the Rust build cache, set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` per worktree, never to one shared directory. |\\n| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\\n| Processes | Kill only PIDs you started, taken from `$!` or `ps -eo pid,args \\\\| grep -v grep`. **Never `pkill -f` or `killall`.** Long background jobs are stopped through the agent's own task controls. |\\n| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\\n| Credentials | Agents never read or copy `~/.config/nexus/credentials.json`, `config.env` values, or gateway tokens. The stripped proxy reads the token file itself. |\\n\\n## 4. Hot files: serialise, do not merge blindly\\n\\nThese files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\\n\\n| File | Plans that touch it | Rule |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `cli/src/agent.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 11 | Claim required. Keep each change local to the line ranges the plan names. Rebase immediately before merge and re-run that slice's tests on the rebased snapshot. |\\n| `cli/src/index.ts` | 01, 03, 04, 06, 08, 10, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-06 PR-6b (unified launcher) lands first.** Other plans add commands and flags afterwards. |\\n| `cli/src/tools.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 06, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-02 PR-2b (signal plumbing) lands before PLAN-03 PR-3c (`safeFetch`)**. |\\n| `cli/src/sidecar.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 05, 08 | Claim required |\\n| `cli/src/doctor.ts` | 01, 03, 05, 06, 08 | Claim required. Each plan adds **new check functions** in separate blocks. Only PLAN-06 PR-6d changes existing checks. |\\n| `cli/src/client.ts` | 03, 05, 08, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-03 PR-3a (env layering) lands before any PLAN-05 slice.** |\\n| `cli/src/repl.ts` | 01, 05, 08 | Claim required |\\n| `cli/src/config.ts`, `security.ts`, `sandbox.ts`, `mcp.ts`, `plugins.ts` | 01, 03 | Claim required. PLAN-01 PR-1e and PLAN-03 must not run at the same time on `sandbox.ts` or `security.ts`. |\\n| `cli/src/core/capabilities.ts` | 01, 02 | **PLAN-01 PR-1a (effect classes) lands first.** PLAN-02 PR-2c adds schema fields afterwards. |\\n| `cli/src/tester.ts` | 01, 11 | **PLAN-01 PR-1c lands before PLAN-11 PR-11b/11c.** |\\n| `cli/src/core/state.ts` | 04, 08 | **PLAN-08 PR-8a (HOME isolation) lands before everything.** |\\n| `core/src/runner.rs`, `core/src/main.rs` | 01, 02, 06 | Claim required. The protocol version number is owned by PLAN-02 PR-2a. PLAN-06 PR-6c only reads it. |\\n| `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/{live_state,live_view}.rs` | 01, 02 | Claim required |\\n| `package.json`, `cli/package.json`, `core/Cargo.toml`, lockfiles | 01, 06, 07, 08 | **Only one agent at a time.** Version fields are written only by `scripts/sync-version.mjs`. Dependency changes are separate commits that touch only the lockfile and manifest. |\\n| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\\n| `cli/dist/**` | all, while tracked | Do not commit `cli/dist` from slices. PLAN-07 PR-7d untracks it (DEC-10). Until that merges, only the merging agent rebuilds and commits dist, in a final separate commit, after rebasing. |\\n| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\\n\\n### Ledger updates (`docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md`)\\n\\nA slice changes only the rows for its own requirement IDs: the status, test-reference and evidence cells, in place. It never reorders, adds or removes rows, and never edits another slice's rows. New requirements discovered during work go to §6, not into the ledger. Because rows are independent lines, git merges these edits cleanly. If a conflict appears anyway, resolve it row by row, keeping both changes.\\n\\n## 5. Commit and merge discipline\\n\\n1. Before **every** commit, compare `git rev-parse HEAD` with the commit you last made. Then run `git log <yours>..HEAD` on the branch. If anything foreign appears, stop and reconcile. Never commit generated artifacts (evidence, dist, lockfiles) over a branch that moved (lessons 2026-10-13).\\n2. Commits are scoped to the slice. Do not reformat or clean up files outside the boundary.\\n3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\\n4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\\n5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\\n6. Preserve unrelated user work: the untracked `nexus-continuity-validation/`, the stashes, and any dirty files you did not create. Never stash, reset, clean or check out over them.\\n\\n## 6. Coordination records\\n\\n| Record | Where | Purpose |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\\n| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\\n| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\\n| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\\n\\n## 7. Safe parallel lanes\\n\\nThe following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\\n\\n| Phase | Parallel lanes |\\n|---|---|\\n| M0 | (a) PLAN-08 PR-8a, which must merge first. Then in parallel: (b) PLAN-06 PR-6a, (c) PLAN-09 PR-9a. |\\n| M1 | (a) PLAN-01 PR-1a → PR-1b → PR-1c (sequential, owns `capabilities.ts`, `agent.ts` dispatch). (b) PLAN-02 PR-2a (Rust only). (c) PLAN-03 PR-3a → PR-3b (config/egress). (d) PLAN-11 PR-11a (`parser.ts`) and PR-11b (`tester.ts`, after PR-1c). Lanes (b), (c) and (d) do not touch `capabilities.ts`. |\\n| M2 (alongside M1) | (a) PLAN-07 PR-7a/7b/7c (workflows, scripts). (b) PLAN-06 PR-6b after PLAN-01 PR-1b (shares `index.ts` flags). |\\n| M3 | (a) PLAN-04 (`agent.ts` turn, operation runner). (b) PLAN-05 (`client.ts`, provider modules). (c) PLAN-10 harness (`eval/`, no product files). (d) Held-out task authoring by the agent author, **outside the repository**: no access to Nexus source or the development set (DEC-05). |\\n| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\\n| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\\n\\n## 8. Independence constraints\\n\\n- The held-out task author must not see Nexus source, the development tasks or tuning history. It runs in a separate session with only the task schema and external repositories. Its output is sealed by a sha256 manifest committed before RC1.\\n- The independent reviewer in ACCEPTANCE §8 must not be the agent or session that implemented the slices under review.\\n- An implementing agent never edits `eval/heldout-manifest.json`, scorer thresholds or ACCEPTANCE §6.4 after the freeze.\\n\"}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1832d-e18e-7161-a886-2d19338160bd","create_time":1793202213.8563292}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
