{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:44:02.212Z","ordinal":462419,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1832e-c2a4-7551-89fd-6603866825fe","call_id":"call_d72cf14b8fb6417f9993b56d497f6e6d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 5.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"0d435e\",\"wall_time_seconds\":5.000871736,\"session_id\":59655,\"original_token_count\":875,\"output\":\"the `--remote` flag is unsupported when a repository argument is provided\\n\\nCreate a fork of a repository.\\n\\nWith no argument, creates a fork of the current repository. Otherwise, forks\\nthe specified repository.\\n\\nBy default, the new fork is set to be your `origin` remote and any existing\\norigin remote is renamed to `upstream`. To alter this behavior, you can set\\na name for the new fork's remote with `--remote-name`.\\n\\nThe `upstream` remote will be set as the default remote repository.\\n\\nAdditional `git clone` flags can be passed after `--`.\\n\\n\\nUSAGE\\n  gh repo fork [<repository>] [-- <gitflags>...] [flags]\\n\\nFLAGS\\n  --clone                 Clone the fork\\n  --default-branch-only   Only include the default branch in the fork\\n  --fork-name string      Rename the forked repository\\n  --org string            Create the fork in an organization\\n  --remote                Add a git remote for the fork\\n  --remote-name string    Specify the name for the new remote (default \\\"origin\\\")\\n\\nINHERITED FLAGS\\n  --help   Show help for command\\n\\nEXAMPLES\\n  # Fork a repository\\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo\\n  \\n  # Fork a repository and clone it locally\\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone\\n  \\n  # Fork a repository without cloning it, skip the prompt\\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone=false\\n\\nLEARN MORE\\n  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\\n  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\\n  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\\n  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\\n\\nerror: this account cannot push to xerj-org/xerj, and forking failed: `gh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork` failed\\nNothing was branched.\\n\\n# Ready-to-run — files ONLY the field report, nothing else.\\n# Run these in a clone of xerj-org/xerj, not in the project you are working in.\\ngit clone https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj.git\\ncd xerj\\ngh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork\\nxerj feedback \\\\\\n --agent \\\"Codex GPT-6\\\" \\\\\\n  --used-for \\\"Locating the checkpoint restore deletion flow before PR302 security remediation\\\" --pointed-at \\\"1051 records under /home/mike/xerj-sources/nexus-code/core/src (autoindex run run-20261028T022152Z-ff10-0000)\\\" \\\\\\n  --verdict \\\"Useful definition-first context in checkpoint.ts; ranked hits identified nearby checkpoint logic, while exact current-head behavior still required direct source inspection\\\" --numbers \\\"not measured\\\" \\\\\\n  -o user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-28-locating-the-checkpoint-restore-deletion-flow.md\\ngit checkout -b field-report/locating-the-checkpoint-restore-deletion-flow\\ngit add user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-28-locating-the-checkpoint-restore-deletion-flow.md\\ngit commit --only user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-28-locating-the-checkpoint-restore-deletion-flow.md -m \\\"docs(field-report): locating-the-checkpoint-restore-deletion-flow\\\"\\ngit push -u xerj-fork field-report/locating-the-checkpoint-restore-deletion-flow\\ngh pr create --repo xerj-org/xerj --base main --head YOUR_LOGIN:field-report/locating-the-checkpoint-restore-deletion-flow \\\\\\n  --title \\\"Agent field report: Locating the checkpoint restore deletion flow before PR302 security remediation\\\" \\\\\\n  --body \\\"Field report only; see user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-28-locating-the-checkpoint-restore-deletion-flow.md.\\\"\\nGitHub is unavailable (the pull request could not be opened (see above)); sending the field report to https://xerj.org/api/field-report instead.\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1832d-e18e-7161-a886-2d19338160bd","create_time":1793202242.2122805}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
