{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:46:38.163Z","ordinal":462546,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18331-23d3-7f42-a995-32567cc96622","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — reviewed `72939ec8da37bc22509c8c87ebaacc5de7724f02` plus the current uncommitted diff (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts`, `cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts`). Diff SHA-256: `31171bfdcd39f83a04bc9fe56a1ef2ce069497fd2b1f5d0515eb78725aa7a639`.\n\nTracked deletion paths are included in the preflight path set before `read-tree` ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:917), [checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:934)). The exact destination is scanned when it is a directory, so a bare repository at that path is rejected before mutation ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:203), [checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:273)).\n\nRegression coverage checks nested repository HEAD/index and canary preservation for tracked deletions ([checkpoint_restore.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:1327)), and outer HEAD/index plus the bare-repository canary for an exact bare destination ([checkpoint_restore.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:1081)). No tests were run."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1832d-e18e-7161-a886-2d19338160bd","create_time":1793202398.1637037,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":22034}}
