{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:54:38.078Z","ordinal":462801,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1832d-e18e-7161-a886-2d19338160bd","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a1832d-e18e-7161-a886-2d19338160bd","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae21abc1de0819fbf5f3aa483e4e251","usage":{"input_tokens":167504,"cached_input_tokens":164096,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":92,"reasoning_output_tokens":16,"total_tokens":167596},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":7599062,"cached_input_tokens":7510528,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24382,"reasoning_output_tokens":14451,"total_tokens":7623444},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8588597788,"cached_input_tokens":8496828288,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24494558,"reasoning_output_tokens":14178650,"total_tokens":8613092346}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:54:39.496Z","ordinal":462802,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1832d-e18e-7161-a886-2d19338160bd","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-477685f6-1170-4ed1-b366-164c6eda46b9","process_id":"38644","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '172,235p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '172,235p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\n- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\n- new: the package PTY smoke\n\n### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n\nThese are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n\n| Scenario | Pass condition |\n|---|---|\n| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The endpoint is named, with a fix hint. The turn ends with guidance in ≤ 2.5 min. |\n| s2 approval under continuous typing, paste and burst, at 40×14 | No decision is made by stray input. A deliberate key decides. |\n| s3 completion | The outcome is shown in words: VERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE or UNVERIFIED. |\n| s4–s6 cancel and steer | Cancel is acknowledged within 1 frame and idle within 5 s. Steering is applied. |\n| s7 resume | The prior conversation is shown. |\n| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\n| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n\n### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n\nTerminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n\nFor each terminal × size, check:\n\n1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\n6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. NO_COLOR.\n\nRecord PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n\n### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n\n- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\n- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\n\n  ```bash\n  set -euo pipefail\n  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\n  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\n  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n  ```\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":34000}},"started_at_ms":1793202879495,"completed_at_ms":1793202879496}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T15:54:40.912Z","ordinal":462803,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18338-8190-7f21-82eb-1a14f65bb8ea","call_id":"call_27824a5273784db5a1b41de1c69da22a","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"5727e2\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000034,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1092,\"output\":\"- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\\n- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\\n- new: the package PTY smoke\\n\\n### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\\n\\nThese are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\\n\\n| Scenario | Pass condition |\\n|---|---|\\n| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The endpoint is named, with a fix hint. The turn ends with guidance in ≤ 2.5 min. |\\n| s2 approval under continuous typing, paste and burst, at 40×14 | No decision is made by stray input. A deliberate key decides. |\\n| s3 completion | The outcome is shown in words: VERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE or UNVERIFIED. |\\n| s4–s6 cancel and steer | Cancel is acknowledged within 1 frame and idle within 5 s. Steering is applied. |\\n| s7 resume | The prior conversation is shown. |\\n| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\\n| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\\n\\n### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\\n\\nTerminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\\n\\nFor each terminal × size, check:\\n\\n1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\\n2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\\n3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\\n4. Resize during streaming.\\n5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\\n6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\\n7. NO_COLOR.\\n\\nRecord PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\\n\\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\\n\\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\\n\\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\\n\\n### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\\n\\n- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\\n- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\\n- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\\n- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\\n- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\\n\\n  ```bash\\n  set -euo pipefail\\n  : \\\"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\\\"\\n  : \\\"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\\\"\\n  test ! -e \\\"$T2_OUT\\\"\\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \\\"$T2_TASKS\\\" --out \\\"$T2_OUT/nexus\\\" --runs 5\\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \\\"$T2_TASKS\\\" --out \\\"$T2_OUT/goose\\\" --runs 5\\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \\\"$T2_TASKS\\\" --out \\\"$T2_OUT/opencode\\\" --runs 5\\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \\\"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\\\" \\\"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\\\" \\\"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\\\"\\n  ```\\n\\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\\n\\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\\n\\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1832d-e18e-7161-a886-2d19338160bd","create_time":1793202880.9121559}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
