{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:07:06.807Z","ordinal":463203,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18343-e336-7683-b68c-da2cf04a70e6","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** for the reviewed change. The worktree is clean at `535b39fe9be6245883b73f603a4daeac2081a717`; there is no uncommitted diff. I reviewed its delta from the requested base `f771590b0da201f5d3f83897f9d2d8a0ce5cee91`. That delta’s SHA-256 is `c7453061823528282610d25571706eeafa32899daf6ab2ab342cfa33a85e503c`.\n\nWrite paths still reject symlink ancestors, while removal paths permit external or dangling symlink ancestors; cleanup itself skips symlinked parents ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:233), [checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:412), [checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:1014)). Removal runs before checkout can install checkpoint symlinks ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:1025)). The regression covers preserving ignored data when a checkpoint symlink could redirect deletion ([checkpoint_restore.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:657)).\n\nNo tests were run."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1833c-73d2-7c02-b686-29bb10a812d6","create_time":1793203626.806988,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":22063}}
