{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:07:47.432Z","ordinal":463236,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a18344-81e8-72c1-b08d-9e060b360908","call_id":"call_7b4b7391c9a94975972db08e106e318a","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/review_pr302\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** for the reviewed change. The worktree is clean at `535b39fe9be6245883b73f603a4daeac2081a717`; there is no uncommitted diff. I reviewed its delta from the requested base `f771590b0da201f5d3f83897f9d2d8a0ce5cee91`. That delta’s SHA-256 is `c7453061823528282610d25571706eeafa32899daf6ab2ab342cfa33a85e503c`.\\n\\nWrite paths still reject symlink ancestors, while removal paths permit external or dangling symlink ancestors; cleanup itself skips symlinked parents ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:233), [checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:412), [checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:1014)). Removal runs before checkout can install checkpoint symlinks ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:1025)). The regression covers preserving ignored data when a checkpoint symlink could redirect deletion ([checkpoint_restore.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:657)).\\n\\nNo tests were run.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1833c-73d2-7c02-b686-29bb10a812d6","create_time":1793203667.4327803}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
