_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a162a0-311d-7271-a76d-8992331bb312","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_pr_file_patch"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16af7-b30b-7543-b5d3-5d0470af8bf9","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_branches"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16b07-bb74-7501-b966-9445743dc69f","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_issue"},{"first_turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"create_agent_identity"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16f03-b5c2-7ab2-ba06-07db849a401d","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_issues"},{"first_turn_id":"01a177a5-7619-7f61-94e2-64d374be9e23","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"observation_search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a17ded-e7ae-7300-8479-0fca92a43367","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_user_login"},{"first_turn_id":"01a18105-4b30-7810-8340-21a990975e0a","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"get_observations"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1819d-146d-73e2-bca2-ef6bf60c3b33","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_search"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1819d-146d-73e2-bca2-ef6bf60c3b33","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_field_report"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a1833c-73d2-7c02-b686-29bb10a812d6","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a1833c-73d2-7c02-b686-29bb10a812d6","turn_id":"01a1833c-73d2-7c02-b686-29bb10a812d6","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae21a9f7104819fbb9357ea44b0a0da","order":22045,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18338-0078-7342-8454-92c09aea432c","text":"While the exact-head CI runs, I’m also checking whether the connected Ubuntu desktop can now support the previously blocked real-terminal qualification setup. I’ll inspect host availability only; I won’t count any automated or synthetic terminal session as manual acceptance.","turn_id":"01a1832d-e18e-7161-a886-2d19338160bd"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae21bb2ef84819fa4c19710f954f34d","order":22049,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a1833c-3eaf-7802-bb4e-a9f24ac1c31a","text":"**Campaign status: `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`.**\n\nI advanced PR #302’s checkpoint restore fix. Commit [`f771590b`](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/commit/f771590b0da201f5d3f83897f9d2d8a0ce5cee91) is now the verified remote head of [PR #302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302). It preflights tracked deletions and exact-directory destinations before `read-tree`, with regressions for nested repositories and bare-repository destinations. Independent source review **ACCEPTED** the diff; `tsc --noEmit` and `git diff --check` passed.\n\nExact-head CI on `f771590b` is still running its Node 22/24 test suites. CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript checks pass; Entire Gates are pending. I did not run local tests because Kimi still owns the active SUITE claim. I recorded the review and validation status in the PR.\n\nI also verified the Ubuntu desktop is reachable and has all five required terminal environments installed. An xterm 80×24 window is open with RC10 in a disposable workspace, **for setup only**; no manual acceptance evidence was collected. RC10 is not the final candidate, so this does not count toward the final terminal matrix.\n\nEntire history lookup remains unavailable: `entire auth status` reports this host is not logged in, and search failed on the missing Secret Service. No login was initiated. No RC was accepted, and no stable release was published.","turn_id":"01a1832d-e18e-7161-a886-2d19338160bd"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae21bc56fe0819f959480dff9e04aed","order":22050,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1833c-7e15-7a12-b6f3-ef8f873e890a","text":"I’m resuming from the current evidence rather than assuming the last CI state. I’ll check PR #302’s exact-head conclusions first, then take the next safe release-critical action while respecting the still-active suite claim.","turn_id":"01a1833c-73d2-7c02-b686-29bb10a812d6"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae21ca97e50819f9ce81c9bca44ee8d","order":22054,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1833f-f9c9-7190-8aec-9ed8fefb819f","text":"The exact-head suites are still progressing through `npm --prefix cli test` (started 15:52Z on Node 24 and 15:53Z on Node 22); they have not failed or completed. PR #302’s current base is eight main commits behind, and those main-only changes do not touch the checkpoint files. I’ll update/requalify the PR on the latest main after this run finishes.","turn_id":"01a1833c-73d2-7c02-b686-29bb10a812d6"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae21d36a3c8819fb359423e8e2bad17","order":22058,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18342-2046-7f31-a91a-95cee2d8ff31","text":"Node 24’s exact-head job has failed at `npm --prefix cli test`; earlier build, Rust tests, packaging prerequisites, and requirements checks passed. Node 22 and the run are still active. I’m retrieving the failed job’s test output to classify the failure before changing code.","turn_id":"01a1833c-73d2-7c02-b686-29bb10a812d6"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae21d66992c819f8c43736453fa5ea7","order":22059,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18342-dbd0-75f3-85af-fbbae735bc44","text":"CI found one regression in the new preflight: an existing test expects tracked-deletion cleanup to leave an external symlink target untouched and let restore succeed. I’ve narrowed the preflight so writes remain strict, while removal paths preserve that safe skip behavior and still reject nested repositories inside the workspace. I’m checking the corrected diff and will re-review it before updating the PR.","turn_id":"01a1833c-73d2-7c02-b686-29bb10a812d6"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae21dae57c4819fb9b3ddcd72ca315f","order":22064,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18343-f397-7f82-812c-95acc8d74b44","text":"The reviewer returned ACCEPT on a correction at `535b39fe`, which differs from the uncommitted tree I last inspected. I’m reconciling the shared branch and PR refs now before acting further; I’ll verify the exact commit and whether the correction was committed or pushed by another lane.","turn_id":"01a1833c-73d2-7c02-b686-29bb10a812d6"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae21e6ecf28819fa0ca7a1df0170d25","order":22069,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a18346-eee0-7030-a699-6f63412bcd78","text":"PR #302 is now rebased onto current `main` (`145d464`) at `c390177`, and independent review ACCEPTED the full rebased diff. The previous Node 24 run exposed one real regression; that correction is in the rebased candidate. On the new exact head, CodeQL and JavaScript/TypeScript pass; both Node matrix jobs have passed build and are running Rust tests.","turn_id":"01a1833c-73d2-7c02-b686-29bb10a812d6"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":22072,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c\nSo