{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:20:31.435Z","ordinal":463789,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18350-2a4a-74f0-a680-495615a0f8e4","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — reviewed `c39017746f4d8be74062508021b3539ab61a7007..49a2af0c1d556912d12b834aa7f2022ef63b528c`. Diff SHA-256: `26ce020bdc1f6865e194f02e45c6889eaa32415cc786a457fbcfae1ddaa78605`.\n\nFor subdirectory workspaces, `checkout-index` now runs from the repository root with a top-anchored literal pathspec for the workspace prefix, so sibling index entries are not checked out ([checkpoint.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/src/checkpoint.ts:1099)). The regression now gives the sibling distinct staged and unstaged content and asserts both the sibling worktree content and index entry survive ([checkpoint_restore.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix/cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:729)). No new issue found; no tests were run."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","create_time":1793204431.434991,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":22089}}
