{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:22:55.189Z","ordinal":463864,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae22153cadc819f972f951059b45c31","usage":{"input_tokens":134954,"cached_input_tokens":134272,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1226,"reasoning_output_tokens":1080,"total_tokens":136180},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5240226,"cached_input_tokens":5188352,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18721,"reasoning_output_tokens":11862,"total_tokens":5258947},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8611200721,"cached_input_tokens":8519266944,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24556835,"reasoning_output_tokens":14218318,"total_tokens":8635757556}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:22:56.767Z","ordinal":463865,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-09cb68cc-7306-4c4d-ba54-62ab709b6c07","process_id":"34168","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","entire agent-help; entire checkpoint --help; entire auth status"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire agent-help; entire checkpoint --help; entire auth status"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"Entire's CLI is the source of truth for its own usage. Do not guess flags or\nsubcommands — read them from this command. You are already inside the repo:\nentire auto-detects it from the git origin remote, so never ask the user for the\nrepo name. Pass --repo only to target a DIFFERENT repo.\nTrails are project-scoped. Trail listing requires an explicit --project; --repo only filters within it.\n\nCurrent repo: gh/mikeholownych/nexus-code  (auto-detected from origin; pass --repo only for a DIFFERENT repo)\n\nWhen to use entire — the commands that bear on the work:\n  checkpoint  Inspect and search checkpoints\n                read-only except: delete, explain\n  search      Search checkpoints, commits, and sessions using semantic and keyword matching\n                read-only\n  session     Manage agent sessions tracked by Entire\n                read-only except: adopt, attach, resume, stop\n  status      Show Entire status\n                read-only\n  trail       Manage trails across repositories and branches\n                read-only: approvals, list, show, watch — others write\n  why         Show why a line exists\n                read-only\n\nAlso available (entire agent-help <command> for any of these):\n  read-only, safe to run:\n    activity · labs · recap · version\n  when the task needs them:\n    api · dispatch · doctor\n  the user's — suggest, don't run:\n    agent · auth · clean · cluster · configure · disable · enable\n    login · logout · org · plugin · project · repo\n\nDrill in for exact, currently-installed flags:  entire agent-help <command>  (e.g. entire agent-help checkpoint)\nAdd --json for structured output.\nOperations on checkpoints — the persistent records of agent work tied to commits.\n\nCommands:\n  list     List checkpoints on the current branch\n  explain  Explain a checkpoint, commit, or session\n  tokens   Show token usage and optimization recommendations\n  search   Search checkpoints (semantic + keyword)\n  delete   Delete a checkpoint locally and from checkpoint remotes\n\nExamples:\n  entire checkpoint list\n  entire checkpoint explain <id|sha>\n  entire checkpoint tokens <id>\n  entire checkpoint search \"fix login\"\n  entire checkpoint delete <id> --dry-run\n\nUsage:\n  entire checkpoint [command]\n\nAliases:\n  checkpoint, cp, checkpoints\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  delete      Delete a checkpoint locally and from checkpoint remotes\n  explain     Explain a session, commit, or checkpoint\n  list        List checkpoints on the current branch\n  search      Search checkpoints, commits, and sessions using semantic and keyword matching\n  tokens      Show token usage and optimization recommendations for a checkpoint\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for checkpoint\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire checkpoint [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n○ Not logged in to us.auth.entire.io\nRun 'entire login' to authenticate.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":175944038}},"started_at_ms":1793204576590,"completed_at_ms":1793204576767}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:22:58.038Z","ordinal":463866,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18352-66f6-7071-9645-f8956777ee62","call_id":"call_72745b0418144d19bb779f8d2d5071cc","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Entire's CLI is the source of truth for its own usage. Do not guess flags or\nsubcommands — read them from this command. You are already inside the repo:\nentire auto-detects it from the git origin remote, so never ask the user for the\nrepo name. Pass --repo only to target a DIFFERENT repo.\nTrails are project-scoped. Trail listing requires an explicit --project; --repo only filters within it.\n\nCurrent repo: gh/mikeholownych/nexus-code  (auto-detected from origin; pass --repo only for a DIFFERENT repo)\n\nWhen to use entire — the commands that bear on the work:\n  checkpoint  Inspect and search checkpoints\n                read-only except: delete, explain\n  search      Search checkpoints, commits, and sessions using semantic and keyword matching\n                read-only\n  session     Manage agent sessions tracked by Entire\n                read-only except: adopt, attach, resume, stop\n  status      Show Entire status\n                read-only\n  trail       Manage trails across repositories and branches\n                read-only: approvals, list, show, watch — others write\n  why         Show why a line exists\n                read-only\n\nAlso available (entire agent-help <command> for any of these):\n  read-only, safe to run:\n    activity · labs · recap · version\n  when the task needs them:\n    api · dispatch · doctor\n  the user's — suggest, don't run:\n    agent · auth · clean · cluster · configure · disable · enable\n    login · logout · org · plugin · project · repo\n\nDrill in for exact, currently-installed flags:  entire agent-help <command>  (e.g. entire agent-help checkpoint)\nAdd --json for structured output.\nOperations on checkpoints — the persistent records of agent work tied to commits.\n\nCommands:\n  list     List checkpoints on the current branch\n  explain  Explain a checkpoint, commit, or session\n  tokens   Show token usage and optimization recommendations\n  search   Search checkpoints (semantic + keyword)\n  delete   Delete a checkpoint locally and from checkpoint remotes\n\nExamples:\n  entire checkpoint list\n  entire checkpoint explain <id|sha>\n  entire checkpoint tokens <id>\n  entire checkpoint search \"fix login\"\n  entire checkpoint delete <id> --dry-run\n\nUsage:\n  entire checkpoint [command]\n\nAliases:\n  checkpoint, cp, checkpoints\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  delete      Delete a checkpoint locally and from checkpoint remotes\n  explain     Explain a session, commit, or checkpoint\n  list        List checkpoints on the current branch\n  search      Search checkpoints, commits, and sessions using semantic and keyword matching\n  tokens      Show token usage and optimization recommendations for a checkpoint\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for checkpoint\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire checkpoint [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n○ Not logged in to us.auth.entire.io\nRun 'entire login' to authenticate.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","create_time":1793204578.0381217}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
