{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:23:00.003Z","ordinal":463871,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae2216263a0819f88485f3495467b40","usage":{"input_tokens":136854,"cached_input_tokens":134912,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":126,"reasoning_output_tokens":60,"total_tokens":136980},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5377080,"cached_input_tokens":5323264,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18847,"reasoning_output_tokens":11922,"total_tokens":5395927},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8611337575,"cached_input_tokens":8519401856,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24556961,"reasoning_output_tokens":14218378,"total_tokens":8635894536}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:23:01.557Z","ordinal":463872,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-1a8473f5-8337-47d5-a7f1-e2f0c4b78bbd","process_id":"6968","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","entire agent-help trail; entire trail --help; entire agent-help review"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire agent-help trail; entire trail --help; entire agent-help review"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"entire trail — Manage trails across repositories and branches\nA trail captures project intent across repositories and branches. Manage intent and discussions on the whole trail; use --repo and --branch to select context for checkout, sessions, findings, and approvals.\n\nWhen to use this:\nTrail commands talk to entire.io and read the saved login from the OS\nkeyring (the Keychain on macOS), so they need network and keyring access.\nIf you run commands in a sandbox, request unsandboxed execution for\n`entire trail` up front. An error saying the Keychain is not accessible or\nthe network is not allowed means the sandbox blocked it, not that the user\nis logged out: ask to re-run it unsandboxed, and do not run `entire login`.\n\nA project trail spans repositories; each change is its branch in one\nrepository. Project trails and changes are numbered separately: never\npass <P> where a change is expected, or <n> where a project trail is.\nPass <repo>/<n> to checkout, resume, finding, watch, approvals or\napprove; given to show, it shows the parent project trail.\nUsers paste Entire trail URLs. Do not pass a URL to any command; map\nthe path after the host to a selector:\n  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<repo>/<n>  change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<n>  change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/trails/<n>                change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>                     project trail <P>\nAdd --project <forge>/<project> unless <project> is origin's owner.\nTo link a trail or change, use the url `entire trail show` prints.\n\nCurrent repo: gh/mikeholownych/nexus-code  (auto-detected from origin; pass --repo only for a DIFFERENT repo)\n\nFlags:\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nInherited flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nSubcommands: approvals · approve · checkout · comment · create · finding · link · list · merge · resume · show · unlink · update · watch\n             read-only: approvals, list, show, watch — others write\nNext:  entire agent-help trail <subcommand>\nA trail captures project intent across repositories and branches. Manage intent and discussions on the whole trail; use --repo and --branch to select context for checkout, sessions, findings, and approvals.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail [flags]\n  entire trail [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  approvals       List approval decisions on a trail\n  approve         Approve a trail\n  checkout        Check out a trail's branch\n  comment         Discuss the whole trail across repositories\n  create          Create a trail and publish its branch\n  finding         Manage a trail's agent findings\n  link            Link a repository branch to a trail\n  list            List trails in a project\n  merge           Merge one of a trail's changes into its base\n  resume          Resume a trail's agent session\n  show            Show trail intent and its repositories and branches\n  unlink          Unlink a repository branch without deleting its work\n  update          Update project intent and lifecycle\n  watch           Tail events for a trail's selected repository branch\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help             help for trail\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire trail [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\nUsage:\n  entire [flags]\n  entire [command]\n\nEntire Setup:\n  agent                      Manage agent integrations (add, remove, list)\n  clean                      Clean up Entire session data\n  configure                  Update Entire settings in the current repository\n  disable                    Disable Entire in current repository\n  doctor                     Diagnose and fix session issues\n  enable                     Enable Entire in current repository\n  plugin                     Manage Entire plugins (install, list, upgrade, search, remove)\n  status                     Show Entire status\n\nSessions & Checkpoints:\n  activity                   Show your activity overview\n  checkpoint                 Inspect and search checkpoints\n  dispatch                   Generate a dispatch summarizing recent agent work\n  recap                      Summarize recent checkpoint activity\n  search                     Search checkpoints, commits, and sessions using semantic and keyword matching\n  session                    Manage agent sessions tracked by Entire\n\nTrails:\n  trail                      Manage trails across repositories and branches\n\nAccount:\n  auth                       Manage authentication\n  login                      Log in to Entire\n  logout                     Log out of Entire\n\nControl Plane:\n  api                        Make an authenticated request to an Entire API and print the response\n  cluster                    Show the Entire clusters you can place projects and repos on\n  org                        Manage Entire organizations\n  project                    Manage Entire projects\n  repo                       Manage Entire repositories\n\nAdditional Commands:\n  agent-help                 Machine-readable usage for coding agents (always matches the installed CLI)\n  help                       Help about any command\n  labs                       Explore experimental Entire workflows\n  version                    Show build information\n\nFlags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n\nError: Invalid usage: unknown command \"review\"; run `entire agent-help` for the list of commands\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":169127088}},"started_at_ms":1793204581387,"completed_at_ms":1793204581557}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:23:03.092Z","ordinal":463873,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18352-7ab4-7f12-be47-8b2545fa940a","call_id":"call_76c8b99435194cf5a5827a9fd6a81bca","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"entire trail — Manage trails across repositories and branches\nA trail captures project intent across repositories and branches. Manage intent and discussions on the whole trail; use --repo and --branch to select context for checkout, sessions, findings, and approvals.\n\nWhen to use this:\nTrail commands talk to entire.io and read the saved login from the OS\nkeyring (the Keychain on macOS), so they need network and keyring access.\nIf you run commands in a sandbox, request unsandboxed execution for\n`entire trail` up front. An error saying the Keychain is not accessible or\nthe network is not allowed means the sandbox blocked it, not that the user\nis logged out: ask to re-run it unsandboxed, and do not run `entire login`.\n\nA project trail spans repositories; each change is its branch in one\nrepository. Project trails and changes are numbered separately: never\npass <P> where a change is expected, or <n> where a project trail is.\nPass <repo>/<n> to checkout, resume, finding, watch, approvals or\napprove; given to show, it shows the parent project trail.\nUsers paste Entire trail URLs. Do not pass a URL to any command; map\nthe path after the host to a selector:\n  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<repo>/<n>  change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<n>  change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/trails/<n>                change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>                     project trail <P>\nAdd --project <forge>/<project> unless <project> is origin's owner.\nTo link a trail or change, use the url `entire trail show` prints.\n\nCurrent repo: gh/mikeholownych/nexus-code  (auto-detected from origin; pass --repo only for a DIFFERENT repo)\n\nFlags:\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nInherited flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nSubcommands: approvals · approve · checkout · comment · create · finding · link · list · merge · resume · show · unlink · update · watch\n             read-only: approvals, list, show, watch — others write\nNext:  entire agent-help trail <subcommand>\nA trail captures project intent across repositories and branches. Manage intent and discussions on the whole trail; use --repo and --branch to select context for checkout, sessions, findings, and approvals.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail [flags]\n  entire trail [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  approvals       List approval decisions on a trail\n  approve         Approve a trail\n  checkout        Check out a trail's branch\n  comment         Discuss the whole trail across repositories\n  create          Create a trail and publish its branch\n  finding         Manage a trail's agent findings\n  link            Link a repository branch to a trail\n  list            List trails in a project\n  merge           Merge one of a trail's changes into its base\n  resume          Resume a trail's agent session\n  show            Show trail intent and its repositories and branches\n  unlink          Unlink a repository branch without deleting its work\n  update          Update project intent and lifecycle\n  watch           Tail events for a trail's selected repository branch\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help             help for trail\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire trail [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\nUsage:\n  entire [flags]\n  entire [command]\n\nEntire Setup:\n  agent                      Manage agent integrations (add, remove, list)\n  clean                      Clean up Entire session data\n  configure                  Update Entire settings in the current repository\n  disable                    Disable Entire in current repository\n  doctor                     Diagnose and fix session issues\n  enable                     Enable Entire in current repository\n  plugin                     Manage Entire plugins (install, list, upgrade, search, remove)\n  status                     Show Entire status\n\nSessions & Checkpoints:\n  activity                   Show your activity overview\n  checkpoint                 Inspect and search checkpoints\n  dispatch                   Generate a dispatch summarizing recent agent work\n  recap                      Summarize recent checkpoint activity\n  search                     Search checkpoints, commits, and sessions using semantic and keyword matching\n  session                    Manage agent sessions tracked by Entire\n\nTrails:\n  trail                      Manage trails across repositories and branches\n\nAccount:\n  auth                       Manage authentication\n  login                      Log in to Entire\n  logout                     Log out of Entire\n\nControl Plane:\n  api                        Make an authenticated request to an Entire API and print the response\n  cluster                    Show the Entire clusters you can place projects and repos on\n  org                        Manage Entire organizations\n  project                    Manage Entire projects\n  repo                       Manage Entire repositories\n\nAdditional Commands:\n  agent-help                 Machine-readable usage for coding agents (always matches the installed CLI)\n  help                       Help about any command\n  labs                       Explore experimental Entire workflows\n  version                    Show build information\n\nFlags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n\nError: Invalid usage: unknown command \"review\"; run `entire agent-help` for the list of commands\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","create_time":1793204583.0924873}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
