{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:23:08.500Z","ordinal":463878,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae221675844819fb3a04b7ed8e2d3c7","usage":{"input_tokens":138315,"cached_input_tokens":136832,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":555,"reasoning_output_tokens":492,"total_tokens":138870},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5515395,"cached_input_tokens":5460096,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":19402,"reasoning_output_tokens":12414,"total_tokens":5534797},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8611475890,"cached_input_tokens":8519538688,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24557516,"reasoning_output_tokens":14218870,"total_tokens":8636033406}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:23:09.995Z","ordinal":463879,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-753599a7-925a-40f6-b968-41e5593d6e8f","process_id":"17082","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","entire agent-help trail approvals; entire trail approvals --help"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire agent-help trail approvals; entire trail approvals --help"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"entire trail approvals — List approval decisions on a trail\n\nWhen to use this:\nTrail commands talk to entire.io and read the saved login from the OS\nkeyring (the Keychain on macOS), so they need network and keyring access.\nIf you run commands in a sandbox, request unsandboxed execution for\n`entire trail` up front. An error saying the Keychain is not accessible or\nthe network is not allowed means the sandbox blocked it, not that the user\nis logged out: ask to re-run it unsandboxed, and do not run `entire login`.\n\nA project trail spans repositories; each change is its branch in one\nrepository. Project trails and changes are numbered separately: never\npass <P> where a change is expected, or <n> where a project trail is.\nPass <repo>/<n> to checkout, resume, finding, watch, approvals or\napprove; given to show, it shows the parent project trail.\nUsers paste Entire trail URLs. Do not pass a URL to any command; map\nthe path after the host to a selector:\n  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<repo>/<n>  change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<n>  change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/trails/<n>                change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>                     project trail <P>\nAdd --project <forge>/<project> unless <project> is origin's owner.\nTo link a trail or change, use the url `entire trail show` prints.\n\nCurrent repo: gh/mikeholownych/nexus-code  (auto-detected from origin; pass --repo only for a DIFFERENT repo)\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string   Select a repository branch within the trail\n      --json            Output as JSON\n\nInherited flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\nList approval decisions on a trail\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail approvals [<trail>] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string   Select a repository branch within the trail\n  -h, --help            help for approvals\n      --json            Output as JSON\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":86868861}},"started_at_ms":1793204589907,"completed_at_ms":1793204589994}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:23:11.768Z","ordinal":463880,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18352-9c98-7341-967b-27fb01415d25","call_id":"call_6bd933d5eb1b46b3aca3890af4911743","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"entire trail approvals — List approval decisions on a trail\n\nWhen to use this:\nTrail commands talk to entire.io and read the saved login from the OS\nkeyring (the Keychain on macOS), so they need network and keyring access.\nIf you run commands in a sandbox, request unsandboxed execution for\n`entire trail` up front. An error saying the Keychain is not accessible or\nthe network is not allowed means the sandbox blocked it, not that the user\nis logged out: ask to re-run it unsandboxed, and do not run `entire login`.\n\nA project trail spans repositories; each change is its branch in one\nrepository. Project trails and changes are numbered separately: never\npass <P> where a change is expected, or <n> where a project trail is.\nPass <repo>/<n> to checkout, resume, finding, watch, approvals or\napprove; given to show, it shows the parent project trail.\nUsers paste Entire trail URLs. Do not pass a URL to any command; map\nthe path after the host to a selector:\n  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<repo>/<n>  change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<n>  change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/trails/<n>                change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>                     project trail <P>\nAdd --project <forge>/<project> unless <project> is origin's owner.\nTo link a trail or change, use the url `entire trail show` prints.\n\nCurrent repo: gh/mikeholownych/nexus-code  (auto-detected from origin; pass --repo only for a DIFFERENT repo)\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string   Select a repository branch within the trail\n      --json            Output as JSON\n\nInherited flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\nList approval decisions on a trail\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail approvals [<trail>] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string   Select a repository branch within the trail\n  -h, --help            help for approvals\n      --json            Output as JSON\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","create_time":1793204591.7680943}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
