{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:23:36.927Z","ordinal":463908,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae2218382a4819f85d87f4ff792606f","usage":{"input_tokens":140237,"cached_input_tokens":139904,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":509,"reasoning_output_tokens":440,"total_tokens":140746},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6074918,"cached_input_tokens":6017408,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":20383,"reasoning_output_tokens":13041,"total_tokens":6095301},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8612035413,"cached_input_tokens":8520096000,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24558497,"reasoning_output_tokens":14219497,"total_tokens":8636593910}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:23:38.382Z","ordinal":463909,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a6d07798-7ba4-4df2-a117-a6025d9e576a","process_id":"33690","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","entire agent-help trail approve; entire trail approve --help; entire agent-help trail show"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire agent-help trail approve; entire trail approve --help; entire agent-help trail show"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"entire trail approve — Approve a trail\nApprove a trail.\n\n<trail> is a project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number>. Without one, follow the current branch's\nparent. --repo and --branch select a working context. Only that branch is approved,\nnot every repository on the trail. The branch work must be open.\n\nWhen to use this:\nTrail commands talk to entire.io and read the saved login from the OS\nkeyring (the Keychain on macOS), so they need network and keyring access.\nIf you run commands in a sandbox, request unsandboxed execution for\n`entire trail` up front. An error saying the Keychain is not accessible or\nthe network is not allowed means the sandbox blocked it, not that the user\nis logged out: ask to re-run it unsandboxed, and do not run `entire login`.\n\nA project trail spans repositories; each change is its branch in one\nrepository. Project trails and changes are numbered separately: never\npass <P> where a change is expected, or <n> where a project trail is.\nPass <repo>/<n> to checkout, resume, finding, watch, approvals or\napprove; given to show, it shows the parent project trail.\nUsers paste Entire trail URLs. Do not pass a URL to any command; map\nthe path after the host to a selector:\n  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<repo>/<n>  change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<n>  change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/trails/<n>                change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>                     project trail <P>\nAdd --project <forge>/<project> unless <project> is origin's owner.\nTo link a trail or change, use the url `entire trail show` prints.\n\nCurrent repo: gh/mikeholownych/nexus-code  (auto-detected from origin; pass --repo only for a DIFFERENT repo)\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string    Select a repository branch within the trail\n  -m, --message string   Optional approval comment\n\nInherited flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\nApprove a trail.\n\n<trail> is a project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number>. Without one, follow the current branch's\nparent. --repo and --branch select a working context. Only that branch is approved,\nnot every repository on the trail. The branch work must be open.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail approve [<trail>] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string    Select a repository branch within the trail\n  -h, --help             help for approve\n  -m, --message string   Optional approval comment\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\nentire trail show — Show trail intent and its repositories and branches\nShow a project trail by its project-local number or ULID, or the trail of <repo>/<number> branch work. Without a selector, follow the current branch's parent. Use --branch to follow another branch's parent.\n\nWhen to use this:\nTrail commands talk to entire.io and read the saved login from the OS\nkeyring (the Keychain on macOS), so they need network and keyring access.\nIf you run commands in a sandbox, request unsandboxed execution for\n`entire trail` up front. An error saying the Keychain is not accessible or\nthe network is not allowed means the sandbox blocked it, not that the user\nis logged out: ask to re-run it unsandboxed, and do not run `entire login`.\n\nA project trail spans repositories; each change is its branch in one\nrepository. Project trails and changes are numbered separately: never\npass <P> where a change is expected, or <n> where a project trail is.\nPass <repo>/<n> to checkout, resume, finding, watch, approvals or\napprove; given to show, it shows the parent project trail.\nUsers paste Entire trail URLs. Do not pass a URL to any command; map\nthe path after the host to a selector:\n  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<repo>/<n>  change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<n>  change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/trails/<n>                change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>                     project trail <P>\nAdd --project <forge>/<project> unless <project> is origin's owner.\nTo link a trail or change, use the url `entire trail show` prints.\n\nTo list a project trail's changes, run `entire trail show <P>\n--project <forge>/<project> --json`; each changes[] entry is the change\n<repository>/<number> with its own url. When show reaches the trail\nthrough a change (the current branch, --branch, or <repo>/<n>), that\nentry has current: true; link its url, the change's page, in preference\nto the top-level url, the whole trail's page. When asked to act on\n(e.g. review) a whole project trail, cover every change. Checkout and\nreview need a clone of that repository: do the ones in this clone and\ntell the user which changes need another clone instead of skipping\nthem silently.\n\nCurrent repo: gh/mikeholownych/nexus-code  (auto-detected from origin; pass --repo only for a DIFFERENT repo)\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string   Discover the project trail through this repository branch (defaults to current branch when no trail is given)\n      --json            Output raw JSON instead of a table\n\nInherited flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":168087750}},"started_at_ms":1793204618213,"completed_at_ms":1793204618382}}
