{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:25:20.313Z","ordinal":463970,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae221eda610819fac86189c0b4f5d6c","usage":{"input_tokens":148755,"cached_input_tokens":147328,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":213,"reasoning_output_tokens":150,"total_tokens":148968},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":7091037,"cached_input_tokens":7024384,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24369,"reasoning_output_tokens":16027,"total_tokens":7115406},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8613051532,"cached_input_tokens":8521102976,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24562483,"reasoning_output_tokens":14222483,"total_tokens":8637614015}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:25:22.217Z","ordinal":463971,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-87de6342-5cdf-4e42-9771-1b5ad82bdc7e","process_id":"43559","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","entire agent-help trail finding; entire trail finding --help"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire agent-help trail finding; entire trail finding --help"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"entire trail finding — Manage a trail's agent findings\nManage a trail's agent-native findings.\n\nRunning 'entire trail finding' shows the finding dashboard for the current\nbranch's trail. Pass a project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> to inspect another trail.\n--repo and --branch select the working context; findings apply only to that\nbranch, not the whole trail. Use 'entire trail list' to discover trails.\n\nWhen to use this:\nTrail commands talk to entire.io and read the saved login from the OS\nkeyring (the Keychain on macOS), so they need network and keyring access.\nIf you run commands in a sandbox, request unsandboxed execution for\n`entire trail` up front. An error saying the Keychain is not accessible or\nthe network is not allowed means the sandbox blocked it, not that the user\nis logged out: ask to re-run it unsandboxed, and do not run `entire login`.\n\nA project trail spans repositories; each change is its branch in one\nrepository. Project trails and changes are numbered separately: never\npass <P> where a change is expected, or <n> where a project trail is.\nPass <repo>/<n> to checkout, resume, finding, watch, approvals or\napprove; given to show, it shows the parent project trail.\nUsers paste Entire trail URLs. Do not pass a URL to any command; map\nthe path after the host to a selector:\n  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<repo>/<n>  change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<n>  change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/trails/<n>                change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>                     project trail <P>\nAdd --project <forge>/<project> unless <project> is origin's owner.\nTo link a trail or change, use the url `entire trail show` prints.\n\nCurrent repo: gh/mikeholownych/nexus-code  (auto-detected from origin; pass --repo only for a DIFFERENT repo)\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string       Select a repository branch within the trail\n      --cursor string       Continue from the next cursor returned by a previous page\n      --freshness string    Filter code-version freshness: current,stale,any (default \"current\")\n      --include-dismissed   Include dismissed findings\n      --json                Output as JSON\n  -n, --limit int           Maximum number of findings to show (default 100)\n      --severity string     Filter by comma-separated severity value(s): high,medium,low\n      --status string       Filter by lifecycle status(es): open,resolved,dismissed; use 'any' for all (default \"open\")\n      --trail string        Project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> (defaults to the current branch's parent)\n\nInherited flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nSubcommands: add · apply · dismiss · list · reopen · resolve · show · update\n             task-driven\nNext:  entire agent-help trail finding <subcommand>\nManage a trail's agent-native findings.\n\nRunning 'entire trail finding' shows the finding dashboard for the current\nbranch's trail. Pass a project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> to inspect another trail.\n--repo and --branch select the working context; findings apply only to that\nbranch, not the whole trail. Use 'entire trail list' to discover trails.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail finding [<trail>] [flags]\n  entire trail finding [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  add         Create a finding on a trail\n  apply       Apply a finding's unified-diff suggestion\n  dismiss     Dismiss a finding\n  list        List findings for a trail\n  reopen      Reopen a finding\n  resolve     Resolve a finding\n  show        Show a finding\n  update      Update a finding's metadata\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string       Select a repository branch within the trail\n      --cursor string       Continue from the next cursor returned by a previous page\n      --freshness string    Filter code-version freshness: current,stale,any (default \"current\")\n  -h, --help                help for finding\n      --include-dismissed   Include dismissed findings\n      --json                Output as JSON\n  -n, --limit int           Maximum number of findings to show (default 100)\n      --severity string     Filter by comma-separated severity value(s): high,medium,low\n      --status string       Filter by lifecycle status(es): open,resolved,dismissed; use 'any' for all (default \"open\")\n      --trail string        Project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> (defaults to the current branch's parent)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nUse \"entire trail finding [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":156645053}},"started_at_ms":1793204722036,"completed_at_ms":1793204722200}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:25:24.366Z","ordinal":463972,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18354-a28e-76a0-890b-ffecc47a2346","call_id":"call_bd21868e73c14325b610b64ab34bb1d8","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"entire trail finding — Manage a trail's agent findings\nManage a trail's agent-native findings.\n\nRunning 'entire trail finding' shows the finding dashboard for the current\nbranch's trail. Pass a project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> to inspect another trail.\n--repo and --branch select the working context; findings apply only to that\nbranch, not the whole trail. Use 'entire trail list' to discover trails.\n\nWhen to use this:\nTrail commands talk to entire.io and read the saved login from the OS\nkeyring (the Keychain on macOS), so they need network and keyring access.\nIf you run commands in a sandbox, request unsandboxed execution for\n`entire trail` up front. An error saying the Keychain is not accessible or\nthe network is not allowed means the sandbox blocked it, not that the user\nis logged out: ask to re-run it unsandboxed, and do not run `entire login`.\n\nA project trail spans repositories; each change is its branch in one\nrepository. Project trails and changes are numbered separately: never\npass <P> where a change is expected, or <n> where a project trail is.\nPass <repo>/<n> to checkout, resume, finding, watch, approvals or\napprove; given to show, it shows the parent project trail.\nUsers paste Entire trail URLs. Do not pass a URL to any command; map\nthe path after the host to a selector:\n  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<repo>/<n>  change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/-/trails/<P>/changes/<n>  change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/<repo>/trails/<n>                change <repo>/<n>\n  <forge>/<project>/-/trails/<P>                     project trail <P>\nAdd --project <forge>/<project> unless <project> is origin's owner.\nTo link a trail or change, use the url `entire trail show` prints.\n\nCurrent repo: gh/mikeholownych/nexus-code  (auto-detected from origin; pass --repo only for a DIFFERENT repo)\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string       Select a repository branch within the trail\n      --cursor string       Continue from the next cursor returned by a previous page\n      --freshness string    Filter code-version freshness: current,stale,any (default \"current\")\n      --include-dismissed   Include dismissed findings\n      --json                Output as JSON\n  -n, --limit int           Maximum number of findings to show (default 100)\n      --severity string     Filter by comma-separated severity value(s): high,medium,low\n      --status string       Filter by lifecycle status(es): open,resolved,dismissed; use 'any' for all (default \"open\")\n      --trail string        Project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> (defaults to the current branch's parent)\n\nInherited flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nSubcommands: add · apply · dismiss · list · reopen · resolve · show · update\n             task-driven\nNext:  entire agent-help trail finding <subcommand>\nManage a trail's agent-native findings.\n\nRunning 'entire trail finding' shows the finding dashboard for the current\nbranch's trail. Pass a project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> to inspect another trail.\n--repo and --branch select the working context; findings apply only to that\nbranch, not the whole trail. Use 'entire trail list' to discover trails.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail finding [<trail>] [flags]\n  entire trail finding [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  add         Create a finding on a trail\n  apply       Apply a finding's unified-diff suggestion\n  dismiss     Dismiss a finding\n  list        List findings for a trail\n  reopen      Reopen a finding\n  resolve     Resolve a finding\n  show        Show a finding\n  update      Update a finding's metadata\n\nFlags:\n      --branch string       Select a repository branch within the trail\n      --cursor string       Continue from the next cursor returned by a previous page\n      --freshness string    Filter code-version freshness: current,stale,any (default \"current\")\n  -h, --help                help for finding\n      --include-dismissed   Include dismissed findings\n      --json                Output as JSON\n  -n, --limit int           Maximum number of findings to show (default 100)\n      --severity string     Filter by comma-separated severity value(s): high,medium,low\n      --status string       Filter by lifecycle status(es): open,resolved,dismissed; use 'any' for all (default \"open\")\n      --trail string        Project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> (defaults to the current branch's parent)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nUse \"entire trail finding [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","create_time":1793204724.3661401}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
