{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:30:46.620Z","ordinal":464177,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-49269614-c5f7-4459-91d6-e1979e16dba6","process_id":"71749","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh run view 40726281681 --json status,conclusion,headSha,jobs --jq '{status,conclusion,headSha,jobs:[.jobs[]|{name,status,conclusion,steps:[.steps[]|select(.status==\"in_progress\" or .conclusion==\"failure\")|{name,status,conclusion}]}]}'; gh pr checks 302; ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=8 mike@10.0.8.3 '/home/mike/.local/bin/entire trail finding list nexus-code/17 --project gh/mikeholownych --json' | jq -r '.counts, (.findings[] | select(.status==\"open\") | [.id,.severity,.staleOutcome,.location.filePath,.location.startLine,(.body|split(\"\\n\")[0])] | @tsv)'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh run view 40726281681 --json status,conclusion,headSha,jobs --jq '{status,conclusion,headSha,jobs:[.jobs[]|{name,status,conclusion,steps:[.steps[]|select(.status==\"in_progress\" or .conclusion==\"failure\")|{name,status,conclusion}]}]}'; gh pr checks 302; ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=8 mike@10.0.8.3 '/home/mike/.local/bin/entire trail finding list nexus-code/17 --project gh/mikeholownych --json' | jq -r '.counts, (.findings[] | select(.status==\"open\") | [.id,.severity,.staleOutcome,.location.filePath,.location.startLine,(.body|split(\"\\n\")[0])] | @tsv)'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"headSha\":\"700d16bb1e3b8050f2dbfe91c4c8fd2f89a6ade4\",\"jobs\":[{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"steps\":[{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"name\":\"Run cargo test --locked --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"}]},{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"steps\":[{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"name\":\"Run cargo build --locked --release --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"}]}],\"status\":\"in_progress\"}\nCodeQL\tpass\t4s\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/122951069680\t\ntest-matrix (22)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40726281681/job/122950316052\t\njavascript-typescript\tpass\t1m25s\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40726281868/job/122950317227\t\nEntire Gates\tpending\t0\thttps://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/17/changes/nexus-code/17\t\ntest-matrix (24)\tpending\t0\thttps://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40726281681/job/122950315719\t\nCodeRabbit\tpass\t0\t\tReview skipped\n{\n  \"Open\": 11,\n  \"OpenHigh\": 0,\n  \"OpenMedium\": 1,\n  \"OpenLow\": 10,\n  \"Resolved\": 0,\n  \"Dismissed\": 0,\n  \"Stale\": 0\n}\n01M61NH13HS04RR184FHAGFVNM\tlow\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t116\tThis code runs only inside the `if (prefix)` path, because the `!prefix` case returned earlier. So `prefix ? [...] : []` and the `workspacePathspec.length ?` check are dead branches. Now that `ls-files` is limited by the `:(top,literal)` pathspec, the `inWorkspace` byte-prefix filter on both entry lists is redundant too. These are leftovers from earlier attempts: pass the pathspec unconditionally and drop the second filter. Better still, replace the whole block with `git reset -q <ref> -- .` run from the workspace.\n01M61MSX4ENBXY9QTT98N45S44\tlow\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t103\t`restoreGitIndex` builds a temporary index, lists both indexes in full with `ls-files --stage`, parses the entries through binary-string round-trips, and writes hand-built `--index-info` delete and add records. All of that only resets the index entries under the workspace prefix. Git already does this in one command: `git reset -q <gitRef> -- .`, run from the workspace with hooks disabled, resets only the matching paths and removes paths that are missing from the checkpoint. Use that instead of keeping a custom index parser, which also drops the `core.fsmonitor=false` flag on its `ls-files` calls.\n01M61JMP021G48EEHD5T0V6SN9\tlow\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t217\tThe new \"ambiguous layout\" rules match on file names alone, so they refuse ordinary project directories. A directory with a `config/` subdirectory next to any `HEAD`, `objects` or `refs` entry fails `!bareConfig.isFile()`. A directory with `objects/` and `refs/` but no `config` fails `hasBareRepositoryShape && !bareConfig`. In both cases restore aborts with \"ambiguous bare Git repository layout\". The lookalike test only covers the case where every marker has its Git type. Ask Git whether the parent is a Git directory (`git -C <parent> rev-parse --git-dir` / `--is-bare-repository`) instead of growing name-based guesses.\n01M61D5NDZKZRHHHS1XF8VXBK7\tmedium\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t212\tThe new bare-repo check hand-parses `config` with regexes and only rejects a parent when `[core] bare` is true. Git doesn't recognise a Git directory that way: it treats a valid `HEAD`, `objects/` and `refs/` as enough. So a gitdir with `bare = false` or no `bare` key (for example a submodule or worktree gitdir), or one whose `bare` comes from an `[include]`, passes this check, and restore will write into it. The parser also misses forms like `[core]bare=true` on one line. Ask Git instead (`git -C <parent> rev-parse --is-bare-repository` / `--git-dir`, or `git config --file <cfg> --type=bool core.bare`), or validate `HEAD` contents the way Git does, instead of keeping a partial config parser here.\n01M61C3JYAE3D3934D411TXF17\tlow\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t193\tSplitting out `assertNoNestedGitRepositoryAncestors` copied its realpath, escape check and ancestor loop into `assertUntrackedDestinationSafe`, so every untracked destination is now walked twice. The two copies already disagree: the new walk silently `break`s on a symlinked or non-directory parent, while the second walk throws. Walk once and run both checks (not a real directory, has `.git`) in that single loop. The tracked-blob path can then call that loop directly.\n01M614XKQJY5ZMCM15GEC67APZ\tlow\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t378\tThe new comment explains why \"a clean preview can be empty\", but the `git clean -nd` preview call was removed in this same edit. The comment now describes the abandoned approach instead of the code beneath it. Rewrite it to say what the walk checks, or drop it.\n01M60XYCRHF2QZ6H2C8NJZJNVE\tlow\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t408\t`directoryContainsOnlyGitCleanRemovableEntries` repeats the same `git check-ignore --no-index` try/catch in its directory branch and its file branch. A third copy appears at line 455, and the call is also used at 485. It spawns one `git` process per descendant entry, so a large untracked directory target means thousands of subprocesses during preflight. Hoist the check into one helper, or run a single `git check-ignore --stdin -z` / `ls-files --others --ignored -z -- <dir>` call for the whole directory.\n01M60S1M740PFJTXBPCV9PX2J8\tlow\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t474\tThe `this.isGit || snapshotDir` condition is always true at this point. A non-Git checkpoint either sets `snapshotDir` or throws before reaching here, so the conditional spread is dead logic. Assign `untrackedFiles: untrackedPaths` directly. The field name is also misleading for non-Git checkpoints, where it holds every workspace file.\n01M60S1M6ZG5AR5A2FN1G6CY56\tlow\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t340\t`assertGitSnapshotTargetsReplaceable` decides safety by comparing human-readable `git clean -nd` output exactly against `Would remove ${relativePath}/`. Git C-quotes paths with non-ASCII or control characters (`core.quotePath` is on by default), so a valid directory target with such a name always fails with a spurious 'preserved by Git clean' error. The same function also refuses restore whenever any tracked `.gitignore` anywhere differs from the checkpoint. That is a coarse heuristic layered on top, not a check of the actual ignore rules that matter. Use machine-readable output (for example `ls-files --others --ignored -z` scoped to the path) instead of matching the porcelain message.\n01M60S1M6VG43E28BBTCR51TNR\tlow\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t243\t`assertLegacyUntrackedRestoreSafe` and `removeTrackedDeletions` both run the same `git diff --name-only --diff-filter=D -z HEAD <ref>` command. The `execFileSync(...).toString(\"utf8\").split(\"\\\\0\").filter(Boolean)` boilerplate is also repeated about six times across the new helpers. A small `gitPathList(args)` helper would remove the duplication and keep the flags (`core.fsmonitor=false`, `maxBuffer`) consistent everywhere.\n01M60S1M6PG8H214MZVTS7EJZK\tlow\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t286\tThe ignored-directory set `[\"node_modules\", \".git\", \"target\", \"dist\", \".nexus\", \".next\", \".cache\"]` now appears in five places: `copyDirFiltered`, `workspaceSnapshotPaths`, `workspaceSnapshotDirectories`, `directoryHasCleanupPreservedEntries` and `removeNonSnapshotEntries`. `workspaceSnapshotPaths` and `workspaceSnapshotDirectories` are also near-identical walkers. If one copy is edited and the others aren't, snapshot, cleanup and restore will disagree about which entries are preserved, which is a data-loss risk. Hoist the set into one constant and use a single walker.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":3,"nanos":447147031}},"started_at_ms":1793205043172,"completed_at_ms":1793205046620}}
