t.ts:801–808`), but this decoding changes the filename\n01M61A9BQMB5AX2RA63XVKVA0Y\tmedium\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t380\tWith an unchanged tracked `.gitignore` containing `a/`, capture an untracked regular file `a`, then replace it with an empty directory\n01M6150QX6BCY3K2QPNPGSWZX1\tmedium\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t231\tAn executable untracked script passes through this call during capture and restore, but `writePrivateFile` defaults to mode `0600` (`cli/src/core/durable_file.ts:127–148`)\n01M6150QX1M25CY0F3N4F5C5M3\tmedium\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t270\tFor a legacy checkpoint that renamed tracked `old.txt` to `new.txt`, restoring after the index returns to HEAD leaves `old.txt` behind\n01M60ZB0XWQ2JV14YBJAXK47TJ\tmedium\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t368\tRenaming a tracked `.gitignore` to `rules` makes `git diff --name-only` report only `rules`, bypassing this guard\n01M60ZB0XA0XV9BM0BXVGZK2J1\tmedium\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t364\tWith a checkpoint tracking `a/child`, replacing directory `a` with a regular file makes this `lstatSync` throw `ENOTDIR` despite `throwIfNoEntry: false`\n01M60Y2YJBXJ4K4PWVFFY8PD7F\tmedium\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t824\tNew checkpoints always contain `untrackedFiles` (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:605`), so this skips collecting their staged additions\n01M60VNF02GTV5H69WNHQ1BB0C\tmedium\tcurrent\tcli/src/checkpoint.ts\t157\tReplacing committed `dir/old.txt` with a regular file `dir` containing different content leaves the deleted descendant in the changed-path list (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:110`)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":386269742}},"started_at_ms":1793205691151,"completed_at_ms":1793205692538}}
