{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:41:49.818Z","ordinal":464589,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae225bfc66c819f84f479d583507ee1","usage":{"input_tokens":239265,"cached_input_tokens":238080,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1579,"reasoning_output_tokens":1446,"total_tokens":240844},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":21476003,"cached_input_tokens":21312384,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":81971,"reasoning_output_tokens":58112,"total_tokens":21557974},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8627436498,"cached_input_tokens":8535390976,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24620085,"reasoning_output_tokens":14264568,"total_tokens":8652056583}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:41:52.909Z","ordinal":464590,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3c654b8b-0446-4fb3-9069-02869aa5805a","process_id":"31059","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=8 mike@10.0.8.3 '/home/mike/.local/bin/entire trail finding list nexus-code/17 --project gh/mikeholownych --severity high,medium --json' | jq -r '.findings[] | \"\\(.id) [\\(.severity)]\\n\\(.body)\\n\"'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=8 mike@10.0.8.3 '/home/mike/.local/bin/entire trail finding list nexus-code/17 --project gh/mikeholownych --severity high,medium --json' | jq -r '.findings[] | \"\\(.id) [\\(.severity)]\\n\\(.body)\\n\"'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"01M61P3F76HN15NJ152KFT1CB5 [medium]\nFor a repository directory ending in a space, `.trim()` changes the path returned by Git, so `realpathSync` looks up a different or nonexistent directory. Checkpoint creation always reaches this through `assertGitChangesSafe` (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:218,777`), making even clean repositories fail; remove only the output terminator and preserve path whitespace in `gitWorkspacePrefix` too.\n\n01M61P3F6W8C1F5WP2AQJY75TF [medium]\nAfter `git merge --no-ff --no-commit`, `/undo` (`cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:111–113`) restores index/worktree contents but leaves `MERGE_HEAD` and `MERGE_MSG` intact; the nested-workspace update at `cli/src/checkpoint.ts:153` does too. Restore reports success while Git still treats the next commit as a merge, potentially recording a merge whose changes were rolled back; clear pending merge state as the previous `reset --hard` did.\n\n01M61NMM8Z9D3EG2SYCRQT3GMW [medium]\nA clean repository with a tracked POSIX filename containing non-UTF-8 bytes can be checkpointed (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:801–808`), but this decoding changes the filename. After that file is edited, restore sends the altered name to `checkout-index` at lines 1107–1113 and cannot restore the original after already replacing the index at line 1098; preserve raw path bytes through enumeration and checkout.\n\n01M61A9BQMB5AX2RA63XVKVA0Y [medium]\nWith an unchanged tracked `.gitignore` containing `a/`, capture an untracked regular file `a`, then replace it with an empty directory. This branch accepts it because the helper checks only children, but Git clean preserves the ignored directory and snapshot copying fails after workspace mutation and cleanup (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:843–849`). Check whether the target directory itself is ignored before allowing mutation.\n\n01M6150QX6BCY3K2QPNPGSWZX1 [medium]\nAn executable untracked script passes through this call during capture and restore, but `writePrivateFile` defaults to mode `0600` (`cli/src/core/durable_file.ts:127–148`). Successful rollback therefore strips its execute bits, making subsequent direct execution fail; capture permission metadata and restore the executable mode.\n\n01M6150QX1M25CY0F3N4F5C5M3 [medium]\nFor a legacy checkpoint that renamed tracked `old.txt` to `new.txt`, restoring after the index returns to HEAD leaves `old.txt` behind. Rename detection excludes it from this deletion scan and the addition scans (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:295–305`), while the legacy restore skips cleaning (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:843–853`), so restore reports success with both files present. Disable rename detection for these path-set comparisons.\n\n01M60ZB0XWQ2JV14YBJAXK47TJ [medium]\nRenaming a tracked `.gitignore` to `rules` makes `git diff --name-only` report only `rules`, bypassing this guard. If the checkpoint captures untracked file `a` and ignores `a/keep`, replacing `a` with directory `a/keep` passes preflight, but checkout restores the ignore rule, clean preserves the directory, and snapshot copying fails after mutation (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:846–852`). Disable rename detection here or inspect both rename paths.\n\n01M60ZB0XA0XV9BM0BXVGZK2J1 [medium]\nWith a checkpoint tracking `a/child`, replacing directory `a` with a regular file makes this `lstatSync` throw `ENOTDIR` despite `throwIfNoEntry: false`. Manifest restores always run this preflight (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:841–843`), so rollback aborts instead of restoring the tracked tree. Handle obstructed descendants during preflight so checkout can replace their ancestors.\n\n01M60Y2YJBXJ4K4PWVFFY8PD7F [medium]\nNew checkpoints always contain `untrackedFiles` (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:605`), so this skips collecting their staged additions. If an ignored file such as `build.log` is force-added after the checkpoint, `read-tree` drops it from the index and `git clean -fd` at line 843 skips it, leaving post-checkpoint content despite reporting success. Collect staged additions before replacing the index for manifest checkpoints too.\n\n01M60VNF02GTV5H69WNHQ1BB0C [medium]\nReplacing committed `dir/old.txt` with a regular file `dir` containing different content leaves the deleted descendant in the changed-path list (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:110`). This `lstatSync` throws `ENOTDIR` despite `throwIfNoEntry: false`, so checkpoint creation aborts through `cli/src/checkpoint.ts:472` for a valid Git state. Treat `ENOTDIR` as a missing worktree entry while retaining symlink-aware inspection.\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":640282989}},"started_at_ms":1793205711268,"completed_at_ms":1793205712908}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:41:54.270Z","ordinal":464591,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18363-bd5d-7761-93cc-83b8aa25dbbc","call_id":"call_ed24641f7fa24a88a51c09dce77a9335","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"01M61P3F76HN15NJ152KFT1CB5 [medium]\nFor a repository directory ending in a space, `.trim()` changes the path returned by Git, so `realpathSync` looks up a different or nonexistent directory. Checkpoint creation always reaches this through `assertGitChangesSafe` (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:218,777`), making even clean repositories fail; remove only the output terminator and preserve path whitespace in `gitWorkspacePrefix` too.\n\n01M61P3F6W8C1F5WP2AQJY75TF [medium]\nAfter `git merge --no-ff --no-commit`, `/undo` (`cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:111–113`) restores index/worktree contents but leaves `MERGE_HEAD` and `MERGE_MSG` intact; the nested-workspace update at `cli/src/checkpoint.ts:153` does too. Restore reports success while Git still treats the next commit as a merge, potentially recording a merge whose changes were rolled back; clear pending merge state as the previous `reset --hard` did.\n\n01M61NMM8Z9D3EG2SYCRQT3GMW [medium]\nA clean repository with a tracked POSIX filename containing non-UTF-8 bytes can be checkpointed (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:801–808`), but this decoding changes the filename. After that file is edited, restore sends the altered name to `checkout-index` at lines 1107–1113 and cannot restore the original after already replacing the index at line 1098; preserve raw path bytes through enumeration and checkout.\n\n01M61A9BQMB5AX2RA63XVKVA0Y [medium]\nWith an unchanged tracked `.gitignore` containing `a/`, capture an untracked regular file `a`, then replace it with an empty directory. This branch accepts it because the helper checks only children, but Git clean preserves the ignored directory and snapshot copying fails after workspace mutation and cleanup (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:843–849`). Check whether the target directory itself is ignored before allowing mutation.\n\n01M6150QX6BCY3K2QPNPGSWZX1 [medium]\nAn executable untracked script passes through this call during capture and restore, but `writePrivateFile` defaults to mode `0600` (`cli/src/core/durable_file.ts:127–148`). Successful rollback therefore strips its execute bits, making subsequent direct execution fail; capture permission metadata and restore the executable mode.\n\n01M6150QX1M25CY0F3N4F5C5M3 [medium]\nFor a legacy checkpoint that renamed tracked `old.txt` to `new.txt`, restoring after the index returns to HEAD leaves `old.txt` behind. Rename detection excludes it from this deletion scan and the addition scans (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:295–305`), while the legacy restore skips cleaning (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:843–853`), so restore reports success with both files present. Disable rename detection for these path-set comparisons.\n\n01M60ZB0XWQ2JV14YBJAXK47TJ [medium]\nRenaming a tracked `.gitignore` to `rules` makes `git diff --name-only` report only `rules`, bypassing this guard. If the checkpoint captures untracked file `a` and ignores `a/keep`, replacing `a` with directory `a/keep` passes preflight, but checkout restores the ignore rule, clean preserves the directory, and snapshot copying fails after mutation (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:846–852`). Disable rename detection here or inspect both rename paths.\n\n01M60ZB0XA0XV9BM0BXVGZK2J1 [medium]\nWith a checkpoint tracking `a/child`, replacing directory `a` with a regular file makes this `lstatSync` throw `ENOTDIR` despite `throwIfNoEntry: false`. Manifest restores always run this preflight (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:841–843`), so rollback aborts instead of restoring the tracked tree. Handle obstructed descendants during preflight so checkout can replace their ancestors.\n\n01M60Y2YJBXJ4K4PWVFFY8PD7F [medium]\nNew checkpoints always contain `untrackedFiles` (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:605`), so this skips collecting their staged additions. If an ignored file such as `build.log` is force-added after the checkpoint, `read-tree` drops it from the index and `git clean -fd` at line 843 skips it, leaving post-checkpoint content despite reporting success. Collect staged additions before replacing the index for manifest checkpoints too.\n\n01M60VNF02GTV5H69WNHQ1BB0C [medium]\nReplacing committed `dir/old.txt` with a regular file `dir` containing different content leaves the deleted descendant in the changed-path list (`cli/src/checkpoint.ts:110`). This `lstatSync` throws `ENOTDIR` despite `throwIfNoEntry: false`, so checkpoint creation aborts through `cli/src/checkpoint.ts:472` for a valid Git state. Treat `ENOTDIR` as a missing worktree entry while retaining symlink-aware inspection.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","create_time":1793205714.2699249}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
