{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:43:15.547Z","ordinal":464653,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae22620a2f8819fb708c98f77a51c59","usage":{"input_tokens":79595,"cached_input_tokens":78208,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":277,"reasoning_output_tokens":205,"total_tokens":79872},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":22335468,"cached_input_tokens":22144640,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":89393,"reasoning_output_tokens":62502,"total_tokens":22424861},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8628295963,"cached_input_tokens":8536223232,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24627507,"reasoning_output_tokens":14268958,"total_tokens":8652923470}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:43:18.069Z","ordinal":464654,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-1869a4f8-7eff-472b-ab46-a1a8242935fa","process_id":"1993","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","entire status; entire search --help; entire checkpoint --help"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire status; entire search --help; entire checkpoint --help"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"○ not set up (run `entire enable` to get started)\nSearch checkpoints, commits, and sessions using hybrid search (semantic + keyword),\npowered by the Entire search service.\n\nRequires authentication via 'entire login' (GitHub device flow).\n\nBy default, results are scoped to the current repository. Use --all-repos to\nsearch across all accessible repos.\n\nRun without arguments to open an interactive search. Results are\ndisplayed in an interactive table. Use --json for machine-readable output,\nand add --compact for a trimmed per-result shape suited to agents (implies\n--json): id, type, repo, branch, author, date, files touched, score, match\nsnippet, and a truncated title instead of the full prompt (repo hits add\ndescription and checkpoint count). Fetch full detail\nfor a single result with 'entire checkpoint explain <id>', or add --full to\nthat command to pull the checkpoint's entire session transcript. For a\ncheckpoint or commit hit from another repo, add --repo gh/<owner>/<repo> for\na GitHub mirror or --repo et/<project>/<repo> for an Entire-native repo. The\nforge prefix is required, and the hit's id must be a full checkpoint ID (12-char hex or 26-char ULID) or a full commit SHA\n(a SHA is resolved to its checkpoint by that repo's Entire API). Prefixes\ncannot be resolved in another repo. This is unrelated to this command's\n--repo filter below.\n\nCLI queries also support inline filters like author:<name>, date:<week|month>,\nbranch:<name>, repo:<owner/name>, and repo:* to search all accessible repos.\n\nUsage:\n  entire search [query] [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  entire search \"retry backoff\" --json\n  entire search \"retry backoff\" --json --compact\n  entire search \"auth timeout author:alice date:week\"\n  entire search --code \"parseToken\"\n\nFlags:\n      --all-repos        Search all accessible repos instead of just the current one\n      --author string    Filter by author name\n      --branch string    Filter by branch name\n      --case-sensitive   Case-sensitive code search (only with --code)\n      --code             Search code content across repositories\n      --compact          Trimmed JSON output for agents: id, repo, files touched, score, match snippet, and a truncated title instead of the full prompt (implies --json)\n      --date string      Filter by time period (week or month)\n  -h, --help             help for search\n      --json             Output as JSON\n      --limit int        Maximum number of results (per page for checkpoint search, total for --code) (default 10)\n      --page int         Page number (1-based) (default 1)\n      --repo strings     Filter by repository (gh/owner/repo, et/proj/repo, owner/repo, ULID, or *); repeatable and comma-separated for multiple repos\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\nOperations on checkpoints — the persistent records of agent work tied to commits.\n\nCommands:\n  list     List checkpoints on the current branch\n  explain  Explain a checkpoint, commit, or session\n  tokens   Show token usage and optimization recommendations\n  search   Search checkpoints (semantic + keyword)\n  delete   Delete a checkpoint locally and from checkpoint remotes\n\nExamples:\n  entire checkpoint list\n  entire checkpoint explain <id|sha>\n  entire checkpoint tokens <id>\n  entire checkpoint search \"fix login\"\n  entire checkpoint delete <id> --dry-run\n\nUsage:\n  entire checkpoint [command]\n\nAliases:\n  checkpoint, cp, checkpoints\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  delete      Delete a checkpoint locally and from checkpoint remotes\n  explain     Explain a session, commit, or checkpoint\n  list        List checkpoints on the current branch\n  search      Search checkpoints, commits, and sessions using semantic and keyword matching\n  tokens      Show token usage and optimization recommendations for a checkpoint\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for checkpoint\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire checkpoint [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":84272552}},"started_at_ms":1793205796984,"completed_at_ms":1793205798069}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:43:19.478Z","ordinal":464655,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18365-0a36-7ba1-af17-2b4bf1db804a","call_id":"call_97f8ed4db08d4fc39fa8ee1cb67fa548","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"○ not set up (run `entire enable` to get started)\nSearch checkpoints, commits, and sessions using hybrid search (semantic + keyword),\npowered by the Entire search service.\n\nRequires authentication via 'entire login' (GitHub device flow).\n\nBy default, results are scoped to the current repository. Use --all-repos to\nsearch across all accessible repos.\n\nRun without arguments to open an interactive search. Results are\ndisplayed in an interactive table. Use --json for machine-readable output,\nand add --compact for a trimmed per-result shape suited to agents (implies\n--json): id, type, repo, branch, author, date, files touched, score, match\nsnippet, and a truncated title instead of the full prompt (repo hits add\ndescription and checkpoint count). Fetch full detail\nfor a single result with 'entire checkpoint explain <id>', or add --full to\nthat command to pull the checkpoint's entire session transcript. For a\ncheckpoint or commit hit from another repo, add --repo gh/<owner>/<repo> for\na GitHub mirror or --repo et/<project>/<repo> for an Entire-native repo. The\nforge prefix is required, and the hit's id must be a full checkpoint ID (12-char hex or 26-char ULID) or a full commit SHA\n(a SHA is resolved to its checkpoint by that repo's Entire API). Prefixes\ncannot be resolved in another repo. This is unrelated to this command's\n--repo filter below.\n\nCLI queries also support inline filters like author:<name>, date:<week|month>,\nbranch:<name>, repo:<owner/name>, and repo:* to search all accessible repos.\n\nUsage:\n  entire search [query] [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  entire search \"retry backoff\" --json\n  entire search \"retry backoff\" --json --compact\n  entire search \"auth timeout author:alice date:week\"\n  entire search --code \"parseToken\"\n\nFlags:\n      --all-repos        Search all accessible repos instead of just the current one\n      --author string    Filter by author name\n      --branch string    Filter by branch name\n      --case-sensitive   Case-sensitive code search (only with --code)\n      --code             Search code content across repositories\n      --compact          Trimmed JSON output for agents: id, repo, files touched, score, match snippet, and a truncated title instead of the full prompt (implies --json)\n      --date string      Filter by time period (week or month)\n  -h, --help             help for search\n      --json             Output as JSON\n      --limit int        Maximum number of results (per page for checkpoint search, total for --code) (default 10)\n      --page int         Page number (1-based) (default 1)\n      --repo strings     Filter by repository (gh/owner/repo, et/proj/repo, owner/repo, ULID, or *); repeatable and comma-separated for multiple repos\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\nOperations on checkpoints — the persistent records of agent work tied to commits.\n\nCommands:\n  list     List checkpoints on the current branch\n  explain  Explain a checkpoint, commit, or session\n  tokens   Show token usage and optimization recommendations\n  search   Search checkpoints (semantic + keyword)\n  delete   Delete a checkpoint locally and from checkpoint remotes\n\nExamples:\n  entire checkpoint list\n  entire checkpoint explain <id|sha>\n  entire checkpoint tokens <id>\n  entire checkpoint search \"fix login\"\n  entire checkpoint delete <id> --dry-run\n\nUsage:\n  entire checkpoint [command]\n\nAliases:\n  checkpoint, cp, checkpoints\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  delete      Delete a checkpoint locally and from checkpoint remotes\n  explain     Explain a session, commit, or checkpoint\n  list        List checkpoints on the current branch\n  search      Search checkpoints, commits, and sessions using semantic and keyword matching\n  tokens      Show token usage and optimization recommendations for a checkpoint\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for checkpoint\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire checkpoint [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","create_time":1793205799.4780397}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
