{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:43:29.518Z","ordinal":464668,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-253bf514-9f56-4f51-8598-273f76c5f9ea","process_id":"94919","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","entire checkpoint explain --commit b9a986edeeb156802b72d246b67c0f2425d92d9b --json --no-pager 2>&1; entire trail --help"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire checkpoint explain --commit b9a986edeeb156802b72d246b67c0f2425d92d9b --json --no-pager 2>&1; entire trail --help"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"commit b9a986edeeb156802b72d246b67c0f2425d92d9b has no Entire-Checkpoint trailer\nA trail captures project intent across repositories and branches. Manage intent and discussions on the whole trail; use --repo and --branch to select context for checkout, sessions, findings, and approvals.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail [flags]\n  entire trail [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  approvals       List approval decisions on a trail\n  approve         Approve a trail\n  checkout        Check out a trail's branch\n  comment         Discuss the whole trail across repositories\n  create          Create a trail and publish its branch\n  finding         Manage a trail's agent findings\n  link            Link a repository branch to a trail\n  list            List trails in a project\n  merge           Merge one of a trail's changes into its base\n  resume          Resume a trail's agent session\n  show            Show trail intent and its repositories and branches\n  unlink          Unlink a repository branch without deleting its work\n  update          Update project intent and lifecycle\n  watch           Tail events for a trail's selected repository branch\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help             help for trail\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire trail [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":154835919}},"started_at_ms":1793205809362,"completed_at_ms":1793205809518}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:43:31.623Z","ordinal":464669,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18365-39a7-7af2-9d8d-42da56272224","call_id":"call_ded5c8bb72b244a7b90d276c9bc67ae9","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"commit b9a986edeeb156802b72d246b67c0f2425d92d9b has no Entire-Checkpoint trailer\nA trail captures project intent across repositories and branches. Manage intent and discussions on the whole trail; use --repo and --branch to select context for checkout, sessions, findings, and approvals.\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail [flags]\n  entire trail [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  approvals       List approval decisions on a trail\n  approve         Approve a trail\n  checkout        Check out a trail's branch\n  comment         Discuss the whole trail across repositories\n  create          Create a trail and publish its branch\n  finding         Manage a trail's agent findings\n  link            Link a repository branch to a trail\n  list            List trails in a project\n  merge           Merge one of a trail's changes into its base\n  resume          Resume a trail's agent session\n  show            Show trail intent and its repositories and branches\n  unlink          Unlink a repository branch without deleting its work\n  update          Update project intent and lifecycle\n  watch           Tail events for a trail's selected repository branch\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help             help for trail\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active 