{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:44:19.963Z","ordinal":464713,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1834a-d12d-7c43-8f4a-96ee044d0ace","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae226625ae0819fa767970a421321d2","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I applied `using-entire` to the current PR #302 work.\n\n- The isolated PR worktree reports Entire is **not set up**.\n- The main checkout has Entire enabled, but checkpoint search needs authentication; the local credential service is unavailable.\n- Commit `b9a986e` has no `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer, so I couldn’t retrieve its session intent from the commit.\n- The worktree has uncommitted changes in `checkpoint.ts` and its restore tests. I left them untouched. The independent reviewer is still active.\n\nI also ran the repository’s Brain brief and recall. The brief returned mostly unrelated or stale context, so it doesn’t establish PR #302 intent. The recorded-history lookup is blocked until Entire authentication is available; for now, the current diff and active review are the usable evidence."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793205858388,"completed_at_ms":1793205859962}}
