\"Required branch checks are test-matrix (22), test-matrix (24), and linux-x86_64; agents serialize CI-triggering pushes through the shared CI slot.\",\n      \"branch\": \"main\",\n      \"origin\": \"distilled\",\n      \"author\": \"google-113003937408701635470\",\n      \"agent\": \"codex\",\n      \"effort\": \"low\",\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"provenance\": [\n        {\n          \"session_id\": \"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403\",\n          \"checkpoint_id\": \"01M5ZZTDS74T864B7F1GCVGKCK\",\n          \"transcript\": \"sessions/unknown/REDACTED.jsonl\",\n          \"line\": 938\n        },\n        {\n          \"session_id\": \"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403\",\n          \"checkpoint_id\": \"01M5ZZTDS74T864B7F1GCVGKCK\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47.162972762Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47.162972762Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fact:f4d1248e6dc934b669842098\",\n      \"paths\": [\n        \"workflow.testing.rules\"\n      ],\n      \"kind\": \"gotcha\",\n      \"locus\": [\n        \"harness.sh\",\n        \"usr/local/bin/nexus\"\n      ],\n      \"text\": \"The /usr/local/bin/nexus launcher can point into the development checkout through harness.sh, so executable location alone does not prove that qualification uses an installed release.\",\n      \"branch\": \"main\",\n      \"origin\": \"distilled\",\n      \"author\": \"google-113003937408701635470\",\n      \"agent\": \"codex\",\n      \"effort\": \"low\",\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"provenance\": [\n        {\n          \"session_id\": \"b79a4439-e6ad-4986-aa16-4a81f838ac71\",\n          \"checkpoint_id\": \"01M568DWD19TM18BY3E38JSGVC\",\n          \"transcript\": \"sessions/unknown/REDACTED.jsonl\",\n          \"line\": 510\n        },\n        {\n          \"session_id\": \"b79a4439-e6ad-4986-aa16-4a81f838ac71\",\n          \"checkpoint_id\": \"01M568DWD19TM18BY3E38JSGVC\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47.162972762Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47.162972762Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fact:0e8659b666c3b2f3b561a5a8\",\n      \"paths\": [\n        \"workflow.testing.rules\"\n      ],\n      \"kind\": \"closed-negative\",\n      \"text\": \"The earlier phase-12 “7B 100% versus 30B 25%” qualification is unsuitable as engineering-quality evidence because its validators largely checked syntax within a 1,024-token budget; reconsider those rankings only after evaluation with correctness validators.\",\n      \"branch\": \"main\",\n      \"origin\": \"distilled\",\n      \"author\": \"google-113003937408701635470\",\n      \"agent\": \"codex\",\n      \"effort\": \"low\",\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"provenance\": [\n        {\n          \"session_id\": \"5e99063d-042c-4962-9221-1650fa0f4489\",\n          \"checkpoint_id\": \"01M41G6TDNTMPXWBKWES1FXNX9\",\n          \"transcript\": \"sessions/unknown/REDACTED.jsonl\",\n          \"line\": 291\n        },\n        {\n          \"session_id\": \"5e99063d-042c-4962-9221-1650fa0f4489\",\n          \"checkpoint_id\": \"01M41G6TDNTMPXWBKWES1FXNX9\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47.162972762Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47.162972762Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fact:e32b45059f28af209e7978e1\",\n      \"paths\": [\n        \"constraints.terminal.geometry\"\n      ],\n      \"kind\": \"gotcha\",\n      \"locus\": [\n        \"-geometry\",\n        \"40x14\",\n        \"resize-window\",\n        \"tmux\",\n        \"xterm\"\n      ],\n      \"text\": \"On the user's Ubuntu desktop, GNOME Terminal has a 43×13 minimum window size, preventing direct 40×14 qualification; this is not a Nexus rendering bug. Use `tmux resize-window -x 40 -y 14` inside a larger window or `xterm -geometry 40x14` to test that size.\",\n      \"branch\": \"main\",\n      \"origin\": \"distilled\",\n      \"author\": \"google-113003937408701635470\",\n      \"agent\": \"codex\",\n      \"effort\": \"low\",\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"provenance\": [\n        {\n          \"session_id\": \"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403\",\n          \"checkpoint_id\": \"01M5ZZTDS74T864B7F1GCVGKCK\",\n          \"transcript\": \"sessions/unknown/REDACTED.jsonl\",\n          \"line\": 1922\n        },\n        {\n          \"session_id\": \"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403\",\n          \"checkpoint_id\": \"01M5ZZTDS74T864B7F1GCVGKCK\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47.162972762Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47.162972762Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fact:8a594d0e92c29b347b3994b9\",\n      \"paths\": [\n        \"architecture.routing.evaluation\"\n      ],\n      \"kind\": \"closed-negative\",\n      \"locus\": [\n        \"deep-planner/lead-coder\"\n      ],\n      \"text\": \"The frozen 11-task comparison did not establish a benefit for first-turn-heavy deep-planner/lead-coder routing: B1 passed 7/11, B2 passed 6/11, exact paired sign-test p=1.0, and B2 took about 21% longer; preserve this bounded finding and revisit only with a larger corpus and a substantive hypothesis about which tasks need deeper planning.\",\n      \"branch\": \"main\",\n      \"origin\": \"distilled\",\n      \"author\": \"google-113003937408701635470\",\n      \"agent\": \"codex\",\n      \"effort\": \"low\",\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"provenance\": [\n        {\n          \"session_id\": \"5e99063d-042c-4962-9221-1650fa0f4489\",\n          \"checkpoint_id\": \"01M41G6TDNTMPXWBKWES1FXNX9\",\n          \"transcript\": \"sessions/unknown/REDACTED.jsonl\",\n          \"line\": 640\n        },\n        {\n          \"session_id\": \"5e99063d-042c-4962-9221-1650fa0f4489\",\n          \"checkpoint_id\": \"01M41G6TDNTMPXWBKWES1FXNX9\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47.162972762Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47.162972762Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fact:d03646b7f483da70cf518747\",\n      \"paths\": [\n        \"workflow.release.acceptance\"\n      ],\n      \"kind\": \"invariant\",\n      \"text\": \"Green CI and independent code review do not constitute qualification or release acceptance; source may merge for RC construction, but publication requires all acceptance gates and evidence tied to the actual candidate.\",\n      \"branch\": \"main\",\n      \"origin\": \"distilled\",\n      \"author\": \"google-113003937408701635470\",\n      \"agent\": \"codex\",\n      \"effort\": \"low\",\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"provenance\": [\n        {\n          \"session_id\": \"f73ff17f-fe7b-4087-bd8d-f26ad4102ad2\",\n          \"checkpoint_id\": \"01M59W4SMWH7G60B0E53VW0D22\",\n          \"transcript\": \"sessions/unknown/REDACTED.jsonl\",\n          \"line\": 180\n        },\n        {\n          \"session_id\": \"f73ff17f-fe7b-4087-bd8d-f26ad4102ad2\",\n          \"checkpoint_id\": \"01M59W4SMWH7G60B0E53VW0D22\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:50:18.135593148Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:50:18.135593148Z\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"query\": \"E3 manual terminal matrix five terminals three sizes screenshots exact RC installed qualification procedure\",\n  \"retrieval_engine\": {\n    \"schema_version\": 1,\n    \"effective_engine\": \"bm25_lexical\",\n    \"identity_verified\": true,\n    \"semantic_requested\": false,\n    \"semantic_applied\": false,\n    \"semantic_available\": false,\n    \"bm25_enabled\": true,\n    \"bm25_applied\": true,\n    \"fallback_used\": false\n  }\n}\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:80:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:120:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:189:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:191:Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:203:Record PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:107:| docs/reviews/evidence/** (~180 files: casts, screenshots, logs, repro scripts) | excluded (raw evidence; not re-executed) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md:14:  bracketed paste \"y\\ny\\nyes\\n\", unbracketed burst \"yyyyyyyy\\r\\r\\r\", 'y' at 40x14, and a lone 'y' after 2.5s quiet\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md:23:  at 80x24. Result banner \"! Done · not verified ... → next: /diff or /test\" (good recovery guidance).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md:24:- 40x14: approval hint truncated mid-word (\"…←→ approve/deny, paus\"), footer \"(t…\" — the key instruction is cut.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:66:| TUI-10 | S3 | Narrow terminal | live_view.rs (approval hint/footer) | RUNTIME s2 @40x14: hint cut \"←→ approve/deny, paus\", footer \"(t…\"; @40x20 idle hint \"? for ke…\" | The instruction that explains how to decide is truncated exactly where it matters | Short-form hints under ~60 cols |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:103:`y` at 40x14, lone `y` after 2.5s quiet -> file absent each time; panel \"typing ignored · ←→ approve/deny, pause, enter\";\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:113:- Not-drawn panel cannot be answered (approval_drawn / shown, live_state.rs:1196-1202); resize to 40x14 kept the panel\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:133:| Kitty keyboard protocol / Shift+Enter, real terminal emulators (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code) | Manual matrix; pyte does not answer `CSI ? u` |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:134:| ZWJ / emoji width correctness | Compare against a real terminal (kitty/wezterm screenshot) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:149:| TUI-R8 | Approval controls are spatially consistent and key hints remain complete at 40 cols | a11y (TUI-09/10) | POST-V1 | 40x14 screen dump contains full decision hint; ← focuses leftmost button |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:31:- Non-mutating, so never prompted even in review mode: fetch_web, search_web, browser_navigate, browser_click, browser_screenshot, spawn_subagent, activate_skill, every read/search tool (capabilities.ts:514,576,772,824,1164,1215).\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":325650547}},"started_at_ms":1793206676676,"completed_at_ms":1793206677002}}
