{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:59:06.634Z","ordinal":465482,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a18373-7e0a-7d80-81dc-e2762c9fbae9","author":"/root/review_pr302","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_pr302\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** for the current draft at base/HEAD `934ed912b8e187c5c418709e472a6313bb4169a8`. The combined source-and-test diff SHA-256 I computed is `38425b0e892f4a0741601516b23ca71a768dc4f08ef06955e6f5869ef47d8527` (source: `7588f4e1ee006a69ae9ca9fb4a939f7723895a9f922d4458892b70072e3a3b4c`; tests: `36fa0f6818606403b1c56497ea9c81e019031851065356931eeac1ea4eb207ea`). These differ from the hashes supplied in the request.\n\n- **Actionable — `cli/src/checkpoint.ts:27–39, 950–957`; regression at `cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts:136–145`:** The UTF-8 path check throws a generic `Error`, but `createCheckpoint` catches it and replaces it with “Checkpoint could not verify protected Git state.” The new regression expects the error to include “not valid UTF-8,” so that assertion will fail. Preserve a dedicated path-encoding error through the catch, or change the assertion to the actual fail-closed error while retaining the no-ref assertion.\n\nThe other listed fixes are present in source and regressions: operation-state refusal, executable-mode preservation, `--no-renames` scans, ENOTDIR-safe lstat, renamed `.gitignore` preflight, and refusal for ignored staged additions. No tests were run."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","create_time":1793206746.634584,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":22119}}
