{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T16:59:25.573Z","ordinal":465499,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae229ec6e04819fbace4bc8dabed02b","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The independent review found one concrete bug in the new non-UTF-8-path regression: checkpoint creation correctly fails closed, but its outer catch converts the specific encoding error into a generic protected-state error, so the test’s expected diagnostic can’t be observed. I’ll preserve that fail-closed error through the catch, keep the no-ref assertion, then request a fresh review. Local tests remain blocked by the active SUITE claim; I’ll use type checking and exact CI once the corrected commit is available."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793206764451,"completed_at_ms":1793206765573}}
