{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:00:57.541Z","ordinal":465580,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae22a489fa4819fbfdf2cb456ca2844","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The fresh review accepted the encoding-error correction but found another actionable pathspec issue: a staged filename beginning with Git’s pathspec magic could make the ignored-file guard inspect a different path. I’m fixing the guard to pass literal pathspecs and adding a regression for a magic-looking filename. The full local test suite remains held by Kimi’s SUITE claim; I’ll keep using non-suite checks and avoid interrupting that owner."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793206856665,"completed_at_ms":1793206857541}}
