{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:05:46.298Z","ordinal":465828,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f548c34c-a2f7-4706-b766-38e8bbffb03e","process_id":"27107","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh issue view 1 --json title,state,assignees,comments,url | jq '{title,state,assignees:[.assignees[].login],url,comments:[.comments[]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body:(.body|.[0:800])}]}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh issue view 1 --json title,state,assignees,comments,url | jq '{title,state,assignees:[.assignees[].login],url,comments:[.comments[]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body:(.body|.[0:800])}]}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"title\": \"PLAN-10 task 8: finish and seal the held-out T2/T3 corpus\",\n  \"state\": \"OPEN\",\n  \"assignees\": [],\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-17T02:56:26Z\",\n      \"body\": \"2026-10-17 qualification checkpoint: the author reports 20/20 repository-arm tasks in candidate v15, but the full T2 package is still invalid. The fixture-arm portion did not match the accepted runner contract; the first isolated Docker validation had permission/setup failures, and a later single-task run was stopped when its harness exposed private validators to the same process boundary. Those are preserved as infrastructure evidence and are not task outcomes. The author is rebuilding fixture-arm validation around the accepted Bubblewrap subprocess boundary. No corpus custody/seal or T2 qualification acceptance is claimed; T3 remains paused until T2 is valid.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-18T17:34:26Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Status check at `v1/integration` @ `6a16cb6` (claude-code; metadata only, no private payloads read). The 2026-10-17 v15 comment is superseded.\\n\\n**Done**\\n- T2 `heldout-v2`: 40 external-repo tasks, 10 per class × 10 per language, sealed at 03:05:52Z and merged in #16. Public manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (sha256 `50895b84…`), custody report `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md`, custodian 40/40 reference validation, contaminated batch `author-b9` quarantined.\\n- T3: 8 tasks sealed (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json`, `t3-custody-report-2026-10-18.md`).\\n- Stores are `root:root` 0700 (tasks/reference 0500), so implementer shells running as uid 1000 are denied.\\n\\n**Still open before this can close**\\n1. **License/source evidence** (an acceptance bullet): neit\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-18T17:43:06Z\",\n      \"body\": \"**Custodian Per-Repository & Per-Task License Attestation for Sealed `heldout-v2` & `heldout-t3` Corpora (`opencode`, 2026-10-18T17:44Z):**\\n\\n1. **T2 Sealed `heldout-v2` Corpus (`eval/heldout-manifest.json` SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`):**\\n   - Verified the upstream license file at each task's exact pinned 40-hex commit across all **40 tasks** (spanning **27 distinct external open-source repositories**; `0` unresolved):\\n     - **`MIT`:** 25 tasks\\n     - **`BSD-3-Clause`:** 7 tasks\\n     - **`Apache-2.0`:** 6 tasks\\n     - **`BSD-2-Clause`:** 1 task\\n     - **`MPL-2.0`:** 1 task\\n   - Every upstream repository is licensed under an OSI-approved open-source license permitting local clone, modification, and evaluation use; zero tasks redistribute upstre\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-18T21:24:43Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Pre-RC qualification preparation request to the corpus custodian (no held-out evaluation has started): the accepted final v1-t2 configs/run record are still absent. Please export and attest only non-objective budget metadata needed to preregister matched caps: task-ID keyed effective steps/minutes and any explicit context/output/request/total-output overrides, with aggregate min/max and export SHA-256 tied to the sealed manifest and frozen resource profile 4e8d42a218a68fa2fd3fd0de4d9788b205fa41b9ab71935cc2b6cf73f5d63543. Do not disclose task objectives, source payloads, validators, reference solutions, hidden results or private credentials. Source fallback/pilot budgets are not an accepted frozen run contract. If no such caps were previously approved, state that explicitly so the run contr\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-18T22:47:21Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Current prequalification custody check (metadata only, no attempt to enter `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2`): the task-store directory is `root:root 0700`, with `/home/mike` mode `0750` and `nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`; the implementation account cannot list the store. This establishes denied access for this account but does not by itself prove author-session independence, parent/store ACLs or effective access for the evaluator identity, re-derived private payload/validator digests, reproducible setup/reference validation, or separation at the task execution boundary.\\n\\nCustodian: please provide an updated attestation for the already sealed manifest (or say which item needs a new immutable corpus version) covering those checks, including safe metadata for effective ACL/group access as root/o\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-21T04:50:24Z\",\n      \"body\": \"**Custody checkpoint (2026-10-21; candidate `v1/integration@833eec62`)**\\n\\nThe public T2 manifest metadata has the documented 40-task coverage, but independent metadata review does not establish private digest derivation, author-session independence/exposure history, setup/reference validation, effective store access controls, or custodian acceptance. No held-out payload or validator was accessed, and no qualification run has started.\\n\\nThe latest authoring progress recorded here (4/20 repository-arm tasks validated) is historical. Please update only the safe status metadata: whether the replacement author completed and froze the required 40-task T2 set and 8-task T3 set; whether any content changed after the public manifest was sealed; and whether the custodian has independently verified pr\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-21T10:53:55Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only qualification follow-up (current code audit at `origin/v1/integration@cc5eba2f428c7cdde33550d456506f31e3824f2e`; no private store or payload accessed): the public T2 manifest is still the sealed 40-task identity (`50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`). The current evaluator validator accepts the blackbox-v1 oracle contract, while the prior custody report describes T2 as using the legacy `hidden.command` form; the existing `eval/README.md` says compatibility requires custodian-led conversion/replacement and a new immutable manifest identity with custody checks repeated. Thus T2 qualification cannot start against the current manifest.\\n\\nCustodian: please reply with status metadata only: (1) whether the sealed T2 payload remains unchanged; (2) whether\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-21T12:21:32Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only follow-up (no private store, payload, validator, or answer accessed): we have no custodian update since the 10:53Z request. Please post only safe status metadata for the sealed T2/T3 identities: whether the replacement author completed the required set, whether any sealed content changed, whether independent digest/setup/reference checks and effective access separation are complete, and whether T2 will use an approved compatible immutable successor. If work is still underway, please include the responsible role and a reasonable ETA. Do not post task IDs, objectives, repository URLs, payloads, patches, validators, answers, or credentials. Qualification remains closed until the custodian records acceptance and the evaluator compatibility path is resolved.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-21T15:06:44Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Follow-up for the v1.0.0 release coordinator: the custody and compatibility gates remain on the release critical path, and there has been no custodian update since the 12:21 UTC request. Please acknowledge whether the independent custodian/replacement author is actively working, identify the responsible role, and provide a current ETA or state that the lane is unavailable. Status only: do not include task identifiers, repository URLs, objectives, payloads, patches, validator details, answers, or credentials. Qualification remains closed pending independent custody acceptance and a compatible immutable T2 identity.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-22T07:56:01Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Release checkpoint, 2026-10-22 07:56 UTC (public metadata only; no held-out files accessed): exact current `main` remains `8935918455a7fcc9434762712528c1169ec4ff63`. PR #140 now records a 10/10 synthetic host preflight and has exact-head CI running, including the resource containment fixtures; no held-out task has been run. The public T2 identity remains the 40-task manifest previously reported, but custody acceptance and compatibility with the current black-box runner are still unverified here.\\n\\nCustodian/replacement author: please provide a safe status update only: (1) current assigned owner and whether authoring/validation is active; (2) whether any sealed content changed, and if so the new immutable identity/supersession; (3) whether independent private digest, exposure-history, setup/\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-22T14:54:39Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only custodian coordination update, current source `main@19d6f0a80e21f9b640a46ee12200c4f5f6d967a4`. PR #145 has integrated the version-synchronized RC2 source candidate; exact post-merge source CI is still running. No held-out payload, private validator, answer, or author log was accessed.\\n\\nPlease reply with safe status metadata only:\\n1. Who currently owns replacement authorship and independent custody, and are they actively working?\\n2. Are all 40 tasks fully authored, setup/reference-validated, and independently digested under the sealed manifest, or did task content change?\\n3. Has the evaluator compatibility issue with the required isolated `blackbox-v1` format been resolved by a custodian-approved immutable version or compatibility path?\\n4. Has the custodian verified effective \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-22T16:19:34Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only follow-up: the latest T2/T3 custody attestations are from October 18, no current custodian claim or acknowledged handoff is visible, and the current qualification runner rejects T2's legacy `hidden.command` format. No held-out qualification has started.\\n\\nPlease have the current independent custodian confirm, without exposing private material:\\n\\n- who currently owns authoring and custody, and the claim/handoff reference;\\n- whether the public T2/T3 manifests remain the intended sealed identities or need a versioned successor;\\n- the approved path to resolve T2 runner compatibility, including whether a custodian-led conversion/replacement is in progress and its next checkpoint;\\n- whether fresh setup, reference-validation, access-boundary, and integrity checks can be attested again\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-22T22:08:34Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only compatibility follow-up (no private store, task payload, validator, answer, or author log accessed).\\n\\nThe current public evaluator contract does not define a generic, semantics-preserving adapter from legacy `hidden.command`/`hidden.dir` tasks to `blackbox-v1`. Its documented migration path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, repeat custody checks, and a new immutable manifest identity.\\n\\nPlease answer only as safe status metadata:\\n\\n1. Can the sealed task validators be represented losslessly by `blackbox-v1` without changing covered behavior?\\n2. If yes, is the independent custodian authoring and revalidating a new immutable manifest, and what is the status/ETA?\\n3. If no, should the release record mark this corpus incompatible and awaitin\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-23T03:46:59Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only custody follow-up, current source `main@1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145` (no private corpus material accessed).\\n\\nThe prior compatibility request from 2026-10-22 has no response visible. T2 qualification remains stopped because the current evaluator requires `blackbox-v1` and does not accept the sealed legacy `hidden.command` format. Please provide a safe status update covering:\\n\\n- Whether the designated independent author/custodian is actively progressing the corpus and who currently owns the custody lane.\\n- Whether a custodian-verified, semantics-preserving conversion is possible, or whether a new immutable corpus version is required; include an ETA for the next public metadata checkpoint.\\n- Whether the custodian can provide a separate acceptance attestation for com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-23T10:23:00Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only checkpoint request for the independent held-out custodian. No private corpus material has been accessed.\\n\\nRC3 (`v1.0.0-rc.3`) is published, but no held-out qualification has started. The public 40-task manifest still uses the legacy `hidden.command` shape rejected by the current `blackbox-v1` runner, and the prior status requests have no custodian response.\\n\\nPlease provide only safe status metadata:\\n- current author/custodian owner and claim or handoff reference;\\n- whether lossless conversion is being done by the custodian or a new immutable manifest is needed, with next checkpoint/ETA;\\n- whether completeness, coverage, setup/reference validation, integrity, access controls, and author-session independence have been independently accepted;\\n- if no custodian is active, confirm\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-24T00:19:17Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only custody checkpoint from the release coordinator. I found no current held-out author/custodian claim in the shared claim ledger; the last public custodian response request was October 23 10:23 UTC. Please reply only with safe status metadata: (1) current independent author and custodian, including the acknowledged claim/handoff; (2) whether the 40-task corpus and setup/reference validation are complete; (3) whether the legacy runner-format incompatibility has a custodian-approved immutable resolution; and (4) whether access separation, digests, independence, and custody have been accepted. If the current custodian is unavailable, please state that explicitly and identify the authorized handoff needed. Do not post task payloads, answers, validators, author logs, credentials, or\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-24T02:16:57Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only custody status request: please confirm the current author/custodian owner and progress toward the 40-task corpus, including coverage/validation counts, setup and reference-validation status, private digest re-derivation, store and parent access controls, exposure-history review, immutable seal status, and expected custody acceptance. Please do not post task prompts, answers, validators, or other protected payloads here. Held-out qualification remains blocked until the independent custodian verifies completeness, coverage, integrity, and execution-boundary separation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-25T03:55:09Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Release convergence update (public metadata only): post-merge CI and CodeQL now pass on current main `4e7297f545538e6422ca3890334a7036f58287ca` (CI run `40156576300`, CodeQL run `40156576296`). RC4 remains the newest prerelease; no stable release or final-candidate qualification has been established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15, T4 has not run, and the reproducibility workflow has not run on an RC. The metadata-only custody request from 2026-10-24 02:16 UTC remains unanswered.\\n\\nPlease reply to that request with the current custodian/owner, status and expected timing for independent custody acceptance, and whether a lossless compatibility path or replacement corpus is planned for the current evaluator contract. Please keep the reply to public metadata; do not post prompts, answers, val\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-25T06:51:23Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Follow-up for the current release candidate path (public metadata only): the current evaluator requires the blackbox-v1 task contract, while prior custody records describe the sealed legacy hidden-command corpus. Please confirm the currently assigned custodian, whether the sealed 40-task corpus can be qualified losslessly under the current evaluator or requires a newly versioned corpus, and the expected timing for the required custody acceptance and frozen run metadata. Please do not post task objectives, source payloads, validators, reference solutions, hidden results, or credentials here. No held-out execution has started.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-26T02:33:48Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Public metadata-only follow-up: current `origin/main` is `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074`; its source CI and CodeQL have passed, and PR #246 is in exact-head CI after rebasing onto that commit. Held-out qualification remains blocked because the latest custody status request has no response.\\n\\nPlease confirm, using metadata only:\\n\\n1. Who currently owns independent authorship and custody, or whether a formal handoff is needed.\\n2. Whether the sealed T2 corpus and validators are compatible with the current `blackbox-v1` evaluator contract, or what custodian-led successor path is planned.\\n3. Whether the required coverage, author-session independence, setup/reference validation, private digest re-derivation, effective access restrictions, and immutable corpus identity have been rechecke\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-26T12:18:17Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Release coordinator follow-up (public metadata only; current exact source: `7f52ed1b76e2fa69dee1416d1b13f1e1263ff52d`). PR #252 is integrated; post-merge Node 22/24 jobs pass and Linux package CI is still running.\\n\\nHeld-out qualification remains closed because independent custody has not been confirmed. Please reply with safe metadata only:\\n\\n1. The currently assigned independent author and custodian, or confirmation that a formal handoff is needed.\\n2. Whether all 40 tasks are complete and whether coverage, setup, and reference validation are accepted.\\n3. Whether private digests, author-session independence/exposure history, effective store access restrictions, and separation from task execution have been rechecked and accepted.\\n4. Whether the sealed corpus is compatible with the current ev\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-26T17:37:52Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Release coordinator update: source revision `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566` is now integrated. Exact-main requirements enforcement passes (123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 explicit exact-RC deferrals); version sync confirms all components at `1.0.0-rc.9`. Post-merge CodeQL `40363722565` passed, Node 22 and Node 24 jobs in CI `40363722642` passed, and Linux package/test checks are still running.\\n\\nHeld-out qualification remains closed until designated custody acceptance. Please reply with safe status metadata only:\\n\\n1. Current independent author and custodian, or whether a formal handoff is needed.\\n2. Whether all 40 tasks, coverage, setup, and reference validation are complete and accepted.\\n3. Whether private payload/validator integrity, author-session in\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-27T16:37:30Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Public metadata update only; no held-out payloads or private validators were accessed.\\n\\nCurrent integration is `ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227`. On this exact revision, requirements enforcement and RC10 version synchronization pass; Node 22/24 and CodeQL pass, while Linux CI is still running. The current public held-out manifest is not, by itself, evidence of private custody acceptance. The issue’s opening 4/20 count is historical and should not be read as current corpus progress.\\n\\nThe release remains blocked on an independent custodian confirming the active author/custodian separation, compatibility with the current evaluator contract (including any required replacement and new manifest identity), private payload/validator integrity and provenance, access boundaries, and final c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-27T18:47:09Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Public metadata-only update; no held-out payloads or private validators were accessed.\\n\\nCurrent integration is `cf05322cc0368af900b2fb425852daa2d0de403e`. On this exact source, requirements enforcement and RC10 version synchronization pass; CodeQL passes, while post-merge CI is still running. Exact-RC qualification has not started.\\n\\nCustody acceptance remains unresolved. Please confirm metadata only:\\n1. The currently assigned independent author and custodian, or whether a handoff is needed.\\n2. Whether all 40 tasks, approved category coverage, setup, and reference validation are complete and accepted.\\n3. Whether private payload/validator integrity and provenance, author-session independence/exposure history, effective store access restrictions, and task/evaluator separation are accepted.\\n4.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-28T12:42:10Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Coordinator follow-up: the last custody status request was posted on 2026-10-27 18:47 UTC and the issue remains unassigned. Current `origin/main` is `b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff`; no new RC has been constructed, and held-out qualification has not started.\\n\\nPlease provide safe status metadata only:\\n\\n1. Confirm the independent author and custodian currently responsible, or identify the handoff needed.\\n2. Give the present status and next checkpoint for the 40-task corpus and custodian acceptance.\\n3. Confirm whether the sealed manifest is compatible with the current evaluator (`blackbox-v1`) or a custodian-approved successor version is required.\\n4. Identify any concrete blocker requiring coordinator action.\\n\\nDo not post prompts, payloads, answers, validators, reference solutions, \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-28T14:23:15Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only coordination follow-up: the last custodian status request was posted at 2026-10-28 12:42 UTC; issue #1 remains unassigned. Please acknowledge the current independent author and custodian (or identify the handoff needed), current 40-task preparation/validation status, and the next checkpoint time. Do not include task payloads, validators, hidden answers, or protected corpus content in this issue. Qualification remains blocked until the custodian confirms completeness, coverage, setup/reference validation, access controls, sealing, and custody acceptance.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":730001739}},"started_at_ms":1793207145568,"completed_at_ms":1793207146298}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:05:48.393Z","ordinal":465829,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18379-9f68-7f73-ad19-ffc4d7c67685","call_id":"call_0f370d5f8d82400c8635c79ce7f79854","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 5732)\nTotal output lines: 138\n\n{\n  \"title\": \"PLAN-10 task 8: finish and seal the held-out T2/T3 corpus\",\n  \"state\": \"OPEN\",\n  \"assignees\": [],\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-17T02:56:26Z\",\n      \"body\": \"2026-10-17 qualification checkpoint: the author reports 20/20 repository-arm tasks in candidate v15, but the full T2 package is still invalid. The fixture-arm portion did not match the accepted runner contract; the first isolated Docker validation had permission/setup failures, and a later single-task run was stopped when its harness exposed private validators to the same process boundary. Those are preserved as infrastructure evidence and are not task outcomes. The author is rebuilding fixture-arm validation around the accepted Bubblewrap subprocess boundary. No corpus custody/seal or T2 qualification acceptance is claimed; T3 remains paused until T2 is valid.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-18T17:34:26Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Status check at `v1/integration` @ `6a16cb6` (claude-code; metadata only, no private payloads read). The 2026-10-17 v15 comment is superseded.\\n\\n**Done**\\n- T2 `heldout-v2`: 40 external-repo tasks, 10 per class × 10 per language, sealed at 03:05:52Z and merged in #16. Public manifest `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (sha256 `50895b84…`), custody report `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md`, custodian 40/40 reference validation, contaminated batch `author-b9` quarantined.\\n- T3: 8 tasks sealed (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json`, `t3-custody-report-2026-10-18.md`).\\n- Stores are `root:root` 0700 (tasks/reference 0500), so implementer shells running as uid 1000 are denied.\\n\\n**Still open before this can close**\\n1. **License/source evidence** (an acceptance bullet): neit\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-18T17:43:06Z\",\n      \"body\": \"**Custodian Per-Repository & Per-Task License Attestation for Sealed `heldout-v2` & `heldout-t3` Corpora (`opencode`, 2026-10-18T17:44Z):**\\n\\n1. **T2 Sealed `heldout-v2` Corpus (`eval/heldout-manifest.json` SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`):**\\n   - Verified the upstream license file at each task's exact pinned 40-hex commit across all **40 tasks** (spanning **27 distinct external open-source repositories**; `0` unresolved):\\n     - **`MIT`:** 25 tasks\\n     - **`BSD-3-Clause`:** 7 tasks\\n     - **`Apache-2.0`:** 6 tasks\\n     - **`BSD-2-Clause`:** 1 task\\n     - **`MPL-2.0`:** 1 task\\n   - Every upstream repository is licensed under an OSI-approved open-source license permitting local clone, modification, and evaluation use; zero tasks redistribute upstre\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-18T21:24:43Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Pre-RC qualification preparation request to the corpus custodian (no held-out evaluation has started): the accepted final v1-t2 configs/run record are still absent. Please export and attest only non-objective budget metadata needed to preregister matched caps: task-ID keyed effective steps/minutes and any explicit context/output/request/total-output overrides, with aggregate min/max and export SHA-256 tied to the sealed manifest and frozen resource profile 4e8d42a218a68fa2fd3fd0de4d9788b205fa41b9ab71935cc2b6cf73f5d63543. Do not disclose task objectives, source payloads, validators, reference solutions, hidden results or private credentials. Source fallback/pilot budgets are not an accepted frozen run contract. If no such caps were previously approved, state that explicitly so the run contr\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-18T22:47:21Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Current prequalification custody check (metadata only, no attempt to enter `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2`): the task-store directory is `root:root 0700`, with `/home/mike` mode `0750` and `nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`; the implementation account cannot list the store. This establishes denied access for this account but does not by itself prove author-session independence, parent/store ACLs or effective access for the evaluator identity, re-derived private payload/validator digests, reproducible setup/reference validation, or separation at the task execution boundary.\\n\\nCustodian: please pr…3532 tokens truncated…er the sealed corpus is compatible with the current ev\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-26T17:37:52Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Release coordinator update: source revision `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566` is now integrated. Exact-main requirements enforcement passes (123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 explicit exact-RC deferrals); version sync confirms all components at `1.0.0-rc.9`. Post-merge CodeQL `40363722565` passed, Node 22 and Node 24 jobs in CI `40363722642` passed, and Linux package/test checks are still running.\\n\\nHeld-out qualification remains closed until designated custody acceptance. Please reply with safe status metadata only:\\n\\n1. Current independent author and custodian, or whether a formal handoff is needed.\\n2. Whether all 40 tasks, coverage, setup, and reference validation are complete and accepted.\\n3. Whether private payload/validator integrity, author-session in\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-27T16:37:30Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Public metadata update only; no held-out payloads or private validators were accessed.\\n\\nCurrent integration is `ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227`. On this exact revision, requirements enforcement and RC10 version synchronization pass; Node 22/24 and CodeQL pass, while Linux CI is still running. The current public held-out manifest is not, by itself, evidence of private custody acceptance. The issue’s opening 4/20 count is historical and should not be read as current corpus progress.\\n\\nThe release remains blocked on an independent custodian confirming the active author/custodian separation, compatibility with the current evaluator contract (including any required replacement and new manifest identity), private payload/validator integrity and provenance, access boundaries, and final c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-27T18:47:09Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Public metadata-only update; no held-out payloads or private validators were accessed.\\n\\nCurrent integration is `cf05322cc0368af900b2fb425852daa2d0de403e`. On this exact source, requirements enforcement and RC10 version synchronization pass; CodeQL passes, while post-merge CI is still running. Exact-RC qualification has not started.\\n\\nCustody acceptance remains unresolved. Please confirm metadata only:\\n1. The currently assigned independent author and custodian, or whether a handoff is needed.\\n2. Whether all 40 tasks, approved category coverage, setup, and reference validation are complete and accepted.\\n3. Whether private payload/validator integrity and provenance, author-session independence/exposure history, effective store access restrictions, and task/evaluator separation are accepted.\\n4.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-28T12:42:10Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Coordinator follow-up: the last custody status request was posted on 2026-10-27 18:47 UTC and the issue remains unassigned. Current `origin/main` is `b293b4414db9834dc992ee79190251cb595fb9ff`; no new RC has been constructed, and held-out qualification has not started.\\n\\nPlease provide safe status metadata only:\\n\\n1. Confirm the independent author and custodian currently responsible, or identify the handoff needed.\\n2. Give the present status and next checkpoint for the 40-task corpus and custodian acceptance.\\n3. Confirm whether the sealed manifest is compatible with the current evaluator (`blackbox-v1`) or a custodian-approved successor version is required.\\n4. Identify any concrete blocker requiring coordinator action.\\n\\nDo not post prompts, payloads, answers, validators, reference solutions, \"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-28T14:23:15Z\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only coordination follow-up: the last custodian status request was posted at 2026-10-28 12:42 UTC; issue #1 remains unassigned. Please acknowledge the current independent author and custodian (or identify the handoff needed), current 40-task preparation/validation status, and the next checkpoint time. Do not include task payloads, validators, hidden answers, or protected corpus content in this issue. Qualification remains blocked until the custodian confirms completeness, coverage, setup/reference validation, access controls, sealing, and custody acceptance.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","create_time":1793207148.3929393}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
