{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:16:20.370Z","ordinal":466272,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18383-4412-7373-b8b9-694289039e55","call_id":"call_7d42e61a4cd44e14a31b92480104a121","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 12.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---0---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Usage:\n  entire [flags]\n  entire [command]\n\nEntire Setup:\n  agent                      Manage agent integrations (add, remove, list)\n  clean                      Clean up Entire session data\n  configure                  Update Entire settings in the current repository\n  disable                    Disable Entire in current repository\n  doctor                     Diagnose and fix session issues\n  enable                     Enable Entire in current repository\n  plugin                     Manage Entire plugins (install, list, upgrade, search, remove)\n  status                     Show Entire status\n\nSessions & Checkpoints:\n  activity                   Show your activity overview\n  checkpoint                 Inspect and search checkpoints\n  dispatch                   Generate a dispatch summarizing recent agent work\n  recap                      Summarize recent checkpoint activity\n  search                     Search checkpoints, commits, and sessions using semantic and keyword matching\n  session                    Manage agent sessions tracked by Entire\n\nTrails:\n  trail                      Manage trails across repositories and branches\n\nAccount:\n  auth                       Manage authentication\n  login                      Log in to Entire\n  logout                     Log out of Entire\n\nControl Plane:\n  api                        Make an authenticated request to an Entire API and print the response\n  cluster                    Show the Entire clusters you can place projects and repos on\n  org                        Manage Entire organizations\n  project                    Manage Entire projects\n  repo                       Manage Entire repositories\n\nAdditional Commands:\n  agent-help                 Machine-readable usage for coding agents (always matches the installed CLI)\n  help                       Help about any command\n  labs                       Explore experimental Entire workflows\n  version                    Show build information\n\nFlags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n\nError: Invalid usage: unknown flag: --no-pager\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---1---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 8546)\nTotal output lines: 664\n\n{\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:16:15.749178339Z\",\n  \"task\": \"Continue PR #302 checkpoint security remediation: validate candidate dd56d7b5 and advance toward exact-head CI without touching shared dirty checkout\",\n  \"facts\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fact:31acf9d2764c3acd6608ce40\",\n      \"paths\": [\n        \"project.tooling.stack\"\n      ],\n      \"kind\": \"closed-negative\",\n      \"locus\": [\n        \"beta.10-to-beta.18\"\n      ],\n      \"text\": \"PR #38 was closed because v1 integration already contained the sharp 0.35.5 security fix, while its bundled Cloudflare cf beta.10-to-beta.18 upgrade was unnecessary and untested in v1; revisit cf through a fresh post-release Dependabot PR or PLAN-C1 hardening.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fact:e4d28bc793806ce6ddb0d0e8\",\n      \"paths\": [\n        \"workflow.coordination.rules\"\n      ],\n      \"kind\": \"convention\",\n      \"locus\": [\n        \"nexus-claims.log\",\n        \"pr/ci\"\n      ],\n      \"text\": \"Release agents must read new nexus-claims.log entries and open PR/CI state each iteration and record their actions in the shared log.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fact:ee3dbe0e2aa53f5c5c362c73\",\n      \"paths\": [\n        \"project.ci_cd.pipeline\"\n      ],\n      \"kind\": \"gotcha\",\n      \"locus\": [\n        \"codeql\",\n        \"github\"\n      ],\n      \"text\": \"An empty GitHub CodeQL alert query on a PR merge ref does not prove existing alerts were fixed, because PR queries may expose only newly introduced alerts; verify remediation against alerts on the integration branch after merging.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"history\": {},\n  \"likely_edit_files\": [\n    \"docs/reviews/NEXUS_POST_REMEDIATION_DOGFOOD_QUALIFICATION.md\",\n    \"docs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md\",\n    \"docs/WP04_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md\",\n    \"docs/WP10_INDEPENDENT_QUALIFICATION.md\",\n    \"docs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/mockgw.py\",\n    \"docs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/ptylib.py\",\n    \"docs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1_repl.py\",\n    \"docs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1d.py\"\n  ],\n  \"likely_test_files\": [\n    \"docs/v1.0.0/evidence/repro/agt_repro.test.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"likely_files\": [\n    \"docs/reviews/NEXUS_POST_REMEDIATION_DOGFOOD_QUALIFICATION.md\",\n    \"docs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md\",\n    \"docs/WP04_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md\",\n    \"docs/WP10_INDEPENDENT_QUALIFICATION.md\",\n    \"docs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/mockgw.py\",\n    \"docs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/ptylib.py\",\n    \"docs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1_repl.py\",\n    \"docs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1d.py\",\n    \"docs/v1.0.0/evidence/repro/agt_repro.test.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"guidance\": [\n    \"Treat the brain as an indexed snapshot, not live memory.\",\n    \"Use likely_edit_files and history matches before text search; if search is still needed, scope it to likely_files and specific identifiers. Use likely_test_files for validation context.\",\n    \"Use the live-state overlay before trusting code-context results for files changed in this session.\",\n    \"Insp