atrix pending, stable release unpublished., terminal_setup=Ubuntu desktop 10.0.8.3 reachable over SSH. GUI session active. xterm 407, kitty 0.45.0, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0, tmux 3.6, VS Code 1.143.1 installed. RC10 binary at ~/.local/nexus-rc10-qualification/bin/nexus reports 1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438). Opened xterm 80x24 using a disposable workspace as setup only; no manual acceptance evidence collected., review_state=Independent ACCEPT of f8f6983 vs 934ed912, exact diff SHA-256 38425b0e892f4a0741601516b23ca71a768dc4f08ef06955e6f5869ef47d8527, findings 0, tests not run. Review specifically covers staged deletion in assertGitChangesSafe and safe cleanup ordering. A newer uncommitted 10/-2 checkpoint.ts delta was excluded., ci_state=PR302 exact 700d16 CI 40726281681 failed on Node22/24, each 1956 pass / 1 fail / 2 skipped; failing test tracked deletion cleanup runs before a checkpoint symlink can redirect it (checkpoint_restore.test.ts:758), createCheckpoint wrapper at line 922. New remote 934ed912 CI 40729450236 in progress, CodeQL 40729450361 passed., next_checkpoint2=No tests until SUITE handoff from kimi-main., updated 9 minutes ago\n  - [doing] Address PR #302 review finding for nested bare Git repository ancestors (detail=Exact PR head 3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7 is remotely verified and independently ACCEPTED (diff SHA-256 d90aeb05a9f5c5d0a35bfa0f597d96cc39a5f6480e22b20094f7523cd4cacdff). Immutable-snapshot validation: checkpoint_restore 51/51, TypeScript --noEmit PASS, diff-check PASS; isolated HOME and logs retained at /var/tmp/nexus-pr302-3c52580.91oUZ9. CodeQL and JS/TS PASS; Node 22/24 and Entire are pending. PR remains open; no merge.), updated about 3 hours ago\n  - [doing] Close partial nested bare repository config bypass and requalify PR302 (detail=Independent reviewer ACCEPTed working diff SHA-256 28524ef98877b37c8d385d0ede5cfdf682d620515fab4a135e05212985841484. Committed as 72939ec8da37bc22509c8c87ebaacc5de7724f02 and pushed fast-forward to PR302. Isolated-HOME tsc --noEmit and diff-check pass; no tests run due kimi-main SUITE claim. Exact PR checks 40717946373/40717945285 started; Entire reviewer asked to verify exact pushed content and then record own approval if policy allows. Ubuntu read-only Entire inspection showed zero approvals on trail 17 before current head check., next_checkpoint=Wait for exact-head CI and independent Entire reviewer response; obtain explicit SUITE safe-boundary transfer before targeted/full validation. Use valid worktree under /home and CI-style capped tmpfs/runtime fixtures. Do not merge until exact candidate tests, review, and all checks pass.), updated about 2 hours ago\n  - [doing] Use Entire history before continuing PR #302 checkpoint remediation (latest_progress=2026-10-28: Applied using-entire workflow. Entire status succeeds on shared main (enabled; 637 outgoing checkpoints), but semantic search fails because org.freedesktop.secrets is unavailable. Isolated PR302 worktree reports Entire not set up. Shared checkout remains untouched. Existing reviewer/owner/claim constraints unchanged., next_checkpoint=Restore the configured secret-service access through its approved host setup or obtain authorized Entire access; rerun Entire search for checkpoint restore history. Preserve PR302 worktree changes until coordinator confirms their ownership. Do not run tests while kimi-main owns SUITE.), updated about 2 hours ago\n  - [done] Remove bare repository marker false positive and add ordinary objects/refs regression (details=Changed marker threshold from two names to complete HEAD/objects/refs set; added restore regression. git diff --check passed. Tests remain queued because kimi-main owns the fresh SUITE claim.), updated about 2 hours ago\n  - [doing] Advance PR302 exact-head remediation and qualification (latest_progress=On 2026-10-28 at 15:50 UTC, PR302 fast-forwarded to f771590b0da201f5d3f83897f9d2d8a0ce5cee91. Independent source reviewer plan05_readonly_review ACCEPTed exact parent-to-head diff SHA 31171bfd. TypeScript noEmit and git diff check pass. Local tests not run because SUITE safe-boundary handoff from kimi-main is unresolved. Exact-head GitHub CI 40720039126 and CodeQL 40720039095 queued; Entire pending, cannot self-approve through the sole owner account. Future timestamps 16:00/16:08/16:12 appended earlier were erroneous and corrected in nexus-claims.log., next_checkpoint=Monitor exact-head CI and Entire status. Obtain Kimi suite-owner safe-boundary release or confirm there is no active suite claim/process, then run targeted checkpoint suite with isolated HOME; preserve evidence and requalify if changes are needed. Do not merge until tests, checks, and independent acceptance pass., release_state=Acceptance IN_PROGRESS; origin/main=b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212; PR302 head=f771590b0da201f5d3f83897f9d2d8a0ce5cee91. User confirms sole-user repository; independent code review can come from distinct agent/session, but Entire approval remains pending. Public latest prerelease RC10; no stable v1.0.0.), updated about 1 hour ago\n  - [doing] Fix nested-workspace restore index scope on PR #302 (detail=Independent review identified read-tree resets sibling index entries during a subdirectory workspace restore. Added scoped index merge and a sibling staged/worktree regression in claimed worktree; diff-check passed. Current TypeScript check unavailable because the worktree has no installed compiler. Active SUITE claim remains kimi-main provider composite focused tests, so no local suite runs.), updated about 1 hour ago\n  - [doing] Resolve PR302 independent checkpoint review findings (details=Current PR head moved to 934ed912b8e187c5c418709e472a6313bb4169a8 while work proceeded. Draft changes in cli/src/checkpoint.ts and cli/test/checkpoint_restore.test.ts cover stale merge state, fail-closed invalid UTF-8 paths, untracked permission preservation, no-rename Git deltas, ENOTDIR-safe lstat, renamed ignore-file detection, and ignored staged additions. TypeScript noEmit, esbuild test parse, and diff-check pass. Tests not run; SUITE claim still kimi-main. Exact-head CI 40729450236 is running on base 934. Independent review requested on exact uncommitted diff. No commit/push yet; avoid overwriting concurrent owner work.), updated 20 minutes ago\n  - [doing] Advance PR #302 remediation and qualification (latest_progress=2026-10-28 17:15 UTC: Worktree reconciled clean at dd56d7b5c9d362888232863ede20a7ac98a7b69c, branch v1/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix, parent 980ac35a. A 7-line change to skip worktree reads after a confirmed absent index entry is committed by Mike and independently ACCEPTed (diff SHA-256 4395784bac928085995c7e0666f55e0d09e1e5950666e4639b5a25debc82cb22). Cumulative review 934..cb31461 and private-write/error-reporting delta also ACCEPTed. Diff-check PASS. Remote PR remains 934ed912 with old failing Node22/24 jobs. Full suite process tree still live under kimi-main at 17:15 UTC (41m). No tests or push., next_checkpoint=Wait for confirmed SUITE release and reconcile process/claim state, then exact-head test the candidate with isolated HOME and update PR with owner coordination. Obtain fresh CI on exact pushed head. Continue independent release gates; terminal screenshots/per-cell evidence and Entire reviewer approval remain unresolved.), updated 2 minutes ago"}]},"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":27354226}},"started_at_ms":1793207821719,"completed_at_ms":1793207821749}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:17:01.793Z","ordinal":466298,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae22e0299cc819fbeec36809ad866b5","usage":{"input_tokens":95260,"cached_input_tokens":88320,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1251,"reasoning_output_tokens":990,"total_tokens":96511},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":32352043,"cached_input_tokens":31970304,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":119588,"reasoning_output_tokens":73623,"total_tokens":32471631},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8661432255,"cached_input_tokens":8568961664,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24749539,"reasoning_output_tokens":14344216,"total_tokens":8686181794}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:17:03.239Z","ordinal":466299,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e14ee624-7da2-4e28-b1ce-7bb0c7fea7e8","process_id":"9131","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","entire search --help"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire search --help"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"Search checkpoints, commits, and sessions using hybrid search (semantic + keyword),\npowered by the Entire search service.\n\nRequires authentication via 'entire login' (GitHub device flow).\n\nBy default, results are scoped to the current repository. Use --all-repos to\nsearch across all accessible repos.\n\nRun without arguments to open an interactive search. Results are\ndisplayed in an interactive table. Use --json for machine-readable output,\nand add --compact for a trimmed per-result shape suited to agents (implies\n--json): id, type, repo, branch, author, date, files touched, score, match\nsnippet, and a truncated title instead of the full prompt (repo hits add\ndescription and checkpoint count). Fetch full detail\nfor a single result with 'entire checkpoint explain <id>', or add --full to\nthat command to pull the checkpoint's entire session transcript. For a\ncheckpoint or commit hit from another repo, add --repo gh/<owner>/<repo> for\na GitHub mirror or --repo et/<project>/<repo> for an Entire-native repo. The\nforge prefix is required, and the hit's id must be a full checkpoint ID (12-char hex or 26-char ULID) or a full commit SHA\n(a SHA is resolved to its checkpoint by that repo's Entire API). Prefixes\ncannot be resolved in another repo. This is unrelated to this command's\n--repo filter below.\n\nCLI queries also support inline filters like author:<name>, date:<week|month>,\nbranch:<name>, repo:<owner/name>, and repo:* to search all accessible repos.\n\nUsage:\n  entire search [query] [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  entire search \"retry backoff\" --json\n  entire search \"retry backoff\" --json --compact\n  entire search \"auth timeout author:alice date:week\"\n  entire search --code \"parseToken\"\n\nFlags:\n      --all-repos        Search all accessible repos instead of just the current one\n      --author string    Filter by author name\n      --branch string    Filter by branch name\n      --case-sensitive   Case-sensitive code search (only with --code)\n      --code             Search code content across repositories\n      --compact          Trimmed JSON output for agents: id, repo, files touched, score, match snippet, and a truncated title instead of the full prompt (implies --json)\n      --date string      Filter by time period (week or month)\n  -h, --help             help for search\n      --json             Output as JSON\n      --limit int        Maximum number of results (per page for checkpoint search, total for --code) (default 10)\n      --page int         Page number (1-based) (default 1)\n      --repo strings     Filter by repository (gh/owner/repo, et/proj/repo, owner/repo, ULID, or *); repeatable and comma-separated for multiple repos\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":31473}},"started_at_ms":1793207823238,"completed_at_ms":1793207823239}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:17:03.257Z","ordinal":466300,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d11d7a47-043d-4689-b03b-58c1b33ede07","process_id":"33395","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","entire search 'PR 302 checkpoint ordinary child restore preflight suite handoff' --json"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire search 'PR 302 checkpoint ordinary child restore preflight suite handoff' --json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"search failed: semantic search: resolving repository \"gh/mikeholownych/nexus-code\": refresh login token: load core token: read access token: The name org.freedesktop.secrets was not provided by any .service files\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":24990}},"started_at_ms":1793207823256,"completed_at_ms":1793207823257}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:17:03.268Z","ordinal":466301,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ed36a94e-bbc9-4a97-aac1-66f041ed11cd","process_id":"42096","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","cat /home/mike/.agents/skills/review/SKILL.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /home/mike/.agents/skills/review/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":"/home/mike/.agents/skills/review/SKILL.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"---\nname: review\ndescription: >\n  Review code changes on the current branch using checkpoint transcript context\n  to understand developer intent before auditing the diff. Use when the user\n  asks for a code review, wants to review branch changes, or asks to audit\n  recent work before merging.\n---\n\n# Review\n\nReview code changes on the current branch by first reading checkpoint transcripts to\nunderstand the intent behind each change, then auditing the actual diff for issues.\nThis produces an intent-aware review that catches mismatches between what the developer\nwanted and what the code actually does.\n\n## Response Format\n\nBegin the first response to this skill invocation with the line:\n\n`Entire Review:`\n\nfollowed by a blank line, then the content.\n\n- Apply the header to the **first response of the invocation only.** Do not re-print it on\n  follow-up turns within the same invocation.\n- Do **not** include the header on error or early-exit responses (e.g. \"not a git repository\",\n  \"no commits found between branch and base\").\n\n## Rules\n\n1. This is a **read-only audit**. Do not modify any files during the review.\n2. Always show a scope banner before findings so the user knows what is being reviewed.\n3. If checkpoint context is unavailable, still perform the review using only the diff and\n   commit messages. Clearly state that the review lacks intent context.\n4. Group findings by file. Within each file, order by severity (Critical > High > Medium > Low).\n5. Every finding must include a concrete suggestion or explanation, not just flag the issue.\n6. After presenting findings, ask the user if they want a fix plan. Do not auto-fix.\n7. Do not review generated files, lock files, or binary files unless the user explicitly\n   asks for them.\n\n## Process\n\n### 1. Verify environment\n\nRun `entire version` to check if the CLI is available. If it is not installed, note that\nthe review will proceed without checkpoint intent context (degraded mode).\n\n### 2. Detect base ref\n\nFind the mainline branch to diff against. Try these refs in order and use the first that\nexists:\n\n```bash\ngit rev-parse --verify origin/HEAD 2>/dev/null\ngit rev-parse --verify origin/main 2>/dev/null\ngit rev-parse --verify origin/master 2>/dev/null\ngit rev-parse --verify main 2>/dev/null\ngit rev-parse --verify master 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nIf none exist, tell the user no base ref was found and ask them to specify one.\n\n### 3. Compute scope\n\n```bash\ngit rev-list --count <base>..HEAD\ngit diff --stat <base>..HEAD\n```\n\nRecord the number of commits and files changed. This forms the scope banner.\n\n### 4. Gather checkpoint intent (skip in degraded mode)\n\n```bash\ngit log --format='%H%x00%s%x00%b' <base>..HEAD\n```\n\nExtract `Entire-Checkpoint:` trailer values from commit bodies. Deduplicate checkpoint IDs.\n\nFor each unique checkpoint ID (up to 20):\n\n```bash\nentire checkpoint explain --checkpoint <checkpoint-id> --json --no-pager\n```\n\nParse the JSON to extract session metadata. For each non-review session in the checkpoint,\nprefer the summary (intent + outcome). If no summary is available, fall back to the latest\nuser prompt. Truncate each checkpoint detail to 320 characters.\n\nIf `--json` fails for a checkpoint, fall back to the bare human-readable output:\n\n```bash\nentire checkpoint explain --checkpoint <checkpoint-id> --no-pager\n```\n\nDo not use `--full` in the review workflow — it produces long narrative text harder for\nagents to parse in bulk. If that also fails, skip the checkpoint and note it was unavailable.\n\nAdditionally, read the current in-progress session (if any) for uncommitted work context:\n\n```bash\nentire session current --json\n```\n\nIf this returns valid JSON, extract `last_prompt` and `files_touched` — these represent\nthe intent behind uncommitted changes that are not yet captured in any checkpoint.\n\nBuild an intent map: for each file in the diff (committed + uncommitted), collect the\nrelevant intent context from all checkpoints and the active session that touched it.\n\n### 5. Read the diff\n\n```bash\ngit diff <base>..HEAD\n```\n\nAlso include uncommitted changes:\n\n```bash\ngit diff HEAD\n```\n\nFor large diffs (>5000 lines total), focus on the most critical files:\n- Files with the most changes\n- Files mentioned in checkpoint intents\n- Source files over generated/config files\n\nRead individual file diffs as needed rather than loading the entire diff at once.\n\n### 6. Perform the review\n\nRead the review rules:\n\n```\nreferences/review-rules.md\n```\n\nFor each file in the diff, review it considering:\n\n**With checkpoint context:**\n- Does the implementation match the stated intent?\n- Were the constraints from the transcript respected?\n- Did the agent miss edge cases it discussed?\n- Are there leftover debugging artifacts or TODOs?\n\n**Always (with or without context):**\n- Logic errors, off-by-one, null safety\n- Security issues (injection, auth bypass, data exposure)\n- Performance concerns (N+1 queries, unnecessary allocations)\n- Error handling gaps\n- API contract violations\n- Dead code or unreachable branches\n\n### 7. Output findings\n\nPresent findings using severity prefixes that align with the `entire review --fix` parser:\n\n```\nEntire Review:\n\nReviewing <branch> vs <base>: N commits, M files changed\n[Intent context: available from K checkpoints | unavailable — reviewing diff only]\n\n## path/to/file.ts\n\nCritical: <issue description>\n  Intent: <what the checkpoint said this should do, if available>\n  Actual: <what the code actually does>\n  Fix: <concrete suggestion>\n\nHigh: <issue description>\n  Intent: <what the checkpoint said this should do, if available>\n  Actual: <what the code actually does>\n  Fix: <concrete suggestion>\n\nMedium: <improvement opportunity>\n  Issue: <what is wrong>\n  Fix: <concrete suggestion>\n\n## path/to/other-file.ts\n\nLow: <observation that is not a bug but worth noting>\n\n---\n\nFound N issues (X critical, Y high, Z medium, W low).\nWould you like me to create a fix plan for the critical and high issues?\n```\n\nWhen checkpoint context is unavailable for a finding, omit the `Intent:` line and use\n`Issue:` / `Fix:` instead.\n\n### 8. Offer follow-up\n\nAfter presenting findings, wait for the user's response:\n- If they say yes to a fix plan, outline specific steps to address each critical/high issue.\n- If they ask to fix directly, switch to implementation mode and address the issues.\n- If they decline, the review is complete.\n\n## Degraded Mode (no Entire CLI or no checkpoints)\n\nWhen checkpoint context is unavailable:\n1. Skip step 4 entirely\n2. In the scope banner, state: \"Intent context unavailable — reviewing diff only\"\n3. Omit the \"Intent:\" line from findings\n4. Still perform the full code-level review from step 6\n5. Note at the end: \"This review was performed without Entire checkpoint context. With\n   checkpoints enabled, the review would also verify that implementation matches the\n   original developer intent.\"\n\n## Failure Modes\n\n- **No commits between base and HEAD**: Tell the user the branch has no changes relative to\n  the base. Do not output a review.\n- **Cannot detect base ref**: Ask the user to specify the base branch or commit.\n- **Diff too large (>100 files)**: Ask the user if they want to review all files or focus on\n  a subset. Suggest reviewing only source files or files with checkpoint context.\n- **`entire checkpoint explain` fails**: Note the specific checkpoint was unavailable, continue reviewing\n  remaining files without that context.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":39266}},"started_at_ms":1793207823268,"completed_at_ms":1793207823268}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:17:04.583Z","ordinal":466302,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18383-f0c7-7a43-a8b9-bbf3d69b66b3","call_id":"call_5340d01a489f4b44b71584a641fa255d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---0---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Search checkpoints, commits, and sessions using hybrid search (semantic + keyword),\npowered by the Entire search service.\n\nRequires authentication via 'entire login' (GitHub device flow).\n\nBy default, results are scoped to the current repository. Use --all-repos to\nsearch across all accessible repos.\n\nRun without arguments to open an interactive search. Results are\ndisplayed in an interactive table. Use --json for machine-readable output,\nand add --compact for a trimmed per-result shape suited to agents (implies\n--json): id, type, repo, branch, author, date, files touched, score, match\nsnippet, and a truncated title instead of the full prompt (repo hits add\ndescription and checkpoint count). Fetch full detail\nfor a single result with 'entire checkpoint explain <id>', or add --full to\nthat command to pull the checkpoint's entire session transcript. For a\ncheckpoint or commit hit from another repo, add --repo gh/<owner>/<repo> for\na GitHub mirror or --repo et/<project>/<repo> for an Entire-native repo. The\nforge prefix is required, and the hit's id must be a full checkpoint ID (12-char hex or 26-char ULID) or a full commit SHA\n(a SHA is resolved to its checkpoint by that repo's Entire API). Prefixes\ncannot be resolved in another repo. This is unrelated to this command's\n--repo filter below.\n\nCLI queries also support inline filters like author:<name>, date:<week|month>,\nbranch:<name>, repo:<owner/name>, and repo:* to search all accessible repos.\n\nUsage:\n  entire search [query] [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  entire search \"retry backoff\" --json\n  entire search \"retry backoff\" --json --compact\n  entire search \"auth timeout author:alice date:week\"\n  entire search --code \"parseToken\"\n\nFlags:\n      --all-repos        Search all accessible repos instead of just the current one\n      --author string    Filter by author name\n      --branch string    Filter by branch name\n      --case-sensitive   Case-sensitive code search (only with --code)\n      --code             Search code content across repositories\n      --compact          Trimmed JSON output for agents: id, repo, files touched, score, match snippet, and a truncated title instead of the full prompt (implies --json)\n      --date string      Filter by time period (week or month)\n  -h, --help             help for search\n      --json             Output as JSON\n      --limit int        Maximum number of results (per page for checkpoint search, total for --code) (default 10)\n      --page int         Page number (1-based) (default 1)\n      --repo strings     Filter by repository (gh/owner/repo, et/proj/repo, owner/repo, ULID, or *); repeatable and comma-separated for multiple repos\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---1---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"search failed: semantic search: resolving repository \"gh/mikeholownych/nexus-code\": refresh login token: load core token: read access token: The name org.freedesktop.secrets was not provided by any .service files\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---2---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1858)\nTotal output lines: 220\n\n---\nname: review\ndescription: >\n  Review code changes on the current branch using checkpoint transcript context\n  to understand developer intent before auditing the diff. Use when the user\n  asks for a code review, wants to review branch changes, or asks to audit\n  recent work before merging.\n---\n\n# Review\n\nReview code changes on the current branch by first reading checkpoint transcripts to\nunderstand the intent behind each change, then auditing the actual diff for issues.\nThis produces an intent-aware review that catches mismatches between what the developer\nwanted and what the code actually does.\n\n## Response Format\n\nBegin the first response to this skill invocation with the line:\n\n`Entire Review:`\n\nfollowed by a blank line, then the content.\n\n- Apply the header to the **first response of the invocation only.** Do not re-print it on\n  follow-up turns within the same invocation.\n- Do **not** include the header on error or early-exit responses (e.g. \"not a git repository\",\n  \"no commits found between branch and base\").\n\n## Rules\n\n1. This is a **read-only audit**. Do not modify any files during the review.\n2. Always show a scope banner before findings so the user knows what is being reviewed.\n3. If checkpoint context is unavailable, still perform the review using only the diff and\n   commit messages. Clearly state that the review lacks intent context.\n4. Group findings by file. Within each file, order by severity (Critical > High > Medium > Low).\n5. Every finding must include a concrete suggestion or explanation, not just flag the issue.\n6. After presenting findings, ask the user if they want a fix plan. Do not auto-fix.\n7. Do not review generated files, lock files, or binary files unless the user explicitly\n   asks for them.\n\n## Process\n\n### 1. Verify environment\n\nRun `entire version` to check if the CLI is available. If it is not installed, note that\nthe review will proceed without checkpoint intent context (degraded mode).\n\n### 2. Detect base ref\n\nFind the mainline branch to diff against. Try these refs in order and use the first that\nexists:\n\n```bash\ngit rev-parse --verify origin/HEAD 2>/dev/null\ngit rev-parse --verify origin/main 2>/dev/null\ngit rev-parse --verify origin/master 2>/dev/null\ngit rev-parse --verify main 2>/dev/null\ngit rev-parse --verify master 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nIf none exist, tell the user no base ref was found and ask them to specify one.\n\n### 3. Compute scope\n\n```bash\ngit rev-list --count <base>..HEAD\ngit diff --stat <base>..HEAD\n```\n\nRecord the number of commits and files changed. This forms the scope banner.\n\n### 4. Gather checkpoint intent (skip in degraded mode)\n\n```bash\ngit log --format='%H%x00%s%x00%b' <base>..HEAD\n```\n\nExtract `Entire-Checkpoint:` trailer values from commit bodies. Deduplicate checkpoint IDs.\n\nFor each unique checkpoint ID (up to 20):\n\n```bash\nentire checkpoint explain --checkpoint <checkpoint-id> --json --no-pager\n```\n\nParse the JSON to extract session metadata. For each non-review session in the checkpoint,\nprefer the summary (intent + outcome). If no summary is available, fall back to the latest\nuser prompt. Truncate each checkpoint detail to 320 characters.\n\nIf `--json` fails for a checkpoint, f…258 tokens truncated… checkpoint intents\n- Source files over generated/config files\n\nRead individual file diffs as needed rather than loading the entire diff at once.\n\n### 6. Perform the review\n\nRead the review rules:\n\n```\nreferences/review-rules.md\n```\n\nFor each file in the diff, review it considering:\n\n**With checkpoint context:**\n- Does the implementation match the stated intent?\n- Were the constraints from the transcript respected?\n- Did the agent miss edge cases it discussed?\n- Are there leftover debugging artifacts or TODOs?\n\n**Always (with or without context):**\n- Logic errors, off-by-one, null safety\n- Security issues (injection, auth bypass, data exposure)\n- Performance concerns (N+1 queries, unnecess"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---3---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"- nexus-pr302-bare-repo-remediation-20261028: latest_progress=Remote exact CI run 40729450236 on PR302 head 934ed912 completed FAIL: both Node22 and Node24 failed the same test at checkpoint_restore.test.ts:758 ('tracked deletion cleanup runs before a checkpoint symlink can redirect it'); each matrix was 1956 pass / 1 fail / 2 skipped; Linux skipped. CodeQL 40729450361 PASS. This remote head predates local commit f8f6983, which has independent ACCEPT but no tests. Local shared worktree is actively changing: saw f8f6983 then detached/branch HEADs b3f7d7b and cb31461 during adjacent read-only checks, with source file updates. Actor/handoff unknown; preserved and untouched., next_checkpoint=Do not write to or push from the rapidly changing worktree. Wait for owner to stabilize and hand off a final pushed branch head; obtain fresh exact CI/review. Keep release objective moving on gates independent of this lane, and retain distinct terminal and Entire acceptance blockers., release_state=PR302 remote head=934ed912b8e187c5c418709e472a6313bb4169a8; exact CI 40729450236 FAILED on Node22/Node24 with the same checkpoint test (1956 pass/1 fail/2 skip each); Linux skipped; CodeQL pass. Local branch/worktree is actively changing around f8f6983, b3f7d7b, cb31461; state not stable and author/handoff unknown, untouched. Independent review accepted f8f6983, but no tests or remote CI on that commit. Entire reviewer approval unresolved, terminal matrix pending, stable release unpublished., terminal_setup=Ubuntu desktop 10.0.8.3 reachable over SSH. GUI session active. xterm 407, kitty 0.45.0, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0, tmux 3.6, VS Code 1.143.1 installed. RC10 binary at ~/.local/nexus-rc10-qualification/bin/nexus reports 1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438). Opened xterm 80x24 using a disposable workspace as setup only; no manual acceptance evidence collected., review_state=Independent ACCEPT of f8f6983 vs 934ed912, exact diff SHA-256 38425b0e892f4a0741601516b23ca71a768dc4f08ef06955e6f5869ef47d8527, findings 0, tests not run. Review specifically covers staged deletion in assertGitChangesSafe and safe cleanup ordering. A newer uncommitted 10/-2 checkpoint.ts delta was excluded., ci_state=PR302 exact 700d16 CI 40726281681 failed on Node22/24, each 1956 pass / 1 fail / 2 skipped; failing test tracked deletion cleanup runs before a checkpoint symlink can redirect it (checkpoint_restore.test.ts:758), createCheckpoint wrapper at line 922. New remote 934ed912 CI 40729450236 in progress, CodeQL 40729450361 passed., next_checkpoint2=No tests until SUITE handoff from kimi-main., updated 9 minutes ago\\n  - [doing] Address PR #302 review finding for nested bare Git repository ancestors (detail=Exact PR head 3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7 is remotely verified and independently ACCEPTED (diff SHA-256 d90aeb05a9f5c5d0a35bfa0f597d96cc39a5f6480e22b20094f7523cd4cacdff). Immutable-snapshot validation: checkpoint_restore 51/51, TypeScript --noEmit PASS, diff-check PASS; isolated HOME and logs retained at /var/tmp/nexus-pr302-3c52580.91oUZ9. CodeQL and JS/TS PASS; Node 22/24 and Entire are pending. PR remains open; no merge.), updated about 3 hours ago\\n  - [doing] Close partial nested bare repository config bypass and requalify PR302 (detail=Independent reviewer ACCEPTed working diff SHA-256 28524ef98877b37c8d385d0ede5cfdf682d620515fab4a135e05212985841484. Committed as 72939ec8da37bc22509c8c87ebaacc5de7724f02 and pushed fast-forward to PR302. Isolated-HOME tsc --noEmit and diff-check pass; no tests run due kimi-main SUITE claim. Exact PR checks 40717946373/40717945285 started; Entire reviewer asked to verify exact pushed content and then record own approval if policy allows. Ubuntu read-only Entire inspection showed zero approvals on trail 17 before current head check., next_checkpoint=Wait for exact-head CI and independent Entire reviewer response; obtain explicit SUITE safe-boundary transfer before targeted/full validation. Use valid "}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","create_time":1793207824.5835447}},