"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> \n> - **Source mode**: Auto\n> - **Repository**: Unavailable\n> - **Branch**: Unavailable\n> - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\n> - **Commit**: Unavailable\n> - **Layers**: defaults\n> - **Review profile**: CHILL\n> - **Plan**: Advanced\n> - **Run ID**: `3371504d-a560-4d1c-96d7-802573faa65f`\n> \n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\"} --> <strong title=\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n\n\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&utm_content=305)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>❤️ Share</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n--\nauthor:\tmikeholownych\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nCI remediation update (exact head `de78839a83429caa67c8d0abf270af11eab23d6a`, base `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`):\n\n- Updated the explicit restart recovery notice so it states the restart happened after recovery, prior conversation was not continued, earlier workspace history may be incomplete, and remaining changes are unverified.\n- Updated the TDD fake agent with the `restartConversation` behavior needed to exercise the explicit restart path.\n- Focused validation with isolated HOME and serial test execution passed 7/7: six durable-history restart variants and the explicit restart RED-evidence regression.\n- `git diff --check` passed. The previous exact-head CI failure was two failures in these areas; new exact-head CI and independent review are running. No full local suite was run.\n\n--\nauthor:\tmikeholownych\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nExact-head status update — `97f1c6ead710bc059126ba65b37ad1e5fde17666` (base `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`):\n\n- Node 22/24, JS/TS, and CodeQL: PASS; Linux packaging/tests and Entire Gates remain in progress.\n- Independent source review: ACCEPT on this exact head.\n\nNo merge until the remaining exact-head checks complete successfully.\n--\nauthor:\tmikeholownych\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n### Independent Review — `97f1c6ea` (base `b2ae2fe8`, diff SHA-256 `5a09bdcf43f81f03e98f3fc368fdcbc388330eedeb11a0ae13e46e9d001132ec`)\n\n- Resolves the open finding from the PR #304 review: in `AgentWorkUnitExecutor.run()`, `ctx.operatorDecision?.restart && !unusable` now calls `agent.restartConversation(...)` and uses `initialPrompt`, instead of resuming a conversation that describes discarded worktree files.\n- Isolated worktree (isolated HOME/XDG): `tsc --noEmit` 0 errors; new `operation_runner_restart.test.ts` and `operation_git.test.ts` pass; `git diff --check` clean.\n- `tdd_work_units.test.ts` shows 10 failures in my isolated harness, **identical (11/21 pass) on unmodified `main` b2ae2fe8** under the same harness, so they are environmental to my runner, not caused by this PR. GitHub CI on this head (test-matrix 22/24, linux-x86_64, CodeQL) is green.\n- Not verified: `Entire Gates` is failing on this PR; I can't see its criteria.\n\n**Verdict: ACCEPT**\n\n--\nauthor:\tmikeholownych\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nclaude-code independent review: **ACCEPT** at exact head `97f1c6ead710bc059126ba65b37ad1e5fde17666` (base `b2ae2fe`).\n\n- **Fix:** on `operatorDecision.restart` with usable history, the executor now calls `agent.restartConversation(!obligationRecordPresent)` and re-prompts from `initialPrompt`. It no longer falls through to the resume branch, whose prompt says \"Your earlier progress on this unit is above\" and refers to files that a recreated worktree has discarded. That resolves the #304 finding. `isResume` (line 332) was already false on restart, and TDD evidence is still cleared on restart (line 338).\n- **Branch order:** the restart branch runs before the `notStarted` and resume branches and after the `interrupted` gate. A restart can't skip the interrupted-tool inspection question.\n- **Obligations:** `restartConversation` keeps the recorded unverified-change obligation, and when no obligation record survived it adds one and invalidates the baseline. Both cases are conservative: a restarted unit can never inherit verification evidence.\n- **Tests:** the new `operation_runner_restart` regression asserts that the old history isn't continued. The `tdd_work_units` fake gains `restartConversation`. Exact-head CI is green: Node 22/24, `linux-x86_64`, CodeQL and JS/TS. I ran no local tests because `kimi-main` holds SUITE.\n\nNeeds an rc.11 notes bullet.\n--\nauthor:\tmikeholownych\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nclaude-code: **ACCEPT** carried forward to exact head `f0f4847af188f0bf029e018cc8147ddd94a06904` (base `145d464`). The cumulative patch-id is the same as at my accepted head, so this is a rebase-only update. Exact-head CI must still pass before merge.\n--\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":457113890}},"started_at_ms":1793207992804,"completed_at_ms":1793207994261}}
