{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:20:21.825Z","ordinal":466467,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae22ece83b0819fbb4d15ad7504d45a","usage":{"input_tokens":125566,"cached_input_tokens":122496,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":786,"reasoning_output_tokens":666,"total_tokens":126352},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":34763228,"cached_input_tokens":34349568,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":131186,"reasoning_output_tokens":80449,"total_tokens":34894414},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8663843440,"cached_input_tokens":8571340928,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24761137,"reasoning_output_tokens":14351042,"total_tokens":8688604577}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:20:23.487Z","ordinal":466468,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-676e2c30-4483-4aa4-a009-564f9e7bb79f","process_id":"24054","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","entire api --help; printf '\\n--- query trail 20 ---\\n'; entire brain query \"PR #305 trail 20 Entire Gates failure review findings acceptance\" --json; printf '\\n--- query trail 17 ---\\n'; entire brain query \"PR #302 trail 17 Entire Gates five high findings approval\" --json"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire api --help; printf '\\n--- query trail 20 ---\\n'; entire brain query \"PR #305 trail 20 Entire Gates failure review findings acceptance\" --json; printf '\\n--- query trail 17 ---\\n'; entire brain query \"PR #302 trail 17 Entire Gates five high findings approval\" --json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"Make an authenticated HTTP request to an Entire API and print the JSON response.\n\nThese endpoints are internal and can change shape without notice; where a\npurpose-built command exists, its output is the stable interface.\n\nThe CLI attaches the right bearer token and dials the right host for the\nchosen backend, so you don't have to plumb auth yourself:\n\n  --to core   the control plane (default): orgs, repos, mirrors, clusters, /me\n  --to cell   your home entire-api cell: /me/* activity, repo aggregates\n\nUse --jurisdiction <slug> (e.g. us, eu) to reach a specific jurisdiction's\nentire-api cell instead of your home one; it implies --to cell.\n\nBoth backends act as ENTIRE_TOKEN when set, else the selected login\n(--context, else $ENTIRE_CONTEXT, else the active context), so a staging\nlogin reaches staging's control plane and cells. The cell host comes from\nenvironment's cluster listing; an explicit ENTIRE_API_BASE_URL names the\ndata host directly instead.\n\n<path> is the full path on that host, e.g. /api/v1/clusters. These\nplaceholders are filled from the current repo's origin remote:\n  {owner} {repo}   the GitHub owner / repo\n  {repo_id}        the repo's Entire ULID (from its mirror) — cells key on this\n\nThe method is GET unless a field/body is given (then POST); override with -X.\n\nUsage:\n  entire api <path> [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  entire api /api/v1/clusters\n  entire api --to cell /api/v1/me/activity\n  entire api --jurisdiction eu /api/v1/me/activity\n  entire api --to cell \"/api/v1/me/recap?repo={repo_id}\"\n  entire api -X POST /api/v1/projects -f name=demo\n\nFlags:\n  -F, --field stringArray       add a typed parameter in key=value format; true/false/null/numbers are converted (repeatable)\n  -H, --header stringArray      add a request header in key:value format (repeatable)\n  -h, --help                    help for api\n  -i, --include                 print the response status line and headers too\n      --input string            file with the request body (\"-\" for stdin)\n  -j, --jurisdiction string     target a specific jurisdiction's cell (e.g. us, eu) instead of your home cell; implies --to cell\n  -X, --method string           HTTP method (default GET, or POST when a field/body is given)\n  -f, --raw-field stringArray   add a string parameter in key=value format (repeatable)\n      --to string               which backend to call: core or cell (default \"core\")\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\n--- query trail 20 ---\n{\n  \"branch\": \"main\",\n  \"query\": \"PR #305 trail 20 Entire Gates failure review findings acceptance\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:d03646b7f483da70cf518747\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.release.acceptance\",\n      \"heading\": \"invariant\",\n      \"text\": \"Green CI and independent code review do not constitute qualification or release acceptance; source may merge for RC construction, but publication requires all acceptance gates and evidence tied to the actual candidate.\",\n      \"score\": 0.01639344262295082,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:50:18Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:50:18Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:1b54f28e98d5720d87a63c30\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.testing.rules\",\n      \"heading\": \"closed-negative\",\n      \"text\": \"The context-convergence branch at 31d6622 was not accepted: its only real acceptance run failed at step 119 without an artifact after repeated long-write timeouts, and an isolated reproduction exposed findings loss and ID reuse after crash/resume; revisit acceptance after fixing recovery and persistence and completing a fact-checked artifact-producing rerun.\",\n      \"score\": 0.016129032258064516,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:050f2a39d9261b65895c0d5c\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.review.rules\",\n      \"heading\": \"invariant\",\n      \"text\": \"Release merges require a recorded independent ACCEPT and green CI for the exact PR head; self-acceptance and unrecorded claims of reviewer acceptance do not satisfy the gate.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015873015873015872,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:3a13462b6dc41c5bde1e8744\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.review.rules\",\n      \"heading\": \"gotcha\",\n      \"text\": \"Review generation once manually expanded a short SHA into a nonexistent full commit ID; obtain full SHAs from Git and verify that review evidence names the actual PR head before counting acceptance.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015625,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:0a7bf21bf921c1a74816f940\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.review.independence\",\n      \"heading\": \"convention\",\n      \"text\": \"Independent architecture reviews must form findings and a proposed architecture from primary repository evidence before consulting another agent’s research; subsequent comparison must preserve the original findings.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015384615384615385,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:31acf9d2764c3acd6608ce40\",\n      \"path\": \"project.tooling.stack\",\n      \"heading\": \"closed-negative\",\n      \"text\": \"PR #38 was closed because v1 integration already contained the sharp 0.35.5 security fix, while its bundled Cloudflare cf beta.10-to-beta.18 upgrade was unnecessary and untested in v1; revisit cf through a fresh post-release Dependabot PR or PLAN-C1 hardening.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015151515151515152,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:728ccdd269fd39d8403cfaf6\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.review.constraints\",\n      \"heading\": \"gotcha\",\n      \"text\": \"All Nexus agents share one GitHub account, so GitHub rejects formal reviews of PRs created by another agent using that account; record independent review verdicts as PR comments and in the shared log.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014925373134328358,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:9a1a6985df61a5fc25dfe89f\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.review.rules\",\n      \"heading\": \"convention\",\n      \"text\": \"Verify each evidence-PR claim against what the producing workflow actually checked, including scope and verification settings; matching numbers alone do not establish that the claim is supported.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014705882352941176,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:b8a2ef4858be622e21023e97\",\n      \"path\": \"project.tooling.stack\",\n      \"heading\": \"decision\",\n      \"text\": \"The user explicitly chose Node.js 22 or newer for v1.0.0, superseding the Node 20 floor in DEC-12 to satisfy the no-deprecated-packages rule.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014492753623188406,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:5bac031b57a68a334050f6e0\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.assessment.authority\",\n      \"heading\": \"invariant\",\n      \"text\": \"Dogfooding readiness is an evidence-based recommendation to the operator, not agent acceptance authority; stop after the assessment report for operator review without beginning remediation or Phase 4.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014285714285714285,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n--- query trail 17 ---\n{\n  \"branch\": \"main\",\n  \"query\": \"PR #302 trail 17 Entire Gates five high findings approval\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:31acf9d2764c3acd6608ce40\",\n      \"path\": \"project.tooling.stack\",\n      \"heading\": \"closed-negative\",\n      \"text\": \"PR #38 was closed because v1 integration already contained the sharp 0.35.5 security fix, while its bundled Cloudflare cf beta.10-to-beta.18 upgrade was unnecessary and untested in v1; revisit cf through a fresh post-release Dependabot PR or PLAN-C1 hardening.\",\n      \"score\": 0.01639344262295082,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:1b54f28e98d5720d87a63c30\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.testing.rules\",\n      \"heading\": \"closed-negative\",\n      \"text\": \"The context-convergence branch at 31d6622 was not accepted: its only real acceptance run failed at step 119 without an artifact after repeated long-write timeouts, and an isolated reproduction exposed findings loss and ID reuse after crash/resume; revisit acceptance after fixing recovery and persistence and completing a fact-checked artifact-producing rerun.\",\n      \"score\": 0.016129032258064516,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:e7f00f83dda26737693392e1\",\n      \"path\": \"architecture.boundaries.rationale\",\n      \"heading\": \"closed-negative\",\n      \"text\": \"Timing delays and repeated Enter presses were rejected as sufficient protection for session-wide approval: independent PTY reviews repeatedly reached auto mode through ordinary composer editing keys despite longer waits; revisit only with a decision key distinct from composer editing, and keep approve-all unreachable through arrow selection.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015873015873015872,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:0a7bf21bf921c1a74816f940\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.review.independence\",\n      \"heading\": \"convention\",\n      \"text\": \"Independent architecture reviews must form findings and a proposed architecture from primary repository evidence before consulting another agent’s research; subsequent comparison must preserve the original findings.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015625,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:9d0b18a6ad13a684969d2681\",\n      \"path\": \"architecture.boundaries.rationale\",\n      \"heading\": \"decision\",\n      \"text\": \"The user confirmed that folder trust must remain separate from approval mode settings: trust controls whether project instructions and integrations load, while tool approval policy is configured independently.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015384615384615385,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:160463488de5e92ed96108fc\",\n      \"path\": \"constraints.invariants.general\",\n      \"heading\": \"gotcha\",\n      \"text\": \"Doctor can cause its own endpoint and subprocess timeouts on installs with substantial saved history: its synchronous state-integrity scan blocked concurrent checks for about five seconds across 53,376 task files, while the same configuration with empty state completed in 463 ms.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015151515151515152,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:2d3baa805e09c255faa321fe\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.testing.rules\",\n      \"heading\": \"decision\",\n      \"text\": \"The next readiness assessment should test sustained supervised engineering behavior afresh, rather than mechanically checking off prior findings; changed lifecycle semantics may alter their relevance or expose new integration problems.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014925373134328358,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:d03646b7f483da70cf518747\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.release.acceptance\",\n      \"heading\": \"invariant\",\n      \"text\": \"Green CI and independent code review do not constitute qualification or release acceptance; source may merge for RC construction, but publication requires all acceptance gates and evidence tied to the actual candidate.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014705882352941176,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:50:18Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:50:18Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:3ee09d8f3cf429b06de6ae2f\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.release.authorization\",\n      \"heading\": \"convention\",\n      \"text\": \"The user authorized necessary commits, pushes, PRs, merges, release candidates, tags, and stable publication after required gates pass; agents should not request these approvals again and must coordinate with one designated release publisher.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014492753623188406,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:9b83f79b3deabb9c14d02ed6\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.testing.rules\",\n      \"heading\": \"convention\",\n      \"text\": \"Terminal acceptance requires real PTY validation where possible; handler-level unit tests alone cannot establish safe approval behavior or terminal usability.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014285714285714285,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":334553162}},"started_at_ms":1793208023152,"completed_at_ms":1793208023487}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:20:24.701Z","ordinal":466469,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18386-fe7d-7b93-9ff7-ee30fe254627","call_id":"call_67c0794ae56f4305a4ef330e09ab1b8f","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3379)\nTotal output lines: 266\n\nMake an authenticated HTTP request to an Entire API and print the JSON response.\n\nThese endpoints are internal and can change shape without notice; where a\npurpose-built command exists, its output is the stable interface.\n\nThe CLI attaches the right bearer token and dials the right host for the\nchosen backend, so you don't have to plumb auth yourself:\n\n  --to core   the control plane (default): orgs, repos, mirrors, clusters, /me\n  --to cell   your home entire-api cell: /me/* activity, repo aggregates\n\nUse --jurisdiction <slug> (e.g. us, eu) to reach a specific jurisdiction's\nentire-api cell instead of your home one; it implies --to cell.\n\nBoth backends act as ENTIRE_TOKEN when set, else the selected login\n(--context, else $ENTIRE_CONTEXT, else the active context), so a staging\nlogin reaches staging's control plane and cells. The cell host comes from\nenvironment's cluster listing; an explicit ENTIRE_API_BASE_URL names the\ndata host directly instead.\n\n<path> is the full path on that host, e.g. /api/v1/clusters. These\nplaceholders are filled from the current repo's origin remote:\n  {owner} {repo}   the GitHub owner / repo\n  {repo_id}        the repo's Entire ULID (from its mirror) — cells key on this\n\nThe method is GET unless a field/body is given (then POST); override with -X.\n\nUsage:\n  entire api <path> [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  entire api /api/v1/clusters\n  entire api --to cell /api/v1/me/activity\n  entire api --jurisdiction eu /api/v1/me/activity\n  entire api --to cell \"/api/v1/me/recap?repo={repo_id}\"\n  entire api -X POST /api/v1/projects -f name=demo\n\nFlags:\n  -F, --field stringArray       add a typed parameter in key=value format; true/false/null/numbers are converted (repeatable)\n  -H, --header stringArray      add a request header in key:value format (repeatable)\n  -h, --help                    help for api\n  -i, --include                 print the response status line and headers too\n      --input string            file with the request body (\"-\" for stdin)\n  -j, --jurisdiction string     target a specific jurisdiction's cell (e.g. us, eu) instead of your home cell; implies --to cell\n  -X, --method string           HTTP method (default GET, or POST when a field/body is given)\n  -f, --raw-field stringArray   add a string parameter in key=value format (repeatable)\n      --to string               which backend to call: core or cell (default \"core\")\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\n--- query trail 20 ---\n{\n  \"branch\": \"main\",\n  \"query\": \"PR #305 trail 20 Entire Gates failure review findings acceptance\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:d03646b7f483da70cf518747\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.release.acceptance\",\n      \"heading\": \"invariant\",\n      \"text\": \"Green CI and independent code review do not constitute qualification or release acceptance; source may merge for RC construction, but publication requires all acceptance gates and evidence tied to the actual candidate.\",\n      \"score\": 0.01639344262295082,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:50:18Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:50:18Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:1b54f28e98d5720d87a63c30\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.testing.rules\",\n      \"heading\": \"closed-negative\",\n      \"text\": \"The context-convergence branch at 31d6622 was not accepted: its only real acceptance run failed at step 119 without an artifact after repeated long-write timeouts, and an isolated reproduction exposed findings loss and ID reuse after crash/resume; revisit acceptance after fixing recovery and persistence and completing a fact-checked artifact-producing rerun.\",\n      \"score\": 0.016129032258064516,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:050f2a39d9261b65895c0d5c\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.review.rules\",\n      \"heading\": \"invariant\",\n      \"text\": \"Release merges require a recorded independent ACCEPT and green CI for the exact PR head; self-acceptance and unrecorded claims of reviewer acceptance do not satisfy the gate.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015873015873015872,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"so…1179 tokens truncated…4516,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:e7f00f83dda26737693392e1\",\n      \"path\": \"architecture.boundaries.rationale\",\n      \"heading\": \"closed-negative\",\n      \"text\": \"Timing delays and repeated Enter presses were rejected as sufficient protection for session-wide approval: independent PTY reviews repeatedly reached auto mode through ordinary composer editing keys despite longer waits; revisit only with a decision key distinct from composer editing, and keep approve-all unreachable through arrow selection.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015873015873015872,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:0a7bf21bf921c1a74816f940\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.review.independence\",\n      \"heading\": \"convention\",\n      \"text\": \"Independent architecture reviews must form findings and a proposed architecture from primary repository evidence before consulting another agent’s research; subsequent comparison must preserve the original findings.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015625,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:9d0b18a6ad13a684969d2681\",\n      \"path\": \"architecture.boundaries.rationale\",\n      \"heading\": \"decision\",\n      \"text\": \"The user confirmed that folder trust must remain separate from approval mode settings: trust controls whether project instructions and integrations load, while tool approval policy is configured independently.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015384615384615385,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:160463488de5e92ed96108fc\",\n      \"path\": \"constraints.invariants.general\",\n      \"heading\": \"gotcha\",\n      \"text\": \"Doctor can cause its own endpoint and subprocess timeouts on installs with substantial saved history: its synchronous state-integrity scan blocked concurrent checks for about five seconds across 53,376 task files, while the same configuration with empty state completed in 463 ms.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015151515151515152,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:2d3baa805e09c255faa321fe\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.testing.rules\",\n      \"heading\": \"decision\",\n      \"text\": \"The next readiness assessment should test sustained supervised engineering behavior afresh, rather than mechanically checking off prior findings; changed lifecycle semantics may alter their relevance or expose new integration problems.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014925373134328358,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:d03646b7f483da70cf518747\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.release.acceptance\",\n      \"heading\": \"invariant\",\n      \"text\": \"Green CI and independent code review do not constitute qualification or release acceptance; source may merge for RC construction, but publication requires all acceptance gates and evidence tied to the actual candidate.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014705882352941176,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:50:18Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:50:18Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:3ee09d8f3cf429b06de6ae2f\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.release.authorization\",\n      \"heading\": \"convention\",\n      \"text\": \"The user authorized necessary commits, pushes, PRs, merges, release candidates, tags, and stable publication after required gates pass; agents should not request these approvals again and must coordinate with one designated release publisher.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014492753623188406,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:9b83f79b3deabb9c14d02ed6\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.testing.rules\",\n      \"heading\": \"convention\",\n      \"text\": \"Terminal acceptance requires real PTY validation where possible; handler-level unit tests alone cannot establish safe approval behavior or terminal usability.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014285714285714285,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","create_time":1793208024.7017848}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
