{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:21:45.099Z","ordinal":466542,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","session_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","root_turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","response_id":"resp_0db389702a7164cc016ae22f27e6c4819f9307f809cbd3e74e","usage":{"input_tokens":139963,"cached_input_tokens":139136,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":60,"reasoning_output_tokens":13,"total_tokens":140023},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":36118671,"cached_input_tokens":35689728,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":135766,"reasoning_output_tokens":83567,"total_tokens":36254437},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":8665198883,"cached_input_tokens":8572681088,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24765717,"reasoning_output_tokens":14354160,"total_tokens":8689964600}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:21:45.156Z","ordinal":466543,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e4086511-6f02-406a-be78-684d7e68c4f3","process_id":"63960","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","xerj feedback --submit --agent \"GPT-6.1 Codex\" --used-for \"Reference lookup for Nexus operation restart rebase and intent context\" --verdict \"Definition-first symbol lookup worked and located AgentWorkUnitExecutor.run. Search returned useful nearby type and change-baseline context, though indexed lines are historical and must be checked against live Git.\" "],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"xerj feedback --submit --agent \"GPT-6.1 Codex\" --used-for \"Reference lookup for Nexus operation restart rebase and intent context\" --verdict \"Definition-first symbol lookup worked and located AgentWorkUnitExecutor.run. Search returned useful nearby type and change-baseline context, though indexed lines are historical and must be checked against live Git.\" "}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"the `--remote` flag is unsupported when a repository argument is provided\n\nCreate a fork of a repository.\n\nWith no argument, creates a fork of the current repository. Otherwise, forks\nthe specified repository.\n\nBy default, the new fork is set to be your `origin` remote and any existing\norigin remote is renamed to `upstream`. To alter this behavior, you can set\na name for the new fork's remote with `--remote-name`.\n\nThe `upstream` remote will be set as the default remote repository.\n\nAdditional `git clone` flags can be passed after `--`.\n\n\nUSAGE\n  gh repo fork [<repository>] [-- <gitflags>...] [flags]\n\nFLAGS\n  --clone                 Clone the fork\n  --default-branch-only   Only include the default branch in the fork\n  --fork-name string      Rename the forked repository\n  --org string            Create the fork in an organization\n  --remote                Add a git remote for the fork\n  --remote-name string    Specify the name for the new remote (default \"origin\")\n\nINHERITED FLAGS\n  --help   Show help for command\n\nEXAMPLES\n  # Fork a repository\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo\n  \n  # Fork a repository and clone it locally\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone\n  \n  # Fork a repository without cloning it, skip the prompt\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone=false\n\nLEARN MORE\n  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\n  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\n  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\n  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\n\n# Ready-to-run — files ONLY the field report, nothing else.\n# Run these in a clone of xerj-org/xerj, not in the project you are working in.\ngit clone https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj.git\ncd xerj\ngh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork\nxerj feedback \\\n --agent \"GPT-6.1 Codex\" \\\n  --used-for \"Reference lookup for Nexus operation restart rebase and intent context\" --pointed-at \"1051 records under /home/mike/xerj-sources/nexus-code/core/src (autoindex run run-20261028T022152Z-ff10-0000)\" \\\n  --verdict \"Definition-first symbol lookup worked and located AgentWorkUnitExecutor.run. Search returned useful nearby type and change-baseline context, though indexed lines are historical and must be checked against live Git.\" --numbers \"not measured\" \\\n  -o user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-28-reference-lookup-for-nexus-operation-restart.md\ngit checkout -b field-report/reference-lookup-for-nexus-operation-restart\ngit add user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-28-reference-lookup-for-nexus-operation-restart.md\ngit commit --only user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-28-reference-lookup-for-nexus-operation-restart.md -m \"docs(field-report): reference-lookup-for-nexus-operation-restart\"\ngit push -u xerj-fork field-report/reference-lookup-for-nexus-operation-restart\ngh pr create --repo xerj-org/xerj --base main --head YOUR_LOGIN:field-report/reference-lookup-for-nexus-operation-restart \\\n  --title \"Agent field report: Reference lookup for Nexus operation restart rebase and intent context\" \\\n  --body \"Field report only; see user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-28-reference-lookup-for-nexus-operation-restart.md.\"\nerror: this account cannot push to xerj-org/xerj, and forking failed: `gh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork` failed\nNothing was branched.\n\nGitHub is unavailable (the pull request could not be opened (see above)); sending the field report to https://xerj.org/api/field-report instead.\nsent field report to https://xerj.org/api/field-report (HTTP 200)\n{\"ok\":true,\"stored\":true,\"note\":\"Thanks. The canonical path is a GitHub PR: https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj/tree/main/user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":15,"nanos":476537725}},"started_at_ms":1793208089677,"completed_at_ms":1793208105154}}
