{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:23:11.290Z","ordinal":466622,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9ae444c7-1a18-480d-a808-41e9a6f78ff7","process_id":"40680","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -i \"entire gates|approvals|trail approval|entire\" .github docs/v1.0.0 .entire 2>/dev/null | head -80; printf '\\n--- Entire CLI checkpoint help ---\\n'; entire checkpoint --help"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -i \"entire gates|approvals|trail approval|entire\" .github docs/v1.0.0 .entire 2>/dev/null | head -80; printf '\\n--- Entire CLI checkpoint help ---\\n'; entire checkpoint --help"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:187:| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:339:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker verifies source/tag/artifact/evidence hash bindings; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:26:| **M1 Safety floor** (critical path) | PLAN-01 (effect classes, DEC-01 posture, verifier gating, REPL approvals, read-only masking, argv sandbox, tripwire); PLAN-02 (process registry, cancel and shutdown sweep, bounds); PLAN-03 (project `.env` allowlist, CIDR locality, SSRF-safe fetch, skills/knowledge trust, plugin directories, EXT-004); PLAN-11 PR-11a/11b (parser, binding) | Untrusted input cannot cause unapproved exec, egress or configuration changes. Stop means stopped. No false VERIFIED from a filename coincidence. | **G1**: all ACC-SAFE, ACC-PROC, ACC-TRUST, ACC-VER-01..04 | 15–25 ed |\n.entire/agent-guide.md:1:# Entire repository agent guide — Brain\n.entire/agent-guide.md:6:    entire brain brief \"<task>\" --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:15:    entire brain recall \"<question>\" --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:26:    entire brain remember \"<memory>\" --path <category.subcategory.type> --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:59:  entire brain query \"<query>\" --json       # hybrid (lexical+vector, RRF) — the default\n.entire/agent-guide.md:60:  entire brain query --keyword \"<query>\" --json      # lexical keyword over memories + history + docs (BM25 for history/docs)\n.entire/agent-guide.md:61:  entire brain query --semantic \"<query>\" --json     # vector/semantic over memories + docs (+ history/conversation with a Gemma-class embedder)\n.entire/agent-guide.md:62:  entire brain get <id> --json              # fetch one item by id (fact:… | history:… | doc:…)\n.entire/agent-guide.md:63:  entire brain multi-get <id>... --json     # fetch several by id\n.entire/agent-guide.md:66:  entire brain status [repo] --json         # sources, memories+verification, semantic coverage/freshness/blind spots, live state\n.entire/agent-guide.md:67:  entire brain status --fail-on release     # CI gate: nonzero when freshness is not ok or blind spots exist (also: unsafe, degraded, blind-spots)\n.entire/agent-guide.md:68:  entire brain overview [repo] --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:69:  entire brain brief \"<task>\" --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:70:  entire brain show <id> --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:71:  entire brain agent-guide\n.entire/agent-guide.md:72:  entire brain path [repo]\n.entire/agent-guide.md:75:  entire brain distill --dry-run --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:76:  entire brain recall \"<query>\" [--scope local|cross-cutting] [--expand] --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:77:  entire brain remember \"<memory>\" [--path category.sub.type] --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:78:  entire brain verify [<memory-id | query>] --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:79:  entire brain memories tree [--path <prefix>] [--depth N]\n.entire/agent-guide.md:80:  entire brain memories retract <memory-id> --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:81:  entire brain inspect blame <memory-id> --json # source anchors a memory was derived from\n.entire/agent-guide.md:84:  entire brain inspect code \"<query>\" --json        # find a symbol in the graph\n.entire/agent-guide.md:85:  entire brain inspect search-graph \"<query>\" --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:86:  entire brain inspect query-graph \"type:CALLS <query>\" --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:87:  entire brain inspect graph-ui semantic-graph.html\n.entire/agent-guide.md:88:  entire brain inspect snippet <symbol-or-id> --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:89:  entire brain inspect trace-path <from-symbol> <to-symbol> --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:90:  entire brain inspect dead-code --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:91:  entire brain inspect ingest-traces <json-or-ndjson-file> --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:92:  entire brain inspect context <symbol-or-id> --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:93:  entire brain inspect impact <symbol-or-file> --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:94:  entire brain inspect changes --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:95:  entire brain inspect tests \"<query>\" --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:96:  entire brain inspect boundaries --kind route|tool|workflow --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:97:  entire brain inspect regressions \"<query>\" --location-only [--include-deletions] --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:99:<!-- entire-agent-activation: {\"schema_version\":1,\"enabled\":[\"brain\"]} -->\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:49:**Options.** (A) Remove the REPL. **(B, chosen)** The REPL is a supported secondary surface: used for non-TTY input, scripting and fallback, with its approvals fixed to the TUI's standard. (C) The REPL stays the default.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:21:Both results are on tuned tasks. The following are missing entirely:\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:33:**Verifier runs bypass the gate entirely (VER-01).** Before the first edit (change baseline, `agent.ts:1602-1617`) and at every `task_completed` (`agent.ts:3432-3436`), Nexus runs the repository's own test command (`make test` / `npm test` / `cargo test` / `pytest`, chosen by `tester.ts:113-136`) through `bridge.executeTool` directly. These calls skip `dispatchToolCall`, so even review mode never asks, and no workspace-trust check applies. Opening a hostile repo and approving one `edit_file` therefore runs that repo's arbitrary test script on the host. `/test` and `nexus eval` run `execSync` on the host, bypassing the sandbox and blocking the event loop (VER-14).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:70:| REQ-TUI-10 | B7/F1-F3 | Approvals cannot be decided by stray typing; approve-all deliberate | TOP_TIER B7; USER_MANUAL Approvals | **ACCEPTED WITH DEFECTS** (independent round 5, NEXUS_TUI_SURFACE_2026-10-12.md:165,259); 028ca90 follow-up implementer-verified only | Y (round 5), N (follow-up) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:80:| REQ-TUI-11 | TUI surface rows 1–20, O1–O3 | Markdown, outcomes in words, bounded output, approvals, crash/recovery, resume history, narrow terminals, 0-byte idle | NEXUS_TUI_SURFACE_2026-10-12.md | PASS rows; independent \"ACCEPTED WITH DEFECTS\" | Y |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:52:  - Approvals cannot be decided by stray typing.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:96:| EVL-005 | S3 | Metric coverage | eval/score.mjs:48-69 | SOURCE. Missing metrics: recovery (after an injected fault), intervention (operator prompts or approvals), an explicit bounded-failure classification, and cost per correct task. Regressions are counted only when the repo's own suite fails. | Missing v1 dimensions. | See §7. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:58:| AGT-15 | S4 | Persistence cost | state.ts recordProgress/recordOperationStart/End (load+redact+fsync rewrite of entire task JSON incl. messages) | INFERENCE/MEASUREMENT gap. ≥3 full-state rewrites per tool call, each O(conversation) with redaction scan and fsync. | Latency on long conversations / slow disks. | Measure (see §6). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:117:| Stop loading the project `.env` entirely | Breaks the documented per-project endpoint/model workflow (CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md). An allowlist keeps it. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:42:  approvals via `rl.question(\"[Y/n/d/a]\")`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:46:- Approval default: both sidecar and REPL default to `auto` (no approvals) unless `--approve` (sidecar.ts:935,\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:63:| TUI-07 | S2 | Default safety posture | sidecar.ts:935; repl.ts:69; quickstart.md:55 | SOURCE + DOC-CLAIM: default mode is `auto` (no approvals) for both surfaces; quickstart says \"Enter a small task, review requested actions\" | New users unknowingly grant the model unprompted write/shell authority | Decide v1 default (recommend review on first run / untrusted workspace); fix quickstart wording |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:132:| Render races (approval arriving during overlay/help/model picker; pending_approvals queue) | PTY: open `?` help, have mock emit 2 tool calls in one reply under --approve; verify title \"n waiting\" and no decision leakage |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:51:| 14 | Docs: USER_MANUAL approvals/modes, quickstart \"review requested actions\", ARCHITECTURE §3 controls-and-limits, release notes entry. | docs | 1-13 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/mockgw.py:25:    if scenario == \"write2\":  # two sequential approvals\n\n--- Entire CLI checkpoint help ---\nOperations on checkpoints — the persistent records of agent work tied to commits.\n\nCommands:\n  list     List checkpoints on the current branch\n  explain  Explain a checkpoint, commit, or session\n  tokens   Show token usage and optimization recommendations\n  search   Search checkpoints (semantic + keyword)\n  delete   Delete a checkpoint locally and from checkpoint remotes\n\nExamples:\n  entire checkpoint list\n  entire checkpoint explain <id|sha>\n  entire checkpoint tokens <id>\n  entire checkpoint search \"fix login\"\n  entire checkpoint delete <id> --dry-run\n\nUsage:\n  entire checkpoint [command]\n\nAliases:\n  checkpoint, cp, checkpoints\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  delete      Delete a checkpoint locally and from checkpoint remotes\n  explain     Explain a session, commit, or checkpoint\n  list        List checkpoints on the current branch\n  search      Search checkpoints, commits, and sessions using semantic and keyword matching\n  tokens      Show token usage and optimization recommendations for a checkpoint\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for checkpoint\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\nUse \"entire checkpoint [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":41066}},"started_at_ms":1793208191289,"completed_at_ms":1793208191290}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:23:13.154Z","ordinal":466623,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18389-9082-7460-b4dd-2259d5c80a7d","call_id":"call_2ca43653d3ce420d8b9d7c6a148fa5c4","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2880)\nTotal output lines: 94\n\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:187:| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:339:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker verifies source/tag/artifact/evidence hash bindings; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:26:| **M1 Safety floor** (critical path) | PLAN-01 (effect classes, DEC-01 posture, verifier gating, REPL approvals, read-only masking, argv sandbox, tripwire); PLAN-02 (process registry, cancel and shutdown sweep, bounds); PLAN-03 (project `.env` allowlist, CIDR locality, SSRF-safe fetch, skills/knowledge trust, plugin directories, EXT-004); PLAN-11 PR-11a/11b (parser, binding) | Untrusted input cannot cause unapproved exec, egress or configuration changes. Stop means stopped. No false VERIFIED from a filename coincidence. | **G1**: all ACC-SAFE, ACC-PROC, ACC-TRUST, ACC-VER-01..04 | 15–25 ed |\n.entire/agent-guide.md:1:# Entire repository agent guide — Brain\n.entire/agent-guide.md:6:    entire brain brief \"<task>\" --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:15:    entire brain recall \"<question>\" --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:26:    entire brain remember \"<memory>\" --path <category.subcategory.type> --json\n.entire/agent-guide.md:59:  entire brain query \"<query>\" --json       # hybrid (lexical+vector, RR…1380 tokens truncated… gap. ≥3 full-state rewrites per tool call, each O(conversation) with redaction scan and fsync. | Latency on long conversations / slow disks. | Measure (see §6). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md:117:| Stop loading the project `.env` entirely | Breaks the documented per-project endpoint/model workflow (CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md). An allowlist keeps it. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:42:  approvals via `rl.question(\"[Y/n/d/a]\")`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:46:- Approval default: both sidecar and REPL 