{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:29:14.837Z","ordinal":466898,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae230e63290819f97c7dd649e120e18","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Claude’s memory observer reports: “Claude rejected the request because its five-hour usage allowance is exhausted.” I left it untouched.\n\n**Using Entire:** status and Brain lookups worked. Checkpoint search could not authenticate because the host lacks the Secret Service needed for `org.freedesktop.secrets`. The independent reviewer confirmed that formal Entire approvals are unavailable for the same reason. XERJ lookup also ran, and its required field report was submitted successfully.\n\n**Release work advanced:**\n\n- Current `main`: `8580c821`. Its CI run `40733687806` is still running; CodeQL passed.\n- PR #302: rebased and pushed as `87b560c7`, with exact-base independent review **ACCEPT**. Requirements enforcement, version sync, TypeScript, and diff checks passed. Exact CI is running. Entire Trail 17 is up to date but reports **two unresolved high findings** and no reviewer approval.\n- PR #305: rebased and pushed as `fde0b7b9`; its three commits are patch-identical to the previously reviewed version. Exact-base review **ACCEPT**; TypeScript and diff checks passed; exact CI is running. Trail 20 has no blocking findings and is up to date, but still needs reviewer approval.\n- PR #300 was independently updated to `2b6490f7`. Its CI is running; Trail 15 has no blocking findings and is up to date, but still needs reviewer approval.\n\nThe SUITE claim is now held by another `codex-root` session for PR #302 validation. Its PID is not visible here, so I did not run tests or take over the claim. I recorded a safe-boundary status and release request.\n\n**Action needed:** an authorized independent reviewer needs a working Entire-authenticated session to inspect Trail 17’s two findings and record approvals for the exact current trails (#15, #17, and #20). The reviewer who accepted #302 and #305 cannot access the approval system from this host.\n\nAcceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**. RC10 is still the latest public prerelease; held-out qualification, manual terminal evidence, and other exact-RC gates remain open. No RC or release is being declared accepted.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":777,"lineEnd":789,"note":"used prior Nexus release workflow context and verified it against current repository state"}],"rolloutIds":["01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0"]}},"started_at_ms":1793208550223,"completed_at_ms":1793208554837}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:29:14.843Z","ordinal":466899,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae230e63290819f97c7dd649e120e18","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Claude’s memory observer reports: “Claude rejected the request because its five-hour usage allowance is exhausted.” I left it untouched.\n\n**Using Entire:** status and Brain lookups worked. Checkpoint search could not authenticate because the host lacks the Secret Service needed for `org.freedesktop.secrets`. The independent reviewer confirmed that formal Entire approvals are unavailable for the same reason. XERJ lookup also ran, and its required field report was submitted successfully.\n\n**Release work advanced:**\n\n- Current `main`: `8580c821`. Its CI run `40733687806` is still running; CodeQL passed.\n- PR #302: rebased and pushed as `87b560c7`, with exact-base independent review **ACCEPT**. Requirements enforcement, version sync, TypeScript, and diff checks passed. Exact CI is running. Entire Trail 17 is up to date but reports **two unresolved high findings** and no reviewer approval.\n- PR #305: rebased and pushed as `fde0b7b9`; its three commits are patch-identical to the previously reviewed version. Exact-base review **ACCEPT**; TypeScript and diff checks passed; exact CI is running. Trail 20 has no blocking findings and is up to date, but still needs reviewer approval.\n- PR #300 was independently updated to `2b6490f7`. Its CI is running; Trail 15 has no blocking findings and is up to date, but still needs reviewer approval.\n\nThe SUITE claim is now held by another `codex-root` session for PR #302 validation. Its PID is not visible here, so I did not run tests or take over the claim. I recorded a safe-boundary status and release request.\n\n**Action needed:** an authorized independent reviewer needs a working Entire-authenticated session to inspect Trail 17’s two findings and record approvals for the exact current trails (#15, #17, and #20). The reviewer who accepted #302 and #305 cannot access the approval system from this host.\n\nAcceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**. RC10 is still the latest public prerelease; held-out qualification, manual terminal evidence, and other exact-RC gates remain open. No RC or release is being declared accepted.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:777-789|note=[used prior Nexus release workflow context and verified it against current repository state]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","create_time":1793208550.20131,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0db389702a7164cc016ae230e63290819f97c7dd649e120e18","turn_id":"01a18366-2421-7770-adb2-8a0eb3a8a68d","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a1838f-155b-74f0-bf68-d6200e1b9347","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":22163}}
