{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:31:17.003Z","ordinal":466984,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1838f-4c7d-7b60-a64b-253c51d0a9ff","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-99f8e187-e48c-4a00-b5ed-070cf0dec0dd","process_id":"87613","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -i 'Claude Code|I.m Claude|you are Claude|assistant identity|Nexus is|You are Nexus' cli/src docs | head -120"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-ordinary-child-fix","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -i 'Claude Code|I.m Claude|you are Claude|assistant identity|Nexus is|You are Nexus' cli/src docs","query":"Claude Code|I.m Claude|you are Claude|assistant identity|Nexus is|You are Nexus","path":"cli"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/README.md:11:| Understand what Nexus is today, what was examined, and what is wrong | [AUDIT.md](AUDIT.md) |\ncli/src/operation_view.ts:335: * only the facts the operator needs to see what Nexus is doing and why.\ndocs/WP05_EGRESS_PROTECTION_EVIDENCE.md:14:In accordance with the Whole-Issue Closure Audit for Nexus Issue #12 (`ISSUE_12_REMAINING_REQUIREMENTS_IDENTIFIED`), WP-05 (INC-06) resolves the core architectural primitive required to satisfy sensitive-data egress interception and secret quarantine across the Nexus Code platform.\ndocs/WP01_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:1:# Nexus Issue #12 — WP-01 Independent Implementation Review\ndocs/WP01_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:15:An independent, adversarial implementation review was conducted on the delivered artifacts for Nexus Issue #12 Work Package 01 (`WP-01: Capability Registry & Common Execution Spine`). The review evaluated whether the implementation satisfies the normative contracts established in the operator-accepted Phase 4 implementation work packages (`docs/PHASE4_IMPLEMENTATION_WORK_PACKAGES.md`) and the Phase 3 implementation decomposition (`docs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md`).\ncli/src/core/capabilities.ts:3: * Nexus Issue #12 — WP-01 (INC-01, CAP-001..007, DEDUP-001..004)\ndocs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-04-nexus-ratatui-live-default-design.md:5:**Goal:** Someone who clones the repo, builds it, and runs `harness` lands in a live, full-screen terminal session whose look and feel competes with frontier coding harnesses (Claude Code, Codex CLI).\ndocs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-04-nexus-ratatui-live-default-design.md:120:4. **Frontier polish.** Empty-state identity, quiet chrome, themes, diff presentation, resize and minimum-size handling. README and first-run docs updated to describe what actually ships. PTY captures compared against a fixed look-and-feel checklist drawn from Claude Code and Codex CLI (feel, not feature parity).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:49:- `/model appliance engineering/b0` and the \"parity with Codex and Claude Code\" claim in the docs.\ncli/src/slash/session_commands.ts:378:      lines.push(`\\nNexus is already up to date (${installed.version}).`);\ncli/src/slash/session_commands.ts:388:    return reply(\"upgrade\", `Nexus is already up to date (${installed.version}). Use /upgrade --force to reinstall.`, true);\ncli/src/ui.ts:139:    if (/Thinking and analyzing/i.test(text)) return \"Nexus is considering the next step\";\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md:26:- \"Parity with Codex and Claude Code\" (HIST-06).\ncli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts:76: * Nexus issued with the authorized task (the first prompt, or a resume prompt where compaction kept only that). The\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CURRENT-NEXUS-CONTEXT-ARCHITECTURE.md:80:**`ContextRouteManager`**: no such symbol exists anywhere in `cli/src` or `core/src` (grep). Nothing in Nexus is currently a context planner/router. (OBSERVED.)\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:91:  - Upgrade command reports: \"Nexus is running from a development checkout. Use `git pull && make build` to update.\"\ncli/src/repl.ts:912:                console.log(pc.green(`\\nNexus is already up to date (${installed.version}).\\n`));\ncli/src/repl.ts:923:              console.log(pc.green(`Nexus is already up to date (${installed.version}). Use /upgrade --force to reinstall.\\n`));\ndocs/ISSUE12_POST_WP05_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:1:# Nexus Issue #12 — Post-WP-05 Whole-Issue Closure Assessment\ndocs/ISSUE12_POST_WP05_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:18:Nexus Issue #12 was chartered to establish a unified, secure, verifiable agentic software engineering runtime across 23 normative requirement domains comprising 122 individual requirements. Its foundational goals were:\ndocs/ISSUE12_POST_WP05_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:285:All closure-blocking normative obligations for Nexus Issue #12 have been satisfied and operator-accepted. The remaining partial items represent accepted bounded limitations and non-blocking follow-up improvements.\ncli/src/core/spine.ts:3: * Nexus Issue #12 — WP-01 (INC-02, EXEC-001..013, FAIL-001..004, F-09)\ncli/src/core/candidate.ts:3: * Nexus Issue #12 — WP-04 (INC-05, DEC-02, CAND-001..004, EVID-002, VER-001..005)\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:84:| REQ-DX-04 | Positioning | \"engineered for direct parity with OpenAI Codex and Anthropic Claude Code\" | USER_MANUAL.md:3 | Contradicted by TOP_TIER §1 (\"not yet top-tier\"); no parity evidence | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:131:| HIST-06 | S3 | Install/positioning docs | docs/USER_MANUAL.md:3,14,19; docs/ARCHITECTURE.md:24-25,43; quickstart.md:21-23 | SOURCE/DOC: manual claims \"direct parity with OpenAI Codex and Anthropic Claude Code\"; `harness repl` (installed binary is `nexus`); `nexus --approve` vs quickstart `nexus repl --approve`; ARCHITECTURE names homelab hardware/port 18010 and calls `repl.ts` the TUI; quickstart \"install another specific version\" example is identical to the pinned command; MCP_GUIDE link is `file:///home/mike/...` | New users get wrong commands and inflated expectations | Reconcile docs to shipped binary (RELEASE-REQUIRED) |\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_ASSESSMENT.md:1:# Nexus Issue #12 — Final Acceptance Assessment\ncli/src/client.ts:1470:   * Real-time SSE token streaming for typewriter terminal output (matching Codex / Claude Code)\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:44:| PRV-17 | S4 | docs | docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md Limitations (\"No model catalog cache\") vs model_catalog.ts:51,86; Credentials (\"error bodies are bounded and redacted\") true only for provider connections (PRV-03); Authority claim (PRV-02); USER_MANUAL.md:3 \"direct parity with OpenAI Codex and Anthropic Claude Code\" | DOC-CLAIM vs SOURCE | Docs overstate guarantees. | Correct docs. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/BRIEF.md:7:Contest (Cloudflare Workers + Artifacts collaboration service, experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice, demo/) is a SEPARATE product; Nexus is its demo harness.\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:581:      \"Nexus is running from a source development checkout. Use `git pull && make build` to update, or install the packaged release via `install.sh`.\"\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:586:      installed.detail || \"Nexus is managed by an external package manager. Use your system package manager to upgrade.\"\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1536:          console.log(`\\nNexus is already up to date (${installed.version}).`);\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1576:              message: `Nexus is already at version ${installed.version}. Use --force to reinstall.`,\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1583:        console.log(`Nexus is already up to date (${installed.version}). Use --force to reinstall.`);\ncli/src/core/authority.ts:3: * Nexus Issue #12 — WP-02 (INC-03, AUTH-001..012, ACT-001..004, RES-001..004)\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1a.screens.txt:47:✔ Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1a.screens.txt:79:✔ Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1a.screens.txt:89:✔ Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1b.screens.txt:13:✔ Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1b.screens.txt:21:⠋ Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1b.screens.txt:22:✔ Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1c.screens.txt:14:✔ Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1c.screens.txt:23:✔ Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1d.screens.txt:15:✔ Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/r1d.screens.txt:25:✔ Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:1:# Nexus Issue #12 — Final Whole-Issue Closure Assessment\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:26:Nexus Issue #12 was chartered to establish a **single, cohesive application and execution contract** governing:\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:262:  The invariant that **resource authority does not confer disclosure authority** is a core governing principle of Nexus Issue #12 established in Phase 2. Because `client.ts` dispatches unquarantined prompts to LLM endpoints and `SecretsVault` uses predictable sequential integers rather than cryptographically unguessable scoped references (`REHYD-001`), the egress security boundary cannot be declared normatively satisfied. Unless the operator explicitly desensitizes the scope of Issue #12 to exclude egress interception, these 12 requirements prevent unconditional issue closure.\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:293:Nexus Issue #12 has successfully achieved its **Critical-Path Capability Integration and System Journey** milestones across `WP-01`, `WP-02`, `WP-04`, `WP-07`, `WP-10`, and `WP-11`. The unified execution spine, capability registry, granular authority engine, candidate validation tracker, durable task persistence, and converged application core are demonstrably operational, robust, and verified.\ncli/src/agent.ts:232:You are Nexus Code, the agent host. The language model provider and model are components Nexus connects to; they do not define or replace the host application. Do not identify this runtime as Claude Code, Codex CLI, OpenCode, or another client based on a model name, provider, skill instructions, or installed executable. When describing the current host or choosing instructions conditional on the host application, identify Nexus Code as the current host. If instructions do not include a compatible Nexus or generic path, explain the mismatch and ask the operator how to proceed.`;\ncli/src/agent.ts:3944:    return `You are Nexus Code, an autonomous AI software engineering agent running in a Linux shell environment.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:3:These rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:14:This document provides a fresh, independent, adversarial review of the Nexus Issue #12 Phase 3 Implementation Decomposition.\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:183:  3. If Nexus is executed in a non-git directory (`worktreeManager.isGitRepo() === false`), `git write-tree` errors out.\ndocs/PHASE2_REQUIREMENTS_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:14:This independent review evaluates the reconciled normative requirements package (`docs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md`) for Nexus Issue #12. The review was conducted from first principles, without deference to prior reviewer classifications, requirement counts, or resolution claims.\ndocs/PHASE2_REQUIREMENTS_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:200:- **Why It Matters:** Nexus is currently a private development project with no remote distribution. Mandating that all builds produce \"byte-identical outputs\" imposes reproducible-build engineering requirements (compiler path remapping, timestamp clamping, canonical archive ordering) that have no justification in Issue #12. Lockfile pinning (which Nexus already maintains) ensures dependency identity; byte-identical binary compilation is an unnecessary enterprise platform concern.\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:672:To avoid costly architectural rework if Nexus is publicly released:\ndocs/PHASE3_CORRECTIONS_VERIFICATION.md:2:**Nexus Issue #12 — Implementation Decomposition Narrow Verification**\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_DOCTOR_RECOVERED_REQUEST.md:17:Use Claude Code and other harnesses as behavioral references, while designing around Nexus’s current architecture.\ndocs/ISSUE12_REQUIREMENT_CLOSURE_MATRIX.md:1:# Nexus Issue #12 — Authoritative Normative Requirements Closure Matrix\ndocs/ISSUE12_REQUIREMENT_CLOSURE_MATRIX.md:113:| `REL-004` | 19: Release & SBOM | WP-11 (INC-12) | If Nexus is publicly distributed, active supported release lines MUST provide security ... | `scripts/generate_sbom.sh, Makefile` | make verify-reproducibility | **DEMONSTRATED** | None |\ndocs/WP05_INDEPENDENT_QUALIFICATION.md:23:All 16 in-scope requirements identified by the Nexus Issue #12 Whole-Issue Closure Audit have been independently inspected and falsification-tested.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_DOGFOODING_READINESS_REVIEW_2026-10-03.md:325:| C-2 | README overclaims (\"comparable to Codex/Claude Code\", \"state-aware\", persisted history, \"live\" TUI) |\ndocs/ISSUE12_POST_WP05_REQUIREMENT_CLOSURE_MATRIX.md:1:# Nexus Issue #12 — Post-WP-05 Normative Requirements Closure Matrix\ndocs/ISSUE12_POST_WP05_REQUIREMENT_CLOSURE_MATRIX.md:116:| `REL-004` | 19: Release & SBOM | WP-11 (INC-12) | If Nexus is publicly distributed, active supported release lines MUST provide security ... | `scripts/generate_sbom.sh, Makefile` | make verify-reproducibility | **DEMONSTRATED** | None |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:22:**Nexus is not yet a top-tier coding harness, and its maturity on representative coding objectives is unmeasured.**\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:113:From `peers.md` (primary sources, versions as of 2026-10-12): Codex CLI 0.162.1, Claude Code 2.1.296, OpenCode 1.19.0,\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:116:- **OS-level sandboxing of commands** (Codex, Claude Code: Seatbelt/bubblewrap; network allowlists). Nexus sandboxes\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:118:- **Workspace trust before executing project configuration** (Claude Code and Codex document trust prompts for\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:122:- **Interrupted-tool awareness on resume** (Claude Code marks cut-off tool calls for the model to check). Nexus records\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:124:- **Checkpoints/rewind with documented limits** (Claude Code rewind excludes shell-made changes). Nexus has checkpoints\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:126:- **Release discipline**: Codex and Claude Code ship signed/packaged releases several times a week with changelogs;\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:128:- Claude Code documents no support for non-Claude models; it cannot be a matched local-inference comparator. Codex\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:341:wire format can be served; Claude Code only in a cloud comparison. Record every deviation (unsupported features,\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1.1/GIT-AWARE-OPERATIONS-20261028/README.md:36:  integration worktree that was deleted outside Nexus is repaired on resume (`worktree add <branch>`), because the\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:14:1. **Role of This Document:** This document is the single authoritative, reconciled normative requirements package for Nexus Issue #12. It establishes the binding architectural and behavioral invariants that Nexus MUST satisfy.\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:588:| **REL-004** | If Nexus is publicly distributed, active supported release lines MUST provide security remediation for newly discovered High/Critical vulnerabilities. End-of-Sale (EOS) or End-of-Life (EOL) releases do NOT carry indefinite patch obligations, but MUST maintain explicit disposition (supersession, safe-version guidance, or withdrawal). | Obsolete vulnerable releases MUST be formally marked deprecated or withdrawn in public catalogs. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/RESULT.md:47:4. Cost: Nexus is the slowest per run (median 28–137 s vs Aider 25–72 s) and the only agent reporting tokens\ndocs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/RESULT.md:84:Total for 30 runs alone: Nexus 22.1 min, Goose 14.9 min (Goose correct 24/30). Nexus is ~1.5× Goose's wall time,\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md:9:**Scope:** Architecture-to-implementation decomposition for Nexus Issue #12.\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md:15:This document performs the Phase 3 **Implementation Decomposition** for Nexus Issue #12. Following the successful completion of Phase 1 (current-state reconstruction), Phase 2 (normative requirements), independent architecture and security reviews, targeted correction, narrow independent verification, and explicit operator acceptance, the Phase 2 requirements package established in [`docs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md`](file:///home/mike/nexus-code/docs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md) is the authoritative, immutable baseline for Nexus.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:8:Peers: OpenAI **Codex CLI** (stable 0.162.1), Anthropic **Claude Code** (2.1.296), **OpenCode** (v1.19.0, anomalyco/opencode),\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:14:| Area | Codex CLI | Claude Code | OpenCode | Goose | Aider |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:20:| **5. Inference compatibility** | Built-in providers `openai`, `ollama`, `lmstudio`; `--oss` with `oss_provider = lmstudio|ollama`; custom `model_providers.<id>.base_url`; `wire_api` only `responses` (Responses API required); `request_max_retries` 4, `stream_max_retries` 5, `stream_idle_timeout_ms` 300000 [CX-CFG]. | Anthropic API, Bedrock, Google Agent Platform (Vertex), Microsoft Foundry, LLM gateways exposing a supported (Anthropic-format) API; Anthropic \"doesn't support routing Claude Code to non-Claude models through any gateway\" [CC-GW]. Cost/token metrics via OTel; `-p --output-format json` returns usage and cost [CC-OTEL][CC-SESS]. | \"75+\" providers; Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp (llama-server) via `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` + `options.baseURL`; `@ai-sdk/openai` for `/v1/responses`; per-model context/output limits [OC-PROV]. | ~60 providers; Ollama (warns 4096 default ctx, `OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH`), LM Studio, Docker Model Runner (llama.cpp path), Ramalama (`--jinja` required), vLLM via `OPENAI_HOST`, custom providers in OpenAI/Anthropic/Ollama formats; \"models without [tool calling] can only do chat completion\" [GS-PROV]. | OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Groq, LM Studio, xAI, Azure, Cohere, DeepSeek, Ollama, OpenAI-compatible, OpenRouter, Copilot, Vertex, Bedrock; text edit formats (no native tool calls needed); warns weaker models may fail to produce applicable edits [AI-LLMS][AI-EDIT]. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:24:| **9. Evaluation (vendor claims)** | OpenAI claims for **models** (not the CLI harness): GPT-5.5 82.7% Terminal-Bench 2.0, 58.6% SWE-Bench Pro [EV-OAI]. | Anthropic claims for **models**: Claude Opus 4.6 65.4% Terminal-Bench 2.0 (max effort), 80.8% SWE-bench Verified (25-trial avg); footnote says runs used the Terminus-2 harness, i.e. not Claude Code [EV-ANT]. | None found. | None found. | Aider publishes its own LLM leaderboards (not read this session). |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:106:| CC-OV | https://code.claude.com/docs/en/overview | Claude Code overview |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:158:- **Claude Code:** licence text not read; foreground Bash default timeout not isolated from background limits; plan-mode\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:170:- WebFetch/WebSearch on each URL in the citation list (2026-10-12); grep over locally saved copies of long Claude Code\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:1:# Nexus Issue #12 — Final Acceptance Requirement Matrix\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md:115:| REL-004 | 19: Release & SBOM | If Nexus is publicly distributed, active supported release lines MUST provide security remediation for newly discovered High/Critical vulnerabilities. End-of-Sale (EOS) or End-of-Life (EOL) releases do NOT carry indefinite patch obligations, but MUST maintain explicit disposition (supersession, safe-version guidance, or withdrawal). | Obsolete vulnerable releases MUST be formally marked deprecated or withdrawn in public catalogs. | Phase 2 §23 | `scripts/generate_sbom.sh, Makefile`; make verify-reproducibility | DEMONSTRATED | None | Satisfied |\ndocs/PHASE4_IMPLEMENTATION_WORK_PACKAGES.md:41:This document executes **Phase 4 (Work-Package Derivation)** of Nexus Issue #12. Its sole objective is to transform the accepted Phase 3 implementation decomposition into 11 execution-ready work-package contracts (`WP-01` through `WP-11`). \ndocs/PHASE4_IMPLEMENTATION_WORK_PACKAGES.md:1360:Coordination for Nexus Issue #12 must maintain high visibility into technical dependencies and evidence receipts while avoiding administrative issue thrashing.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:7:# - Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:8:# ✔ Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:438:        You are Nexus Code, an autonomous AI software engineering agent running in a Linux shell environment.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:495:        You are Nexus Code, an autonomous AI software engineering agent running in a Linux shell environment.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:879:# - Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:880:# ✔ Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:888:# - Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:889:# ✔ Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:919:# - Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:934:# - Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:948:# - Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:979:# - Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:980:# ✔ Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:985:# - Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:986:# ✔ Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:998:# - Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:999:# ✔ Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:1007:# - Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/broader-failed.txt:1008:# ✔ Nexus is considering the next step\ndocs/reviews/evide