{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:31:17.974Z","ordinal":466985,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a181ab-bb8d-7471-bcfe-7451f754e731","turn_id":"01a1838f-4c7d-7b60-a64b-253c51d0a9ff","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c499ddbf-60f4-49f3-b10a-4e1db332843a","process_id":"94016","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","entire brain query \"Nexus identifies itself as Claude model-specific identity user reported fix regardless provider\" --json"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire brain query \"Nexus identifies itself as Claude model-specific identity user reported fix regardless provider\" --json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"branch\": \"main\",\n  \"query\": \"Nexus identifies itself as Claude model-specific identity user reported fix regardless provider\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:e5927510d389c11f18fad89b\",\n      \"path\": \"preferences.workflow.general\",\n      \"heading\": \"preference\",\n      \"text\": \"The user wants cloud providers selectable through the /model picker, with Ctrl-P opening provider connection options for API keys and subscription sign-ins; opencode and crush are the reference experiences.\",\n      \"score\": 0.01639344262295082,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:fad10c59d271dafb33fbf8a6\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.testing.comparisons\",\n      \"heading\": \"closed-negative\",\n      \"text\": \"openrouter/free was rejected for matched model comparisons because three requests were served by three different models; revisit only if every compared request can be pinned to the same model.\",\n      \"score\": 0.016129032258064516,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:d4bcc7cc5b5e160b8afcca62\",\n      \"path\": \"architecture.context.strategy\",\n      \"heading\": \"closed-negative\",\n      \"text\": \"Turn-specific context rebuilding was tested and rejected on the measured local-gateway stack: length sensitivity showed no accuracy decline from roughly 10k to 49k tokens, while prefix-stable rebuilding doubled wall time and reordered rebuilding increased it roughly ninefold by invalidating prefix-cache reuse; revisit only with materially different models, cache behavior, or workloads demonstrating a correctness benefit.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015873015873015872,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:e8e016b022c44c8db03f109f\",\n      \"path\": \"preferences.workflow.general\",\n      \"heading\": \"preference\",\n      \"text\": \"Use gstack /browse for web browsing; never use claude-in-chrome tools.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015625,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:c8696763e5c6cdd56cb984a2\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.testing.rules\",\n      \"heading\": \"decision\",\n      \"text\": \"Resolving the four original A blockers authorizes reassessment, not general dogfooding acceptance; qualify supervised use before considering unattended autonomy or using Nexus to improve itself.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015384615384615385,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:56161a52c62e5dd9380bdc3f\",\n      \"path\": \"architecture.boundaries.rationale\",\n      \"heading\": \"decision\",\n      \"text\": \"Nexus's primary product gap is accepted as absent objective continuity; a supervisor above runTurn warrants an architectural spike, but the supervisor architecture itself is not yet accepted.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015151515151515152,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:f4a9e32a42e5384afe754102\",\n      \"path\": \"constraints.invariants.general\",\n      \"heading\": \"invariant\",\n      \"text\": \"Optional provider capability failures must remain scoped to that connection and capability, preserve standalone operation, and never silently select another provider or disclose task content elsewhere.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014925373134328358,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:7a77d8047e2e3ae72e419cac\",\n      \"path\": \"preferences.workflow.general\",\n      \"heading\": \"preference\",\n      \"text\": \"The user prioritizes model accuracy over token throughput when choosing the local inference setup.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014705882352941176,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:a5f808879561493804920881\",\n      \"path\": \"architecture.routing.requirements\",\n      \"heading\": \"invariant\",\n      \"text\": \"The user expects the gateway, also called the orchestrator, to support model routing and wants different models considered rather than assuming both GPUs should serve the same model.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014492753623188406,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:22fb6442dee5e3f0374c55f6\",\n      \"path\": \"architecture.boundaries.rationale\",\n      \"heading\": \"invariant\",\n      \"text\": \"The inference host provides capabilities to Nexus without coupling Nexus to a particular model or runtime; Nexus must drive escalation after validation failures because the gateway cannot observe validation outcomes.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014285714285714285,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":2,"nanos":206488833}},"started_at_ms":1793208675767,"completed_at_ms":1793208677974}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:31:19.672Z","ordinal":466986,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18390-fcf8-7250-9a4e-0f222d1fe4cd","call_id":"call_7487484389c0401988fddb498bff7c23","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 5.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---0---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1285)\nTotal output lines: 106\n\n{\n  \"branch\": \"main\",\n  \"query\": \"Nexus identifies itself as Claude model-specific identity user reported fix regardless provider\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:e5927510d389c11f18fad89b\",\n      \"path\": \"preferences.workflow.general\",\n      \"heading\": \"preference\",\n      \"text\": \"The user wants cloud providers selectable through the /model picker, with Ctrl-P opening provider connection options for API keys and subscription sign-ins; opencode and crush are the reference experiences.\",\n      \"score\": 0.01639344262295082,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:fad10c59d271dafb33fbf8a6\",\n      \"path\": \"workflow.testing.comparisons\",\n      \"heading\": \"closed-negative\",\n      \"text\": \"openrouter/free was rejected for matched model comparisons because three requests were served by three different models; revisit only if every compared request can be pinned to the same model.\",\n      \"score\": 0.016129032258064516,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:d4bcc7cc5b5e160b8afcca62\",\n      \"path\": \"architecture.context.strategy\",\n      \"heading\": \"closed-negative\",\n      \"text\": \"Turn-specific context rebuilding was tested and rejected on the measured local-gateway stack: length sensitivity showed no accuracy decline from roughly 10k to 49k tokens, while prefix-stable rebuilding doubled wall time and reordered rebuilding increased it roughly ninefold by invalidating prefix-cache reuse; revisit only with materially different models, cache behavior, or workloads demonstrating a correctness benefit.\",\n      \"score\": 0.015873015873015872,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:e8e016b022c44c8db03f109f\",\n      \"path\": \"preferences.workflow.general…285 tokens truncated…eated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:f4a9e32a42e5384afe754102\",\n      \"path\": \"constraints.invariants.general\",\n      \"heading\": \"invariant\",\n      \"text\": \"Optional provider capability failures must remain scoped to that connection and capability, preserve standalone operation, and never silently select another provider or disclose task content elsewhere.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014925373134328358,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:7a77d8047e2e3ae72e419cac\",\n      \"path\": \"preferences.workflow.general\",\n      \"heading\": \"preference\",\n      \"text\": \"The user prioritizes model accuracy over token throughput when choosing the local inference setup.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014705882352941176,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:a5f808879561493804920881\",\n      \"path\": \"architecture.routing.requirements\",\n      \"heading\": \"invariant\",\n      \"text\": \"The user expects the gateway, also called the orchestrator, to support model routing and wants different models considered rather than assuming both GPUs should serve the same model.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014492753623188406,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"fact\",\n      \"id\": \"fact:22fb6442dee5e3f0374c55f6\",\n      \"path\": \"architecture.boundaries.rationale\",\n      \"heading\": \"invariant\",\n      \"text\": \"The inference host provides capabilities to Nexus without coupling Nexus to a particular model or runtime; Nexus must drive escalation after validation failures because the gateway cannot observe validation outcomes.\",\n      \"score\": 0.014285714285714285,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T07:43:47Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---1---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"xerj search: these hits are lexical; this command does not consult the embedding.\n\n─── agent.ts:232  (score 53.63)\n    const TOKEN_COUNT_COOLDOWN_MS = 60_000;\n    \n    /** Consecutive low-yield pressure compactions after which compaction waits until a request would not fit. */\n    const LOW_YIELD_COMPACTIONS_BEFORE_HOLD = 2;\n    \n    const NEXUS_RUNTIME_IDENTITY = `### Runtime Identity\n    You are Nexus Code, the agent host. The language model provider and model are components Nexus connects to; they do not define or replace the host application. Do not identify this runtime as Claude Code, Codex CLI, OpenCode, or another client based on a model name, provider, skill instructions, or installed executable. When describing the current \n    … (--full 1200 to see more)\n\n─── types.ts:97  (score 25.78)\n    export interface HarnessConfig {\n      endpoint: string;          // e.g. \"http://localhost:1234/v1\" (LM Studio) or \"http://localhost:8000/v1\" (vLLM)\n      model: string;             // e.g. \"qwen2.5-coder-32b-instruct\"\n      apiKey?: string;           // Optional for local servers (defaults to \"local\")\n      maxSteps: number;          // Steps per segment (default 30). With `continuation` (the default), a segment boundary is a durable checkpoint, never the end of the task.\n      /**\n       * Automatic continuation past `maxSteps` while the work makes progress (see AutonomousAgent.runTurn). Absent:\n       * `maxSteps` en\n    … (--full 1200 to see more)\n\n─── client.ts:886  (score 22.52)\n              saveCredential(id, cred);\n            } else if (id === \"copilot\" && cred.refresh) {\n              if (force || !fresh(this.exchangedToken) || this.exchangedToken?.refresh !== cred.refresh) {\n                this.exchangedToken = REDACTED copilotToken(cred.refresh)) as OAuthCredential;\n              }\n              cred = this.exchangedToken!;\n            } else if (!fresh(cred)) {\n              throw new Error(`the ${label} sign-in read from ${found.source} has expired. Use ${found.source} once to refresh it, or sign in from Nexus (/model, then ctrl+p).`);\n            }\n          } catch (err: any) {\n            throw fail(\n    … (--full 1200 to see more)\n\n─── safe_fs.ts:25  (score 18.03)\n    /**\n     * Filesystem changes that cannot be redirected by symbolic links: the primitives `doctor --fix` uses.\n     *\n     * A path check followed by a path-based change is racy, and checking only the last component misses a linked parent\n     * (`~/.nexus -> /elsewhere` makes `~/.nexus/sessions` point outside the home). Here every change is made through a\n     * file descriptor that has been proven to be the expected object:\n     *\n     * 1. Ancestry: every component of the target below a trusted root (the operator's home, which may itself be a link)\n     *    must be a real directory entry — not a symbolic link — owned by \n    … (--full 1200 to see more)\n\n─── protocols/anthropic.ts:2  (score 17.14)\n    /**\n     * Anthropic Messages API: request projection from Nexus history and assembly of streamed/non-streamed responses.\n     *\n     * Tool calls are emitted only from complete tool_use blocks of a response that reached message_stop; a stream that\n     * ends earlier is \"incomplete\" and none of its calls run. Signed thinking blocks are kept as provider_state owned by\n     * \"anthropic:<model>\" and replayed only to that owner, and only when extended thinking is enabled for the request.\n     */\n    import type { ChatMessage, ToolCall } from \"../types.js\";\n    import type { UsageReport } from \"../usage.js\";\n    import {\n      argument\n    … (--full 1200 to see more)\n\n5 passage(s) from 'nexus-cli-*'. Cite ax_path:line (ax_path#locator for a data row) for anything you rely on.\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---2---"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 6030)\nTotal output lines: 120\n\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:11:| Understand what Nexus is today, what was examined, and what is wrong | [AUDIT.md](AUDIT.md) |\ncli/src/operation_view.ts:335: * only the facts the operator needs to see what Nexus is doing and why.\ndocs/WP05_EGRESS_PROTECTION_EVIDENCE.md:14:In accordance with the Whole-Issue Closure Audit for Nexus Issue #12 (`ISSUE_12_REMAINING_REQUIREMENTS_IDENTIFIED`), WP-05 (INC-06) resolves the core architectural primitive required to satisfy sensitive-data egress interception and secret quarantine across the Nexus Code platform.\ndocs/WP01_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:1:# Nexus Issue #12 — WP-01 Independent Implementation Review\ndocs/WP01_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:15:An independent, adversarial implementation review was conducted on the delivered artifacts for Nexus Issue #12 Work Package 01 (`WP-01: Capability Registry & Common Execution Spine`). The review evaluated whether the implementation satisfies the normative contracts established in the operator-accepted Phase 4 implementation work packages (`docs/PHASE4_IMPLEMENTATION_WORK_PACKAGES.md`) and the Phase 3 implementation decomposition (`docs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md`).\ncli/src/core/capabilities.ts:3: * Nexus Issue #12 — WP-01 (INC-01, CAP-001..007, DEDUP-001..004)\ndocs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-04-nexus-ratatui-live-default-design.md:5:**Goal:** Someone who clones the repo, builds it, and runs `harness` lands in a live, full-screen terminal session whose look and feel competes with frontier coding harnesses (Claude Code, Codex CLI).\ndocs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-04-nexus-ratatui-live-default-design.md:120:4. **Frontier polish.** Empty-state identity, quiet chrome, themes, diff presentation, resize and minimum-size handling. README and first-run docs updated to describe what actually ships. PTY captures compared against a fixed look-and-feel checklist drawn from Claude Code and Codex CLI (feel, not feature parity).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md:49:- `/model appliance engineering/b0` and the \"parity with Codex and Claude Code\" claim in the docs.\ncli/src/slash/session_commands.ts:378:      lines.push(`\\nNexus is already up to date (${installed.version}).`);\ncli/src/slash/session_commands.ts:388:    return reply(\"upgrade\", `Nexus is already up to date (${installed.version}). Use /upgrade --force to reinstall.`, true);\ncli/src/ui.ts:139:    if (/Thinking and analyzing/i.test(text)) return \"Nexus is considering the next step\";\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md:26:- \"Parity with Codex and Claude Code\" (HIST-06).\ncli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts:76: * Nexus issued with the authorized task (the first prompt, or a resume prompt where compaction kept only that). The\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CURRENT-NEXUS-CONTEXT-ARCHITECTURE.md:80:**`ContextRouteManager`**: no such symbol exists anywhere in `cli/src` or `core/src` (grep). Nothing in Nexus is currently a context planner/router. …4530 tokens truncated…ERY/broader-failed.txt:495:        You are Nexus Code, an autonomous AI software engineering agent running in a Linux she